/* GENERATED by lib/ — do not hand-edit; edit exams/<id>/research/q*.json then run lib/merge.py */
window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["aip-c01"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"A retail company has a generative AI (GenAI) product recommendation application that uses Amazon Bedrock. The application suggests products to customers based on browsing history and demographics. The company needs to implement fairness evaluation across multiple demographic groups to detect and measure bias in recommendations between two prompt approaches. The company wants to collect and monitor fairness metrics in real time. The company must receive an alert if the fairness metrics show a discrepancy of more than 15% between demographic groups. The company must receive weekly reports that compare the performance of the two prompt approaches. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST custom development effort?","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard to display default metrics from Amazon Bedrock API calls. Create custom metrics based on model outputs. Set up Amazon EventBridge rules to invoke AWS lambda functions that perform post-processing analysis on model responses and publish custom fairness metrics.","B":"Create the two prompt variants in Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management. Use Amazon Bedrock Flows to deploy the prompt variants with defined traffic allocation. Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails that have content filters to monitor demographic fairness. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms on the GuardrailContentSource dimension that use InvocationsIntervened metrics to detect recommendation discrepancy threshold violations.","C":"Set up Amazon SageMaker Clarify to analyze model outputs. Publish fairness metrics to Amazon CloudWatch. Create CloudWatch composite alarms that combine SageMaker Clarify bias metrics with Amazon Bedrock latency metrics to provide a comprehensive fairness evaluation dashboard.","D":"Create an Amazon Bedrock model evaluation job to compare fairness between the two prompt variants. Enable model invocation logging in Amazon CloudWatch. Set up CloudWatch alarms for InvocationsIntervened metrics with a dimension for each demographic group."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":62,"A":18,"D":15,"B":6},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":1,"pages":[2,3,4]},"question_zh":"一家零售公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建置生成式 AI（GenAI）商品推薦應用程式，依顧客的瀏覽紀錄及人口統計資料推薦商品。公司需要對多個人口群體進行公平性評估，以偵測及衡量兩種提示方法在推薦結果上的偏差。公司希望即時收集及監控公平性指標；當不同人口群體之間的指標差異超過 15% 時，必須收到警示，並且每週收到比較兩種提示方法表現的報告。哪個方案能以最少的自訂開發工作滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Amazon CloudWatch 儀表板，顯示 Amazon Bedrock API 呼叫的預設指標。依據模型輸出建立自訂指標。設定 Amazon EventBridge 規則，叫用 AWS Lambda 函數對模型回應進行後處理分析，並發布自訂公平性指標。","B":"在 Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management 中建立兩種提示變體。使用 Amazon Bedrock Flows 按指定的流量比例部署提示變體。設定含有內容篩選器的 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，監控人口群體間的公平性。在 GuardrailContentSource 維度的 InvocationsIntervened 指標上設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示，偵測推薦差異是否超過門檻。","C":"設定 Amazon SageMaker Clarify 分析模型輸出，將公平性指標發布至 Amazon CloudWatch。建立 CloudWatch 複合警示，結合 SageMaker Clarify 偏差指標與 Amazon Bedrock 延遲指標，提供完整的公平性評估儀表板。","D":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 模型評估工作，比較兩種提示變體的公平性。啟用 Amazon CloudWatch 模型叫用日誌。針對 InvocationsIntervened 指標設定 CloudWatch 警示，並為每個人口群體設定一個維度。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C is the closest available choice because Clarify provides demographic bias metrics and publishes them to CloudWatch. However, the official bias-monitoring workflow computes metrics over scheduled data windows; a real-time inference endpoint does not make its bias evaluation instantaneous. Combining bias and latency alarms does not itself create weekly comparisons of two prompts, and the option omits collection and integration of Bedrock outputs. Treat C as the intended best fit, not a fully specified solution satisfying every requirement; the question is underspecified.","explanation_zh":"C 是選項中最接近需求的答案：Clarify 能計算人口群體偏差指標，並發布至 CloudWatch。但官方偏差監控是依排程彙整資料視窗計算；監控即時推論端點不代表公平性評估本身即時執行。結合偏差與延遲警示不會自動產生兩種提示的每週比較報告，選項也未交代 Bedrock 輸出的收集與整合。應將 C 視為題目意圖上的最佳選項，而非已完整滿足全部條件的方案；本題敘述不充分。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Custom post-processing can calculate fairness, but requires more custom implementation and does not specify weekly reports.","why_zh":"自訂後處理能計算公平性，但開發工作較多，也未交代每週報告。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Guardrail interventions measure content-policy enforcement, not demographic recommendation fairness; the stated traffic and fairness behavior is not established.","why_zh":"防護機制介入次數衡量內容政策處理，並非人口群體推薦公平性；選項所稱的流量與公平性行為缺乏依據。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Model evaluation is job based; guardrail intervention metrics do not become demographic fairness metrics by enabling invocation logging.","why_zh":"模型評估以工作方式執行；啟用叫用日誌，不會讓防護機制介入指標變成人口群體公平性指標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-model-monitor-bias-drift-cw.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-model-monitor-bias-drift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Create_Composite_Alarm.html"],"issues":["underspecified_realtime_and_reporting"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:05:52.171676+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・多選項拉鋸・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":2,"question_en":"A finance company is developing an AI assistant to help clients plan investments and manage their portfolios. The company identifies several high-risk conversation patterns such as requests for specific stock recommendations or guaranteed returns. High-risk conversation patterns could lead to regulatory violations if the company cannot implement appropriate controls. The company must ensure that the AI assistant does not provide inappropriate financial advice, generate content about competitors, or make claims that are not factually grounded in the company's approved financial guidance. The company wants to use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to implement a solution. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","options_en":{"A":"Add the high-risk conversation patterns to a denied topics guardrail.","B":"Configure a content filter guardrail to filter prompts that contain the high-risk conversation patterns.","C":"Configure a content filter guardrail to filter prompts that contain competitor names.","D":"Add the names of competitors as custom word filters. Set the input and output actions to block.","E":"Set a low grounding score threshold.","F":"Set a high grounding score threshold."},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ADF":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":2,"pages":[5,6]},"question_zh":"一家金融公司正在開發 AI 助理，協助客戶規劃投資及管理投資組合。公司辨識出數種高風險對話模式，例如要求推薦特定股票或保證報酬。如果無法實施適當控制，這些對話模式可能導致違反監管規定。公司必須確保 AI 助理不提供不當財務建議、不產生與競爭對手有關的內容，也不提出缺乏公司核准財務指引依據的主張。公司希望使用 Amazon Bedrock Guardrails 實作方案。哪三個步驟的組合能滿足需求？（選三項。）","options_zh":{"A":"將高風險對話模式加入防護機制的禁止主題。","B":"設定內容篩選防護機制，篩選包含高風險對話模式的提示。","C":"設定內容篩選防護機制，篩選包含競爭對手名稱的提示。","D":"將競爭對手名稱加入自訂字詞篩選器，並將輸入及輸出的動作設為封鎖。","E":"設定較低的 grounding 分數門檻。","F":"設定較高的 grounding 分數門檻。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Denied topics address prohibited financial subject matter, whereas exact-match custom word filters address competitor names. A higher contextual grounding threshold blocks responses with insufficient support in the supplied reference, so A, D and F match the three requested controls. Provide the approved guidance as grounding source and the user request as query. This is not a guarantee that a multi-turn financial chatbot is factually safe: the grounding documentation explicitly excludes conversational QA/chatbot use cases, and controls must be evaluated within the supported grounded-answer workflow.","explanation_zh":"禁止主題用來控制不允許的財務議題，自訂字詞篩選器則以精確比對封鎖競爭對手名稱。提高 contextual grounding 門檻，可封鎖缺乏參考資料支持的回應，因此 A、D、F 分別對應三項控制。必須提供核准指引作為 grounding source，以及使用者問題作為 query。這不代表多輪財務聊天機器人已獲得事實正確性保證：grounding 文件明列不支援 conversational QA／chatbot 使用情境，應在受支援的有來源問答流程內評估控制效果。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Predefined harmful-content categories do not replace application-specific denied financial topics.","why_zh":"預先定義的有害內容類別不能取代應用程式特定的禁止財務主題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Competitor names belong in custom word filters, not the predefined content categories.","why_zh":"競爭對手名稱應使用自訂字詞篩選，而非預先定義的內容類別。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A lower threshold permits responses with weaker grounding scores.","why_zh":"較低門檻會允許 grounding 分數較低的回應。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-word-filters.html"],"issues":["grounding_chatbot_scope"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:05:52.173091+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":3,"question_en":"A company has deployed an AI assistant as a React application that uses AWS Amplify, an AWS AppSync GraphQL API, and Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. The application uses the GraphQL API to call the Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API for knowledge base interactions. The company configures an AWS Lambda resolver to use the RequestResponse invocation type. Application users report frequent timeouts and slow response times. Users report these problems more frequently for complex questions that require longer processing. The company needs a solution to fix these performance issues and enhance the user experience. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Amplify AI Kit to implement streaming responses from the GraphQL API and to optimize client- side rendering.","B":"Increase the timeout value of the Lambda resolver. Implement retry logic with exponential backoff.","C":"Update the application to send an API request to an Amazon SQS queue. Update the AWS AppSync resolver to poll and process the queue.","D":"Change the RetrieveAndGenerate API to the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API. Update the application to use an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API to support the streaming response."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":67,"D":33},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":3,"pages":[7,8]},"question_zh":"一家公司部署了以 React 開發的 AI 助理應用程式，使用 AWS Amplify、AWS AppSync GraphQL API 與 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases。應用程式透過 GraphQL API 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API，與知識庫互動。公司將 AWS Lambda 解析器設定為使用 RequestResponse 叫用類型。使用者反映經常逾時及回應緩慢，尤其是需要較長處理時間的複雜問題。公司需要解決效能問題並改善使用者體驗。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Amplify AI Kit 實作 GraphQL API 的串流回應，並最佳化用戶端渲染。","B":"增加 Lambda 解析器的逾時時間，並實作指數退避重試邏輯。","C":"修改應用程式，將 API 請求送至 Amazon SQS 佇列。修改 AWS AppSync 解析器以輪詢並處理佇列。","D":"將 RetrieveAndGenerate API 改為 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API，並修改應用程式，使用 Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API 支援串流回應。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amplify AI Kit streams Bedrock output through Lambda and AppSync subscriptions, and its React hook updates messages as chunks arrive. This supports progressive rendering instead of holding a synchronous resolver open for the complete answer. The existing knowledge-base retrieval must still be integrated into the conversation workflow. InvokeModelWithResponseStream alone performs model inference and does not preserve the retrieval performed by RetrieveAndGenerate. Native knowledge-base streaming is available through RetrieveAndGenerateStream, which option D does not name.","explanation_zh":"Amplify AI Kit 透過 Lambda 與 AppSync 訂閱傳遞 Bedrock 的串流輸出，React hook 會在收到片段時更新訊息，讓介面逐步顯示內容，避免同步解析器一直等待完整答案。既有知識庫檢索仍須整合進對話流程。單獨使用 InvokeModelWithResponseStream 只會執行模型推論，並不保留 RetrieveAndGenerate 所提供的檢索步驟。 知識庫原生串流可使用 RetrieveAndGenerateStream，但 D 並未指定這個 API。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Longer Lambda execution and retries do not establish streaming and can increase waiting time.","why_zh":"延長 Lambda 執行時間與重試不會建立串流，可能使等待更久。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Queueing requires an asynchronous result-delivery design; polling from the resolver does not solve progressive rendering.","why_zh":"佇列需要非同步結果傳遞設計；由解析器輪詢不能直接解決逐步呈現問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The inference-streaming API is not a drop-in replacement for knowledge-base retrieval and generation.","why_zh":"模型推論串流 API 不能直接取代知識庫檢索與生成。"}],"sources":["https://docs.amplify.aws/react/ai/concepts/streaming/","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_RetrieveAndGenerateStream.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:05:52.174255+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":4,"question_en":"An ecommerce company operates a global product recommendation system that needs to switch between multiple foundation models (FM) in Amazon Bedrock based on regulations, cost optimization, and performance requirements. The company must apply custom controls based on proprietary business logic, including dynamic cost thresholds, AWS Region-specific compliance rules, and real-time A/B testing across multiple FMs. The system must be able to switch between FMs without deploying new code. The system must route user requests based on complex rules including user tier, transaction value, regulatory zone, and real-time cost metrics that change hourly and require immediate propagation across thousands of concurrent requests. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that uses environment variables to store routing rules and Amazon Bedrock FM IDs. Use the Lambda console to update the environment variables when business requirements change. Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API to read request parameters to make routing decisions.","B":"Deploy Amazon API Gateway REST API request transformation templates to implement routing logic based on request attributes. Store Amazon Bedrock FM endpoints as REST API stage variables. Update the variables when the system switches between models.","C":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to fetch routing configurations from the AWS AppConfig Agent for each user request. Run business logic in the Lambda function to select the appropriate FM for each request. Expose the FM through a single Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoint.","D":"Use AWS Lambda authorizers for an Amazon API Gateway REST API to evaluate routing rules that are stored in AWS AppConfig. Return authorization contexts based on business logic. Route requests to model- specific Lambda functions for each Amazon Bedrock FM."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":4,"pages":[9,10]},"question_zh":"一家電子商務公司營運全球商品推薦系統，需要依監管、成本最佳化及效能需求，在 Amazon Bedrock 的多個基礎模型（FM）之間切換。公司必須依專有商業邏輯套用自訂控制，包括動態成本門檻、AWS 區域特定合規規則，以及多個 FM 之間的即時 A/B 測試。系統必須能在不部署新程式碼的情況下切換 FM。系統必須依複雜規則路由使用者請求，包括使用者等級、交易金額、監管區域，以及每小時變更且必須立即傳播至數千個並行請求的即時成本指標。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"部署 AWS Lambda 函數，使用環境變數儲存路由規則與 Amazon Bedrock FM ID。商業需求變更時，在 Lambda 主控台更新環境變數。設定 Amazon API Gateway REST API 讀取請求參數以決定路由。","B":"部署 Amazon API Gateway REST API 請求轉換範本，依請求屬性實作路由邏輯。將 Amazon Bedrock FM 端點儲存為 REST API 階段變數，並在系統切換模型時更新變數。","C":"設定 AWS Lambda 函數，針對每個使用者請求從 AWS AppConfig Agent 取得路由設定。在 Lambda 函數中執行商業邏輯，為每個請求選擇適當的 FM。透過單一 Amazon API Gateway REST API 端點提供 FM 存取。","D":"使用 Amazon API Gateway REST API 的 AWS Lambda 授權器，評估儲存在 AWS AppConfig 的路由規則。依商業邏輯傳回授權內容，將請求路由至各個 Amazon Bedrock FM 專用的 Lambda 函數。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AppConfig separates routing configuration from Lambda code, and the agent provides a local cached configuration endpoint. Lambda can use this configuration with request attributes to implement the required custom routing behind one API. C is the best architectural fit. The word immediate is too strong: each concurrent Lambda environment has its own cache, and propagation depends on deployment strategy and polling interval; AppConfig does not promise instantaneous global consistency.","explanation_zh":"AppConfig 將路由設定與 Lambda 程式碼分離，Agent 提供本機快取設定端點。Lambda 可結合設定與請求屬性，在單一 API 後方執行自訂路由，因此 C 最符合架構需求。但題目所稱「立即」過於絕對：每個並行 Lambda 執行環境都有獨立快取，更新傳播受部署策略與輪詢間隔影響，AppConfig 並不保證瞬間全球一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Environment-variable updates are function configuration changes and do not provide the requested centrally managed dynamic routing mechanism.","why_zh":"更新環境變數屬函數設定變更，未提供題目所需的集中式動態路由機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Request transformations and stage variables are not a suitable home for the full proprietary decision engine and dynamic cost rules.","why_zh":"請求轉換與階段變數不適合承載完整的專有決策引擎及動態成本規則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An authorizer supplies access decisions/context; using it as the routing engine adds coupling and does not directly define the selected backend integration.","why_zh":"授權器負責存取判斷與授權內容；將其作為路由引擎會增加耦合，也不會直接定義所選後端整合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-integration-lambda-extensions-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-integration-lambda-extensions-config.html"],"issues":["immediate_propagation_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:05:52.175457+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":5,"question_en":"A company is developing an internal generative AI (GenAI) assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock to summarize corporate documents for multiple business units. The GenAI assistant must generate responses in a consistent format that includes a document summary, classification of business risks, and terms that are flagged for review. The GenAI assistant must adapt the tone of responses for each user's business unit, such as legal, human resources, or finance. The GenAI assistant must block hate speech, inappropriate topics, and sensitive information such as personal health information. The company needs a solution to centrally manage prompt variants across business units and teams. The company wants to minimize ongoing orchestration efforts and maintenance for post-processing logic. The company also wants to have the ability to adjust content moderation criteria for the GenAI assistant over time. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST maintenance overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to configure reusable templates and business unit-specific prompt variants. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails that have category filters and sensitive term lists to block prohibited content.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to define base templates. Enforce business unit-specific tone by using system prompt variables. Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply audience-based threshold tuning. Manage the guardrails by using an internal administration API.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock with business unit-based instruction injection in API calls. Store response formatting rules in Amazon DynamoDB. Use AWS Step functions to validate responses. Use Amazon Comprehend to apply content filters after the GenAI assistant generates responses.","D":"Use Amazon Bedrock with custom prompt templates that are stored in Amazon DynamoDB. Create one AWS Lambda function to select business unit-specific prompts. Create a second Lambda function to call Amazon Comprehend to filter prohibited content from responses."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":5,"pages":[11,12]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在開發內部生成式 AI（GenAI）助理，使用 Amazon Bedrock 為多個事業單位摘要公司文件。助理必須以一致格式產生回應，包含文件摘要、業務風險分類及標記為需要審查的詞彙。助理必須依使用者所屬的法務、人力資源或財務等事業單位調整回應語氣，並封鎖仇恨言論、不適當主題及個人健康資訊等敏感資料。公司需要集中管理各事業單位與團隊的提示變體，盡量減少持續的流程編排及後處理邏輯維護工作，也希望能隨時調整內容審核標準。哪個方案能以最低的維護負擔滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management 設定可重複使用的範本，以及各事業單位專用的提示變體。套用具有類別篩選器與敏感詞彙清單的 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，封鎖禁止內容。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management 定義基礎範本，透過系統提示變數強制採用各事業單位專用的語氣。設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，依受眾調整門檻，並使用內部管理 API 管理防護機制。","C":"使用 Amazon Bedrock，在 API 呼叫中注入各事業單位專用的指令。將回應格式規則儲存在 Amazon DynamoDB。使用 AWS Step Functions 驗證回應，並使用 Amazon Comprehend 在助理產生回應後套用內容篩選。","D":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 搭配儲存在 Amazon DynamoDB 的自訂提示範本。建立一個 AWS Lambda 函數選擇事業單位專用提示，再建立另一個 Lambda 函數呼叫 Amazon Comprehend，從回應中篩除禁止內容。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Prompt management provides reusable prompts, variables, variants and versions, reducing custom prompt-storage and orchestration code. Guardrails provides content-category, denied-topic, word and sensitive-information controls; A is the closest managed-service combination. Sensitive term lists alone cannot detect every form of personal health information: configure supported sensitive-information entities and custom patterns, evaluate coverage, and apply topic controls as appropriate. Prompt formatting instructions also require output validation when a strict schema is mandatory.","explanation_zh":"Prompt management 提供可重複使用的提示、變數、變體與版本，可減少自行儲存提示與編排流程的程式。Guardrails 提供內容類別、禁止主題、字詞及敏感資訊控制，A 是最接近需求的受管服務組合。僅靠敏感詞彙清單無法辨識所有個人健康資訊：仍須設定受支援的敏感資訊實體與自訂模式、評估涵蓋率，並視需要套用主題控制。若輸出必須嚴格符合結構，也需要驗證，不能只依賴提示中的格式指令。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Audience-based automatic threshold tuning is not established by the documented guardrail controls and the internal administration API adds maintenance.","why_zh":"文件中的防護控制未建立依受眾自動調整門檻的能力，內部管理 API 也增加維護工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Custom instruction injection, DynamoDB rules, Step Functions and Comprehend add orchestration and post-processing.","why_zh":"自訂指令注入、DynamoDB 規則、Step Functions 與 Comprehend 增加編排及後處理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom prompt store and separate selection/filtering Lambdas create more components to maintain.","why_zh":"自訂提示儲存及分離的選擇／篩選 Lambda 增加待維護元件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html"],"issues":["sensitive_term_lists_not_complete_phi_detection"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:05:52.176309+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":6,"question_en":"A financial services company is building a customer support application that retrieves relevant financial regulation documents from a database based on semantic similarities to user queries. The application must integrate with Amazon Bedrock to generate responses. The application must be able to search documents that are in English, Spanish, and Portuguese. The application must filter documents by metadata such as publication date, regulatory agency, and document type. The database stores approximately 10 million document embeddings. To minimize operational overhead, the company wants a solution that minimizes management and maintenance effort. The application must provide low-latency responses for real-time customer interactions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to provide vector search capabilities and metadata filtering. Connect to Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to enable Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities that use an Anthropic Claude foundation model (FM).","B":"Deploy an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database with the pgvector extension. Define tables to store embeddings and metadata. Use SQL queries to perform similarity searches. Send retrieved documents to Amazon Bedrock to generate responses.","C":"Use Amazon S3 Vectors to configure a vector index and non-filterable metadata fields. Integrate S3 Vectors with Amazon Bedrock to enable Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities.","D":"Set up an Amazon Neptune Analytics graph database. Configure a vector index that has appropriate dimensionality to store document embeddings. Use Amazon Bedrock to perform graph-based retrieval and to generate responses."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":6,"pages":[13,14]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在建立客服應用程式，依使用者查詢的語意相似度，從資料庫檢索相關金融監管文件，並整合 Amazon Bedrock 產生回應。應用程式必須能搜尋英文、西班牙文及葡萄牙文文件，並依發布日期、監管機關及文件類型等中繼資料篩選文件。資料庫約儲存 1,000 萬筆文件嵌入向量。公司希望盡量減少管理與維護工作，降低維運負擔。應用程式必須以低延遲支援即時客服互動。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch Serverless 提供向量搜尋及中繼資料篩選。連接 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases，使用 Anthropic Claude 基礎模型（FM）提供檢索增強生成（RAG）功能。","B":"部署具有 pgvector 擴充功能的 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 資料庫。定義資料表以儲存嵌入向量及中繼資料。使用 SQL 查詢執行相似度搜尋，並將檢索到的文件傳給 Amazon Bedrock 產生回應。","C":"使用 Amazon S3 Vectors 設定向量索引及不可篩選的中繼資料欄位。將 S3 Vectors 與 Amazon Bedrock 整合，提供檢索增強生成（RAG）功能。","D":"設定 Amazon Neptune Analytics 圖形資料庫，並設定適當維度的向量索引以儲存文件嵌入向量。使用 Amazon Bedrock 執行圖形檢索及產生回應。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"OpenSearch Serverless with Bedrock Knowledge Bases provides managed vector retrieval with metadata filters, making A the best fit for low operational overhead. The embedding model must support the document languages; Claude generates the answer but is not itself the vector index or embedding model. Configure filterable publication-date, agency and type metadata and validate retrieval latency at the expected scale. C explicitly selects non-filterable metadata, which conflicts with the filtering requirement; this does not mean S3 Vectors lacks metadata filtering in general.","explanation_zh":"OpenSearch Serverless 搭配 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 提供受管向量檢索及中繼資料篩選，因此 A 最符合低維運負擔需求。嵌入模型必須支援文件語言；Claude 用於產生答案，本身不是向量索引或嵌入模型。發布日期、機關及類型須設定為可篩選的中繼資料，並依預期規模驗證延遲。C 明確選用不可篩選的中繼資料，與篩選需求衝突；這不代表 S3 Vectors 一般而言不支援中繼資料篩選。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Technically viable, but this option implements tables, SQL retrieval and model orchestration explicitly rather than using the managed RAG integration.","why_zh":"技術上可行，但此選項明列自行建立資料表、SQL 檢索及模型串接，維護工作較受管 RAG 整合多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Non-filterable metadata cannot be used for the required attribute filters.","why_zh":"不可篩選的中繼資料無法作為所需屬性篩選條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"No graph relationship traversal is requested; introducing a graph model adds unnecessary design work.","why_zh":"需求沒有圖形關係走訪；引入圖形資料模型增加不必要的設計工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-vectors-metadata-filtering.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:15:57.044977+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":7,"question_en":"A medical company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses RAG to provide evidence-based medical information. The application uses Amazon OpenSearch Service to retrieve vector embeddings. Users report that searches frequently miss results that contain exact medical terms and acronyms and return too many semantically similar but irrelevant documents. The company needs to improve retrieval quality and maintain low end user latency, even as the document collection grows to millions of documents. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Configure hybrid search by combining vector similarity with keyword matching to improve semantic understanding and exact term and acronym matching.","B":"Increase the dimensions of the vector embeddings from 384 to 1536. Use a post-processing AWS Lambda function to filter out irrelevant results after retrieval.","C":"Replace OpenSearch Service with Amazon Kendra. Use query expansion to handle medical acronyms and terminology variants during pre-processing.","D":"Implement a two-stage retrieval architecture in which initial vector search results are re-ranked by an ML model that is hosted on Amazon SageMaker AI."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":7,"pages":[15]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司正在建立使用 RAG 的生成式 AI（GenAI）應用程式，提供有實證依據的醫療資訊。應用程式使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 檢索向量嵌入。使用者反映搜尋經常漏掉包含精確醫療術語及縮寫的結果，並傳回過多語意相似但不相關的文件。公司需要改善檢索品質，且即使文件數增加至數百萬份，仍須維持低使用者端延遲。哪個方案能以最少的維運負擔滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定混合搜尋，結合向量相似度與關鍵字比對，同時改善語意理解及精確術語、縮寫的比對。","B":"將向量嵌入維度從 384 增加至 1536。使用後處理 AWS Lambda 函數，在檢索後篩除不相關結果。","C":"將 OpenSearch Service 換成 Amazon Kendra，並在前處理時使用查詢擴展，處理醫療縮寫及術語變體。","D":"實作兩階段檢索架構，由託管在 Amazon SageMaker AI 的 ML 模型，對初步向量搜尋結果重新排序。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Hybrid search combines lexical matching with semantic vector retrieval, directly addressing missed exact medical terms and acronyms. OpenSearch provides hybrid queries and score-combination pipelines, so the existing search architecture can be improved without adding a separate reranking service. Tune score normalization and weights using representative queries. Increasing embedding dimensions alone does not guarantee exact keyword recall.","explanation_zh":"混合搜尋結合詞彙比對與語意向量檢索，可直接改善漏掉精確醫療術語及縮寫的問題。OpenSearch 提供混合查詢及分數合併管線，能在既有搜尋架構中改善結果，無須額外建立獨立重排序服務。仍應使用代表性查詢調整分數正規化及權重。單純增加嵌入維度不能保證召回精確關鍵字。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Higher dimensionality increases storage/compute, and post-filtering does not recover documents that were never retrieved.","why_zh":"提高維度增加儲存與運算需求，後處理篩選也無法取回原先未檢索到的文件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Replacing the existing search service and adding query expansion introduces migration and preprocessing work.","why_zh":"替換既有搜尋服務並加入查詢擴展，需要遷移及前處理工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reranking can improve ordering but adds a hosted model and cannot recover missing candidates outside the first-stage result set.","why_zh":"重新排序能改善順序，但增加模型託管，而且無法取回不在第一階段候選集中的文件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/serverless-configure-neural-search.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:15:57.046633+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":8,"question_en":"A company runs a generative AI (GenAI)-powered summarization application in an application AWS account that uses Amazon Bedrock. The application architecture includes an Amazon API Gateway REST API that forwards requests to AWS Lambda functions that are attached to private VPC subnets. The application summarizes sensitive customer records that the company stores in a governed data lake in a centralized data storage account. The company has enabled Amazon S3, Amazon Athena, and AWS Glue in the data storage account. The company must ensure that calls that the application makes to Amazon Bedrock use only private connectivity between the company's application VPC and Amazon Bedrock. The company's data lake must provide fine-grained column-level access across the company's AWS accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"In the application account, create interface VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock runtimes. Run Lambda functions in private subnets. Use IAM conditions on inference and data-plane policies to allow calls only to approved endpoints and roles. In the data storage account, use AWS Lake Formation LF-tag-based access control to create table and column-level cross-account grants.","B":"Run Lambda functions in private subnets. Configure a NAT gateway to provide access to Amazon Bedrock and the data lake. Use S3 bucket policies and ACLs to manage permissions. Export AWS CloudTrail logs to Amazon S3 to perform weekly reviews.","C":"Create a gateway endpoint only for Amazon S3 in the application account. Invoke Amazon Bedrock through public endpoints. Use database-level grants in AWS Lake Formation to manage data access. Stream AWS CloudTrail logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Do not set up metric filters or alarms.","D":"Use VPC endpoints to provide access to Amazon Bedrock and Amazon S3 in the application account. Use only IAM path-based policies to manage data lake access. Send AWS CloudTrail logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Periodically create dashboards and allow public fallback for cross-Region reads to reduce setup time."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":8,"pages":[17,18]},"question_zh":"一家公司在應用程式 AWS 帳戶中執行使用 Amazon Bedrock 的生成式 AI（GenAI）摘要應用程式。架構包含 Amazon API Gateway REST API，將請求轉送至連接私有 VPC 子網路的 AWS Lambda 函數。應用程式摘要的敏感客戶紀錄，儲存在集中式資料儲存帳戶中受治理的資料湖。公司已在資料儲存帳戶啟用 Amazon S3、Amazon Athena 與 AWS Glue。公司必須確保應用程式對 Amazon Bedrock 的呼叫，僅使用應用程式 VPC 與 Bedrock 之間的私有連線。資料湖也必須在公司各 AWS 帳戶之間提供精細的欄位層級存取控制。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在應用程式帳戶建立 Amazon Bedrock 執行期的介面 VPC 端點，並在私有子網路執行 Lambda 函數。在推論與資料平面政策中使用 IAM 條件，只允許核准的端點及角色進行呼叫。在資料儲存帳戶使用 AWS Lake Formation 的 LF 標籤式存取控制，建立資料表與欄位層級的跨帳戶授權。","B":"在私有子網路執行 Lambda 函數，設定 NAT 閘道以存取 Amazon Bedrock 與資料湖。使用 S3 儲存貯體政策及 ACL 管理權限，並將 AWS CloudTrail 日誌匯出至 Amazon S3，每週審查。","C":"僅在應用程式帳戶建立 Amazon S3 閘道端點。透過公有端點呼叫 Amazon Bedrock。使用 AWS Lake Formation 資料庫層級授權管理資料存取，並將 AWS CloudTrail 日誌串流至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，但不設定指標篩選器或警示。","D":"在應用程式帳戶使用 VPC 端點存取 Amazon Bedrock 與 Amazon S3。僅使用 IAM 路徑式政策管理資料湖存取。將 AWS CloudTrail 日誌送至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，定期建立儀表板，並允許跨區域讀取退回公有連線以縮短設定時間。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Bedrock runtime interface endpoints use PrivateLink to provide VPC-private access without a NAT or internet gateway. Apply appropriate IAM source-endpoint conditions and endpoint policies rather than assuming that creating an endpoint alone prevents public access. Lake Formation LF-TBAC supports permissions on tables and columns and cross-account grants. Together these features match both the network and fine-grained governance requirements in A.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock 執行期介面端點透過 PrivateLink 提供 VPC 私有存取，不需要 NAT 或網際網路閘道。應同時套用適當的 IAM 來源端點條件及端點政策，不能假設僅建立端點就會禁止公有存取。Lake Formation LF-TBAC 支援資料表與欄位權限及跨帳戶授權，兩者結合符合 A 所述的私有網路及精細治理需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"NAT access does not enforce PrivateLink-only calls, and bucket ACLs do not provide column-level query permissions.","why_zh":"NAT 存取不會強制僅透過 PrivateLink 呼叫，儲存貯體 ACL 也不提供欄位層級查詢權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Public Bedrock endpoints violate the network requirement; database-level grants are too coarse.","why_zh":"Bedrock 公有端點違反網路需求，資料庫層級授權也過於粗略。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM paths do not implement data-column permissions, and public fallback violates private-only connectivity.","why_zh":"IAM 路徑不能實作資料欄位權限，公有連線備援也違反僅限私有連線的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/lf-tag-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/cross-account-permissions.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:15:57.047732+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":9,"question_en":"A media company must use Amazon Bedrock to implement a robust governance process for AI-generated content. The company needs to manage hundreds of prompt templates. Multiple teams use the templates across multiple AWS Regions to generate content. The solution must provide version control with approval workflows that include notifications for pending reviews. The solution must also provide detailed audit trails that document prompt activities and consistent prompt parameterization to enforce quality standards. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Bedrock Studio prompt templates. Use Amazon CloudWatch to create dashboards that display prompt usage metrics. Store the approval status of content in Amazon DynamoDB. Use AWS Lambda functions to enforce approvals.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to implement version control. Configure AWS CloudTrail for audit logging. Use IAM policies to control approval permissions. Create parameterized prompt templates by specifying variables.","C":"Use AWS Step Functions to create an approval workflow. Store prompts as documents in Amazon S3. Use tags to implement version control. Use Amazon EventBridge to send notifications.","D":"Deploy Amazon SageMaker Canvas with prompt templates that are stored in Amazon S3. Use AWS CloudFormation to implement version control. Use AWS Config to enforce approval policies."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":9,"pages":[19,20]},"question_zh":"一家媒體公司必須使用 Amazon Bedrock 為 AI 產生的內容建立完善的治理流程。公司需要管理數百個提示範本，由多個團隊在多個 AWS 區域中使用以產生內容。方案必須提供版本控制與核准工作流程，包括待審查事項的通知；也必須提供詳細的提示活動稽核軌跡，以及一致的提示參數化機制，以落實品質標準。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Amazon Bedrock Studio 提示範本。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 建立顯示提示使用量指標的儀表板。將內容核准狀態儲存在 Amazon DynamoDB，並使用 AWS Lambda 函數強制執行核准。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management 實作版本控制。設定 AWS CloudTrail 進行稽核記錄。使用 IAM 政策控制核准權限，並透過指定變數建立參數化提示範本。","C":"使用 AWS Step Functions 建立核准工作流程。將提示以文件形式儲存在 Amazon S3，使用標籤實作版本控制，並使用 Amazon EventBridge 傳送通知。","D":"部署 Amazon SageMaker Canvas，將提示範本儲存在 Amazon S3。使用 AWS CloudFormation 實作版本控制，並使用 AWS Config 強制執行核准政策。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B is the closest core design: Prompt management provides versions and variables, while CloudTrail records API activity. IAM policies restrict which principals may perform actions, but they are not an approval workflow engine and do not send pending-review notifications. AWS governance guidance explicitly adds CodePipeline or Step Functions approval gates. The offered answer omits that mechanism and cross-Region distribution details, so it does not fully satisfy the question as written.","explanation_zh":"B 最接近核心設計：Prompt management 提供版本與變數，CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動。但 IAM 政策控制的是哪些主體能執行操作，並非核准流程引擎，也不會傳送待審查通知。AWS 治理指引明確另外使用 CodePipeline 或 Step Functions 實作核准關卡。此選項缺少這項機制及跨區域散布細節，因此並未完整滿足題目原文的全部需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A usage dashboard and custom approval state do not establish full prompt versioning and consistent parameterization.","why_zh":"使用量儀表板及自訂核准狀態未建立完整的提示版本控制與一致參數化。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Step Functions can implement approvals, but object tags alone are not immutable version control and the option omits prompt-management/audit requirements.","why_zh":"Step Functions 可實作核准，但物件標籤本身不等於不可變版本控制，選項也缺少提示管理及稽核需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation versions infrastructure templates; AWS Config is not a human prompt-approval workflow.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 處理基礎設施範本，AWS Config 不是人工提示核准流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/agentic-ai-lens/agentops02-bp01.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html"],"issues":["missing_approval_notifications"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:15:57.048676+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":10,"question_en":"A company is developing a customer support application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to provide real-time AI assistance to the company's employees. The application must display AI-generated responses character by character as the responses are generated. The application needs to support thousands of concurrent users with minimal latency. The responses typically take 15 to 45 seconds to finish. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API with an AWS Lambda integration. Configure the WebSocket API to invoke the Amazon Bedrock InvokeModelWithResponseStream API and stream partial responses through WebSocket connections.","B":"Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API with an AWS Lambda integration. Configure the REST API to invoke the Amazon Bedrock standard InvokeModel API and implement frontend client-side polling every 100 ms for complete response chunks.","C":"Implement direct frontend client connections to Amazon Bedrock by using IAM user credentials and the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API without any intermediate gateway or proxy layer.","D":"Configure an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with an AWS Lambda integration. Configure the HTTP API to cache complete responses in an Amazon DynamoDB table and serve the responses through multiple paginated GET requests to frontend clients."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":10,"pages":[21,22]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在開發客服應用程式，使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）向員工提供即時 AI 協助。應用程式必須在回應產生時逐字顯示 AI 產生的內容，並以最低延遲支援數千名並行使用者。回應通常需要 15 至 45 秒才能完成。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定具有 AWS Lambda 整合的 Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API。設定 WebSocket API 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock InvokeModelWithResponseStream API，並透過 WebSocket 連線串流傳送部分回應。","B":"設定具有 AWS Lambda 整合的 Amazon API Gateway REST API。設定 REST API 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 標準 InvokeModel API，並由前端用戶端每 100 毫秒輪詢完整的回應區塊。","C":"使用 IAM 使用者憑證及 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API，讓前端用戶端直接連接 Amazon Bedrock，不經任何中介閘道或代理層。","D":"設定具有 AWS Lambda 整合的 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API。設定 HTTP API 將完整回應快取至 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表，再透過多個分頁 GET 請求將回應提供給前端用戶端。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A is the appropriate push-streaming architecture: consume Bedrock response chunks in a backend and send them to the connected client with the API Gateway Management API. Chunks are not necessarily one character, so the frontend can progressively render their text. WebSocket integrations have a 29-second maximum timeout, while the prompt allows 45-second generation; acknowledge the route quickly and run long generation asynchronously with callbacks. A is therefore the best option but requires this implementation detail and concurrency/quota planning.","explanation_zh":"A 是合適的主動推送串流架構：後端接收 Bedrock 回應片段，再透過 API Gateway Management API 傳送給已連線的用戶端。片段不一定是一個字元，前端可逐步呈現其中的文字。WebSocket 整合逾時上限為 29 秒，但題目允許生成耗時 45 秒，因此應快速回覆路由請求，讓長時間生成非同步執行並透過回呼傳送內容。A 是最佳選項，但實作仍需這項設計及並行配額規劃。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Standard InvokeModel buffers the result; polling completed output does not expose generation as it happens.","why_zh":"標準 InvokeModel 等待完整結果；輪詢已完成輸出無法在生成時取得內容。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Distributing IAM user credentials to frontend clients creates credential exposure and lacks a controlled backend boundary.","why_zh":"將 IAM 使用者憑證散布至前端會暴露憑證，也缺少受控後端邊界。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Caching completed output and paginating it occurs after generation, not during generation.","why_zh":"快取完整輸出並分頁發送發生在生成完成後，並非生成過程中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-execution-service-websocket-limits-table.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-how-to-call-websocket-api-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_InvokeModelWithResponseStream.html"],"issues":["websocket_29_second_integration_limit"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:15:57.049718+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":11,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Bedrock to design an application to help researchers apply for grants. The application is based on an Amazon Nova Pro foundation model (FM). The application contains four required inputs and must provide responses in a consistent text format. The company wants to receive a notification in Amazon Bedrock if a response contains bullying language. However, the company does not want to block all flagged responses. The company creates an Amazon Bedrock flow that takes an input prompt and sends it to the Amazon Nova Pro FM. The Amazon Nova Pro FM provides a response. Which additional steps must the company take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to specify the required inputs as variables. Select an Amazon Nova Pro FM. Specify the output format for the response. Add the prompt to the prompts node of the flow.","B":"Create an Amazon Bedrock guardrail that applies the hate content filter. Set the filter response to block. Add the guardrail to the prompts node of the flow.","C":"Create an Amazon Bedrock prompt router. Specify an Amazon Nova Pro FM. Add the required inputs as variables to the input node of the flow. Add the prompt router to the prompts node. Add the output format to the output node.","D":"Create an Amazon Bedrock guardrail that applies the insults content filter. Set the filter response to detect. Add the guardrail to the prompts node of the flow.","E":"Create an Amazon Bedrock application inference profile that specifies an Amazon Nova Pro FM. Specify the output format for the response in the description. Include a tag for each of the input variables. Add the profile to the prompts node of the flow."},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AD":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":11,"pages":[23,24]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 設計協助研究人員申請補助的應用程式，以 Amazon Nova Pro 基礎模型（FM）為基礎。應用程式有四個必填輸入，且必須以一致的文字格式回覆。若回應包含霸凌語言，公司希望在 Amazon Bedrock 收到通知，但不希望封鎖所有被標記的回應。公司已建立 Bedrock 流程，接收輸入提示並傳送至 Amazon Nova Pro FM，再由模型提供回應。還需要採取哪兩個步驟才能滿足需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management 將必填輸入指定為變數。選擇 Amazon Nova Pro FM，指定回應輸出格式，並將提示加入流程的提示節點。","B":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，套用仇恨內容篩選器，將篩選回應設為封鎖，並將防護機制加入流程的提示節點。","C":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 提示路由器並指定 Amazon Nova Pro FM。將必填輸入以變數形式加入流程的輸入節點，將提示路由器加入提示節點，並將輸出格式加入輸出節點。","D":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，套用侮辱內容篩選器，將篩選回應設為偵測，並將防護機制加入流程的提示節點。","E":"建立指定 Amazon Nova Pro FM 的 Amazon Bedrock 應用程式推論設定檔。在描述中指定回應輸出格式，為每個輸入變數加入標籤，並將設定檔加入流程的提示節點。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Prompt management supplies reusable variables and formatting instructions for the flow prompt. Bullying is classified as Insults, and detect mode reports findings in the trace without blocking the response. Thus A and D match the requested behavior. Detect mode is not an out-of-band notification service; if push notifications are required, the application must process the trace and send them.","explanation_zh":"Prompt management 可在流程提示中提供可重複使用的變數與格式指令。霸凌語言屬於 Insults，detect 模式會在 trace 回傳偵測結果，而不封鎖回應，因此選 A、D。Detect 模式本身不是外部推播通知服務；若需要推播通知，應由應用程式處理 trace 後另行傳送。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Hate is identity-based abuse, and blocking conflicts with the detect-only requirement.","why_zh":"Hate 針對身分類別的仇恨；封鎖也不符合僅偵測需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A model router is not the prompt-template/variable management mechanism described in A.","why_zh":"模型路由器不是 A 所述的提示範本與變數管理機制。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Inference-profile descriptions and tags do not define prompt variables or enforce response formats.","why_zh":"推論設定檔的描述與標籤不會定義提示變數或強制回應格式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-harmful-content-handling-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-content-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-bedrock-flow-promptflownodeconfiguration.html"],"issues":["notification_requires_trace_handling"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:20:17.762536+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":12,"question_en":"A healthcare company is using Amazon Bedrock to build a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that helps practitioners make clinical decisions. The application must achieve high accuracy for patient information retrievals, identify hallucinations in generated content, and reduce human review costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Comprehend to analyze and classify RAG responses and to extract medical entities and relationships. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate automated evaluations. Configure Amazon CloudWatch metrics to track entity recognition confidence scores. Configure CloudWatch to send an alert when accuracy falls below specified thresholds.","B":"Implement automated large language model (LLM)-based evaluations that use a specialized model that is fine-tuned for medical content to assess all responses. Deploy AWS Lambda functions to parallelize evaluations. Publish results to Amazon CloudWatch metrics that track relevance and factual accuracy.","C":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics to generate test queries that have known answers on a regular schedule, and track model success rates. Set up dashboards that compare synthetic test results against expected outcomes.","D":"Deploy a hybrid evaluation system that uses an automated LLM-as-a-judge evaluation to initially screen responses and targeted human reviews for edge cases. Use Amazon SageMaker Feature Store to maintain evaluation datasets. Use a built-in Amazon Bedrock evaluation to track retrieval precision and hallucination rates."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":12,"pages":[25,26]},"question_zh":"一家醫療保健公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建置檢索增強生成（RAG）應用程式，協助醫療人員進行臨床決策。應用程式必須高準確度地檢索病患資訊、辨識生成內容中的幻覺，並降低人工審查成本。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 分析及分類 RAG 回應，並擷取醫療實體與關係。使用 AWS Step Functions 編排自動評估。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 指標追蹤實體辨識信心分數，並在準確度低於指定門檻時傳送警示。","B":"實作自動大型語言模型（LLM）評估，以針對醫療內容微調的專用模型評估所有回應。部署 AWS Lambda 函數並行執行評估，並將結果發布至追蹤相關性及事實準確度的 Amazon CloudWatch 指標。","C":"設定 Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics，定期產生有已知答案的測試查詢，並追蹤模型成功率。設定儀表板，比較合成測試結果與預期結果。","D":"部署混合評估系統，先使用自動 LLM-as-a-judge 評估篩選回應，再針對邊界案例進行人工審查。使用 Amazon SageMaker Feature Store 維護評估資料集，並使用 Amazon Bedrock 內建評估追蹤檢索精確度及幻覺率。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D combines scalable automated judging with focused human review, which is the best fit for lowering review cost while examining difficult responses. Bedrock RAG evaluation offers context relevance/coverage for retrieval and faithfulness/correctness for generation. The option uses imprecise metric names: citation precision is not retrieval precision, and faithfulness is not a universal factual-truth guarantee. Feature Store is not required as the evaluation dataset store; maintain a suitable evaluation dataset and use the supported input format. Bedrock evaluation consumes JSONL datasets stored in Amazon S3.","explanation_zh":"D 結合可擴展的自動評分與重點人工審查，最符合降低審查成本、同時檢查困難回應的方向。Bedrock RAG 評估提供檢索的 context relevance／coverage，以及生成的 faithfulness／correctness。選項的指標名稱不夠精確：citation precision 不等於檢索精確度，faithfulness 也不保證所有事實均正確。評估資料集並不必然需要 Feature Store；應維護合適的資料集，並依評估服務支援的輸入格式提供。 Bedrock 評估使用儲存在 Amazon S3 的 JSONL 資料集。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Entity extraction confidence does not measure retrieval relevance or hallucination against evidence.","why_zh":"實體擷取信心分數不能衡量檢索相關性或相對於證據的幻覺。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A specialized judge may help, but automated review of every response lacks targeted human adjudication of difficult cases.","why_zh":"專用評分模型可能有幫助，但全自動評估缺少困難案例的人工判斷。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Synthetic known-answer tests cover selected paths and do not provide the requested full evaluation strategy.","why_zh":"已知答案的合成測試只涵蓋選定路徑，未提供完整的評估策略。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-evaluation-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-evaluation-prompt.html"],"issues":["metric_names_and_dataset_store_imprecise"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:20:17.766174+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":13,"question_en":"Company configures a landing zone in AWS Control Tower. The company handles sensitive data that must remain within the European Union. The company must use only the eu-central-1 Region. The company uses SCPs to enforce data residency policies. GenAI developers at the company are assigned IAM roles that have full permissions for Amazon Bedrock. The company must ensure that GenAI developers can use the Amazon Nova Pro model through Amazon Bedrock only by using cross-Region inference (CRI) and only in eu-central-1. The company enables model access for the GenAI developer IAM roles in Amazon Bedrock. However, when a GenAI developer attempts to invoke the model through the Amazon Bedrock Chat/Text playground, the GenAI developer receives the following error. User: arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/AssumedDevRole/DevUserName Action: bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream On resource(s): arn:aws:bedrock:eu-west-3::foundation-model/amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 Context: a service control policy explicitly denies the action The company needs a solution to resolve the error. The solution must retain the company's existing governance controls and must provide precise access control. The solution must comply with the company's existing data residency policies. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Add an AdministratorAccess policy to the GenAI developer IAM role.","B":"Extend the existing SCPs to enable CRI for the eu.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 inference profile.","C":"Enable Amazon Bedrock model access for Amazon Nova Pro in the eu-west-3 Region.","D":"Validate that the GenAI developer IAM roles have permissions to invoke Amazon Nova Pro through the eu.amazon.nova-pro.v1:0 inference profile on all European Union AWS Regions that can serve the model.","E":"Extend the existing SCP to enable CRI for the eu.* inference profile."},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":75,"B":25},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":13,"pages":[27,28]},"question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Control Tower 設定登陸區域，處理的敏感資料必須留在歐盟境內，且公司只能使用 eu-central-1 區域。公司使用 SCP 強制執行資料駐留政策。GenAI 開發人員獲派具有完整 Amazon Bedrock 權限的 IAM 角色。公司必須確保開發人員只能使用跨區域推論（CRI），且只能在 eu-central-1 透過 Bedrock 使用 Amazon Nova Pro。公司已為開發人員 IAM 角色啟用模型存取，但開發人員在 Bedrock Chat/Text playground 叫用模型時收到以下錯誤：\nUser: arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/AssumedDevRole/DevUserName\nAction: bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream\nOn resource(s): arn:aws:bedrock:eu-west-3::foundation-model/amazon.nova-pro-v1:0\nContext: a service control policy explicitly denies the action\n公司需要解決錯誤，保留既有治理控制、提供精確的存取控制，並符合既有資料駐留政策。哪兩個方案的組合能滿足需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"將 AdministratorAccess 政策加入 GenAI 開發人員的 IAM 角色。","B":"擴充既有 SCP，允許 eu.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 推論設定檔使用 CRI。","C":"在 eu-west-3 區域啟用 Amazon Bedrock 的 Amazon Nova Pro 模型存取。","D":"確認 GenAI 開發人員 IAM 角色有權限，在所有可提供該模型的歐盟 AWS 區域中，透過 eu.amazon.nova-pro.v1:0 推論設定檔叫用 Amazon Nova Pro。","E":"擴充既有 SCP，允許 eu.* 推論設定檔使用 CRI。"},"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B and D are the intended pair for an EU geographic profile: narrowly exempt the specific inference profile from the Region-deny SCP and permit the profile plus models in its source and destination Regions. Adding AdministratorAccess cannot override an explicit SCP deny. However, geographic CRI can process prompts in other EU Regions, so it cannot satisfy a literal eu-central-1-only processing requirement. The question is inconsistent unless eu-central-1 means only the originating API Region; option D also contains a profile-ID punctuation typo.","explanation_zh":"若使用歐盟地理區域推論設定檔，B、D 是題目意圖的組合：在限制區域的 SCP 中只對指定推論設定檔加入例外，並授權該設定檔及來源、目的區域中的模型。加入 AdministratorAccess 不能覆蓋 SCP 的明確拒絕。但地理 CRI 可能在其他歐盟區域處理提示，無法滿足字面上的「僅在 eu-central-1 處理」。除非 eu-central-1 僅指 API 請求來源區域，否則題目條件互相矛盾；D 的設定檔 ID 也有標點誤植。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An identity-policy allow does not override an explicit service-control-policy deny.","why_zh":"身分政策允許不能覆蓋服務控制政策的明確拒絕。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Model access in a destination Region does not remove the SCP restriction.","why_zh":"目的區域中的模型存取不會移除 SCP 限制。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A wildcard for every EU profile is broader than the requested precise access to Nova Pro.","why_zh":"允許全部歐盟設定檔的萬用字元，比僅授權 Nova Pro 的精確控制範圍更大。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html"],"issues":["single_region_processing_contradicts_cri","source_profile_id_typo"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:20:17.768851+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":14,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a customer service AI assistant by using Amazon Bedrock. The AI assistant must not discuss investment advice with users. The AI assistant must block harmful content, mask personally identifiable information (PII), and maintain audit trails for compliance reporting. The AI assistant must apply content filtering to both user inputs and model responses based on content sensitivity. The company requires an Amazon Bedrock guardrail configuration that will effectively enforce policies with minimal false positives. The solution must provide multiple handling strategies for multiple types of sensitive content. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure a single guardrail and set content filters to high for all categories. Set up denied topics for investment advice and include sample phrases to block. Set up sensitive information filters that apply the block action for all PII entities. Apply the guardrail to all model inference calls.","B":"Configure multiple guardrails by using tiered policies. Create one guardrail and set content filters to high. Configure the guardrail to block PII for public interactions. Configure a second guardrail and set content filters to medium. Configure the second guardrail to mask PII for internal use. Configure multiple topic- specific guardrails to block investment advice and set up contextual grounding checks.","C":"Configure a guardrail and set content filters to medium for harmful content. Set up denied topics for investment advice and include clear definitions and sample phrases to block. Configure sensitive information filters to mask PII in responses and to block financial information in inputs. Enable both input and output evaluations that use custom blocked messages for audits.","D":"Create a separate guardrail for each use case. Create one guardrail that applies a harmful content filter. Create a guardrail to apply topic filters for investment advice. Create a guardrail to apply sensitive information filters to block PII. Use AWS Step Functions to chain the guardrails together sequentially. Use conditional logic based on content classification."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":14,"pages":[29,30]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 開發客服 AI 助理。助理不得與使用者討論投資建議，必須封鎖有害內容、遮罩個人識別資訊（PII），並保留合規報告所需的稽核軌跡。助理必須依內容敏感程度，對使用者輸入及模型回應都套用內容篩選。公司需要有效執行政策且盡量減少誤判的 Bedrock 防護機制設定，並針對不同敏感內容提供多種處理策略。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定單一防護機制，將所有內容類別的篩選強度設為高。將投資建議設為禁止主題，並提供應封鎖的範例語句。將所有 PII 實體的敏感資訊處理動作設為封鎖，並對所有模型推論呼叫套用防護機制。","B":"使用分層政策設定多個防護機制。第一個防護機制採用高強度內容篩選，在公開互動中封鎖 PII；第二個採用中強度內容篩選，在內部使用時遮罩 PII。再建立多個特定主題防護機制，以封鎖投資建議並設定 contextual grounding 檢查。","C":"設定防護機制，使用中強度內容篩選處理有害內容。將投資建議設為禁止主題，提供清楚定義及應封鎖的範例語句。設定敏感資訊篩選器，遮罩回應中的 PII，並封鎖輸入中的財務資訊。啟用輸入及輸出評估，使用自訂封鎖訊息供稽核使用。","D":"為每個使用情境建立獨立防護機制，分別套用有害內容篩選、投資建議主題篩選，以及封鎖 PII 的敏感資訊篩選。使用 AWS Step Functions 依序串接防護機制，並依內容分類套用條件邏輯。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C best combines topic restrictions, category filtering and different input/output PII handling actions. Guardrails supports independently configured runtime actions and masking for sensitive information. Medium strength is a starting configuration, not a guarantee of minimal false positives; evaluate representative inputs and tune it. Custom blocked messages do not create an audit trail by themselves, so assessment/log capture is additionally required for the stated audit requirement.","explanation_zh":"C 最能結合主題限制、類別篩選，以及輸入／輸出的不同 PII 處理動作。Guardrails 支援分別設定執行期動作，敏感資訊亦可遮罩。中強度只是初始設定，不保證誤判最少；仍需用代表性輸入評估並調整。自訂封鎖訊息本身不會建立稽核軌跡，還須額外記錄評估結果或日誌，才符合題目的稽核需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Blocking every PII category conflicts with masking and all-high thresholds can increase false positives.","why_zh":"封鎖所有 PII 與遮罩需求不同，全部設高強度可能增加誤判。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The public/internal split is not requested and separate guardrails complicate consistent policy application.","why_zh":"題目未要求區分公開／內部使用，多個防護機制也使一致套用政策更複雜。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sequential custom orchestration adds complexity while still specifying only blocking for PII.","why_zh":"自訂依序編排增加複雜度，而且 PII 仍只指定封鎖。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-harmful-content-handling-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-guardrails-cw-metrics.html"],"issues":["blocked_message_not_audit_logging"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:20:17.771557+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":15,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) solution that uses Amazon Bedrock with Anthropic Claude to recommend products to customers. Customers report that some of the recommended products are not available for sale on the website or are not relevant to the customer. Customers also report that the solutions takes a long time to generate some recommendations. The company investigates the issues and finds that most interactions between customers and the product recommendation solution are unique. The company confirms that the solutions recommends products that are not in the company's product catalog. The company must resolve these issues. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Increase grounding within Amazon Bedrock Guardrails. Enable Automated Reasoning checks. Set up provisioned throughput.","B":"Use prompt engineering to restrict the model responses to relevant products. Use streaming techniques such as the InvokeModelWithResponseStream action to reduce perceived latency for the customers.","C":"Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Implement Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). Set the PerformanceConfigLatency parameter to optimized.","D":"Store product catalog data in Amazon OpenSearch Service. Validate the model's product recommendations against the product catalog. Use Amazon DynamoDB to implement response caching."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":15,"pages":[31]},"question_zh":"一家電子商務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 與 Anthropic Claude 開發生成式 AI（GenAI）商品推薦方案。顧客反映部分推薦商品並未在網站販售，或與顧客不相關，也反映部分推薦生成時間過長。公司調查後發現，大多數顧客與推薦方案的互動都是獨特的，並確認方案會推薦不在公司商品目錄中的商品。公司必須解決這些問題。哪個方案能滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"提高 Amazon Bedrock Guardrails 的 grounding，啟用 Automated Reasoning 檢查，並設定佈建輸送量。","B":"使用提示工程限制模型只回覆相關商品，並使用 InvokeModelWithResponseStream 等串流技術降低顧客感受到的延遲。","C":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫並實作檢索增強生成（RAG）。將 PerformanceConfigLatency 參數設為 optimized。","D":"將商品目錄儲存在 Amazon OpenSearch Service，依商品目錄驗證模型推薦結果，並使用 Amazon DynamoDB 實作回應快取。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A knowledge base containing the current catalog can ground recommendations through RAG, addressing nonexistent and irrelevant product suggestions. Latency-optimized inference can reduce generation latency for supported models and Regions. Claude alone is not a sufficiently specific model designation: the latency documentation lists particular supported versions, so support must be checked. Mostly unique requests reduce the benefit of whole-response caching; streaming improves perceived latency but does not supply missing catalog evidence.","explanation_zh":"知識庫納入最新商品目錄後，可透過 RAG 為推薦提供依據，改善推薦不存在或不相關商品的問題。延遲最佳化推論可降低受支援模型與區域的生成延遲。但只寫 Claude 並不足以確認支援：官方文件列的是特定模型版本，必須核對。大多數請求各不相同，會降低完整回應快取的效益；串流能改善感受延遲，但不能補上模型缺少的商品目錄證據。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reasoning checks and throughput do not populate the model with an up-to-date product catalog.","why_zh":"推理檢查及輸送量設定不會讓模型自動取得最新商品目錄。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Prompt constraints and streaming do not guarantee that recommendations refer to real current catalog items.","why_zh":"提示限制及串流無法保證推薦指向目前目錄中的真實商品。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Catalog validation helps factuality, but whole-response caching provides limited reuse for mostly unique requests.","why_zh":"目錄驗證有助正確性，但大多為獨特請求時，完整回應快取可重用的比例有限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/latency-optimized-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent_PerformanceConfiguration.html"],"issues":["latency_optimization_model_and_region_dependent"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:20:17.773558+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":16,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Lambda and REST APIs to build a reasoning agent to automate support workflows. The system must preserve memory across interactions, share the relevant agent state, and support event- driven invocation and synchronous invocation. The system must also enforce access control and session-based permissions. Which combination of steps provides the MOST scalable solution? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to manage memory and session-aware reasoning. Deploy the agent with built-in identity support, event handling, and observability.","B":"Register the Lambda functions and the REST APIs as actions by using Amazon API Gateway and Amazon EventBridge. Enable Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to invoke the Lambda functions and the REST APIs without custom orchestration code.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Agents for reasoning and conversation management. Use AWS Step Functions and Amazon SQS queues for orchestration. Store the agent state in Amazon DynamoDB to maintain memory between steps.","D":"Deploy the reasoning logic as a container on Amazon ECS behind Amazon API Gateway. Use Amazon Aurora to store memory data and identity data.","E":"Build a custom RAG pipeline by using Amazon Kendra and Amazon Bedrock. Use AWS Lambda to orchestrate tool invocations. Store the agent state in Amazon S3."},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":71,"A":29},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":16,"pages":[32,33]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Lambda 與 REST API 建立推理代理程式，自動處理支援工作流程。系統必須跨互動保留記憶、共享相關代理程式狀態，並支援事件驅動與同步呼叫，也必須強制執行存取控制及工作階段式權限。哪一組步驟提供最具擴展性的解決方案？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Bedrock AgentCore 管理記憶及具工作階段感知能力的推理。部署代理程式，使用內建身分支援、事件處理及可觀測性。","B":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 與 Amazon EventBridge，將 Lambda 函數及 REST API 註冊為動作。讓 Amazon Bedrock AgentCore 無須自訂協調程式碼即可呼叫這些函數與 API。","C":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Agents 管理推理與對話，使用 AWS Step Functions 與 Amazon SQS 佇列進行協調。將代理程式狀態存於 Amazon DynamoDB，以在步驟之間保留記憶。","D":"將推理邏輯部署為 Amazon API Gateway 後方的 Amazon ECS 容器。使用 Amazon Aurora 儲存記憶及身分資料。","E":"使用 Amazon Kendra 與 Amazon Bedrock 建立自訂 RAG 管線。使用 AWS Lambda 協調工具呼叫，並將代理程式狀態儲存在 Amazon S3。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AgentCore provides managed components for agent hosting, memory, identity and tool access, so A and B express the intended scalable architecture. However, B names the wrong registration mechanism: AgentCore Gateway targets expose Lambda functions and OpenAPI-described APIs as tools; API Gateway and EventBridge alone do not register AgentCore actions. Event triggers and synchronous invocation must be configured explicitly, and application reasoning still requires agent code. AB is the closest intended pair, not a fully correct implementation recipe.","explanation_zh":"AgentCore 提供代理程式執行、記憶、身分及工具存取等受管元件，因此 A、B 表達了題目預期的可擴展架構。不過 B 的註冊機制寫得不正確：應透過 AgentCore Gateway 目標將 Lambda 及以 OpenAPI 描述的 API 公開為工具；只有 API Gateway 與 EventBridge 不會註冊 AgentCore 動作。事件觸發及同步呼叫仍須明確設定，應用程式推理仍需要代理程式程式碼。AB 是最接近題意的組合，不能視為完全正確的實作步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Possible, but adds separate orchestration and state-management components.","why_zh":"技術上可行，但增加額外協調與狀態管理元件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Requires custom memory, identity integration and container operations.","why_zh":"需要自訂記憶、身分整合及容器維運。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"RAG retrieval does not itself supply agent sessions or authorization.","why_zh":"RAG 檢索本身不提供代理程式工作階段或授權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/gateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/memory.html"],"issues":["incorrect_gateway_registration_wording"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.800567+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":17,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application to help investment analysts query complex financial relationships across multiple investment vehicles, market sectors, and regulatory environments. The dataset contains highly interconnected entities that have multi-hop relationships. The analysts must be able to examine the relationships holistically to provide accurate investment guidance. The application must deliver comprehensive answers that capture indirect relationships between financial entities. The application must produce responses in less than 3 seconds. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases with Graph RAG and Amazon Neptune Analytics to store the financial data. Analyze the multi-hop relationships between entities and automatically identify related information across documents.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases and an Amazon OpenSearch Service vector store to implement custom relationship identification logic that uses AWS Lambda functions to query multiple vector embeddings in sequence.","C":"Use an Amazon OpenSearch Serverless vector database with k-nearest neighbor (k-NN) searches. Implement manual relationship mapping in an application layer that runs in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group.","D":"Use Amazon DynamoDB to store financial data in a custom indexing system. Use an AWS Lambda function to query relevant records based on input questions. Use Amazon SageMaker AI to generate responses."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":17,"pages":[34,35]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發檢索增強生成（RAG）應用程式，協助投資分析師查詢跨多種投資工具、市場產業及法規環境的複雜金融關係。資料集包含高度相互連結、具有多跳關係的實體。分析師必須整體檢視這些關係，以提供準確的投資建議。應用程式必須提供完整答案，涵蓋金融實體間的間接關係，並在 3 秒內產生回應。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用具有 Graph RAG 的 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 與 Amazon Neptune Analytics 儲存金融資料。分析實體間的多跳關係，並自動找出跨文件的相關資訊。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 與 Amazon OpenSearch Service 向量儲存，實作自訂關係辨識邏輯，讓 AWS Lambda 函數依序查詢多個向量嵌入。","C":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch Serverless 向量資料庫執行 k 最近鄰（k-NN）搜尋。在 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 群組中的應用層實作人工關係對映。","D":"使用 Amazon DynamoDB 在自訂索引系統中儲存金融資料。使用 AWS Lambda 函數依輸入問題查詢相關紀錄，並使用 Amazon SageMaker AI 產生回應。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Bedrock Knowledge Bases GraphRAG combines vector retrieval with graph traversal in Neptune Analytics and automatically derives relationships across ingested documents. This directly matches the multi-hop requirement with less custom relationship logic. The documented feature supports S3 data sources and has graph configuration and scaling limitations. It does not guarantee a sub-three-second end-to-end response; that target requires representative load and latency testing.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock Knowledge Bases GraphRAG 結合向量檢索與 Neptune Analytics 圖形走訪，並自動推導匯入文件間的關係，可直接滿足多跳關聯需求，減少自訂關係邏輯。官方功能支援 S3 資料來源，且圖形設定與擴展有其限制。這項功能不保證端到端回應低於 3 秒，仍須以具代表性的負載及延遲測試確認。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Sequential custom vector queries increase latency and engineering effort.","why_zh":"依序執行自訂向量查詢會增加延遲與開發工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manual relationship mapping and EC2 operations add maintenance.","why_zh":"人工關係對映及 EC2 維運增加管理負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom indexing and retrieval do not provide managed graph traversal.","why_zh":"自訂索引及檢索沒有提供受管圖形走訪能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-build-graphs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/neptune-analytics/latest/userguide/best-practices-graphrag-filters.html"],"issues":["latency_target_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.801752+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":18,"question_en":"A healthcare company uses Amazon Bedrock to deploy an application that generates summaries of clinical documents. The application experiences inconsistent response quality with occasional factual hallucinations. Monthly costs exceed the company's projections by 40%. A GenAI developer must implement a near real-time monitoring solution to detect hallucinations, identify abnormal token consumption, and provide early warnings of cost anomalies. The solution must require minimal custom development work and maintenance overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor InputTokenCount and OutputTokenCount metrics to detect anomalies. Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use AWS Glue and Amazon Athena to identify potential hallucinations.","B":"Run Amazon Bedrock evaluation jobs that use LLM-based judgments to detect hallucinations. Configure Amazon CloudWatch to track token usage. Create an AWS Lambda function to process CloudWatch metrics. Configure the Lambda function to send usage pattern notifications.","C":"Configure Amazon Bedrock to store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable text output logging. Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to run contextual grounding checks to detect hallucinations. Create Amazon CloudWatch anomaly detection alarms for token usage metrics.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail to log all Amazon Bedrock API calls. Create a custom dashboard in Amazon QuickSight to visualize token usage patterns. Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect quality drift in generated summaries."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":89,"B":11},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":18,"pages":[36,37]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 部署產生臨床文件摘要的應用程式。應用程式回應品質不一致，偶爾產生事實幻覺，每月費用比預估高出 40%。生成式 AI 開發人員必須實作近乎即時的監控方案，偵測幻覺、辨識異常 token 消耗，並及早警告成本異常，且盡量減少自訂開發及維護負擔。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示監控 InputTokenCount 與 OutputTokenCount 指標以偵測異常。將模型呼叫日誌存於 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，並使用 AWS Glue 與 Amazon Athena 辨識潛在幻覺。","B":"執行採用 LLM 評判的 Amazon Bedrock 評估作業以偵測幻覺。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 追蹤 token 用量，建立 AWS Lambda 函數處理 CloudWatch 指標並傳送用量模式通知。","C":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 將模型呼叫日誌儲存至 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，啟用文字輸出日誌。設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制執行情境依據檢查以偵測幻覺，並為 token 用量指標建立 Amazon CloudWatch 異常偵測警示。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 記錄所有 Amazon Bedrock API 呼叫。建立自訂 Amazon QuickSight 儀表板呈現 token 用量模式，並使用 Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor 偵測生成摘要的品質漂移。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Contextual grounding checks evaluate a generated summary against a supplied reference source and user query, making them directly applicable to clinical-document summarization. Model invocation logging supplies inspection records, while CloudWatch token metrics and anomaly detection provide early usage warnings. The source documents must be supplied as grounding context; logging alone cannot detect hallucinations. Token anomalies are a cost proxy, so actual costs still depend on model pricing and input/output mix.","explanation_zh":"情境依據檢查會對照提供的參考來源及使用者查詢評估生成摘要，直接適用於臨床文件摘要。模型呼叫日誌提供檢查紀錄，CloudWatch token 指標及異常偵測則提供早期用量警告。必須將來源文件提供為檢查依據，單靠日誌無法偵測幻覺。Token 異常只是成本的替代指標，實際費用仍取決於模型價格與輸入／輸出比例。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Glue and Athena need custom analysis and do not natively judge factual grounding.","why_zh":"Glue 與 Athena 需要自訂分析，並不原生判斷事實依據。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Evaluation jobs are not inline per-response checks and add custom notification logic.","why_zh":"評估作業不是每次回應的即時檢查，且另需自訂通知邏輯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail is an API audit source; SageMaker monitoring does not automatically evaluate Bedrock summary grounding.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 是 API 稽核來源；SageMaker 監控不會自動判斷 Bedrock 摘要的依據。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-runtime-metrics.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.802405+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":19,"question_en":"A company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that produces content based on a variety of internal and external data sources. The company wants to ensure that the generated output is fully traceable. The application must support data source registration and enable metadata tagging to attribute content to its original source. The application must also maintain audit logs of data access and usage throughout the pipeline. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lake Formation to catalog data sources and control access. Apply metadata tags directly in Amazon S3. Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor API activity.","B":"Use AWS Glue Data Catalog to register and tag data sources. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to monitor access patterns and application behavior.","C":"Store data in Amazon S3 and use object tagging for attribution. Use AWS Glue Data Catalog to manage schema information. Use AWS CloudTrail to log access to S3 buckets.","D":"Use AWS Glue Data Catalog to register all data sources. Apply metadata tags to attribute data sources. Use AWS CloudTrail to log access and activity across services."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":86,"C":14},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":19,"pages":[38,39]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在建立生成式 AI 應用程式，根據各種內部及外部資料來源產生內容。公司希望生成輸出完全可追溯。應用程式必須支援資料來源登錄及中繼資料標記，將內容歸屬至原始來源，也必須在整個管線維護資料存取與使用的稽核日誌。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lake Formation 編目資料來源並控制存取。直接在 Amazon S3 套用中繼資料標籤，並使用 AWS CloudTrail 監控 API 活動。","B":"使用 AWS Glue Data Catalog 登錄及標記資料來源。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 監控存取模式與應用程式行為。","C":"將資料儲存於 Amazon S3，以物件標籤記錄歸屬。使用 AWS Glue Data Catalog 管理結構描述資訊，並使用 AWS CloudTrail 記錄 S3 儲存貯體的存取。","D":"使用 AWS Glue Data Catalog 登錄所有資料來源，套用中繼資料標籤標示來源歸屬，並使用 AWS CloudTrail 記錄跨服務的存取與活動。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D provides the closest combination of a central metadata catalog and cross-service API auditing. CloudTrail records Glue operations with caller and request context, while catalog metadata can retain source identifiers. However, neither tags nor CloudTrail automatically trace each generated claim back to retrieved passages. Full output lineage requires application-level retrieval and citation records, and applicable data events must be enabled explicitly.","explanation_zh":"D 最接近集中式中繼資料目錄加上跨服務 API 稽核的組合。CloudTrail 會記錄 Glue 操作的呼叫者及請求脈絡，目錄中繼資料則可保留來源識別資訊。不過，標籤與 CloudTrail 都不會自動將每一項生成主張追溯至檢索段落。完整輸出血緣仍需要應用層的檢索及引用紀錄，適用的資料事件也必須明確啟用。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3-only tags do not provide a consistent catalog attribution scheme for all sources.","why_zh":"只在 S3 設標籤不足以為所有來源建立一致的目錄歸屬機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Application logs can help but do not replace configured cross-service CloudTrail auditing.","why_zh":"應用日誌有幫助，但不能取代已設定的跨服務 CloudTrail 稽核。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Limits attribution and audit scope to S3 rather than the entire pipeline.","why_zh":"將歸屬及稽核範圍侷限於 S3，未涵蓋整個管線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/monitor-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/catalog-and-crawler.html"],"issues":["catalog_and_audit_not_complete_output_lineage"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.803342+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":20,"question_en":"A financial services company needs to build a document analysis system that uses Amazon Bedrock to process quarterly reports. The system must analyze financial data, perform sentiment analysis, and validate compliance across batches of reports. Each batch contains 5 reports. Each report requires multiple foundation model (FM) calls. The solution must finish the analysis within 10 seconds for each batch. Current sequential processing takes 45 seconds for each batch. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lambda functions with provisioned concurrency to process each analysis type sequentially. Configure the Lambda function timeouts to 10 seconds. Configure automatic retries with exponential backoff.","B":"Use AWS Step Functions with a Parallel state to invoke separate AWS Lambda functions for each analysis type simultaneously. Configure Amazon Bedrock client timeouts. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to track execution time and model inference latency.","C":"Create an Amazon SQS queue to buffer analysis requests. Deploy multiple AWS Lambda functions with reserved concurrency. Configure each Lambda function to process different aspects of each report sequentially and then combine the results.","D":"Deploy an Amazon ECS cluster that runs containers that process each report sequentially. Use a load balancer to distribute batch workloads. Configure an auto-scaling policy based on CPU utilization to handle demand fluctuations."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":80,"A":10,"C":10},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":20,"pages":[40,41]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司需要使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立季度報告文件分析系統。系統必須對成批報告分析財務資料、進行情緒分析並驗證合規性。每批包含 5 份報告，每份報告需要多次基礎模型（FM）呼叫，且每批必須在 10 秒內完成分析。目前循序處理每批需要 45 秒。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用具有佈建並行性的 AWS Lambda 函數，依序處理各分析類型。將 Lambda 函數逾時設為 10 秒，並設定具指數退避的自動重試。","B":"使用 AWS Step Functions 的 Parallel 狀態，同時呼叫各分析類型的個別 AWS Lambda 函數。設定 Amazon Bedrock 用戶端逾時，並以 Amazon CloudWatch 指標追蹤執行時間及模型推論延遲。","C":"建立 Amazon SQS 佇列緩衝分析請求。部署具有保留並行性的多個 AWS Lambda 函數，讓各函數依序處理每份報告的不同面向，再合併結果。","D":"部署 Amazon ECS 叢集，以容器依序處理各報告。使用負載平衡器分散批次工作負載，並設定根據 CPU 使用率的自動擴展政策，以處理需求波動。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A Parallel state starts independent branches concurrently and waits for all branches to finish, directly removing sequential analysis dependencies. Separate functions and latency metrics make B the best architecture among these choices. Client timeouts limit waiting rather than accelerate model inference. A reduction from 45 seconds to under 10 seconds is not established by three analysis branches alone; report-level concurrency, quotas and measured critical-path latency must also meet the budget.","explanation_zh":"Parallel 狀態會並行啟動獨立分支，並等待所有分支完成，可直接移除各分析工作的循序執行限制。搭配個別函數及延遲指標，B 是選項中最適合的架構。用戶端逾時只限制等待時間，不會加速模型推論。僅有三個分析分支無法證明可從 45 秒縮短至 10 秒以下，仍須讓報告層級的並行度、配額及實測關鍵路徑延遲符合時間預算。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Sequential execution remains and retries can increase total latency.","why_zh":"仍採循序執行，重試還可能增加總延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Queueing and reserved concurrency do not remove sequential work inside each function.","why_zh":"佇列及保留並行性不會消除各函數內的循序工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CPU scaling does not directly shorten sequential remote FM calls.","why_zh":"CPU 擴展無法直接縮短循序遠端 FM 呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-parallel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-step-functions.html"],"issues":["ten_second_sla_not_proven"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.804250+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Bedrock to build a customer-facing AI assistant to handle sensitive customer inquiries. The company must use defense-in-depth safety controls to block sophisticated prompt injection attacks. The company must keep audit logs of all safety interventions. The AI assistant must have cross-Region failover capabilities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to use content filters to protect against prompt injection attacks. Set the content filters to high. Use a guardrail profile to implement cross-Region guardrail inference. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs with custom metrics to capture detailed guardrail intervention events.","B":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to use content filters to protect against prompt injection attacks. Set the content filters to high. Use AWS WAF to block suspicious inputs. Use AWS CloudTrail to log API calls for audits.","C":"Deploy Amazon Comprehend custom classification to detect prompt injection attacks. Use Amazon API Gateway to validate requests. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs with custom metrics to capture detailed intervention events.","D":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to use custom content filters to protect against harmful content. Set the content filters to high. Use word filters to protect against known attack patterns. Configure cross-Region guardrail replication to provide failover capabilities. Store logs in AWS CloudTrail for compliance auditing."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":80,"D":7,"B":7},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":21,"pages":[42,43]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立面向客戶的 AI 助理，處理敏感客戶詢問。公司必須採用縱深防禦安全控制，封鎖複雜的提示注入攻擊，保留所有安全介入的稽核日誌，並讓 AI 助理具備跨區域容錯移轉能力。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制使用內容篩選器防範提示注入攻擊，並將強度設為高。使用防護機制設定檔實作跨區域防護機制推論，並使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 搭配自訂指標擷取詳細的防護介入事件。","B":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制使用內容篩選器防範提示注入攻擊，並將強度設為高。使用 AWS WAF 封鎖可疑輸入，並使用 AWS CloudTrail 記錄 API 呼叫供稽核。","C":"部署 Amazon Comprehend 自訂分類以偵測提示注入攻擊。使用 Amazon API Gateway 驗證請求，並以 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 搭配自訂指標擷取詳細介入事件。","D":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制使用自訂內容篩選器防範有害內容，並將強度設為高。使用字詞篩選器防範已知攻擊模式，設定跨區域防護機制複寫以提供容錯移轉，並將日誌存至 AWS CloudTrail 供合規稽核。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Guardrail profiles support cross-Region routing of guardrail evaluation, and the prompt-attack content filter is the relevant policy for injection attempts. A also includes detailed intervention logging instead of relying solely on API audit events. The application must actually emit evaluation details to logs; custom metrics alone do not preserve full events. Guardrail cross-Region inference covers policy evaluation, not automatic failover of the entire assistant, its model and data stores.","explanation_zh":"防護機制設定檔支援跨區域路由防護評估，提示攻擊內容篩選器則是處理注入嘗試的相關政策。A 也納入詳細介入日誌，而非只依賴 API 稽核事件。應用程式仍須實際將評估細節寫入日誌，自訂指標本身不保存完整事件。防護機制跨區域推論涵蓋政策評估，不代表整個助理、模型及資料儲存都會自動容錯移轉。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lacks cross-Region guardrail routing and detailed content-intervention records.","why_zh":"缺少跨區域防護路由及詳細內容介入紀錄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Custom classification adds development and lacks the requested failover mechanism.","why_zh":"自訂分類增加開發負擔，且缺少要求的容錯移轉機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Replication and word matching do not substitute for guardrail profiles and detailed evaluation logs.","why_zh":"複寫與字詞比對無法取代防護設定檔及詳細評估日誌。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-cross-region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-prompt-attack.html"],"issues":["guardrail_failover_not_full_application_failover"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.805323+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":22,"question_en":"A company is designing a canary deployment strategy for a payment processing API. The system must support automated gradual traffic shifting between multiple Amazon Bedrock models based on real-time inference metrics, historical traffic patterns, and service health. The solution must be able to gradually increase traffic to new model versions. The system must increase traffic if metrics remain healthy and decrease traffic if the performance degrades below acceptable thresholds. The company needs to comprehensively monitor inference latency and error rates during the deployment phase. The company must also be able to halt deployments and revert to a previous model version without any manual intervention. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock with provisioned throughput to host the versions of the model. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Step Functions workflow when a new model version is released. Configure the workflow to shift traffic in stages, wait for a specified time period, and invoke an AWS Lambda function to check Amazon CloudWatch performance metrics. Configure the workflow to increase traffic if the metrics meet thresholds and to trigger a traffic rollback if performance metrics fall below thresholds.","B":"Use AWS Lambda functions to invoke various Amazon Bedrock model versions. Use an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with stage variables and weighted routing to shift traffic gradually to new model versions. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor performance metrics. Use external logic to adjust traffic between model versions and to roll back if performance falls below thresholds.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint variants to represent multiple Amazon Bedrock model versions. Use variant weights to shift traffic. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor performance metrics. Use SageMaker Model Monitor to trigger AWS Lambda functions to roll back a model deployment if performance drops below a specified threshold. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to roll back model deployments if an anomaly is detected.","D":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to track inference logs. Configure OpenSearch Service to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to update Amazon Bedrock model endpoints to shift traffic based on the inference logs."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":90,"C":10},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":22,"pages":[44,45]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在為付款處理 API 設計金絲雀部署策略。系統必須根據即時推論指標、歷史流量模式及服務健康狀態，在多個 Amazon Bedrock 模型間自動逐步轉移流量，逐漸增加新模型版本的流量。指標維持健康時應增加流量，效能低於可接受門檻時應減少流量。公司需要在部署期間全面監控推論延遲與錯誤率，並能在無人工介入的情況下停止部署及恢復先前模型版本。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 佈建輸送量託管模型版本。設定 Amazon EventBridge 規則，在新模型版本發佈時呼叫 AWS Step Functions 工作流程。讓工作流程分階段轉移流量、等待指定時間，再呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數檢查 Amazon CloudWatch 效能指標；達到門檻時增加流量，未達門檻時觸發流量回復。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數呼叫不同 Amazon Bedrock 模型版本。使用具階段變數及加權路由的 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API 逐步轉移流量至新版本。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 監控效能指標，並以外部邏輯調整版本間流量及在效能低於門檻時回復。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker AI 端點變體代表多個 Amazon Bedrock 模型版本。使用變體權重轉移流量，並以 Amazon CloudWatch 監控效能指標。設定 SageMaker Model Monitor 在模型效能低於指定門檻時觸發 AWS Lambda 函數回復部署，並設定 Amazon EventBridge 規則在偵測異常時回復模型部署。","D":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 追蹤推論日誌，並設定其呼叫 AWS Systems Manager Automation 執行手冊，更新 Amazon Bedrock 模型端點，依據推論日誌轉移流量。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Step Functions can coordinate staged waits, metric checks and conditional promotion or rollback, so A describes a viable automated control loop. The application still needs a routing configuration that chooses a model ARN according to the selected weights. Provisioned Throughput itself does not provide weighted canary routing. The release event and historical-traffic assessment must also be implemented; they are not automatic properties of a purchased model capacity.","explanation_zh":"Step Functions 可協調分階段等待、指標檢查，以及條件式晉升或回復，因此 A 描述了可行的自動控制流程。應用程式仍須具備路由設定，依選定權重挑選模型 ARN。佈建輸送量本身不提供加權金絲雀路由。版本發佈事件及歷史流量評估也必須實作，購買模型容量不會自動取得這些能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"API Gateway HTTP APIs do not offer the described native weighted canary deployment feature.","why_zh":"API Gateway HTTP API 不提供選項所描述的原生加權金絲雀部署功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SageMaker endpoint variants cannot directly host Bedrock-managed model endpoints.","why_zh":"SageMaker 端點變體不能直接託管 Bedrock 受管模型端點。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Log indexing does not provide native Bedrock endpoint traffic-weight updates.","why_zh":"日誌索引不提供原生 Bedrock 端點流量權重更新能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-choice.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/canary-release.html"],"issues":["application_router_and_release_events_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.806233+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":23,"question_en":"A financial services company uses an AI application to process financial documents by using Amazon Bedrock. During business hours, the application handles approximately 10,000 requests each hour, which requires consistent throughput. The company uses the CreateProvisionedModelThroughput API to purchase provisioned throughput. Amazon CloudWatch metrics show that the provisioned capacity is unused while on-demand requests are being throttled. The company finds the following code in the application: python response = bedrock_runtime.invoke_model(modelId=\"anthropic.claude-v2\", body=json.dumps(payload)) The company needs the application to use the provisioned throughput and to resolve the throttling issues. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Increase the number of model units (MUs) in the provisioned throughput configuration.","B":"Replace the model ID parameter with the ARN of the provisioned model that the CreateProvisionedModelThroughput API returns.","C":"Add exponential backoff retry logic to handle throttling exceptions during peak hours.","D":"Modify the application to use the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API instead of the InvokeModel API."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":91,"C":9},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":23,"pages":[46,47]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock AI 應用程式處理金融文件。應用程式在營業時間每小時約處理 10,000 個請求，需要穩定輸送量。公司使用 CreateProvisionedModelThroughput API 購買佈建輸送量，但 Amazon CloudWatch 指標顯示佈建容量未被使用，而隨需請求卻遭到節流。公司在應用程式中發現以下程式碼：python response = bedrock_runtime.invoke_model(modelId=\"anthropic.claude-v2\", body=json.dumps(payload))。公司需要讓應用程式使用佈建輸送量並解決節流問題。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"增加佈建輸送量設定中的模型單位（MU）數量。","B":"將模型 ID 參數替換成 CreateProvisionedModelThroughput API 回傳的佈建模型 ARN。","C":"加入指數退避重試邏輯，以處理尖峰時段的節流例外。","D":"修改應用程式，使用 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API，而非 InvokeModel API。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The Bedrock documentation explicitly requires the provisioned model ARN in modelId to use purchased Provisioned Throughput. Passing a base-model ID continues to select the on-demand invocation path. Replacing the identifier therefore directs requests to the existing reserved capacity. Capacity sizing must still fit the workload, but the observed unused capacity is first a routing error.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock 文件明確要求將佈建模型 ARN 填入 modelId，才能使用已購買的佈建輸送量。傳入基礎模型 ID 仍會選擇隨需呼叫路徑。因此，替換識別碼即可將請求導向既有預留容量。容量仍須足以承載工作負載，但目前容量閒置的首要原因是呼叫目標錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"More unused capacity does not change the invocation target.","why_zh":"增加未使用的容量不會改變呼叫目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Retries do not redirect requests to the provisioned model.","why_zh":"重試不會將請求改送至佈建模型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Streaming also requires the provisioned ARN in modelId.","why_zh":"串流呼叫同樣必須將佈建 ARN 填入 modelId。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prov-thru-use.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_InvokeModel.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.807072+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company is building an AI advisory application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application will provide recommendations to customers. The company needs the application to explain its reasoning process and cite specific sources for data. The application must retrieve information from company data sources and show step- by-step reasoning for recommendations. The application must also link data claims to source documents and maintain response latency under 3 seconds. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases with source attribution enabled. Use the Anthropic Claude Messages API with RAG to set high-relevance thresholds for source documents. Store reasoning and citations in Amazon S3 for auditing purposes.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock with Anthropic Claude models and extended thinking. Configure a 4,000-token thinking budget. Store reasoning traces and citations in Amazon DynamoDB for auditing purposes.","C":"Configure Amazon SageMaker AI with a custom Anthropic Claude model. Use the model's reasoning parameter and AWS Lambda to process responses. Add source citations from a separate Amazon RDS database.","D":"Use Amazon Bedrock with Anthropic Claude models and chain-of-thought reasoning. Configure custom retrieval tracking with the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases API. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor response latency metrics."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":64,"D":21,"B":14},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":24,"pages":[48,49]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立 AI 諮詢應用程式，向客戶提供建議。公司要求應用程式解釋推理過程，並引用特定資料來源。應用程式必須檢索公司資料來源的資訊，展示建議的逐步推理，將資料主張連結至來源文件，並將回應延遲維持在 3 秒以下。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用已啟用來源歸屬的 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases。使用 Anthropic Claude Messages API 搭配 RAG，為來源文件設定高相關性門檻，並將推理及引用儲存在 Amazon S3 供稽核。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 中具有延伸思考功能的 Anthropic Claude 模型。設定 4,000 token 的思考預算，並將推理軌跡及引用存至 Amazon DynamoDB 供稽核。","C":"使用自訂 Anthropic Claude 模型設定 Amazon SageMaker AI。使用模型的推理參數及 AWS Lambda 處理回應，並從獨立 Amazon RDS 資料庫加入來源引用。","D":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 中的 Anthropic Claude 模型及思維鏈推理。透過 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases API 設定自訂檢索追蹤，並使用 Amazon CloudWatch 監控回應延遲指標。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Knowledge Bases RetrieveAndGenerate returns generated answers with citations linked to retrieved source data, making A the closest low-maintenance choice for source attribution. A plain Claude Messages request does not itself create the managed citation mapping or a knowledge-base relevance threshold; retrieval and prompting must be configured correctly. A user-facing explanation can summarize the supporting evidence without treating a model reasoning trace as verified proof. Neither citations nor RAG guarantee the stated three-second latency.","explanation_zh":"Knowledge Bases 的 RetrieveAndGenerate 會回傳生成答案及連結至檢索來源的引用，因此 A 最接近低維護負擔的來源歸屬方案。單純的 Claude Messages 請求本身不會建立受管引用對映，也不會設定知識庫相關性門檻，仍須正確設定檢索及提示。面向使用者的說明可以摘要支持證據，不能把模型推理軌跡當成已驗證的證明。引用與 RAG 都不保證題目要求的 3 秒延遲。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Thinking alone retrieves no company sources and adds generation latency.","why_zh":"只有思考功能不會檢索公司來源，且增加生成延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The described custom Claude hosting and reasoning setup is not a supported generic SageMaker recipe.","why_zh":"所述自訂 Claude 託管及推理設定不是通用的受支援 SageMaker 做法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom retrieval tracking adds work while chain-of-thought does not establish source attribution.","why_zh":"自訂檢索追蹤增加工作，思維鏈也不會建立來源歸屬。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-retrieve-generate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/claude-messages-extended-thinking.html"],"issues":["messages_api_citation_wording_imprecise","latency_target_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.807985+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":25,"question_en":"A financial services company uses multiple foundation models (FMs) through Amazon Bedrock for its generative AI (GenAI) applications. To comply with a new regulation for GenAI use with sensitive financial data, the company needs a token management solution. The token management solution must proactively alert when applications approach model-specific token limits. The solution must also process more than 5,000 requests each minute and maintain token usage metrics to allocate costs across business units. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Develop model-specific tokenizers in an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to estimate token usage before sending requests to Amazon Bedrock. Configure the Lambda function to publish metrics to Amazon CloudWatch and trigger alarms when requests approach thresholds. Store detailed token usage in Amazon DynamoDB to report costs.","B":"Implement Amazon Bedrock Guardrails with token quota policies. Capture metrics on rejected requests. Configure Amazon EventBridge rules to trigger notifications based on Amazon Bedrock Guardrails metrics. Use Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to visualize token usage trends across models.","C":"Deploy an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue for failed requests. Configure an AWS Lambda function to analyze token-related failures. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to generate reports on token usage patterns based on error logs from Amazon Bedrock API responses.","D":"Use Amazon API Gateway to create a proxy for all Amazon Bedrock API calls. Configure request throttling based on custom usage plans with predefined token quotas. Configure API Gateway to reject requests that will exceed token limits."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":83,"D":17},"tags":["GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":25,"pages":[50,51]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司透過 Amazon Bedrock 使用多個基礎模型（FM）提供生成式 AI 應用程式。為遵守敏感金融資料使用生成式 AI 的新法規，公司需要 token 管理方案，在應用程式接近特定模型的 token 限制時主動發出警告。方案也必須每分鐘處理超過 5,000 個請求，並保留 token 用量指標，以便在各事業單位間分攤成本。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Lambda 函數中開發各模型專屬的 tokenizer。讓函數在送出 Amazon Bedrock 請求前估算 token 用量，將指標發佈至 Amazon CloudWatch，並在請求接近門檻時觸發警示。將詳細 token 用量儲存於 Amazon DynamoDB 供成本報告使用。","B":"實作具有 token 配額政策的 Amazon Bedrock Guardrails。擷取被拒絕請求的指標，設定 Amazon EventBridge 規則依防護指標觸發通知，並使用 Amazon CloudWatch 儀表板呈現各模型 token 用量趨勢。","C":"部署 Amazon SQS 無效信件佇列保存失敗請求。設定 AWS Lambda 函數分析 token 相關失敗，並使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights，根據 Amazon Bedrock API 錯誤回應日誌產生 token 用量模式報告。","D":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 為所有 Amazon Bedrock API 呼叫建立代理。設定具有預定 token 配額的自訂用量計畫，據此限制請求流量，並讓 API Gateway 拒絕將超出 token 限制的請求。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Pre-invocation model-specific counting plus usage metrics and attributed records is the only proactive architecture among the options. A is therefore the closest choice, but maintaining handwritten tokenizers is unnecessary where the Bedrock CountTokens API supports the chosen model. Input counts cannot predict the exact output length; reserve an output budget and aggregate usage per model and business unit. Processing more than 5,000 requests per minute requires checking counting, inference and application quotas, not just selecting Lambda.","explanation_zh":"呼叫前依模型計算 token，搭配用量指標及帶歸屬資訊的紀錄，是選項中唯一主動管理的架構，因此 A 最接近需求。不過，若 Bedrock CountTokens API 支援選定模型，就不必自行維護 tokenizer。輸入計數無法精確預測輸出長度，應預留輸出預算，並依模型與事業單位彙總用量。每分鐘超過 5,000 個請求仍須檢查計數、推論及應用程式配額，不能只因選用 Lambda 就認定可達標。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Guardrails do not provide the described token-quota policy.","why_zh":"Guardrails 不提供此處描述的 token 配額政策。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Failure analysis is reactive and omits successful usage.","why_zh":"失敗分析屬事後處理，且遺漏成功請求用量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"API Gateway usage plans count requests rather than model-specific tokens.","why_zh":"API Gateway 用量計畫計算請求數，而非模型專屬 token。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/count-tokens.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html"],"issues":["prefer_supported_counttokens","throughput_requires_quota_validation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:47.808779+00:00"},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":26,"question_en":"A retail company is developing a customer service application that must process 10,000 daily queries about products, orders, and warranties. The application must be able to respond to queries about 50,000 product documents that are updated every day. The application must integrate with an order management API to check the status of orders and to help process returns. The application must maintain context throughout multi-turn interactions with customers. The company must collect complete audit trails for application responses. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a fine-tuned Amazon Bedrock Anthropic Claude model for each product category. Create AWS Lambda functions to connect each model to the order management API. Store conversation history in Amazon DynamoDB.","B":"Create a custom model that uses continued pre-training on Amazon Bedrock to handle all product documentation. Set up an Amazon API Gateway REST API that uses AWS Lambda functions to connect the model to the order management API.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker AI with containers to deploy models. Use Amazon Kendra to search product documents. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate calls to the order management API.","D":"Use an Amazon Bedrock agent with action groups to integrate with the order management API. Associate an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base with the agent to search product documentation by using Retrieval Augmentation Generation (RAG). Enable trace events to capture audit trails."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":83,"A":17},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":26,"pages":[52,53]},"question_zh":"一家零售公司正在開發客服應用程式，每天必須處理 10,000 個關於商品、訂單及保固的查詢。應用程式必須能針對每日更新的 50,000 份商品文件回答問題，整合訂單管理 API 以查詢訂單狀態並協助處理退貨，在多輪客戶互動中維持脈絡，並收集應用程式回應的完整稽核軌跡。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為每個商品類別部署一個經微調的 Amazon Bedrock Anthropic Claude 模型。建立 AWS Lambda 函數將各模型連接至訂單管理 API，並將對話歷史存於 Amazon DynamoDB。","B":"在 Amazon Bedrock 使用持續預先訓練建立自訂模型，處理所有商品文件。設定 Amazon API Gateway REST API，透過 AWS Lambda 函數將模型連接至訂單管理 API。","C":"使用具有容器的 Amazon SageMaker AI 部署模型。使用 Amazon Kendra 搜尋商品文件，並使用 AWS Step Functions 協調訂單管理 API 呼叫。","D":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式，透過動作群組整合訂單管理 API。將 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫與代理程式關聯，以檢索增強生成（RAG）搜尋商品文件。啟用追蹤事件以擷取稽核軌跡。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Action groups integrate operational APIs while a knowledge base retrieves current product documents without repeatedly training a model. Agent sessions preserve conversational context and trace events expose orchestration and tool activity. D therefore minimizes custom orchestration for the stated architecture. Schedule data-source synchronization and persist emitted traces with retention controls; enabling trace does not itself establish a durable audit archive. Current documentation labels this service Agents Classic and restricts new-customer availability, so new implementations must check availability.","explanation_zh":"動作群組可整合作業 API，知識庫則檢索最新商品文件，免於反覆訓練模型。代理程式工作階段維持對話脈絡，追蹤事件呈現協調及工具活動，因此 D 在題目架構下可減少自訂協調。仍須安排資料來源同步，並持久保存追蹤資料及設定保留政策；啟用追蹤本身不等於建立耐久稽核檔案。目前文件將此服務標示為 Agents Classic，並限制新客戶使用，新實作須確認可用性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Category-specific tuning and state integration add maintenance and daily retraining pressure.","why_zh":"依類別微調及狀態整合增加維護工作與每日更新負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Continued pretraining is poorly suited to rapidly changing facts and omits managed session/trace orchestration.","why_zh":"持續預先訓練不適合快速變動的事實，也缺少受管工作階段及追蹤協調。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Requires managing containers and separate search/orchestration components.","why_zh":"需要管理容器與獨立搜尋、協調元件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/agents-action-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/trace-events.html"],"issues":["agents_classic_current_availability","trace_requires_durable_storage"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.987292+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":27,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is using Amazon Bedrock to build a generative AI (GenAI) application. The application uses AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a multi-agent workflow to produce detailed product descriptions. The workflow consists of three sequential states: a description generator, a technical specifications validator, and a brand voice consistency checker. Each state produces intermediate reasoning traces and outputs that are passed to the next state. The application uses an Amazon S3 bucket for process storage and to store outputs. During testing, the company discovers that outputs between Step Functions states frequently exceed the 256 KB quota and cause workflow failures. A GenAI Developer needs to revise the application architecture to efficiently handle the Step Functions 256 KB quota and maintain workflow observability. The revised architecture must preserve the existing multi-agent reasoning and acting (ReAct) pattern. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Store intermediate outputs in Amazon DynamoDB. Pass only references between states. Create a Map state that retrieves the complete data from DynamoDB when required for each agent's processing step.","B":"Configure an Amazon Bedrock integration to use the S3 bucket URI in the input parameter for large outputs. Use the ResultPath field and the ResultSelector field to route S3 references between the agent steps while maintaining the sequential validation workflow.","C":"Use AWS Lambda functions to compress outputs to less than 256 KB before each agent state. Configure each agent task to decompress the outputs before processing and to compress results before passing them to the next state.","D":"Configure a separate Step Functions state machine to handle each agent's processing. Use Amazon EventBridge to coordinate the execution flow between state machines. Use S3 references for the outputs as event data."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":88,"A":13},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":27,"pages":[54,55]},"question_zh":"一家電子商務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立生成式 AI 應用程式，並以 AWS Step Functions 協調多代理程式工作流程，產生詳細商品描述。流程有三個循序狀態：描述產生器、技術規格驗證器及品牌語調一致性檢查器。各狀態產生中間推理軌跡及輸出，傳給下一狀態。應用程式使用 Amazon S3 儲存貯體儲存流程資料及輸出。測試時，公司發現狀態間輸出經常超過 256 KB 配額，導致工作流程失敗。開發人員必須調整架構，有效處理此配額並維持流程可觀測性，同時保留既有多代理程式推理與行動（ReAct）模式。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將中間輸出存於 Amazon DynamoDB，只在狀態間傳遞參照。建立 Map 狀態，在各代理程式處理步驟需要時從 DynamoDB 取得完整資料。","B":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 整合，在輸入參數使用 S3 儲存貯體 URI 處理大型輸出。使用 ResultPath 與 ResultSelector 欄位，在代理程式步驟間傳遞 S3 參照，同時維持循序驗證工作流程。","C":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數，在各代理程式狀態前將輸出壓縮至 256 KB 以下。讓各代理程式任務在處理前解壓縮輸入，並在傳給下一狀態前壓縮結果。","D":"為各代理程式的處理設定獨立 Step Functions 狀態機。使用 Amazon EventBridge 協調狀態機間的執行流程，並以 S3 輸出參照作為事件資料。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The optimized Bedrock InvokeModel integration accepts Input.S3Uri and Output.S3Uri. Output writes the response to S3 and replaces the state result body with a reference, avoiding the 256 KiB state-payload limit while preserving sequential tasks. ResultSelector and ResultPath can then retain only the required references and metadata. B has imprecise wording: Input reads a large request, while Output must be configured to offload a large response; Input alone does not fix oversized outputs.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock InvokeModel 最佳化整合支援 Input.S3Uri 與 Output.S3Uri。Output 會將回應寫入 S3，並以參照替換狀態結果本文，避開 256 KiB 狀態承載限制，同時保留循序任務。ResultSelector 與 ResultPath 可只保留所需參照及中繼資料。B 的措辭不精確：Input 用於讀取大型請求，必須設定 Output 才能外存大型回應，只有 Input 無法解決輸出過大。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adds a storage service and a Map pattern that is unnecessary for the existing sequential flow.","why_zh":"增加額外儲存服務及既有循序流程不需要的 Map 模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Compression is not guaranteed to fit every output and adds code at each step.","why_zh":"壓縮無法保證所有輸出都符合上限，且每步都增加程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Splitting state machines adds coordination and observability complexity.","why_zh":"拆分狀態機增加協調與可觀測性複雜度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/input-output-resultpath.html"],"issues":["must_configure_output_s3uri"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.988785+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":28,"question_en":"A company provides a service that helps users from around the world discover new restaurants. The service has 50 million monthly active users. The company wants to implement a semantic search solution across a database that contains 20 million restaurants and 200 million reviews. The company currently stores the data in a PostgresQL database. The solution must support complex natural language queries and return results for at least 95% of queries within 500 ms. The solution must maintain data freshness for restaurant details that update hourly. The solution must also scale cost-effectively during peak usage periods. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the restaurant data to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Implement keyword-based search rules that use custom analyzers and relevance tuning to find restaurants based on attributes such as cuisine type, feature, and location. Create Amazon API Gateway HTTP API endpoints to transform user queries into structured search parameters.","B":"Migrate the restaurant data to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Use a foundation model (FM) in Amazon Bedrock to generate vector embeddings from restaurant descriptions, reviews, and menu items. When users submit natural language queries, convert the queries to embeddings by using the same FM. Perform k- nearest neighbors (k-NN) searches to find semantically similar results.","C":"Keep the restaurant data in PostgresQL and implement a pgvector extension. Use a foundation model (FM) in Amazon Bedrock to generate vector embeddings from restaurant data. Store the vector embeddings directly in PostgreSQL. Create an AWS Lambda function to convert natural language queries to vector representations by using the same FM. Configure the Lambda function to perform similarity searches within the database.","D":"Migrate restaurant data to an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base by using a custom ingestion pipeline. Configure the knowledge base to automatically generate embeddings from restaurant information. Use the Amazon Bedrock Retrieve API with built-in vector search capabilities to query the knowledge base directly by using natural language input."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":67,"D":22,"A":11},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":28,"pages":[56,57]},"question_zh":"一家公司提供全球餐廳探索服務，每月有 5,000 萬活躍使用者。公司希望對包含 2,000 萬家餐廳及 2 億筆評論的資料庫實作語意搜尋。目前資料儲存在 PostgreSQL 資料庫。方案必須支援複雜自然語言查詢，至少 95% 的查詢須在 500 毫秒內回傳結果，維持每小時更新的餐廳詳細資訊新鮮度，並在尖峰時段以具成本效益的方式擴展。哪個方案能以最少開發工作符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將餐廳資料移轉至 Amazon OpenSearch Service。以自訂分析器及相關性調整實作關鍵字搜尋規則，根據料理類型、特色及地點等屬性尋找餐廳。建立 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API 端點，將使用者查詢轉成結構化搜尋參數。","B":"將餐廳資料移轉至 Amazon OpenSearch Service。使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM），為餐廳描述、評論及菜單品項產生向量嵌入。使用者送出自然語言查詢時，以相同 FM 將查詢轉成嵌入，並執行 k 最近鄰（k-NN）搜尋找出語意相近結果。","C":"將餐廳資料保留於 PostgreSQL 並實作 pgvector 擴充套件。使用 Amazon Bedrock FM 產生餐廳資料的向量嵌入，直接存於 PostgreSQL。建立 AWS Lambda 函數，以相同 FM 將自然語言查詢轉成向量，並在資料庫內執行相似度搜尋。","D":"使用自訂匯入管線將餐廳資料移轉至 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫。設定知識庫自動從餐廳資訊產生嵌入，並使用具內建向量搜尋能力的 Amazon Bedrock Retrieve API，直接以自然語言輸入查詢知識庫。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"OpenSearch semantic search supports vector retrieval and Bedrock embedding connectors, making B a natural scalable search architecture. The same embedding model must be used for indexed content and queries. However, neither a 500-ms percentile nor hourly freshness follows automatically from this choice: indexing updates, capacity, embedding latency and load testing are required. PostgreSQL with pgvector and managed knowledge-base retrieval are also possible; the question supplies insufficient measurements to prove B uniquely meets the performance target.","explanation_zh":"OpenSearch 語意搜尋支援向量檢索及 Bedrock 嵌入連接器，因此 B 是合理的可擴展搜尋架構。索引內容及查詢應使用相同嵌入模型。不過，這項選擇不會自動保證 500 毫秒百分位延遲或每小時資料新鮮度，仍須安排索引更新、容量、嵌入延遲及負載測試。PostgreSQL 搭配 pgvector 或受管知識庫檢索也可能可行；題目缺少實測資料，無法證明只有 B 達標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Keyword rules do not directly supply semantic similarity for complex natural language.","why_zh":"關鍵字規則不直接提供複雜自然語言的語意相似性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Possible, but requires database index/capacity engineering at this scale; performance is not established.","why_zh":"可行，但此規模需要資料庫索引及容量工程，效能尚未證明。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Possible managed retrieval, but custom ingestion and large-scale latency/freshness still require validation.","why_zh":"受管檢索可行，但自訂匯入及大規模延遲、新鮮度仍需驗證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/semantic-search.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/knn.html"],"issues":["performance_and_unique_best_not_proven"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.989803+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":29,"question_en":"A medical company uses Amazon Bedrock to power a clinical documentation summarization system. The system produces inconsistent summaries when handling complex clinical documents. The system performed well on simple clinical documents. The company needs a solution that diagnoses inconsistencies, compares prompt performance against established metrics, and maintains historical records of prompt versions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create multiple prompt variants by using Prompt management in Amazon Bedrock. Manually test the prompts with simple clinical documents. Deploy the highest performing version by using the Amazon Bedrock console.","B":"Implement version control for prompts in a code repository with a test suite that contains complex clinical documents and quantifiable evaluation metrics. Use an automated testing framework to compare prompt versions and document performance patterns.","C":"Deploy each new prompt version to separate Amazon Bedrock API endpoints. Split production traffic between the endpoints. Configure Amazon CloudWatch to capture response metrics and user feedback for automatic version selection.","D":"Create a custom prompt evaluation flow in Amazon Bedrock Flows that applies the same clinical document inputs to different prompt variants. Use Amazon Comprehend Medical to analyze and score the factual accuracy of each version."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":62,"D":31,"A":8},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":29,"pages":[58,59]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 提供臨床文件摘要系統。系統處理簡單臨床文件時表現良好，處理複雜臨床文件時卻產生不一致摘要。公司需要能診斷不一致性、依既定指標比較提示效能，並保留提示版本歷史紀錄的方案。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Prompt management 建立多個提示變體，以簡單臨床文件手動測試提示，再透過 Amazon Bedrock 主控台部署表現最好的版本。","B":"在程式碼儲存庫對提示實作版本控制，並建立包含複雜臨床文件及可量化評估指標的測試套件。使用自動測試框架比較提示版本，並記錄效能模式。","C":"將各新提示版本部署至獨立 Amazon Bedrock API 端點，在端點間分流正式環境流量。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 擷取回應指標及使用者回饋，以自動選擇版本。","D":"在 Amazon Bedrock Flows 建立自訂提示評估流程，將相同臨床文件輸入套用至不同提示變體。使用 Amazon Comprehend Medical 分析及評分各版本的事實正確性。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B couples reproducible version history with representative difficult examples and quantitative regression metrics. This makes failures attributable to prompt changes and enables controlled comparisons against a known baseline. AWS guidance similarly recommends versioned behavioral configurations linked to evaluation results. Comprehend Medical extracts medical entities and relationships; it is not a general factual-accuracy judge for arbitrary summaries.","explanation_zh":"B 將可重現的版本歷史、具代表性的困難案例及量化回歸指標結合，可將失敗歸因至提示變更，並與已知基準做受控比較。AWS 指引同樣建議將行為設定版本化並連結評估結果。Comprehend Medical 用於擷取醫療實體及關係，不是任意摘要的通用事實正確性評分器。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Testing only simple documents misses the failure distribution.","why_zh":"只測簡單文件會漏掉實際失敗情境。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Production splitting lacks a controlled complex-document test set and explicit version history.","why_zh":"正式環境分流缺少受控複雜文件測試集及明確版本歷史。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Comprehend Medical does not supply the claimed factual-accuracy scoring.","why_zh":"Comprehend Medical 不提供所宣稱的事實正確性評分。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/agentic-ai-lens/agentops02-bp03.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management-version-compare.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.990937+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Bedrock to generate technical content for customers. The company has recently experienced a surge in hallucination outputs when the company's model generates summaries of long technical documents. The model outputs include inaccurate or fabricated details. The company's current solution uses a large foundation model (FM) with a basic one-shot prompt that includes the full document in a single input. The company needs a solution that will reduce hallucinations and meet factual accuracy goals. The solution must process more than 1,000 documents each hour and deliver summaries within 3 seconds for each document. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Implement zero-shot chain-of-thought (CoT) instructions that require step-by-step reasoning with explicit fact verification before the model generates each summary.","B":"Use Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Apply semantic chunking and tuned embeddings to ground summaries in source content.","C":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to block any generated output that matches patterns that are associated with hallucinated content.","D":"Increase the temperature parameter in Amazon Bedrock.","E":"Prompt the Amazon Bedrock model to summarize each full document in one pass."},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AB":88,"BC":6,"C":6},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":30,"pages":[60,61]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 為客戶產生技術內容。最近模型摘要長篇技術文件時，幻覺輸出大幅增加，內容出現不準確或虛構細節。目前方案使用大型基礎模型（FM），以基本單次提示將完整文件放入單一輸入。公司需要降低幻覺並達成事實正確性目標，每小時必須處理超過 1,000 份文件，且每份文件須在 3 秒內產出摘要。哪一組方案符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"實作零樣本思維鏈（CoT）指示，要求模型在產生各摘要前逐步推理並明確驗證事實。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫實作檢索增強生成（RAG），套用語意分塊及調整後的嵌入，讓摘要以來源內容為依據。","C":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，封鎖所有符合幻覺內容相關模式的生成輸出。","D":"提高 Amazon Bedrock 的 temperature 參數。","E":"提示 Amazon Bedrock 模型一次摘要每份完整文件。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"RAG grounding in B directly addresses unsupported details by retrieving relevant source passages. A can request a structured evidence check, but a model checking its own reasoning is not independent factual verification and can increase latency. AB is the best intended pair among weak alternatives; it does not establish the three-second SLA or guarantee complete long-document summaries. Contextual grounding checks would be useful, but C describes generic hallucination pattern matching rather than the required source-based check.","explanation_zh":"B 的 RAG 透過檢索相關來源段落，可直接改善無依據細節。A 可要求結構化證據檢查，但模型自我檢查推理並非獨立事實驗證，而且可能增加延遲。AB 是這些薄弱選項中最接近題意的組合，不能證明達到 3 秒 SLA，也不能保證長文件摘要完整。情境依據檢查確實有用，但 C 描述的是通用幻覺模式比對，並非必要的來源對照檢查。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"No universal textual pattern identifies all hallucinations; grounding requires source comparison.","why_zh":"不存在能辨識所有幻覺的通用文字模式，依據檢查需要對照來源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Higher temperature increases randomness rather than enforcing factuality.","why_zh":"提高 temperature 會增加隨機性，而非強制事實正確。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Repeats the failing full-document one-pass approach.","why_zh":"重複目前已出問題的完整文件單次處理方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/agentic-ai-lens/agentrel05-bp03.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html"],"issues":["self_verification_not_factual_guarantee","latency_target_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.991716+00:00"},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":31,"question_en":"A company has a recommendation system. The system's applications run on Amazon EC2 instances. The applications make API calls to Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to analyze customer behavior and generate personalized product recommendations. The system is experiencing intermittent issues. Some recommendations do not match customer preferences. The company needs an observability solution to monitor operational metrics and detect patterns of operational performance degradation compared to established baselines. The solution must also generate alerts with correlation data within 10 minutes when FM behavior deviates from expected patterns. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for the application infrastructure. Set up CloudWatch alarms for latency thresholds. Add custom metrics for token counts by using the CloudWatch embedded metric format. Create CloudWatch dashboards to visualize the data.","B":"Implement AWS X-Ray to trace requests through the application components. Enable CloudWatch Logs Insights for error pattern detection. Set up AWS CloudTrail to monitor all API calls to Amazon Bedrock. Create custom dashboards in Amazon QuickSight.","C":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Application Insights for the application resources. Create custom metrics for recommendation quality, token usage, and response latency by using the CloudWatch embedded metric format with dimensions for request types and user segments. Configure CloudWatch anomaly detection on the model metrics. Establish log pattern analysis by using CloudWatch Logs Insights.","D":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Service with the Observability plugin. Ingest model metrics and logs by using Amazon Kinesis. Create custom Piped Processing Language (PPL) queries to analyze model behavior patterns. Establish operational dashboards to visualize anomalies in real time."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":88,"B":13},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":31,"pages":[62,63]},"question_zh":"一家公司的推薦系統應用程式執行於 Amazon EC2 執行個體，透過 API 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM），分析客戶行為並產生個人化商品推薦。系統間歇出現問題，部分推薦不符合客戶偏好。公司需要可觀測性方案，監控作業指標，與既定基準比較以偵測作業效能惡化模式；FM 行為偏離預期模式時，必須在 10 分鐘內產生含關聯資料的警示。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為應用程式基礎設施設定 Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights。設定延遲門檻警示，以 CloudWatch 嵌入式指標格式加入 token 計數自訂指標，並建立 CloudWatch 儀表板呈現資料。","B":"實作 AWS X-Ray 追蹤跨應用元件的請求。啟用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 偵測錯誤模式，以 AWS CloudTrail 監控所有 Amazon Bedrock API 呼叫，並建立 Amazon QuickSight 自訂儀表板。","C":"為應用程式資源啟用 Amazon CloudWatch Application Insights。以 CloudWatch 嵌入式指標格式建立推薦品質、token 用量及回應延遲自訂指標，加入請求類型與使用者區隔維度。為模型指標設定 CloudWatch 異常偵測，並使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 建立日誌模式分析。","D":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 的 Observability 外掛。透過 Amazon Kinesis 匯入模型指標及日誌，以自訂管線處理語言（PPL）查詢分析模型行為模式，並建立作業儀表板即時呈現異常。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Application Insights correlates metric anomalies and log errors for EC2 applications, while CloudWatch anomaly detection learns expected metric baselines. Custom quality metrics provide the semantic signal that infrastructure latency alone lacks. C therefore covers quality, operations and correlation most directly. Define how recommendation quality is scored, configure alarm evaluation periods and notifications within the ten-minute objective, and include correlation identifiers in logs.","explanation_zh":"Application Insights 可為 EC2 應用程式關聯指標異常及日誌錯誤，CloudWatch 異常偵測則學習預期指標基準。自訂品質指標補足單靠基礎設施延遲無法提供的語意訊號，因此 C 最直接涵蓋品質、作業與關聯分析。仍須定義推薦品質評分方法，在 10 分鐘目標內設定警示評估週期及通知，並在日誌加入關聯識別碼。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Container Insights does not match plain EC2 applications and omits recommendation-quality baselines.","why_zh":"Container Insights 不直接對應一般 EC2 應用程式，且缺少推薦品質基準。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Traces and API audits do not by themselves detect deviations in recommendation quality.","why_zh":"追蹤及 API 稽核本身不會偵測推薦品質偏離。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Dashboards and custom queries lack the explicit baseline alarms and correlation workflow.","why_zh":"儀表板及自訂查詢缺少明確的基準警示與關聯流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Anomaly_Detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/appinsights-what-is.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.992258+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":32,"question_en":"An enterprise application uses an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM) to process and analyze 50 to 200 pages of technical documents. Users are experiencing inconsistent responses and receiving truncated outputs when processing documents that exceed the FM's context window limits. Which solution will resolve this problem?","options_en":{"A":"Configure fixed-size chunking at 4,000 tokens for each chunk with 20% overlap. Use application-level logic to link multiple chunks sequentially until the FM's maximum context window of 200,000 tokens is reached before making inference calls.","B":"Use hierarchical chunking with parent chunks of 8,000 tokens and child chunks of 2,000 tokens. Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases built-in retrieval to automatically select relevant parent chunks based on query context. Configure overlap tokens to maintain semantic continuity.","C":"Use semantic chunking with a breakpoint percentile threshold of 95% and a buffer size of 3 sentences. Use the Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API call to dynamically select the most relevant chunks based on embedding similarity scores.","D":"Create a pre-processing AWS Lambda function that analyzes document token count by using the FM's tokenizer. Configure the lambda function to split documents into equal segments that fit within 80% of the context window. Configure the Lambda function to process each segment independently before aggregating the results."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":67,"B":25,"D":8},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":32,"pages":[64,65]},"question_zh":"一家企業應用程式使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）處理及分析 50 至 200 頁的技術文件。處理超過 FM 上下文視窗限制的文件時，使用者遇到回應不一致與輸出遭截斷的問題。哪個方案能解決此問題？","options_zh":{"A":"設定固定大小分塊，每塊 4,000 token、重疊 20%。使用應用層邏輯依序串接多個區塊，直到達到 FM 的 200,000 token 最大上下文視窗，再進行推論呼叫。","B":"使用階層式分塊，父區塊為 8,000 token，子區塊為 2,000 token。使用 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 內建檢索，依查詢脈絡自動選取相關父區塊，並設定重疊 token 以維持語意連續性。","C":"使用語意分塊，將中斷點百分位門檻設為 95%，緩衝大小設為 3 個句子。使用 Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API，依嵌入相似度分數動態選取最相關區塊。","D":"建立前處理 AWS Lambda 函數，以 FM tokenizer 分析文件 token 數。讓函數將文件分成等長片段，使各片段不超過上下文視窗的 80%，獨立處理各片段後再彙整結果。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"B uses supported hierarchical retrieval: relevant child chunks are found and replaced by their parent chunks to preserve broader context without sending every page. If the marked C means an API bufferSize value of 3, it is invalid because SemanticChunkingConfiguration.bufferSize accepts only 0 or 1; bufferSize 1 produces a three-sentence window. D is a possible custom map-and-aggregate approach but loses cross-segment context unless carefully implemented. No chunking strategy alone prevents output truncation: retrieved-context size and generation max-token budgets must also fit the chosen model. The phrase \"buffer size of 3 sentences\" is ambiguous: if it means a total three-sentence window, bufferSize=1 implements that and C becomes viable. The choice of B is therefore conditional on interpreting 3 as the configured buffer value, not a conclusive rejection of semantic chunking.","explanation_zh":"B 使用受支援的階層式檢索：先找到相關子區塊，再以父區塊替換，保留較完整脈絡而不必送入所有頁面。若原標答 C 指 API bufferSize 值為 3，則不符合規格，因 SemanticChunkingConfiguration.bufferSize 只接受 0 或 1；bufferSize 為 1 會形成三句視窗。D 是可能的自訂分段彙整方案，但若未妥善實作會失去跨段脈絡。任何分塊策略都不能單獨防止輸出截斷，仍須讓檢索脈絡大小與生成 token 預算符合選定模型。 「緩衝大小為 3 個句子」也有語意歧義：若指總共三句的視窗，以 bufferSize=1 即可實作，此時 C 也成立。因此選 B 是將 3 理解為設定值下的判斷，不能毫無保留地否定語意分塊。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Fills the context window without reserving room for instructions and output.","why_zh":"填滿上下文視窗，未為指示及輸出保留空間。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Invalid if 3 is the API bufferSize; viable if it means a total three-sentence window configured with bufferSize=1.","why_zh":"若 3 指 API bufferSize 則無效；若指總共三句、設定 bufferSize=1 的視窗，則可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Independent equal segments require custom aggregation and may break semantic dependencies.","why_zh":"等長獨立片段需自訂彙整，且可能破壞語意關聯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-chunking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent_SemanticChunkingConfiguration.html"],"issues":["marked_answer_invalid_buffer_size","output_budget_also_required","three_sentence_window_interpretation_ambiguous"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.992850+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌・查證與標答及社群不同"},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application that analyzes customer service calls in real-time and generates suggested responses for human customer service agents. The application must process 500,000 concurrent calls during peak hours with less than 200 ms end-to-end latency for each suggestion. The company uses existing architecture to transcribe customer call audio streams. The application must not exceed a pre- defined monthly compute budget and must maintain auto scaling capabilities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a large, complex reasoning model on Amazon Bedrock. Purchase provisioned throughput and optimize for batch processing.","B":"Deploy a low-latency, real-time optimized model on Amazon Bedrock. Purchase provisioned throughput and set up automatic scaling policies.","C":"Deploy a large language model (LLM) on an Amazon SageMaker AI real-time endpoint that uses dedicated GPU instances.","D":"Deploy a mid-sized language model on an Amazon SageMaker AI serverless endpoint that is optimized for batch processing."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":75,"C":25},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":33,"pages":[66,67]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在開發生成式 AI 應用程式，即時分析客服通話，並為人工客服人員產生建議回應。應用程式尖峰時段必須處理 500,000 路同時通話，每項建議的端到端延遲低於 200 毫秒。公司使用既有架構轉錄客戶通話音訊串流。應用程式不得超過預定每月運算預算，且必須維持自動擴展能力。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Bedrock 部署大型複雜推理模型，購買佈建輸送量並針對批次處理最佳化。","B":"在 Amazon Bedrock 部署低延遲、即時最佳化模型，購買佈建輸送量並設定自動擴展政策。","C":"在使用專用 GPU 執行個體的 Amazon SageMaker AI 即時端點部署大型語言模型（LLM）。","D":"在針對批次處理最佳化的 Amazon SageMaker AI 無伺服器端點部署中型語言模型。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B expresses the intended preference for low-latency managed inference and predictable purchased capacity. However, the documentation for Model-Unit Provisioned Throughput does not provide the stated native autoscaling policy; purchased MU capacity cannot simply be edited as traffic changes. Tokens-based provisioning has different update capabilities and still needs an explicit scaling design. None of the options establishes 500,000 concurrent calls, sub-200-ms complete suggestions and the unspecified budget simultaneously; B is only the closest intended answer.","explanation_zh":"B 表達了低延遲受管推論及可預期購買容量的題目意圖。不過，以模型單位計費的佈建輸送量文件並未提供所述原生自動擴展政策，已購買 MU 容量不能隨流量直接修改。以 token 佈建的模式具有不同更新能力，但仍需要明確擴展設計。所有選項都未證明能同時達成 500,000 路並行通話、完整建議低於 200 毫秒，以及未指明的預算；B 只能視為最接近題意的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Large reasoning and batching conflict with tight interactive latency.","why_zh":"大型推理與批次處理不利於嚴格互動延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Dedicated GPU hosting could be engineered, but no model, scaling or budget evidence is provided.","why_zh":"專用 GPU 託管可另行設計，但未提供模型、擴展或預算證據。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Serverless batch-oriented processing is not suited to this extreme real-time requirement.","why_zh":"偏向批次的無伺服器處理不適合此極端即時需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prov-throughput.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prov-thru-edit.html"],"issues":["no_native_mu_autoscaling","latency_concurrency_budget_unproven"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.993331+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":34,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is building an internal platform to develop generative AI applications by using Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). Developers need to select models based on evaluations that are aligned to ecommerce use cases. The platform must display accuracy metrics for text generation and summarization in dashboards. The company has custom ecommerce datasets to use as standardized evaluation inputs. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Import the datasets to an Amazon S3 bucket. Provide appropriate IAM permissions and cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) permissions to give the evaluation jobs access to the datasets.","B":"Import the datasets to an Amazon S3 bucket. Provide appropriate IAM permissions and a VPC endpoint configuration to give the evaluation jobs access to the datasets.","C":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to create model evaluation jobs on a schedule in the Amazon Bedrock console. Provide the URI of the S3 bucket that contains the datasets as an input. Configure the evaluation jobs to measure the real world knowledge (RWK) score for text generation and BERT Score for summarization. Configure a second Lambda function to check the status of the jobs and publish custom logs to Amazon CloudWatch. Create a custom Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights dashboard.","D":"Use Amazon SageMaker Clarify on a schedule to create model evaluation jobs. Use open source frameworks to create and run standardized evaluations. Publish results to Amazon CloudWatch namespaces. Use the word error rate score for text generation and toxicity for summarization as metrics for accuracy. Configure an AWS Lambda function to check the status of the jobs and publish custom logs to CloudWatch. Create a custom Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights dashboard.","E":"Run an Amazon SageMaker AI notebook job on a schedule by using the fmevals or ragas framework to run evaluations that use the datasets in the S3 bucket. Write Python code in the notebook that makes direct InvokeModel API calls to the FMs and processes their responses for evaluation. Publish job status and results to Amazon CloudWatch Logs to measure the real world knowledge (RWK) score for text generation and toxicity for summarization as metrics for accuracy. Create a custom CloudWatch Logs Insights dashboard."},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"AC":75,"BC":19,"C":6},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":34,"pages":[68,69]},"question_zh":"一家電子商務公司正在建立內部平台，使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）開發生成式 AI 應用程式。開發人員需要依符合電子商務案例的評估選擇模型。平台必須在儀表板顯示文字生成及摘要的準確性指標。公司已有自訂電子商務資料集作為標準化評估輸入。哪一組步驟能以最低維運負擔符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"將資料集匯入 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，提供適當 IAM 權限及跨來源資源共用（CORS）權限，讓評估作業存取資料集。","B":"將資料集匯入 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，提供適當 IAM 權限及 VPC 端點設定，讓評估作業存取資料集。","C":"設定 AWS Lambda 函數，定期在 Amazon Bedrock 主控台建立模型評估作業，並以資料集所在 S3 儲存貯體 URI 作為輸入。設定文字生成評估採用真實世界知識（RWK）分數、摘要採用 BERT Score。設定第二個 Lambda 函數檢查作業狀態並發佈自訂日誌至 Amazon CloudWatch，再建立自訂 CloudWatch Logs Insights 儀表板。","D":"定期使用 Amazon SageMaker Clarify 建立模型評估作業，使用開源框架建立及執行標準化評估，並將結果發佈至 Amazon CloudWatch 命名空間。將文字生成的字詞錯誤率及摘要的毒性分數作為準確性指標。設定 AWS Lambda 函數檢查作業狀態並發佈自訂日誌至 CloudWatch，再建立自訂 CloudWatch Logs Insights 儀表板。","E":"定期執行 Amazon SageMaker AI 筆記本作業，使用 fmevals 或 ragas 框架評估 S3 儲存貯體中的資料集。在筆記本撰寫 Python 程式，直接呼叫 FM 的 InvokeModel API 並處理回應進行評估。將作業狀態及結果發佈至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，使用 RWK 分數作為文字生成準確性指標、毒性作為摘要準確性指標，再建立自訂 CloudWatch Logs Insights 儀表板。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The documented automated evaluation metrics are RWK for text-generation accuracy and BERTScore for summarization accuracy, matching C. Managed evaluation jobs using S3 datasets reduce custom evaluation code compared with notebook frameworks. A is the intended setup choice, but IAM authorizes service access; CORS concerns browser access and does not grant an evaluation job permission. Lambda must call the evaluation API on a schedule, not operate the console; a VPC endpoint is not a general prerequisite.","explanation_zh":"官方自動評估指標以 RWK 衡量文字生成準確性，以 BERTScore 衡量摘要準確性，符合 C。受管評估作業使用 S3 資料集，相較筆記本框架可減少自訂評估程式。A 是題目預期的設定選項，但服務存取由 IAM 授權，CORS 處理瀏覽器存取，不會授予評估作業權限。Lambda 應按排程呼叫評估 API，而非操作主控台；VPC 端點並非通用必要條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A VPC endpoint is not required for ordinary managed evaluation access to S3.","why_zh":"一般受管評估作業存取 S3 不要求 VPC 端點。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Word error rate measures robustness here, and toxicity is not summarization accuracy.","why_zh":"此處字詞錯誤率用於穩健性，毒性也不是摘要準確性。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Adds custom code and incorrectly uses toxicity as an accuracy metric.","why_zh":"增加自訂程式碼，且錯將毒性當成準確性指標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-report-programmatic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-security.html"],"issues":["cors_not_service_authorization","lambda_uses_api_not_console"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.993938+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":35,"question_en":"An elevator service company has developed an AI assistant application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application generates elevator maintenance recommendations to support the company's elevator technicians. The company uses Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to collect the elevator sensor data. New regulatory rules require that a human technician must review all AI-generated recommendations. The company needs to establish human oversight workflows to review and approve AI recommendations. The company must store all human technician review decisions for audit purposes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom approval workflow by using AWS Lambda functions and Amazon SQS queues for human review of AI recommendations. Store all review decisions in Amazon DynamoDB for audit purposes.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow that has a human approval step that uses the waitForTaskToken API to pause execution. After a human technician completes a review, use an AWS Lambda function to call the SendTaskSuccess API that has the approval decision. Store all review decisions in Amazon DynamoDB.","C":"Create an AWS Glue workflow that has a human approval step. After the human technician review, integrate the application with an AWS Lambda function that calls the SendTaskSuccess API. Store all human technician review decisions in Amazon DynamoDB.","D":"Configure Amazon EventBridge rules with custom event patterns to route AI recommendations to human technicians for review. Create AWS Glue jobs to process human technician approval queues. Use Amazon ElastiCache to cache all human technician review decisions."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":88,"A":13},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":35,"pages":[70,71]},"question_zh":"一家電梯服務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 開發 AI 助理應用程式，為公司的電梯技術人員產生維護建議。公司使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 收集電梯感測器資料。新法規要求所有 AI 建議都必須由人工技術人員審查。公司需要建立人工監督工作流程，以審查及核准 AI 建議，並儲存所有技術人員的審查決定供稽核。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數及 Amazon SQS 佇列建立自訂核准流程，供人工審查 AI 建議，並將所有審查決定存於 Amazon DynamoDB 供稽核。","B":"建立具有人工核准步驟的 AWS Step Functions 工作流程，使用 waitForTaskToken API 暫停執行。技術人員完成審查後，以 AWS Lambda 函數呼叫帶有核准決定的 SendTaskSuccess API，並將所有審查決定存於 Amazon DynamoDB。","C":"建立具有人工核准步驟的 AWS Glue 工作流程。技術人員完成審查後，整合 AWS Lambda 函數呼叫 SendTaskSuccess API，並將所有人工審查決定存於 Amazon DynamoDB。","D":"設定具有自訂事件模式的 Amazon EventBridge 規則，將 AI 建議路由至技術人員審查。建立 AWS Glue 作業處理人工核准佇列，並使用 Amazon ElastiCache 快取所有審查決定。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Step Functions Standard workflows support the callback task-token integration pattern, which waits for an external reviewer before resuming. SendTaskSuccess returns the review payload to the waiting task, and DynamoDB can persist the decision with reviewer identity and timestamps. A Choice state should explicitly branch on approval versus rejection; successful callback delivery does not itself mean approval. The option calls waitForTaskToken an API, but it is an integration suffix rather than a standalone API operation.","explanation_zh":"Step Functions Standard 工作流程支援回呼任務 token 整合模式，可等待外部審查者再繼續執行。SendTaskSuccess 將審查結果傳回等待中的任務，DynamoDB 可保存決定、審查者身分與時間戳。應以 Choice 狀態明確區分核准及拒絕，回呼成功送達本身不代表核准。選項將 waitForTaskToken 稱為 API，但它實際上是整合後綴，而非獨立 API 操作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Possible, but requires custom waiting, correlation and retry orchestration.","why_zh":"可行，但需自訂等待、關聯及重試協調。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Glue workflows do not use the Step Functions callback task-token mechanism.","why_zh":"Glue 工作流程不使用 Step Functions 回呼任務 token 機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Event routing and an evictable cache do not provide a durable approval state machine and audit record.","why_zh":"事件路由及可能淘汰資料的快取，不提供耐久核准狀態機及稽核紀錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-to-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/apireference/API_SendTaskSuccess.html"],"issues":["waitfortasktoken_is_integration_pattern"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:10.994625+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":36,"question_en":"A bank is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to assess loan applications by using scanned financial documents. The application must extract structured data from the documents. The application must redact personally identifiable information (PII) before inference. The application must use foundation models (FMs) to generate approvals. The application must route low-confidence document extraction results to human reviewers who are within the same AWS Region as the loan applicant. The company must ensure that the application complies with strict Regional data residency and auditability requirements. The application must be able to scale to handle 25,000 applications each day and provide 99.9% availability. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","options_en":{"A":"Deploy Amazon Textract and Amazon Augmented AI (Amazon A2I) within the same Region to extract relevant data from the scanned documents. Route low-confidence pages to human reviewers.","B":"Use AWS Lambda functions to detect and redact PII from submitted documents before inference. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to prevent inappropriate or unauthorized content in model outputs. Configure Region-specific IAM roles to enforce data residency requirements and to control access to the extracted data.","C":"Use Amazon Kendra and Amazon OpenSearch Service to extract field level values semantically from the uploaded documents before inference.","D":"Store uploaded documents in Amazon S3 and apply object metadata. Configure IAM policies to store original documents within the same Region as each applicant. Enable object tagging for future audits.","E":"Use AWS Glue Data Quality to validate the structured document data. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a review workflow that includes a prompt engineering step that transforms validated data into optimized prompts before invoking Amazon Bedrock to assess loan applications.","F":"Use Amazon SageMaker Clarify to generate fairness and bias reports based on model scoring decisions that Amazon Bedrock makes."},"answer":["A","B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"ABE":50,"ADE":25,"ABD":13,"B":13},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":36,"pages":[72,73]},"question_zh":"一家銀行正在建立生成式 AI 應用程式，使用 Amazon Bedrock 根據掃描的財務文件評估貸款申請。應用程式必須擷取結構化資料，在推論前遮蔽個人可識別資訊（PII），並使用基礎模型（FM）產生核准結果。低信心的文件擷取結果必須送交與申請人位於相同 AWS 區域的人工審查者。公司必須遵守嚴格區域資料落地及可稽核性要求，並能擴展至每日 25,000 件申請、提供 99.9% 可用性。哪一組方案符合需求？（選三項。）","options_zh":{"A":"在相同區域部署 Amazon Textract 及 Amazon Augmented AI（Amazon A2I），從掃描文件擷取相關資料，並將低信心頁面交給人工審查者。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數在推論前偵測及遮蔽提交文件中的 PII。套用 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制，防止模型輸出不當或未授權內容。設定區域專屬 IAM 角色，強制資料落地要求並控制擷取資料的存取。","C":"使用 Amazon Kendra 及 Amazon OpenSearch Service，在推論前從上傳文件以語意方式擷取欄位值。","D":"將上傳文件存於 Amazon S3 並套用物件中繼資料。設定 IAM 政策，讓原始文件儲存在各申請人相同的區域，並啟用物件標籤供未來稽核。","E":"使用 AWS Glue Data Quality 驗證結構化文件資料。使用 AWS Step Functions 協調審查流程，包含提示工程步驟，將驗證後資料轉換成最佳化提示，再呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 評估貸款申請。","F":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Clarify，根據 Amazon Bedrock 模型評分決定產生公平性及偏差報告。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","B","D"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Textract with A2I can route low-confidence form extraction to review, while preprocessing can redact PII and regional S3 storage can retain source documents. ABD is the intended combination, but region-specific IAM role names and object tags do not enforce residency or provide complete audit logs. Policies must constrain actual regional resources and inference destinations; the human workforce location must be separately controlled. The options also do not prove the workload capacity or end-to-end availability, and current A2I documentation restricts new-customer access.","explanation_zh":"Textract 搭配 A2I 可將低信心表單擷取送交審查，前處理可遮蔽 PII，區域 S3 儲存可保留來源文件。ABD 是題目預期組合，但區域專屬 IAM 角色名稱及物件標籤不會強制資料落地，也不提供完整稽核日誌。政策必須限制實際區域資源與推論目的地，人工工作團隊所在地也須另行控制。選項亦未證明工作負載容量或端到端可用性，目前 A2I 文件並限制新客戶使用。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Search services do not replace document form extraction.","why_zh":"搜尋服務無法取代文件表單擷取。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Validation and orchestration do not replace PII redaction, regional storage or confidence-triggered review.","why_zh":"驗證與協調無法取代 PII 遮蔽、區域儲存或信心觸發審查。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Bias analysis does not implement the required extraction and residency controls.","why_zh":"偏差分析沒有實作必要的擷取與資料落地控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/a2i-json-humantaskactivationconditions-textract-example.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html"],"issues":["human_location_not_region_setting","tags_not_audit","capacity_availability_unproven","a2i_current_availability"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.056821+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・複選・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":37,"question_en":"A software company is using Amazon Q Business to build an AI assistant that allows employees to access company information and personal information by using natural language prompts. The company stores this information in an Amazon S3 bucket. Each department in the company has a dedicated prefix in the S3 bucket. Each object name includes the S3 prefix of the department that it belongs to. Each department can belong to only a single group in AWS IAM Identity Center. Each employee belongs to a single department. The company configures Amazon Q Business to access data stored in an S3 bucket as a data source. The company needs to ensure that the AI assistant respects access controls based on the user's IAM Identity Center group membership. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Create a JSON file named acl.json in each department folder. In each file, create access control entries that specify the IAM Identity Center group that should have access to that department's data. Indicate the location of the JSON file in the Access Control section of the data source settings.","B":"Create a single JSON file named acl.json at the top level of the S3 bucket. Add access control entries that map each department's S3 prefix to its corresponding IAM Identity Center group. Indicate the location of the JSON file in the Access Control section of the data source settings.","C":"For each IAM Identity Center group, create a separate permissions set that denies access to all prefixes in the S3 bucket. Add a StringNotEquals condition key to the permissions set for each group that specifies the department each group is associated with. Attach the permissions sets to the Identity Center groups.","D":"Create a metadata file named metadata.json at the top level of the S3 bucket. Add an AccessControlList object to the file that specifies the S3 path of each department's prefix. Specify the IAM Identity Center group that should have access to each department's prefix. Reference the file location in the data source metadata settings."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":37,"pages":[74,75]},"question_zh":"一家軟體公司使用 Amazon Q Business 建立 AI 助理，讓員工透過自然語言提示存取公司及個人資訊。資訊儲存在 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，每個部門有專屬前綴，每個物件名稱都包含所屬部門的 S3 前綴。每個部門只能對應 AWS IAM Identity Center 中的一個群組，每位員工只屬於單一部門。公司將 S3 儲存貯體設定為 Amazon Q Business 資料來源。公司需要確保助理依使用者的 IAM Identity Center 群組成員資格遵守存取控制。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在每個部門資料夾建立 acl.json 檔案，加入存取控制項目，指定可存取該部門資料的 IAM Identity Center 群組，並在資料來源設定的 Access Control 區段指定 JSON 檔案位置。","B":"在 S3 儲存貯體最上層建立單一 acl.json 檔案，加入存取控制項目，將各部門 S3 前綴對映至相應 IAM Identity Center 群組，並在資料來源設定的 Access Control 區段指定 JSON 檔案位置。","C":"為各 IAM Identity Center 群組建立個別權限集，拒絕存取 S3 儲存貯體所有前綴。為各群組權限集加入 StringNotEquals 條件鍵，指定群組對應部門，並將權限集附加至 Identity Center 群組。","D":"在 S3 儲存貯體最上層建立 metadata.json 檔案，加入 AccessControlList 物件，指定各部門前綴的 S3 路徑及可存取各前綴的 IAM Identity Center 群組，並在資料來源中繼資料設定參照檔案位置。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The S3 connector supports one ACL configuration file containing keyPrefix entries and USER or GROUP allow/deny entries. A prefix entry applies to documents beneath that path, matching the department structure with little maintenance. Configure the file path in the data source and map group identities correctly. Every protected prefix must be covered: the documentation warns that prefixes absent from the ACL file are accessible to all users.","explanation_zh":"S3 連接器支援單一 ACL 設定檔，包含 keyPrefix 項目及 USER 或 GROUP 的允許／拒絕項目。前綴設定適用於路徑下所有文件，能以低維護負擔對應部門結構。應在資料來源設定檔案路徑，並正確對映群組身分。所有受保護前綴都必須涵蓋，因官方文件警告：未列於 ACL 檔案的前綴可由所有使用者存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single connector ACL configuration path with multiple prefixes is simpler than per-folder files.","why_zh":"單一連接器 ACL 設定檔含多前綴，比每個資料夾各建檔案簡單。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS account permission sets do not automatically implement document-level Q retrieval ACLs.","why_zh":"AWS 帳戶權限集不會自動實作 Q 檢索的文件層 ACL。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses the wrong schema for a prefix-level ACL configuration file.","why_zh":"前綴 ACL 設定檔使用的結構不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/s3-user-management-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/connector-concepts.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.058081+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":38,"question_en":"A healthcare company is using Amazon Bedrock to build a system to help practitioners make clinical decisions. The system must provide treatment recommendations to physicians based only on approved medical documentation and must cite specific sources. The system must not hallucinate or produce factually incorrect information. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Integrate Amazon Bedrock with Amazon Kendra to retrieve approved documents. Implement custom post- processing to compare generated responses against source documents and to include citations.","B":"Deploy an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base and connect it to approved clinical source documents. Use the Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API to return citations from the knowledge base.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock and Amazon Comprehend Medical to extract medical entities. Implement verification logic against a medical terminology database.","D":"Use an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base with Retrieve API calls and InvokeModel API calls to retrieve approved clinical source documents. Implement verification logic to compare against retrieved sources and to cite sources."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"C":17},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":38,"pages":[76]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立系統，協助醫療人員做臨床決策。系統必須只依據核准的醫療文件向醫師提供治療建議，並引用特定來源，且不得產生幻覺或事實錯誤資訊。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"整合 Amazon Bedrock 與 Amazon Kendra，檢索核准文件。實作自訂後處理，對照來源文件檢查生成回應並加入引用。","B":"部署 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫，連接核准的臨床來源文件。使用 Amazon Bedrock RetrieveAndGenerate API 回傳知識庫引用。","C":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 及 Amazon Comprehend Medical 擷取醫療實體，並實作對照醫療術語資料庫的驗證邏輯。","D":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫，透過 Retrieve API 及 InvokeModel API 呼叫檢索核准臨床來源文件。實作驗證邏輯，對照檢索來源並引用來源。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"RetrieveAndGenerate integrates retrieval, generation and source citations, so B has the lowest implementation overhead for approved-source RAG. Restricting the knowledge base to approved documents controls what evidence is retrieved. It does not guarantee that every generated claim is correct or that hallucinations are impossible. Source-grounding evaluation, abstention when evidence is insufficient and appropriate clinical review are still needed to satisfy the absolute safety wording.","explanation_zh":"RetrieveAndGenerate 整合檢索、生成及來源引用，因此 B 是核准來源 RAG 中實作負擔最低的方案。將知識庫限制為核准文件，可控制檢索證據範圍，但不能保證每項生成主張正確，也不能保證完全沒有幻覺。若要符合題目絕對安全措辭，仍需要來源依據評估、證據不足時拒答，以及適當臨床審查。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Requires custom retrieval/citation verification plumbing.","why_zh":"需要自訂檢索、引用及驗證整合。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Medical entity extraction does not ground recommendations in approved source passages.","why_zh":"醫療實體擷取不會讓建議以核准來源段落為依據。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Provides more custom control but higher development and maintenance overhead.","why_zh":"提供較多自訂控制，但開發及維護負擔較高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-retrieve-generate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html"],"issues":["rag_citations_not_zero_hallucination_guarantee"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.059305+00:00"},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":39,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a real-time generative AI (GenAI) assistant to support human call center agents. The GenAI assistant must transcribe live customer speech, analyze context, and provide incremental suggestions to call center agents while a customer is still speaking. To preserve responsiveness, the GenAI assistant must maintain end-to-end latency under 1 second from speech to initial response display. The architecture must use only managed AWS services and must support bidirectional streaming to ensure that call center agents receive updates in real time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon Transcribe streaming API to transcribe calls. Pass the text to Amazon Comprehend to perform sentiment analysis. Feed the results to Anthropic Claude on Amazon Bedrock by using the InvokeModel API. Store results in Amazon DynamoDB. Use a WebSocket API to display the results.","B":"Use Amazon Transcribe streaming with partial results enabled to deliver fragments of transcribed text before customers finish speaking. Forward text fragments to Amazon Bedrock by using the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API. Stream responses to call center agents through an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API.","C":"Use Amazon Transcribe batch processing to convert calls to text. Pass complete transcripts to Anthropic Claude on Amazon Bedrock by using the ConverseStream API. Return responses through an Amazon Lex chatbot interface that call center agents can access from their work computers.","D":"Use the Amazon Transcribe streaming API with an AWS Lambda function to transcribe each audio segment. Configure the Lambda function to call the Amazon Titan Embeddings model on Amazon Bedrock by using the InvokeModel API. Configure the Lambda function to publish results to an Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the call center agents to the SNS topic."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":39,"pages":[78,79]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發即時生成式 AI 助理，支援人工客服中心人員。助理必須轉錄客戶即時語音、分析脈絡，並在客戶仍在說話時逐步提供建議。為維持反應速度，從語音到首次回應顯示的端到端延遲必須低於 1 秒。架構只能使用受管 AWS 服務，並必須支援雙向串流，讓客服人員即時收到更新。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Transcribe 串流 API 轉錄通話，將文字送至 Amazon Comprehend 進行情緒分析。透過 InvokeModel API 將結果送至 Amazon Bedrock 的 Anthropic Claude，將結果存於 Amazon DynamoDB，並使用 WebSocket API 顯示結果。","B":"使用 Amazon Transcribe 串流並啟用部分結果，在客戶說完之前提供文字片段。透過 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API 將文字片段送至 Amazon Bedrock，再以 Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API 將回應串流給客服人員。","C":"使用 Amazon Transcribe 批次處理將通話轉成文字。透過 ConverseStream API 將完整逐字稿送至 Amazon Bedrock 的 Anthropic Claude，再透過客服人員可從工作電腦存取的 Amazon Lex 聊天介面回傳回應。","D":"搭配 AWS Lambda 函數使用 Amazon Transcribe 串流 API 轉錄各音訊片段。讓 Lambda 函數透過 InvokeModel API 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 的 Amazon Titan Embeddings 模型，再將結果發佈至 Amazon SNS 主題，並讓客服人員訂閱該主題。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B combines incremental transcription, streamed model output and a bidirectional WebSocket client channel. Partial-result stabilization can reduce revisions, but incomplete transcripts still require deduplication and update handling. InvokeModelWithResponseStream streams the response to a fixed request; it is not a bidirectional model-input stream, so new fragments require application orchestration. The architecture reduces perceived latency but does not document a guaranteed sub-second end-to-end SLA.","explanation_zh":"B 結合增量轉錄、模型串流輸出及雙向 WebSocket 用戶端通道。部分結果穩定化可減少修訂，但未完成逐字稿仍需去重及更新處理。InvokeModelWithResponseStream 是對固定請求串流回應，不是雙向模型輸入串流，因此新片段仍需應用程式協調。此架構有助降低感受延遲，但沒有文件保證端到端低於 1 秒。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Nonstreaming model inference and extra synchronous steps delay initial suggestions.","why_zh":"非串流模型推論及額外同步步驟延後初始建議。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Batch transcription waits for complete audio and cannot suggest while the caller speaks.","why_zh":"批次轉錄等待完整音訊，無法在客戶說話時提供建議。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Embedding vectors are not generated textual suggestions, and SNS is not the requested live bidirectional channel.","why_zh":"嵌入向量不是生成文字建議，SNS 也不是所需即時雙向通道。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/streaming-partial-results.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_InvokeModelWithResponseStream.html"],"issues":["model_api_response_stream_only","latency_target_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.059801+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":40,"question_en":"A media company is launching a platform that allows thousands of users every hour to upload images and text content. The platform uses Amazon Bedrock to process the uploaded content to generate creative compositions. The company needs a solution to ensure that the platform does not process or produce inappropriate content. The platform must not expose personally identifiable information (PII) in the compositions. The solution must integrate with the company's existing Amazon S3 storage workflow. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST infrastructure management overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Enable the Enhanced Monitoring tool. Use an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to filter traffic to the platform. Use Amazon Comprehend PII detection to pre-process the data. Create a CloudWatch alarm to monitor for Amazon Comprehend PII detection events. Create an AWS Step Functions workflow that includes an Amazon Rekognition image moderation step.","B":"Use an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with request validation templates to screen content before storing the uploaded content in Amazon S3. Use Amazon SageMaker AI to build custom content moderation models that process content before sending the processed content to Amazon Bedrock.","C":"Create an Amazon Cognito user pool that uses pre-authentication AWS Lambda functions to run content moderation checks. Use Amazon Textract to filter text content and Amazon Rekognition to filter image content before allowing users to upload content to the platform.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow that uses built-in Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use Amazon Comprehend PII detection to pre-process the content. Use Amazon Rekognition image moderation."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":40,"pages":[80,81]},"question_zh":"一家媒體公司即將推出平台，每小時讓數千名使用者上傳影像及文字。平台使用 Amazon Bedrock 處理上傳內容，產生創意作品。公司需要確保平台不處理或產生不當內容，且作品不得洩露個人可識別資訊（PII）。方案必須整合既有 Amazon S3 儲存流程。哪個方案能以最低基礎設施管理負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"啟用 Enhanced Monitoring 工具，使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警示過濾平台流量。使用 Amazon Comprehend PII 偵測前處理資料，建立 CloudWatch 警示監控 PII 偵測事件，並建立含 Amazon Rekognition 影像審核步驟的 AWS Step Functions 工作流程。","B":"使用帶有請求驗證範本的 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API，在內容存入 Amazon S3 前篩選。使用 Amazon SageMaker AI 建立自訂內容審核模型，處理內容後再送至 Amazon Bedrock。","C":"建立 Amazon Cognito 使用者集區，在驗證前 AWS Lambda 函數中執行內容審核。使用 Amazon Textract 過濾文字、Amazon Rekognition 過濾影像，再允許使用者上傳內容。","D":"建立 AWS Step Functions 工作流程，使用內建 Amazon Bedrock 防護機制篩選內容，使用 Amazon Comprehend PII 偵測前處理內容，並使用 Amazon Rekognition 影像審核。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D composes managed orchestration, text safety controls, PII detection and image moderation without hosting custom models. Rekognition detects inappropriate image content; Comprehend PII detection supplies text entity locations for redaction, and Guardrails can filter or mask supported sensitive text. Configure both input and output checks and connect S3 events to the workflow. Detection alone is not redaction, and PII embedded in images needs extraction and appropriate image-redaction handling rather than relying on content-moderation labels.","explanation_zh":"D 結合受管協調、文字安全控制、PII 偵測與影像審核，無須託管自訂模型。Rekognition 偵測不當影像，Comprehend PII 偵測提供文字實體位置供遮蔽，Guardrails 則可篩選或遮罩受支援的敏感文字。應同時設定輸入及輸出檢查，並將 S3 事件連接至流程。偵測本身不等於遮蔽，影像中的 PII 還需要擷取及適當影像遮蔽，不能只依賴內容審核標籤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms do not filter traffic or redact content.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 警示不會過濾流量或遮蔽內容。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Custom moderation models add infrastructure and development work; HTTP API templates are misstated.","why_zh":"自訂審核模型增加基礎設施及開發工作，HTTP API 範本描述也不正確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Authentication occurs separately from individual content uploads, and Textract is extraction rather than safety filtering.","why_zh":"身分驗證與各次內容上傳分離，Textract 用於擷取而非安全篩選。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/moderation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/how-pii.html"],"issues":["image_pii_requires_additional_handling"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.060535+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":41,"question_en":"A company has set up Amazon Q Developer Pro licenses for all developers at the company. The company maintains a list of approved resources that developers must use when developing applications. The approved resources include internal libraries, proprietary algorithmic techniques, and sample code with approved styling. A new team of developers is using Amazon Q Developer to develop a new Java-based application. The company must ensure that the new developer team uses the company's approved resources. The company does not want to make project-level modifications. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a Git repository that contains all of the approved internal libraries, algorithms, and code samples. Include this Git repository in the application project locally as part of the workspace. Ensure that the developers use the @workspace context to retrieve suggestions from the Git repository.","B":"In the project root folder, create a folder named .amazonq/rules. Add the approved internal libraries, algorithms, and code samples to the folder.","C":"Create a folder in the application project named rules. Store the guidelines and code in the folder for Amazon Q Developer to reference product code suggestions.","D":"Create an Amazon Q Developer customization that includes the approved data sources. Ensure that the developers use the customization to develop the application."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":41,"pages":[82,83]},"question_zh":"一家公司已為所有開發人員設定 Amazon Q Developer Pro 授權，並維護一份開發應用程式時必須使用的核准資源清單，包含內部程式庫、專有演算法技巧，以及符合核准風格的範例程式碼。新的開發團隊正在使用 Amazon Q Developer 開發 Java 應用程式。公司必須確保團隊使用核准資源，但不希望進行專案層級修改。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立包含所有核准內部程式庫、演算法及範例的 Git 儲存庫，將它加入本機應用專案工作區，並確保開發人員使用 @workspace 脈絡取得該儲存庫的建議。","B":"在專案根目錄建立 .amazonq/rules 資料夾，加入核准內部程式庫、演算法及範例程式碼。","C":"在應用專案建立名為 rules 的資料夾，儲存指引及程式碼，供 Amazon Q Developer 參考並提供產品程式碼建議。","D":"建立包含核准資料來源的 Amazon Q Developer 自訂項目，並確保開發人員使用該自訂項目開發應用程式。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon Q Developer customizations were designed to tailor inline suggestions to an organization’s repositories and reusable internal patterns. D therefore matches centralized approved-source recommendations without changing each project. Workspace context and project rules require project-local configuration, contrary to the requirement. A customization influences suggestions rather than proving every generated line uses only approved resources; code review and policy checks remain necessary, and this historical feature should be checked for current availability before new deployment.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Q Developer 自訂項目的設計，是依組織儲存庫及可重用內部模式調整行內建議，因此 D 符合集中提供核准來源建議、無須逐一修改專案的需求。工作區脈絡及專案規則都需要專案本機設定，違反題目限制。自訂項目會影響建議，但不能證明每行生成程式只使用核准資源，仍需程式碼審查及政策檢查；新部署也應確認此歷史功能目前是否可用。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adds the repository to each project workspace.","why_zh":"需將儲存庫加入每個專案工作區。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Requires a project-level rules directory and is not centralized repository customization.","why_zh":"需要專案規則目錄，並非集中式儲存庫自訂。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A generic rules folder is not the documented customization mechanism.","why_zh":"一般 rules 資料夾不是官方自訂項目機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/best-practices-code-generation/advanced-capabilities.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/best-practices-code-generation/faq.html"],"issues":["customization_not_absolute_enforcement","historical_feature_availability_check"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.061416+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":42,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is using Amazon Bedrock to build a customer service AI assistant. The AI assistant needs to process over 50,000 customer inquiries every day. The AI assistant occasionally experiences traffic spikes of up to 150,000 inquiries every day during promotional events. Analysis shows that 40% of inquiries follow similar patterns that share the same context. A GenAI developer must design a solution that will ensure low latency and consistent performance for the AI assistant during traffic spikes. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","options_en":{"A":"Configure latency-optimized inference by setting the latency parameter to optimized in the performance configuration of the request to Amazon Bedrock. Use prompt caching to handle the repetitive inquiries.","B":"Purchase provisioned throughput and model units (MUs) that are sized to handle peak traffic loads. Use Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) to cache repetitive inquiries.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Agents and custom knowledge bases to pre-process customer inquiries. Configure cross-Region inference to distribute traffic.","D":"Use AWS Lambda functions to pre-process requests by using a custom prompt routing mechanism. Use Amazon DynamoDB as a caching layer to handle frequently asked questions."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":86,"B":14},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":42,"pages":[84,85]},"question_zh":"一家電子商務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立客服 AI 助理，每天需要處理超過 50,000 個客戶詢問，促銷時偶爾暴增至每日 150,000 個。分析顯示 40% 的詢問具有相似模式並共用相同脈絡。生成式 AI 開發人員必須設計方案，在流量尖峰時確保低延遲及一致效能。哪個方案最具成本效益？","options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Bedrock 請求的效能設定將 latency 參數設為 optimized，啟用延遲最佳化推論，並使用提示快取處理重複詢問。","B":"購買按尖峰流量規模配置的佈建輸送量及模型單位（MU），並使用 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）快取重複詢問。","C":"使用 Amazon Bedrock Agents 及自訂知識庫前處理客戶詢問，並設定跨區域推論分散流量。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數，以自訂提示路由機制前處理請求，並使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作為常見問題快取層。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Prompt caching reuses shared prompt prefixes to reduce repeated input processing and token cost, while latency-optimized inference can accelerate supported model invocations. A avoids reserving peak capacity for occasional spikes and is the best intended cost-oriented choice. Similar questions alone are not cache hits: eligible context prefixes must match and satisfy model token/TTL rules. Optimized mode is model/Region dependent and may fall back to standard latency after its quota is reached, so peak performance still requires quota and workload validation.","explanation_zh":"提示快取重用共用提示前綴，降低重複輸入處理及 token 成本；延遲最佳化推論則可加速受支援模型呼叫。A 不必為偶發尖峰預留全量容量，是題目預期最具成本考量的選擇。不過，相似問題本身不代表快取命中，合格脈絡前綴須相符，並符合模型 token 及 TTL 規則。最佳化模式受模型與區域限制，達配額後可能退回標準延遲，因此仍須驗證尖峰配額及工作負載。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Peak-sized reserved capacity can be underused outside promotions and adds a cache service.","why_zh":"依尖峰配置的預留容量可能在非促銷期閒置，且增加快取服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Agents and knowledge bases add orchestration without directly exploiting repeated prompt context.","why_zh":"代理程式與知識庫增加協調，未直接重用重複提示脈絡。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Requires custom routing and response-cache validity logic.","why_zh":"需自訂路由及回應快取有效性邏輯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-caching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/latency-optimized-inference.html"],"issues":["cache_requires_matching_prefix","optimized_quota_fallback"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.062351+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":43,"question_en":"A legal research company has a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses Amazon Bedrock and Amazon OpenSearch Service. The application stores 768-dimensional vector embeddings for 15 million legal documents, including statutes, court rulings, and case summaries. The company's current chunking strategy segments text into fixed-length blocks of 500 tokens. The current chunking strategy often splits contextually linked information such as legal arguments, court opinions, or statute references across separate chunks. Researchers report that generated outputs frequently omit key context or cite outdated legal information. Recent application logs show a 40% increase in response times. The p95 latency metric exceeds 2 seconds. The company expects storage needs for the application to grow from 90 GB to 360 GB within a year. The company needs a solution to improve retrieval relevance and system performance at scale. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Increase the embedding vector dimensionality from 768 to 4,096 without changing the existing chunking or pre-processing strategy.","B":"Replace dynamic retrieval with static, pre-written summaries that are stored in Amazon S3. Use Amazon CloudFront to serve the summaries to reduce compute demand and improve predictability.","C":"Update the chunking strategy to use semantic boundaries such as complete legal arguments, clauses, or sections rather than fixed token limits. Regenerate vector embeddings to align with the new chunk structure.","D":"Migrate from OpenSearch Service to Amazon DynamoDB. Implement keyword-based indexes to enable faster lookups for legal concepts."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":43,"pages":[86,87]},"question_zh":"一家法律研究公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 及 Amazon OpenSearch Service 建立 RAG 應用程式，為 1,500 萬份法規、法院判決及案例摘要儲存 768 維向量嵌入。目前以 500 token 固定長度分塊，經常將法律論證、法院意見或法條引用等相關內容切到不同區塊。研究人員指出生成輸出常遺漏關鍵脈絡，或引用過時法律資訊。近期日誌顯示回應時間增加 40%，p95 延遲超過 2 秒。公司預期一年內儲存需求將從 90 GB 增至 360 GB，需要改善大規模檢索相關性與效能。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將嵌入維度由 768 增至 4,096，但不改變既有分塊或前處理策略。","B":"以存於 Amazon S3 的靜態預寫摘要取代動態檢索，再透過 Amazon CloudFront 提供摘要，降低運算需求並提高可預測性。","C":"更新分塊策略，以完整法律論證、條款或章節等語意邊界取代固定 token 限制，並依新區塊結構重新產生向量嵌入。","D":"從 OpenSearch Service 移轉至 Amazon DynamoDB，實作關鍵字索引以更快查找法律概念。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Semantic or structure-aware boundaries keep related legal statements together, directly addressing the context fragmentation. Re-embedding and reindexing are necessary because the indexed unit has changed. Larger dimensions alone cannot repair broken context and increase storage and computation. C improves the stated relevance defect, but outdated sources need freshness/version filtering and the capacity/latency problem still requires index and workload tuning.","explanation_zh":"語意或文件結構邊界能將相關法律敘述保留在一起，直接改善脈絡破碎問題。索引單位改變後，必須重新嵌入及建立索引。只增加維度無法修復破碎脈絡，還會增加儲存與運算。C 能改善題目指出的相關性缺陷，但過時來源仍需新鮮度與版本篩選，容量及延遲問題仍須進行索引與負載調校。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"More dimensions increase cost without changing the broken chunk boundaries.","why_zh":"提高維度增加成本，卻未改變有問題的分塊邊界。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Static summaries lose query-specific retrieval and source coverage.","why_zh":"靜態摘要失去查詢專屬檢索與來源涵蓋能力。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keyword indexes do not replace semantic vector retrieval or preserve fragmented arguments.","why_zh":"關鍵字索引不能取代語意向量檢索，也不能修復分散論證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-chunking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-chunking.html"],"issues":["freshness_and_capacity_need_separate_controls"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.063265+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":44,"question_en":"A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI)-powered customer support application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application must maintain conversational context across multiple interactions with the same user. The application must run clarification workflows to handle ambiguous user queries. The company must store encrypted records of each user conversation to use for personalization. The application must be able to handle thousands of concurrent users while responding to each user quickly. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Step Functions Express workflow to orchestrate conversation flow. Invoke AWS Lambda functions to run clarification logic. Store conversation history in Amazon RDS and use session IDs as the primary key.","B":"Use an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow to orchestrate clarification workflows. Include Wait for a Callback patterns to manage the workflows. Store conversation history in Amazon DynamoDPurchase on- demand capacity and configure server-side encryption.","C":"Deploy the application by using an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route user requests to an AWS Lambda function to update and retrieve conversation context. Store conversation history in Amazon S3 and configure server-side encryption. Save each interaction as a separate JSON file.","D":"Use AWS Lambda functions to call Amazon Bedrock inference APIs. Use Amazon SQS queues to orchestrate clarification steps. Store conversation history in an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster. Configure encryption at rest."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":56,"A":33,"D":11},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":44,"pages":[88,89]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在開發使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）的生成式 AI 客服應用程式。應用程式必須在同一使用者的多次互動間維持對話脈絡，執行釐清工作流程以處理模糊查詢，並儲存加密的各使用者對話紀錄供個人化使用。應用程式必須能處理數千名並行使用者，並快速回應。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Step Functions Express 工作流程協調對話流程，呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數執行釐清邏輯，並將對話歷史存於 Amazon RDS，以工作階段 ID 作為主鍵。","B":"使用 AWS Step Functions Standard 工作流程協調釐清流程，加入等待回呼模式來管理流程。將對話歷史存於 Amazon DynamoDPurchase〔原文連字有誤，意指 DynamoDB 並購買〕隨需容量，並設定伺服器端加密。","C":"部署 Amazon API Gateway REST API，將使用者請求路由至 AWS Lambda 函數以更新及取得對話脈絡。將對話歷史存於 Amazon S3 並設定伺服器端加密，各次互動儲存為獨立 JSON 檔案。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 推論 API，以 Amazon SQS 佇列協調釐清步驟，將對話歷史存於 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）叢集，並設定靜態加密。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Standard workflows support durable callback waits for a user clarification, unlike Express workflows. DynamoDB on-demand capacity provides managed scaling for session-keyed conversation records, with encryption at rest. B is the intended design; its merged word DynamoDPurchase is a source typo meaning DynamoDB plus purchase/configure on-demand capacity. Keep user/session authorization and bounded history retrieval in application logic so one session cannot access another user’s context.","explanation_zh":"Standard 工作流程支援耐久回呼等待，可等候使用者釐清，Express 則不支援此模式。DynamoDB 隨需容量能為以工作階段為鍵的對話紀錄提供受管擴展及靜態加密。B 是預期設計；其中 DynamoDPurchase 是原文連字錯誤，意指 DynamoDB 及購買／設定隨需容量。應用程式仍須實作使用者與工作階段授權及有界歷史檢索，避免某工作階段讀取其他使用者脈絡。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Express workflows do not support callback waits, and RDS requires additional capacity management.","why_zh":"Express 不支援回呼等待，RDS 也需額外容量管理。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Per-interaction S3 objects add retrieval orchestration and omit a managed clarification workflow.","why_zh":"逐次 S3 物件增加檢索協調工作，且缺少受管釐清流程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Queues and a cache require custom conversational workflow and durable-history handling.","why_zh":"佇列與快取需自訂對話流程及耐久歷史處理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/choosing-workflow-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/HowItWorks.ReadWriteCapacityMode.html"],"issues":["source_dynamodb_word_merge_typo"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.064357+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧"},{"id":45,"question_en":"A financial services company needs to pre-process unstructured data such as customer transcripts, financial reports, and documentation. The company stores the unstructured data in Amazon S3 to support an Amazon Bedrock application. The company must validate data quality, create auditable metadata, monitor data metrics, and customize text chunking to optimize foundation model (FM) performance. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler to create a data flow. Configure Amazon CloudWatch metrics and alarms to monitor data quality. Use a custom AWS Lambda function to pre-process the data. Load processed data into Amazon Bedrock.","B":"Set up an AWS Glue crawler to catalog data sources. Create AWS Glue ETL jobs to run custom transformation scripts. Use AWS Glue Data Quality to validate and monitor data quality. Load processed data into Amazon Bedrock.","C":"Use Amazon Comprehend to extract entities. Create an AWS Lambda function to chunk text. Run Amazon Athena to query and validate data quality. Load processed data into Amazon Bedrock.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to orchestrate data pre-processing tasks. Run custom code on Amazon EC2 instances to process the data. Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to monitor data quality. Load processed data into Amazon Bedrock."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":45,"pages":[90]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司需要前處理客戶逐字稿、財務報告及文件等非結構化資料，這些資料存於 Amazon S3，以支援 Amazon Bedrock 應用程式。公司必須驗證資料品質、建立可稽核中繼資料、監控資料指標，並自訂文字分塊以最佳化基礎模型（FM）效能。哪個方案能以最少開發工作符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler 建立資料流程，設定 Amazon CloudWatch 指標及警示監控資料品質，使用自訂 AWS Lambda 函數前處理資料，再將處理後資料載入 Amazon Bedrock。","B":"設定 AWS Glue 爬蟲編目資料來源，建立 AWS Glue ETL 作業執行自訂轉換指令碼，使用 AWS Glue Data Quality 驗證及監控資料品質，再將處理後資料載入 Amazon Bedrock。","C":"使用 Amazon Comprehend 擷取實體，建立 AWS Lambda 函數分塊文字，執行 Amazon Athena 查詢及驗證資料品質，再將處理後資料載入 Amazon Bedrock。","D":"建立 AWS Step Functions 工作流程協調資料前處理任務，在 Amazon EC2 執行個體執行自訂資料處理程式，以 Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor 監控資料品質，再將處理後資料載入 Amazon Bedrock。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Glue combines catalog metadata, serverless ETL and Data Quality rule evaluation and monitoring. Custom ETL can normalize documents and implement the required text chunking, while the catalog retains source metadata. Data Quality evaluates structured tables or records, so raw documents must first be parsed into a suitable representation. It does not automatically judge semantic factuality or eliminate the need to write domain-specific transformations.","explanation_zh":"Glue 結合目錄中繼資料、無伺服器 ETL，以及 Data Quality 規則評估與監控。自訂 ETL 可正規化文件並實作所需文字分塊，目錄則保留來源中繼資料。Data Quality 評估的是結構化資料表或紀錄，因此原始文件須先解析為合適表示法。它不會自動判斷語意事實正確性，也不會免除領域專屬轉換程式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Splits cataloging, transformation and quality management across custom components.","why_zh":"將編目、轉換與品質管理拆散至自訂元件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Entity extraction and SQL alone require custom quality and metadata governance logic.","why_zh":"實體擷取及 SQL 仍需自訂品質與中繼資料治理邏輯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 processing and custom orchestration add operational effort; Model Monitor targets deployed model data.","why_zh":"EC2 處理及自訂協調增加維運，Model Monitor 主要監控部署模型資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/data-quality-getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/glue-data-quality.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:56:37.065291+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Bedrock to build a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) system. The RAG system uses an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that is based on an Amazon S3 bucket as the data source for emergency news video content. The system retrieves transcripts, archived reports, and related documents from the S3 bucket. The RAG system uses state-of-the-art embedding models and a high-performing retrieval setup. However, users report slow responses and irrelevant results, which cause decreased user satisfaction. The company notices that vector searches are evaluating too many documents across too many content types and over long periods of time. The company determines that the underlying models will not benefit from additional fine tuning. The company must improve retrieval accuracy by applying smarter constraints. The company wants a solution that requires minimal changes to the existing architecture. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Enhance embeddings by using a domain-adapted model that is specifically trained on emergency news content for improved vector similarity.","B":"Migrate to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Use vector fields and metadata filters to define the scope of results retrieval.","C":"Enable metadata-aware filtering within the Amazon Bedrock knowledge base by indexing S3 object metadata.","D":"Migrate to an Amazon Q Business index to perform structured metadata filtering and document categorization during retrieval."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":88,"B":13},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":46,"pages":[91,92]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 建立 RAG 系統，以 Amazon S3 儲存貯體作為緊急新聞影片內容的知識庫資料來源。系統從 S3 取得逐字稿、封存報告及相關文件，使用先進嵌入模型及高效能檢索設定。但使用者反映回應緩慢且結果不相關，滿意度下降。公司發現向量搜尋評估了過多文件、過多內容類型及過長時間範圍，並判定額外微調無益。公司必須透過更聰明的限制改善檢索準確性，同時盡量少改既有架構。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用專為緊急新聞內容訓練的領域調整模型改善嵌入，提高向量相似性。","B":"移轉至 Amazon OpenSearch Service，使用向量欄位及中繼資料篩選器界定檢索範圍。","C":"在 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫中，透過建立 S3 物件中繼資料索引，啟用具中繼資料感知的篩選。","D":"移轉至 Amazon Q Business 索引，在檢索期間執行結構化中繼資料篩選及文件分類。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Knowledge-base metadata filters can restrict retrieval by content type and date, directly addressing the excessive candidate scope without replacing the architecture. Add suitable metadata attributes and apply them through vectorSearchConfiguration.filter. For ordinary S3 documents, provide the supported companion .metadata.json files and synchronize ingestion; arbitrary S3 object metadata is not automatically a searchable knowledge-base field. C is correct when interpreted as ingesting explicit document metadata rather than merely setting object headers.","explanation_zh":"知識庫中繼資料篩選可依內容類型及日期限制檢索，直接改善候選範圍過大問題，無須更換架構。應加入適當中繼資料屬性，並透過 vectorSearchConfiguration.filter 套用。一般 S3 文件須提供受支援的伴隨 .metadata.json 檔案並同步匯入，任意 S3 物件中繼資料不會自動成為可搜尋知識庫欄位。因此 C 應理解為明確匯入文件中繼資料，而非只設定物件標頭。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The problem is retrieval scope, and the stem rules out further model tuning.","why_zh":"問題在檢索範圍，且題目已排除進一步模型調整效益。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A migration is unnecessary because the existing knowledge base supports filtering.","why_zh":"既有知識庫支援篩選，無須移轉。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Changing retrieval products adds architecture work without addressing a missing capability.","why_zh":"更換檢索產品增加架構工作，而既有產品並未缺少此能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-metadata.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html"],"issues":["s3_metadata_sidecar_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.515111+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":47,"question_en":"A financial services company is creating a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to generate summaries of market activities. The application relies on a vector database that stores a small proprietary dataset that has a low index count. The application must perform similarity searches. The Amazon Bedrock model's responses must maximize accuracy and maintain high performance. The company needs to configure the vector database and integrate it with the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Launch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Flat algorithm. Configure a horizontal scaling policy based on performance metrics.","B":"Launch an Amazon MemoryDB cluster and configure the index by using the Hierarchical Navigable Small World (HNSW) algorithm. Configure a vertical policy based on performance metrics.","C":"Launch an Amazon Aurora PostgresSQL cluster and configure the index by using the Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) algorithm. Configure the instance class to scale to a larger size when the load increases.","D":"Launch an Amazon DocumentDB cluster that has an Inverted File with Flat Compression (IVFFlat) index and a high probe value. Configure connections to the cluster as a replica set Distribute reads to replica instances."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":67,"B":33},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":47,"pages":[93,94]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司建立使用 Amazon Bedrock 的 RAG 應用程式，產生市場活動摘要。應用程式依賴向量資料庫，儲存小型專有資料集，索引數量也低。應用程式必須執行相似度搜尋，讓 Amazon Bedrock 模型回應盡可能準確並維持高效能。公司需要設定向量資料庫並整合至應用程式。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"啟動 Amazon MemoryDB 叢集，以 Flat 演算法設定索引，並依效能指標設定水平擴展政策。","B":"啟動 Amazon MemoryDB 叢集，以階層式可導航小世界（HNSW）演算法設定索引，並依效能指標設定垂直擴展政策。","C":"啟動 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 叢集，以倒排檔案平面壓縮（IVFFlat）演算法設定索引，並在負載增加時將執行個體類別擴展至較大規格。","D":"啟動具有 IVFFlat 索引及高 probe 值的 Amazon DocumentDB 叢集。將叢集連線設定為複本集，並將讀取分散至複本執行個體。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"MemoryDB FLAT scans all indexed vectors and returns exact nearest neighbors within numeric precision, which suits a small dataset prioritizing recall. HNSW and IVFFlat trade search completeness for speed and are more useful when exact scans become costly. Thus A best matches the dataset characteristics. Exact retrieval does not guarantee factual model responses, and the unspecified horizontal scaling policy needs a supported cluster-scaling implementation and workload validation.","explanation_zh":"MemoryDB FLAT 掃描所有索引向量，在數值精度範圍內回傳精確最近鄰，適合重視召回的小型資料集。HNSW 及 IVFFlat 以搜尋完整性換取速度，較適用於精確掃描成本高的情況，因此 A 最符合資料集特性。精確檢索不保證模型回應事實正確，未具體描述的水平擴展政策也需要受支援的叢集擴展實作及負載驗證。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Approximate HNSW is not needed to maximize recall on a small index.","why_zh":"小型索引若以最高召回為目標，無須採近似 HNSW。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IVFFlat introduces approximate-search tuning despite the small dataset.","why_zh":"小型資料集採 IVFFlat 反而增加近似搜尋調校。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"High probes increase work without providing a simpler exact-search choice.","why_zh":"高 probe 增加工作，並未提供更簡單的精確搜尋方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/vector-search-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/vector-search-overview.html"],"issues":["scaling_policy_unspecified"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.516142+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":48,"question_en":"A GenAI developer is building a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)-based customer support application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application needs to process 50 GB of historical customer conversations that are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket as JSON files. The application must use the processed data as its retrieval corpus. The application's data processing workflow must extract relevant data from customer support documents, remove customer personally identifiable information (PII), and generate embeddings for vector storage. The processing workflow must be cost-effective and must finish within 4 hours. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lambda and Amazon Comprehend to process files in parallel, remove PII, and call Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Configure Lambda concurrency limits and memory settings to optimize throughput.","B":"Create an AWS Glue ETL job to run PII detection scripts on the data. Use Amazon SageMaker Processing to run the HuggingFaceProcessor to generate embeddings by using a pre-trained model. Store the embeddings in Amazon OpenSearch Service.","C":"Deploy an Amazon EMR cluster that runs Apache Spark with user-defined functions (UDFs) that call Amazon Comprehend to detect PII. Use Amazon Bedrock APIs to generate vectors. Store outputs in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension.","D":"Implement a data processing pipeline that uses AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workload that uses Amazon Comprehend to detect PII and Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings. Directly integrate the workflow with Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to store vectors and provide similarity search capabilities."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":79,"B":14,"A":7},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":48,"pages":[95,96]},"question_zh":"一名生成式 AI 開發人員正在使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）建立 RAG 客服應用程式。應用程式需要處理存於 Amazon S3、JSON 格式的 50 GB 歷史客戶對話，並以處理後資料作為檢索語料。處理流程必須從客服文件擷取相關資料、移除客戶 PII，並產生向量儲存用嵌入。流程必須具成本效益，並在 4 小時內完成。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 及 Amazon Comprehend 平行處理檔案、移除 PII，並呼叫 Amazon Bedrock API 產生向量。設定 Lambda 並行限制及記憶體以最佳化輸送量。","B":"建立 AWS Glue ETL 作業，在資料上執行 PII 偵測指令碼。使用 Amazon SageMaker Processing 的 HuggingFaceProcessor，以預先訓練模型產生嵌入，並存至 Amazon OpenSearch Service。","C":"部署執行 Apache Spark 的 Amazon EMR 叢集，以使用者定義函數（UDF）呼叫 Amazon Comprehend 偵測 PII。使用 Amazon Bedrock API 產生向量，並將輸出存於具有 pgvector 擴充套件的 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL。","D":"實作資料處理管線，使用 AWS Step Functions 協調 Amazon Comprehend PII 偵測及 Amazon Bedrock 嵌入生成。直接整合 Amazon OpenSearch Serverless，儲存向量並提供相似度搜尋。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D is the intended managed pipeline: workflow orchestration, managed PII analysis, Bedrock embeddings and serverless vector storage. Large files must be partitioned and processed with bounded concurrency, and detected PII must actually be redacted before embedding. The Step Functions OpenSearch Serverless SDK integration exposes service APIs, not a turnkey vector-document bulk writer; collection data-plane indexing still needs an authenticated integration or adapter. Neither D nor A proves the four-hour target without token volume, service quotas and throughput measurements.","explanation_zh":"D 是題目預期的受管管線：工作流程協調、受管 PII 分析、Bedrock 嵌入及無伺服器向量儲存。大型檔案必須切分並以受限並行度處理，偵測到的 PII 也須在嵌入前實際遮蔽。Step Functions 的 OpenSearch Serverless SDK 整合提供服務 API，並非可直接使用的向量文件批次寫入器；集合資料平面索引仍需具驗證能力的整合或轉接程式。缺少 token 量、服務配額及輸送量實測時，D 與 A 都無法證明 4 小時達標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Also feasible and serverless, but leaves durable coordination, vector storage and retries to application code.","why_zh":"同樣可行且無伺服器，但耐久協調、向量儲存及重試留給應用程式實作。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adds a separate embedding processing service and custom ETL/model management.","why_zh":"增加獨立嵌入處理服務及自訂 ETL、模型管理。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EMR and Aurora introduce cluster/database operations beyond the managed serverless design.","why_zh":"EMR 及 Aurora 增加受管無伺服器設計之外的叢集與資料庫維運。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/supported-services-awssdk.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/serverless-vector-search.html"],"issues":["direct_vector_write_adapter_required","four_hour_target_unproven"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.517453+00:00"},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":49,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application that serves both premium customers and standard customers. The application uses AWS Lambda functions behind an Amazon API Gateway REST API to process requests. The company needs to dynamically switch between AI models based on which customer tier each user belongs to. The company also wants to perform A/B testing for new features without redeploying code. The company needs to validate model parameters like temperature and maximum token limits before applying changes. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameters for each configuration. Use Lambda functions to poll for parameter updates. Use Amazon EventBridge events to trigger redeployments when configurations change.","B":"Store model configurations in Amazon DynamoDB tables. Optimize access patterns to retrieve configurations according to customer tier. Configure Lambda functions to query DynamoDB at the beginning of each request to determine which model to use.","C":"Use AWS AppConfig to manage model configurations. Use feature flags to perform A/B testing. Define JSON schema validation rules for model parameters. Configure Lambda functions to retrieve configurations by using the AWS AppConfig Agent.","D":"Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster to store model configurations. Set short TTL values. Run custom validation logic in Lambda functions. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor configuration usage."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":49,"pages":[97]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司開發同時服務高階及一般客戶的生成式 AI 應用程式，以 Amazon API Gateway REST API 後方的 AWS Lambda 函數處理請求。公司需要依使用者客戶等級動態切換 AI 模型，也希望無須重新部署程式碼即可對新功能進行 A/B 測試，並在套用變更前驗證 temperature、最大 token 限制等模型參數。哪個方案能以最低維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為各設定建立 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 參數。以 Lambda 函數輪詢更新，並透過 Amazon EventBridge 事件在設定改變時觸發重新部署。","B":"將模型設定存於 Amazon DynamoDB 資料表，最佳化依客戶等級取得設定的存取模式，並讓 Lambda 函數在每次請求開始時查詢 DynamoDB，以決定使用的模型。","C":"使用 AWS AppConfig 管理模型設定，以功能旗標進行 A/B 測試，為模型參數定義 JSON 結構描述驗證規則，並讓 Lambda 函數透過 AWS AppConfig Agent 取得設定。","D":"建立 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）叢集儲存模型設定，設定短 TTL，在 Lambda 函數執行自訂驗證邏輯，並以 Amazon CloudWatch 指標監控設定用量。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AppConfig supports dynamic configuration deployment, feature-flag variants evaluated against request context, and validators before deployment. Lambda can retrieve cached configuration through the AppConfig Agent extension, avoiding per-request custom polling. Use validated free-form configuration for model parameter schemas and feature-flag attributes/variants for tier or experiment selection. Custom JSON Schema validators apply to free-form profiles; feature flags have their own built-in schema and may use Lambda validators for additional semantics.","explanation_zh":"AppConfig 支援動態設定部署、依請求脈絡評估的功能旗標變體，以及部署前驗證器。Lambda 可透過 AppConfig Agent 擴充功能取得快取設定，避免每次請求自訂輪詢。模型參數結構可使用經驗證的自由格式設定，客戶等級或實驗選擇則使用功能旗標屬性及變體。自訂 JSON Schema 驗證器適用於自由格式設定檔；功能旗標有自身內建結構，額外語意可使用 Lambda 驗證器。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Polling and redeployment conflict with the low-overhead dynamic configuration requirement.","why_zh":"輪詢及重新部署不符合低負擔動態設定需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Stores values but requires custom validation, rollout and experiment assignment.","why_zh":"可儲存值，但仍需自訂驗證、推出及實驗分配。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adds cache infrastructure and custom validation without managed configuration deployment.","why_zh":"增加快取基礎設施及自訂驗證，卻沒有受管設定部署。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-code-samples-agent-read-feature-flag-with-variants.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-creating-configuration-and-profile-validators.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.519230+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Bedrock and Anthropic Claude 3 Haiku to develop an AI assistant. The AI assistant normally processes 10,000 requests each hour but experiences surges of up 30,000 requests each hour during peak usage periods. The AI assistant must respond within 2 seconds while operating across multiple AWS Regions. The company observes that during peak usage periods, the AI assistant experiences throughput bottlenecks that cause increased latency and occasional request timeouts. The company must resolve the performance issues. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Purchase provisioned throughput and sufficient model units (MUs) in a single Region. Configure the application to retry failed requests with exponential backoff.","B":"Implement token batching to reduce API overhead. Use cross-Region inference profiles to automatically distribute traffic across available Regions.","C":"Set up auto scaling AWS Lambda functions in each Region. Implement client-side round-robin request distribution. Purchase one model unit (MU) of provisioned throughput as a backup.","D":"Implement batch inference for all requests by using Amazon S3 buckets across multiple Regions. Use Amazon SQS to set up an asynchronous retrieval process."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":50,"pages":[98]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 及 Anthropic Claude 3 Haiku 開發 AI 助理，平常每小時處理 10,000 個請求，尖峰時可增至每小時 30,000 個。助理必須跨多個 AWS 區域運作，並在 2 秒內回應。公司發現尖峰時輸送量瓶頸造成延遲增加及偶發請求逾時，必須解決效能問題。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在單一區域購買佈建輸送量及足夠模型單位（MU），並設定應用程式以指數退避重試失敗請求。","B":"實作 token 批次處理以降低 API 額外負擔，並使用跨區域推論設定檔，自動將流量分散至可用區域。","C":"在各區域設定自動擴展的 AWS Lambda 函數，實作用戶端循環輪詢分流，並購買一個佈建輸送量模型單位（MU）作為備援。","D":"使用跨多區域的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，為所有請求實作批次推論，再以 Amazon SQS 建立非同步結果取得流程。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Cross-Region inference profiles route requests across supported Regions and can relieve regional on-demand capacity pressure, making B the intended architecture. The term token batching is not a general Bedrock online-inference switch, and delaying requests to form batches may worsen interactive latency. Cross-Region profiles do not use Provisioned Throughput and do not guarantee two-second responses. The named Claude 3 Haiku model card also lists an end-of-life date, so a current deployment must select an available supported successor and verify its profiles and quotas.","explanation_zh":"跨區域推論設定檔會在受支援區域間路由請求，可緩解區域隨需容量壓力，因此 B 是題目預期架構。Token 批次處理並非 Bedrock 線上推論的通用開關，等待湊批也可能增加互動延遲。跨區域設定檔不使用佈建輸送量，也不保證 2 秒回應。題目指定的 Claude 3 Haiku 模型卡亦列有生命週期終止日期，因此現行部署必須選擇仍可用的受支援後繼模型，並核對設定檔及配額。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Single-Region capacity does not meet the multi-Region design and retries add latency.","why_zh":"單區域容量不符合多區域設計，重試也增加延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Lambda scaling does not increase model capacity, and one unspecified MU does not prove backup capacity.","why_zh":"Lambda 擴展不會增加模型容量，未定義的一個 MU 也不能證明備援充足。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Asynchronous batch inference does not meet interactive two-second responses.","why_zh":"非同步批次推論不符合 2 秒互動回應。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-anthropic-claude-3-haiku.html"],"issues":["token_batching_undefined","latency_target_not_guaranteed","named_model_lifecycle"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.520338+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":51,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Bedrock to develop an AI assistant to provide customer support. Analysis shows that 40% of customer queries use varied phrasing or wording to ask the same questions. The company wants a solution to reduce redundant model calls. The solution must ensure that semantically equivalent questions receive consistent answers. The solution must ensure low latency. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster as an in-memory cache. Specify the query text as the partition key and the model response text as the sort key. Query the cache by using a filter expression with the LIKE operator.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock to generate embeddings from customer queries. Use Amazon MemoryDB for Valkey to store hash sets of vector embeddings and model responses. Use a RANGE query to find similar queries and their responses.","C":"Deploy Amazon OpenSearch Service that has k-nearest neighbor (k-NN) capabilities to store query- response text pairs. Use an approximate k-NN technique to find similar queries and their responses.","D":"Create a caching solution by using Amazon DynamoDB to create a global secondary index on the normalized query text. Apply stemming to incoming queries. Query the index of cached customer queries."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":51,"pages":[100]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 開發客服 AI 助理。分析顯示 40% 客戶查詢以不同措辭詢問相同問題。公司希望減少重複模型呼叫，確保語意相同問題得到一致答案，並維持低延遲。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"部署 Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator（DAX）叢集作為記憶體快取，以查詢文字為分割區鍵、模型回應文字為排序鍵，並使用帶 LIKE 運算子的篩選運算式查詢快取。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 為客戶查詢產生嵌入。使用 Amazon MemoryDB for Valkey 儲存向量嵌入及模型回應的雜湊集合，並使用 RANGE 查詢找出相似查詢及回應。","C":"部署具 k 最近鄰（k-NN）能力的 Amazon OpenSearch Service，儲存查詢與回應文字配對，並使用近似 k-NN 技術找出相似查詢及回應。","D":"使用 Amazon DynamoDB 建立快取，為正規化查詢文字建立全域次要索引。對傳入查詢進行詞幹化，再查詢已快取的客戶查詢索引。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"OpenSearch k-NN can implement a semantic response cache when query embeddings are indexed alongside responses and incoming embeddings are compared against a calibrated similarity threshold. Cache keys must also include relevant user context, policy/model version and freshness constraints. However, current MemoryDB documentation explicitly supports Valkey vector indexes and VECTOR_RANGE queries over HASH or JSON records, so B is also technically viable when RANGE means VECTOR_RANGE. C remains a valid marked answer, but the options do not establish a unique winner; ordinary numeric RANGE alone would not be semantic search.","explanation_zh":"OpenSearch k-NN 可建立語意回應快取：將查詢嵌入與回應一同索引，再以校準過的相似度門檻比對新查詢嵌入。快取鍵也必須包含相關使用者脈絡、政策／模型版本及新鮮度限制。不過，目前 MemoryDB 文件明確支援 Valkey 向量索引，以及 HASH 或 JSON 紀錄的 VECTOR_RANGE 查詢，因此若 B 的 RANGE 指 VECTOR_RANGE，B 在技術上也可行。C 仍是有效標答，但選項無法確立唯一最佳答案；一般數值 RANGE 本身則不是語意搜尋。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DynamoDB filter expressions do not provide SQL LIKE or semantic vector matching.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 篩選運算式不提供 SQL LIKE 或語意向量比對。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Viable with a vector index and VECTOR_RANGE; not a sound distractor under current documentation.","why_zh":"搭配向量索引及 VECTOR_RANGE 即可行，依目前文件不能視為明確錯選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Stemming and exact normalized-key lookup do not capture arbitrary semantic paraphrases.","why_zh":"詞幹化及正規化鍵的精確查詢無法涵蓋任意語意改寫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/vector-search-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/memorydb/latest/devguide/vector-search-overview.html"],"issues":["memorydb_vector_range_also_supported","no_unique_answer"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.521176+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":52,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Lambda functions to build an AI agent solution. A GenAI developer must set up a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that accesses user information. The GenAI developer must also configure the AI agent to use the new MCP server. The GenAI developer must ensure that only authorized users can access the MCP server. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent's MCP client to invoke the MCP server asynchronously.","B":"Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Grant the AI agent Lambda functions permission to invoke the Lambda function that hosts the MCP server. Configure the AI agent to use the STDIO transport with the MCP server.","C":"Use a Lambda function to host the MCP server. Create an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that proxies requests to the Lambda function. Configure the AI agent solution to use the Streamable HTTP transport to make requests through the HTTP API. Use Amazon Cognito to enforce OAuth 2.1.","D":"Use a Lambda layer to host the MCP server. Add the Lambda layer to the AI agent Lambda functions. Configure the agentic AI solution to use the STDIO transport to send requests to the MCP server. In the AI agent's MCP configuration, specify the Lambda layer ARN as the command. Specify the user credentials as environment variables."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Agents"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":52,"pages":[101,102]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Lambda 函數建立 AI 代理程式方案。生成式 AI 開發人員必須設定可存取使用者資訊的模型脈絡協定（MCP）伺服器，並設定代理程式使用新伺服器，同時確保只有獲授權使用者可以存取。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Lambda 函數託管 MCP 伺服器，授予 AI 代理程式 Lambda 函數呼叫此函數的權限，並將代理程式的 MCP 用戶端設為非同步呼叫 MCP 伺服器。","B":"使用 Lambda 函數託管 MCP 伺服器，授予 AI 代理程式 Lambda 函數呼叫此函數的權限，並將代理程式設為透過 STDIO 傳輸與伺服器通訊。","C":"使用 Lambda 函數託管 MCP 伺服器，建立 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API，將請求代理至 Lambda。將代理程式設為透過 HTTP API 使用 Streamable HTTP 傳輸，並使用 Amazon Cognito 強制 OAuth 2.1。","D":"使用 Lambda 層託管 MCP 伺服器，將此層加入 AI 代理程式 Lambda 函數，並使用 STDIO 傳輸向伺服器送出請求。在 MCP 設定將 Lambda 層 ARN 指定為命令，並將使用者憑證指定為環境變數。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C provides the suitable remote HTTP endpoint plus user-token authorization, unlike process-local STDIO or asynchronous Lambda invocation. Configure an HTTP API JWT authorizer with issuer, audience and scopes, and enforce user-level data authorization in the server. Cognito documentation describes OAuth 2.0; the application must configure the protections and discovery behavior required by the MCP authorization profile rather than assume a generic OAuth 2.1 switch. Lambda/HTTP API deployments should use a compatible stateless Streamable HTTP mode or explicitly support required streaming/session behavior.","explanation_zh":"C 提供適合遠端使用的 HTTP 端點及使用者 token 授權，不同於行程本機 STDIO 或非同步 Lambda 呼叫。應設定 HTTP API JWT 授權器的簽發者、受眾及範圍，並在伺服器強制使用者層級資料授權。Cognito 文件描述的是 OAuth 2.0，應用程式必須設定 MCP 授權規範要求的保護及探索行為，不能假設存在通用 OAuth 2.1 開關。Lambda／HTTP API 部署應使用相容的無狀態 Streamable HTTP 模式，或明確支援所需串流與工作階段行為。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Asynchronous invocation does not provide the normal MCP request/response transport or end-user authorization.","why_zh":"非同步呼叫不提供一般 MCP 請求／回應傳輸，也不實作終端使用者授權。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"STDIO connects local processes rather than separate Lambda services.","why_zh":"STDIO 連接本機行程，並非獨立 Lambda 服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A layer ARN is not an executable STDIO command, and embedded credentials are not user authorization.","why_zh":"層 ARN 不是可執行的 STDIO 命令，內嵌憑證也不是使用者授權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/solutions/latest/distributed-load-testing-on-aws/MCP-Server.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-accessing-resources-api-gateway-and-lambda.html"],"issues":["oauth21_wording_requires_explicit_controls","streamable_http_deployment_constraints"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.521956+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company wants to create an annual rewards program for its customers. The rewards that customers earn vary based on different parameters such as the categories of the items ordered and the customers' purchase history. The company needs a generative AI (GenAI) solution that uses three Amazon Bedrock agents to help customers during online catalog browsing. The agents must use knowledge bases and action groups to handle the search, recommendation, and order modules. The modules must operate sequentially. An AWS Lambda function must calculate estimated rewards for each recommended item. The solution must provide graceful degradation during service disruptions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","options_en":{"A":"Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind each agent. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Configure the second Lambda function with a retry/fallback mechanism.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with four tasks that run the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for each of the task steps.","C":"Configure each agent with a separate retry/fallback mechanism. Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Define an Amazon API Gateway REST API behind the second Lambda function.","D":"Create a second Lambda function to orchestrate the calls to the agents and the rewards Lambda function. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine with one task that runs the second Lambda function. Set up retry and catch branches for the task step."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":80,"C":20},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":53,"pages":[103,104]},"question_zh":"一家公司想建立年度客戶獎勵計畫，獎勵依訂購品項類別及購買歷史等參數而異。公司需要生成式 AI 方案，使用三個 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式，在客戶瀏覽線上目錄時提供協助。代理程式必須透過知識庫及動作群組處理搜尋、推薦與訂單模組，且模組須依序執行。AWS Lambda 函數必須計算各推薦品項的預估獎勵，方案也必須在服務中斷時優雅降級。哪個方案最具維運效率？","options_zh":{"A":"在每個代理程式後方定義 Amazon API Gateway REST API。建立第二個 Lambda 函數協調代理程式與獎勵 Lambda 的呼叫，並為第二個函數設定重試／後備機制。","B":"建立包含四個任務的 AWS Step Functions 狀態機，執行代理程式及獎勵 Lambda 函數，並為各任務步驟設定 retry 及 catch 分支。","C":"為各代理程式設定獨立重試／後備機制。建立第二個 Lambda 函數協調代理程式及獎勵 Lambda 呼叫，並在第二個函數後方定義 Amazon API Gateway REST API。","D":"建立第二個 Lambda 函數協調代理程式及獎勵 Lambda 呼叫。建立只有一項任務的 AWS Step Functions 狀態機來執行第二個函數，並為該任務設定 retry 及 catch 分支。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Four explicit workflow tasks make sequencing, per-step retries, catches and fallback paths visible and independently manageable. This avoids placing all orchestration in a single Lambda function and retrying already completed steps together. Agent invocation can be wrapped in Lambda because the Step Functions AWS SDK integration does not support InvokeAgent directly. Fallback branches must actually define safe degraded behavior, and order/reward side effects should be idempotent under retries.","explanation_zh":"四個明確工作流程任務讓循序執行、各步重試、錯誤攔截及後備路徑可見，且可個別管理，避免將所有協調塞入單一 Lambda 並一起重跑已完成步驟。代理程式呼叫可用 Lambda 包裝，因 Step Functions AWS SDK 整合不直接支援 InvokeAgent。後備分支仍須實際定義安全降級行為，訂單及獎勵副作用也應在重試時保持冪等。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adds per-agent APIs and custom orchestration code.","why_zh":"增加各代理程式 API 及自訂協調程式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Distributes error handling and orchestration across custom components.","why_zh":"將錯誤處理與協調分散於自訂元件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"One opaque task loses per-agent retry and fallback granularity.","why_zh":"單一不透明任務失去各代理程式的重試及後備粒度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/concepts-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/supported-services-awssdk.html"],"issues":["invokeagent_requires_adapter"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.522899+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":54,"question_en":"A company is creating a workflow to review customer-facing communications before the company sends the communications. The company uses a pre-defined message template to generate the communications and stores the communications in an Amazon S3 bucket. The workflow needs to capture a specific portion from the template and send it to an Amazon Bedrock model. The workflow must store model responses back to the original S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a flow in Amazon Bedrock Flows. Configure S3 action nodes at the beginning and end of the flow to retrieve and store the communications and the model responses. In the middle of the flow, configure an expression to parse each communication. Configure an agent step to send the parsed input to the model for review.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow state machine. Use an Amazon S3 integration GetObject step to retrieve the original communications. Use an intrinsic function Pass step to parse the communications and to pass the results to an Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel step. Configure an Amazon S3 integration PutObject step to store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has an action group. Configure instructions to define how the agent should parse the communications. Configure the action group to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon Bedrock agent that has a single action group. Configure three AWS Lambda functions in the action group. Configure the functions to retrieve the communications from the S3 bucket, parse the communications and invoke the Amazon Bedrock model, and store the model responses back to the S3 bucket."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":50,"B":50},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":54,"pages":[105,106]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在建立流程，在寄出面向客戶的通訊前進行審查。公司使用預定訊息範本產生通訊，並將內容存於 Amazon S3 儲存貯體。流程需要擷取範本中特定部分，送至 Amazon Bedrock 模型，並將模型回應存回原 S3 儲存貯體。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Bedrock Flows 建立流程，在起點及終點設定 S3 動作節點以取得及儲存通訊與模型回應。在流程中間設定運算式解析各通訊，再設定代理程式步驟，將解析輸入送至模型審查。","B":"建立 AWS Step Functions Express 狀態機。使用 Amazon S3 整合 GetObject 步驟取得原始通訊，以包含內建函數的 Pass 步驟解析通訊，將結果傳至 Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel 步驟，再使用 Amazon S3 整合 PutObject 步驟將模型回應存回儲存貯體。","C":"建立具有動作群組的 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式，以指示定義解析通訊的方法。設定動作群組從 S3 取得通訊、呼叫 Bedrock 模型，並將回應存回 S3。","D":"建立只有一個動作群組的 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式，在群組中設定三個 Lambda 函數，分別取得 S3 通訊、解析通訊並呼叫 Bedrock 模型，以及將模型回應存回 S3。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B expresses the deterministic sequence directly with managed service integrations and a lightweight transformation step. Step Functions supports S3 SDK operations and Bedrock InvokeModel, while Pass-state intrinsics can parse simple predictable template structures. Keep the object and intermediate payloads within state limits and use JSONPath for intrinsic functions. Complex template parsing would require JSONata or a small parsing function rather than assuming arbitrary parsing is supported by intrinsics.","explanation_zh":"B 以受管服務整合及輕量轉換步驟直接表達確定的循序流程。Step Functions 支援 S3 SDK 操作及 Bedrock InvokeModel，Pass 狀態內建函數可解析簡單、可預期的範本結構。物件及中間承載必須符合狀態大小限制，內建函數也需使用 JSONPath。複雜範本解析則需要 JSONata 或小型解析函數，不能假設內建函數支援任意解析。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An agent step adds unnecessary reasoning and setup for a fixed extraction-and-review sequence.","why_zh":"對固定擷取及審查流程而言，代理程式步驟增加不必要推理及設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Agent-driven parsing is less deterministic and adds orchestration beyond the fixed workflow.","why_zh":"由代理程式決定解析較不確定，且在固定流程外增加協調。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An action group has one executor; three separate Lambda executors cannot be configured as stated.","why_zh":"一個動作群組只有一個執行器，不能依描述設定三個獨立 Lambda 執行器。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/supported-services-awssdk.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/intrinsic-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent_ActionGroupExecutor.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.523632+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識"},{"id":55,"question_en":"A financial technology company is using Amazon Bedrock to build an assessment system for the company's customer service AI assistant. The AI assistant must provide financial recommendations that are factually accurate, compliant with financial regulations, and conversationally appropriate. The company needs to combine automated quality evaluations at scale with targeted human reviews of critical interactions. What solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure a pipeline in which financial experts manually score all responses for accuracy, compliance, and conversational quality. Use Amazon SageMaker notebooks to analyze results to identify improvement areas.","B":"Configure Amazon Bedrock evaluations that use Anthropic Claude Sonnet as a judge model to assess response accuracy and appropriateness. Configure custom Amazon Bedrock guardrails to check responses for compliance with financial policies. Add Amazon Augmented AI (Amazon A2I) human reviews for flagged critical interactions.","C":"Create an Amazon Lex bot to manage the customer service interactions. Configure AWS Lambda functions to check responses against a static compliance database. Configure intents in the bot that call the Lambda functions to check the responses. Add an additional intent to collect end-user reviews.","D":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch to monitor response patterns from the AI assistant. Configure CloudWatch alerts for potential compliance violations. Establish a team of human evaluators to review flagged interactions."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":55,"pages":[107,108]},"question_zh":"一家金融科技公司使用 Amazon Bedrock，為客服 AI 助理建立評估系統。助理必須提供事實準確、符合法規，且對話方式恰當的金融建議。公司需要結合大規模自動品質評估，以及對關鍵互動的針對性人工審查。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定管線，由金融專家手動為所有回應的準確性、合規性及對話品質評分，再使用 Amazon SageMaker 筆記本分析結果，找出改善面向。","B":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 評估，以 Anthropic Claude Sonnet 作為評判模型，評估回應準確性與適切性。設定自訂 Bedrock 防護機制，依金融政策檢查回應，並為標記的關鍵互動加入 Amazon Augmented AI（Amazon A2I）人工審查。","C":"建立 Amazon Lex 機器人管理客服互動，設定 AWS Lambda 函數對照靜態合規資料庫檢查回應。在機器人設定會呼叫函數檢查回應的意圖，並加入額外意圖收集終端使用者評價。","D":"設定 Amazon CloudWatch 監控 AI 助理回應模式，為潛在合規違規設定警示，並建立人工評估團隊審查標記互動。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Bedrock model-as-a-judge evaluation supports scalable quality scoring with custom rubrics, and an A2I custom task can send selected interactions to human experts. This combination matches automated breadth plus targeted expert review. Guardrails implement configured policies but do not independently certify regulatory compliance; expert-defined criteria and evidence are still necessary. Use a supported specific judge-model version, implement A2I routing and worker templates, and check current A2I availability because it is no longer open to new customers.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock 模型評判評估支援以自訂評分規準大規模評分，A2I 自訂任務則可將選定互動交給專家人工審查，符合廣泛自動評估加上針對性專家覆核的需求。Guardrails 執行設定的政策，但不能獨立證明法規合規，仍需專家定義準則與證據。應選擇受支援的特定評判模型版本，實作 A2I 路由及工作者範本，並確認 A2I 目前可用性，因其已不開放新客戶。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Manual scoring of every response does not provide scalable automated evaluation.","why_zh":"每個回應都人工評分，不提供可擴展自動評估。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Static checks and user feedback are not a comprehensive expert-calibrated quality evaluation.","why_zh":"靜態檢查與使用者回饋不是完整且經專家校準的品質評估。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch does not automatically judge factual accuracy or conversational appropriateness.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 不會自動判斷事實正確性或對話適切性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/a2i-task-types-custom.html"],"issues":["guardrails_not_regulatory_certification","a2i_current_availability"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:02:02.524447+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":56,"question_en":"A healthcare company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a real-time patient care AI assistant to respond to queries for separate departments that handle clinical inquiries, insurance verification, appointment scheduling, and insurance claims. The company wants to use a multi-agent architecture. The company must ensure that the AI assistant is scalable and can onboard new features for patients. The AI assistant must be able to handle thousands of parallel patient interactions. The company must ensure that patients receive appropriate domain-specific responses to queries. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Isolate data for each agent by using separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a supervisor agent to perform natural language intent classification on patient inquiries. Configure the supervisor agent to route queries to specialized collaborator agents to respond to department-specific queries. Configure each specialized collaborator agent to use Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with the agent's department-specific knowledge base.","B":"Create a separate supervisor agent for each department. Configure individual collaborator agents to perform natural language intent classification for each specialty domain within each department. Integrate each collaborator agent with department-specific knowledge bases only. Implement manual handoff processes between the supervisor agents.","C":"Isolate data for each department in separate knowledge bases. Use IAM filtering to control access to each knowledge base. Deploy a single general-purpose agent. Configure multiple action groups within the general-purpose agent to perform specific department functions. Implement rule-based routing logic within the general-purpose agent instructions.","D":"Implement multiple independent supervisor agents that run in parallel to respond to patient inquiries for each department. Configure multiple collaborator agents for each supervisor agent. Integrate all agents with the same knowledge base. Use external routing logic to merge responses from multiple supervisor agents."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":56,"pages":[109,110]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 開發即時病患照護 AI 助理，回答分別負責臨床諮詢、保險資格驗證、預約排程及保險理賠的各部門問題。公司希望採用多代理架構，確保助理可擴展並能為病患加入新功能。助理必須處理數千個平行病患互動，並提供適切的領域專屬回答。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"以個別知識庫隔離每個代理的資料，使用 IAM 篩選控制各知識庫存取。部署監督代理，對病患問題進行自然語言意圖分類，並將查詢路由至專門的協作代理回答部門專屬問題。讓每個協作代理使用其部門專屬知識庫進行檢索增強生成（RAG）。","B":"為每個部門建立個別監督代理。設定各協作代理，對部門內各專業領域進行自然語言意圖分類，且只整合部門專屬知識庫。在監督代理之間實作人工交接流程。","C":"將各部門資料隔離於不同知識庫，以 IAM 篩選控制存取。部署單一通用代理，在其中設定多個動作群組執行特定部門功能，並在代理指示內實作規則式路由邏輯。","D":"實作多個平行執行的獨立監督代理，回答各部門的病患問題。為每個監督代理設定多個協作代理，讓所有代理整合同一個知識庫，並使用外部路由邏輯合併多個監督代理的回應。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A matches Bedrock multi-agent collaboration: a supervisor can route to specialized collaborators, each with its own knowledge base. Separate IAM-authorized resources support department boundaries; IAM is an authorization policy mechanism, not an automatic document filter. Thousands of parallel sessions still require checking model and agent quotas and load testing. Routing and domain specialization do not by themselves guarantee clinical correctness.","explanation_zh":"A 符合 Bedrock 多代理協作：監督代理可將問題導向專業協作代理，各自連接知識庫。不同資源配合 IAM 授權能支援部門隔離；IAM 是權限政策機制，不是自動文件篩選器。數千個平行工作階段仍須確認模型與代理配額並做負載測試。路由與領域分工本身不保證臨床答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manual inter-supervisor handoffs impede a scalable unified workflow.","why_zh":"監督代理之間人工交接不利於可擴展的統一流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single agent with action groups does not implement the requested multi-agent architecture.","why_zh":"單一代理搭配動作群組並未實作要求的多代理架構。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Shared data and external result merging add complexity and weaken the stated departmental separation.","why_zh":"共用資料及外部合併結果增加複雜度，也未清楚落實部門隔離。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/create-multi-agent-collaboration.html"],"issues":["iam_filtering_imprecise","concurrency_requires_quota_validation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.410303+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company uses an AI assistant application to summarize the company's website content and provide information to customers. The company plans to use Amazon Bedrock to give the application access to a foundation model (FM). The company needs to deploy the AI assistant application to a development environment and a production environment. The solution must integrate the environments with the FM. The company wants to test the effectiveness of various FMs in each environment. The solution must provide product owners with the ability to easily switch between FMs for testing purposes in each environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create one AWS CDK application. Create multiple pipelines in AWS CodePipeline. Configure each pipeline to have its own settings for each FM. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method.","B":"Create a separate AWS CDK application for each environment. Configure the applications to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() method. Create a separate pipeline in AWS CodePipeline for each environment.","C":"Create one AWS CDK application. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() method. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline pipeline that has a deployment stage for each environment that uses AWS CodeBuild deploy actions.","D":"Create one AWS CDK application for the production environment. Configure the application to invoke the Amazon Bedrock FMs by using the aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() method. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Configure the pipeline to deploy to the production environment by using an AWS CodeBuild deploy action. For the development environment, manually recreate the resources by referring to the production application code."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":57,"pages":[111,112]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 AI 助理應用程式摘要公司網站內容並向客戶提供資訊，計畫透過 Amazon Bedrock 讓應用程式存取基礎模型（FM）。公司需要將應用程式部署至開發及正式環境，並讓兩個環境整合 FM。公司希望在各環境測試不同 FM 的成效，且讓產品負責人能輕鬆切換模型進行測試。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立一個 AWS CDK 應用程式及多條 AWS CodePipeline 管線，為每條管線設定各 FM 的專屬設定。設定應用程式使用 aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() 方法呼叫 Amazon Bedrock FM。","B":"為每個環境建立個別 AWS CDK 應用程式，設定其使用 aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() 方法呼叫 Amazon Bedrock FM，並為每個環境建立個別 AWS CodePipeline 管線。","C":"建立一個 AWS CDK 應用程式，設定其使用 aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId() 方法呼叫 Amazon Bedrock FM。建立一條 AWS CodePipeline 管線，為各環境加入使用 AWS CodeBuild 部署動作的部署階段。","D":"為正式環境建立一個 AWS CDK 應用程式，設定其使用 aws_bedrock.ProvisionedModel.fromProvisionedModelArn() 方法呼叫 Amazon Bedrock FM。建立 AWS CodePipeline 管線，以 AWS CodeBuild 部署動作部署至正式環境。開發環境則參考正式應用程式程式碼，手動重建資源。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C is the best shared infrastructure-as-code approach: one CDK application can instantiate environment-specific stages and model identifiers. FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId creates a model reference; it does not itself perform runtime inference. The application still needs a Bedrock runtime invocation and an exposed configuration mechanism for product-owner switching. A pipeline alone does not create a model-selection interface.","explanation_zh":"C 是最適合共用基礎設施即程式碼的方案：同一個 CDK 應用程式可建立環境專屬階段並指定模型 ID。FoundationModel.fromFoundationModelId 建立的是模型參照，本身不執行執行期推論。應用程式仍需呼叫 Bedrock 執行期 API，並提供產品負責人可操作的設定切換機制。管線本身不會產生模型選擇介面。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Provisioned throughput references are unnecessary for freely testing foundation model identifiers and multiply pipeline configuration.","why_zh":"測試不同基礎模型 ID 不必使用佈建輸送量參照，且多管線增加設定維護。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Separate applications and pipelines duplicate maintenance without improving model switching.","why_zh":"個別應用程式及管線重複維護工作，並未改善模型切換。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Manual development-resource recreation causes drift and does not provide equivalent test environments.","why_zh":"手動重建開發資源容易產生差異，也未提供一致的測試環境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/api/v2/docs/aws-cdk-lib.aws_bedrock.FoundationModel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/cdk-pipeline.html"],"issues":["cdk_reference_is_not_runtime_invocation","switching_interface_unspecified"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.411347+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":58,"question_en":"A hotel company wants to enhance a legacy Java-based property management system (PMS) by adding AI capabilities. The company wants to use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to provide staff with room availability information and hotel-specific details. The solution must maintain separate access controls for each hotel that the company manages. The solution must provide room availability information in near real time and must maintain consistent performance during peak usage periods. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a single Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that contains combined data for all hotels. Configure AWS Lambda functions to synchronize data from each hotel's PMS database through direct API connections. Implement AWS CloudTrail logging with hotel-specific filters to audit access logs for each hotel's data.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for each hotel that is invoked by changes to the PMS database for each hotel. Configure the rule to send updates to a centralized Amazon Bedrock knowledge base in a management AWS account. Configure resource-based policies to enforce hotel-specific access controls for hotel staff.","C":"Implement one Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for each hotel in a multi-account structure. Use direct data ingestion to provide real-time room availability information. Schedule regular synchronization for less critical information.","D":"Build a centralized Amazon Bedrock agent that uses multiple knowledge bases. Implement AWS IAM Identity Center with hotel-specific permission sets to control hotel staff data access."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":58,"pages":[113,114]},"question_zh":"一家飯店公司希望為舊有 Java 物業管理系統（PMS）加入 AI 能力，使用 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases 向員工提供客房供應狀態與飯店專屬資訊。方案須為各飯店維持獨立存取控制，近乎即時提供客房供應資訊，並在尖峰使用期間保持一致效能。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"部署一個合併所有飯店資料的 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫。設定 AWS Lambda 函數，透過直接 API 連線同步各飯店 PMS 資料庫。實作帶有飯店專屬篩選條件的 AWS CloudTrail 日誌，以稽核各飯店資料的存取紀錄。","B":"為每間飯店建立由該飯店 PMS 資料庫變更觸發的 Amazon EventBridge 規則，將更新傳送至管理 AWS 帳戶內的集中式 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫。設定資源型政策，為飯店員工強制執行各飯店專屬存取控制。","C":"在多帳戶架構中，為每間飯店實作一個 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫。使用直接擷取提供即時客房供應資訊，並定期同步較不重要的資訊。","D":"建立集中式 Amazon Bedrock 代理並使用多個知識庫。實作 AWS IAM Identity Center，透過飯店專屬權限集控制員工資料存取。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C gives the clearest hotel isolation and direct ingestion avoids a separate data-source sync step. Direct ingestion indexes documents into the configured vector store; it is not a transactional room-inventory query or a guaranteed real-time SLA. For authoritative booking availability, a PMS action/API and measured ingestion lag are still needed. Peak consistency requires capacity and quota validation.","explanation_zh":"C 最清楚提供飯店隔離，直接擷取也省去獨立同步資料來源的步驟。直接擷取會將文件索引至設定的向量儲存區，並非交易式客房庫存查詢，也不是即時 SLA 保證。若要取得可用於訂房的權威庫存，仍需 PMS 動作/API 並量測索引延遲。尖峰效能一致性也須驗證容量及配額。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Audit filters record access; they do not enforce hotel isolation.","why_zh":"稽核篩選只記錄存取，不會強制隔離飯店資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Database-change events and per-hotel enforcement on a shared index need additional integration not specified.","why_zh":"資料庫變更事件與共用索引上的各飯店隔離都需要題目未交代的整合。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Staff identity permission sets alone do not implement agent retrieval authorization or freshness.","why_zh":"員工身分權限集本身不會實作代理檢索授權或資料即時更新。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-direct-ingestion.html"],"issues":["real_time_inventory_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.412240+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":59,"question_en":"A company is implementing a serverless inference API by using AWS Lambda. The API will dynamically invoke multiple AI models hosted on Amazon Bedrock. The company needs to design a solution that can switch between model providers without modifying or redeploying Lambda code in real time. The design must include safe rollout of configuration changes and validation and rollback capabilities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Store the active model provider in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Configure a Lambda function to read the parameter at runtime to determine which model to invoke.","B":"Store the active model provider in AWS AppConfig. Configure a Lambda function to read the configuration at runtime to determine which model to invoke.","C":"Configure an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests to separate Lambda functions. Hardcode each Lambda function to a specific model provider. Switch the integration target manually.","D":"Store the active model provider in a JSON file hosted on Amazon S3. Use AWS AppConfig to reference the S3 file as a hosted configuration source. Configure a Lambda function to read the file through AppConfig at runtime to determine which model to invoke."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"D":17},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":59,"pages":[115,116]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Lambda 建立無伺服器推論 API，動態呼叫 Amazon Bedrock 託管的多種 AI 模型。公司需要能即時切換模型供應商，且不必修改或重新部署 Lambda 程式碼。設計須具備設定變更的安全推出、驗證及回復能力。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將使用中的模型供應商存於 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store，讓 Lambda 函數在執行時讀取參數，以決定呼叫哪個模型。","B":"將使用中的模型供應商存於 AWS AppConfig，讓 Lambda 函數在執行時讀取設定，以決定呼叫哪個模型。","C":"設定 Amazon API Gateway REST API，將請求路由至不同 Lambda 函數；在各函數中寫死特定模型供應商，再手動切換整合目標。","D":"將使用中的模型供應商存於 Amazon S3 託管的 JSON 檔案。使用 AWS AppConfig 參照 S3 檔案作為託管設定來源，讓 Lambda 函數在執行時透過 AppConfig 讀取該檔案，以決定呼叫哪個模型。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AppConfig supplies configuration validators, controlled deployment strategies, and alarm-triggered rollback when configured, making B the simplest choice. Runtime polling/caching means propagation is not necessarily instantaneous. D can also implement the requirements if S3 is configured as an external AppConfig source; its wording incorrectly conflates S3 with the AppConfig hosted configuration store. Thus the distinction is simplicity and terminology, not that S3-backed AppConfig is unsupported.","explanation_zh":"AppConfig 可配置設定驗證器、漸進部署策略及警報觸發回復，因此 B 最簡單。執行期輪詢與快取代表變更不一定瞬間傳播。若 S3 被設定為外部 AppConfig 來源，D 也能達成要求；但其用語將 S3 與 AppConfig 託管設定儲存區混為一談。因此差異在簡潔度與術語，不能宣稱 AppConfig 不支援 S3 來源。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Parameter retrieval alone omits the managed validation, deployment, and rollback workflow.","why_zh":"單純取得參數未提供所要求的託管驗證、部署及回復流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hardcoded providers and manual integration changes do not provide the requested configuration rollout.","why_zh":"供應商寫死及手動改整合目標未提供要求的設定推出機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 is a valid external source, but adds a source and uses hosted-store terminology imprecisely; it is also technically viable when configured correctly.","why_zh":"S3 是有效外部來源，但增加來源且錯用託管儲存區術語；若正確設定，技術上也可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-creating-deployment-strategy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-creating-configuration-and-profile.html"],"issues":["multiple_viable_options_B_D"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.413278+00:00"},"difficulty":4,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":60,"question_en":"A company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock APIs to process complex customer inquiries. During peak usage periods, the application experiences intermittent API timeouts that cause issues such as broken response chunks and delayed data delivery. The application struggles to ensure that prompts remain within token limits when handling complex customer inquiries of varying lengths. Users have reported truncated inputs and incomplete responses. The company has also observed foundation model (FM) invocation failures. The company needs a retry strategy that automatically handles transient service errors and prevents overwhelming Amazon Bedrock during peak usage periods. The strategy must also adapt to changing service availability and support response streaming and token-aware request handling. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Implement a standard retry strategy that uses a 1-second fixed delay between attempts and a 3-retry maximum for all errors. Handle streaming response timeouts by restarting streams. Cap token usage for each session.","B":"Implement an adaptive retry strategy that uses exponential backoff with jitter and a circuit breaker pattern that temporarily disables retries when error rates exceed a predefined threshold. Implement a streaming response handler that monitors for chunk delivery timeouts. Configure the handler to buffer successfully received chunks and intelligently resume streaming from the last received chunk when connections are re- established.","C":"Use the AWS SDK to configure a retry strategy in standard mode. Wrap Amazon Bedrock API calls in try- catch blocks that handle timeout exceptions. Return cached completions for failed streaming requests. Enforce a global token limit for all users. Add jitter-based retry logic and lightweight token trimming for each request. Resume broken streams by requesting only the missing chunks from the point of failure. Maintain a small in-memory buffer of the most recent chunks to minimize redundant data transfer.","D":"Set Amazon Bedrock client request timeouts to 30 seconds. Implement client-side load shedding. Buffer partial results and stop new requests when the application performance begins to degrade. Set static token usage caps for all requests. Configure exponential backoff retries, dynamic chunk sizing, and context-aware token limits."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":75,"C":25},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":60,"pages":[117,118]},"question_zh":"一家公司建立使用 Amazon Bedrock API 處理複雜客戶問題的生成式 AI 應用程式。尖峰期間偶發 API 逾時，造成回應區塊中斷及資料傳遞延遲。面對長度不同的複雜問題，應用程式難以確保提示符合 token 限制，使用者回報輸入遭截斷、回應不完整，公司也觀察到基礎模型呼叫失敗。公司需要可自動處理暫時性服務錯誤、避免尖峰時壓垮 Bedrock 的重試策略，且須適應服務可用性變化，支援串流回應及理解 token 限制的請求處理。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"實作標準重試策略，所有錯誤固定間隔 1 秒，最多重試 3 次。串流回應逾時時重新啟動串流，並限制各工作階段的 token 使用量。","B":"實作自適應重試策略，採用帶抖動的指數退避及斷路器模式，在錯誤率超過預定門檻時暫停重試。實作監控區塊傳遞逾時的串流回應處理器，緩衝成功收到的區塊，並在重新連線時智慧地從最後收到的區塊續傳。","C":"使用 AWS SDK 設定標準模式重試策略。以 try-catch 包住 Bedrock API 呼叫來處理逾時，串流請求失敗時回傳快取完成內容，對所有使用者施加全域 token 限制。加入帶抖動的重試邏輯及輕量請求 token 裁切。從失敗點僅請求遺失區塊以續傳，並在記憶體保留最近區塊的小型緩衝區，以減少重複傳輸。","D":"將 Bedrock 用戶端請求逾時設為 30 秒，實作用戶端卸載負載。緩衝部分結果，並在應用程式效能開始下降時停止新請求。為所有請求設定固定 token 上限，配置指數退避重試、動態區塊大小及依上下文調整的 token 限制。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B captures the intended adaptive backoff and overload protection, but no option fully satisfies the question as written. ConverseStream has no resume cursor or API for fetching missing chunks; buffered content cannot make server-side generation resumable. B also does not specify token-aware admission, and adaptive mode can delay first attempts and couple requests sharing a client. Use explicit token budgeting and application-level restart/reconciliation rather than claiming transparent chunk resumption.","explanation_zh":"B 符合題目想考的自適應退避及過載保護，但依原文沒有任何選項完整成立。ConverseStream 沒有續傳游標或補取遺失區塊 API；緩衝已收內容不會使伺服器端生成變成可續傳。B 也未交代 token 感知的請求准入，而自適應模式可能延遲首次請求，並讓共用用戶端的請求互相影響。實作須明確分配 token 預算，並在應用層重新啟動及協調內容，不能宣稱可透明續傳區塊。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Fixed-delay retries for all errors ignore non-retryable errors and adaptive load control.","why_zh":"所有錯誤固定延遲重試，忽略不可重試錯誤及自適應負載控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The API does not expose missing-chunk retrieval; global caps do not track individual context windows.","why_zh":"API 不提供補取遺失區塊；全域上限也不等於每筆上下文視窗管理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fixed timeout and static caps do not establish a complete adaptive, resumable streaming design; client control of generated chunk sizing is unspecified.","why_zh":"固定逾時與靜態上限未建立完整自適應可續傳設計，且未說明如何控制伺服器生成區塊大小。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdkref/latest/guide/feature-retry-behavior.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_ConverseStream.html"],"issues":["no_fully_correct_option","stream_resume_unsupported","B_omits_token_aware_handling"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.414242+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":61,"question_en":"A bank is developing a generative AI (GenAI)-powered AI assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock to assist the bank's website users with account inquiries and financial guidance. The bank must ensure that the AI assistant does not reveal any personally identifiable information (PII) in customer interactions. The AI assistant must not send PII in prompts to the GenAI model. The AI assistant must not respond to customer requests to provide investment advice. The bank must collect audit logs of all customer interactions, including any images or documents that are transmitted during customer interactions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Macie to detect and redact PII in user inputs and in the model responses. Apply prompt engineering techniques to force the model to avoid investment advice topics. Use AWS CloudTrail to capture conversation logs.","B":"Use an AWS Lambda function and Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII. Use Amazon Comprehend topic modeling to prevent the AI assistant from discussing investment advice topics. Set up custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch to capture customer conversations.","C":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply a sensitive information policy to detect and filter PII. Set up a topic policy to ensure that the AI assistant avoids investment advice topics. Use the Converse API to log model invocations. Enable delivery and image logging to Amazon S3.","D":"Use regex controls to match patterns for PII. Apply prompt engineering techniques to avoid returning PII or investment advice topics to customers. Enable model invocation logging, delivery logging, and image logging to Amazon S3."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":61,"pages":[119,120]},"question_zh":"一家銀行正使用 Amazon Bedrock 開發生成式 AI 助理，協助網站使用者查詢帳戶及取得財務指引。銀行須確保助理不會在互動中洩漏個人識別資訊（PII），也不得在傳給模型的提示內包含 PII。助理不得回應提供投資建議的要求。銀行須收集所有客戶互動的稽核日誌，包括互動中傳送的圖片及文件。哪個方案可用最少維運工作滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Macie 偵測並遮蔽使用者輸入及模型回應中的 PII。透過提示工程強制模型避免投資建議主題，使用 AWS CloudTrail 擷取對話日誌。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 函數及 Amazon Comprehend 偵測並遮蔽 PII，使用 Comprehend 主題建模防止助理討論投資建議，並在 CloudWatch 設定自訂指標擷取客戶對話。","C":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 防護措施，套用敏感資訊政策以偵測及篩除 PII，並設定主題政策使助理避免投資建議。使用 Converse API 記錄模型呼叫，啟用將日誌傳送及圖片記錄至 Amazon S3。","D":"使用正規表示式控制比對 PII 模式，透過提示工程避免回傳 PII 或投資建議，啟用模型呼叫日誌、傳送日誌及圖片日誌至 Amazon S3。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C combines managed sensitive-information and denied-topic controls with invocation logging. Guardrails must evaluate input before inference and output before delivery; configure blocking or masking and apply to all relevant text. Converse is the invocation API, not a logging switch: model invocation logging must separately be enabled, with S3 for image/document payloads. These controls do not prove perfect detection of every PII form or automatically inspect all binary document content.","explanation_zh":"C 結合託管敏感資訊及拒絕主題控制與模型呼叫日誌。須在推論前檢查輸入、傳送前檢查輸出，設定封鎖或遮蔽並涵蓋相關文字。Converse 是呼叫 API，不是日誌開關；須另外啟用模型呼叫日誌，圖片與文件負載則需 S3。這些控制不代表能完美辨識每一種 PII，也不代表自動檢查所有二進位文件內容。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Macie classifies S3 data and CloudTrail records API activity; neither replaces request-time guardrails and complete conversation logging.","why_zh":"Macie 分類 S3 資料，CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動，不能取代請求當下防護及完整對話日誌。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Topic modeling is not a denied-topic enforcement policy, and metrics are not conversation payload logs.","why_zh":"主題建模不是拒絕主題強制政策，指標也不是對話內容日誌。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Regex and prompts require custom maintenance and do not provide equivalent managed semantic topic controls.","why_zh":"正規表示式及提示需要自訂維護，也未提供相同的託管語意主題控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html"],"issues":["logging_requires_explicit_enablement","absolute_PII_guarantee_not_supported"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.415302+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":62,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a customer service AI assistant application that uses a foundation model (FM) in Amazon Bedrock. The application must provide transparent responses by documenting reasoning and by citing sources that are used for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). The application must capture comprehensive audit trails for all responses to users. The application must be able to serve up to 10,000 concurrent users and must respond to each customer inquiry within 2 seconds. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Enable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Configure structured prompts that direct the FM to provide evidence presentations. Integrate Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases with data sources to enable RAG. Configure the application to reference and cite authoritative content. Deploy the application in a Multi-AZ architecture. Use Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda functions to scale the application. Use Amazon CloudFront to provide low-latency delivery.","B":"Enable tracing for Amazon Bedrock agents. Integrate a custom RAG pipeline with Amazon OpenSearch Service to retrieve and cite sources. Configure structured prompts to present retrieved evidence. Deploy the application behind an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Use AWS Lambda functions and Amazon CloudFront to scale the application and to provide low latency. Store logs in Amazon S3 and use AWS CloudTrail to capture audit trails.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor latency and error rates. Embed model prompts directly in the application backend to cite sources. Store application interactions with users in Amazon RDS for audits.","D":"Store generated responses and supporting evidence in an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable versioning on the bucket for audits. Use AWS Glue to catalog retrieved documents. Process the retrieved documents in Amazon Athena to generate periodic compliance reports."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":62,"pages":[121,122]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型建立客服 AI 助理。應用程式須記錄推理並引用檢索增強生成（RAG）所用來源，提供透明回應，且須為所有使用者回應擷取完整稽核軌跡。應用程式須服務最多 10,000 名同時使用者，並在 2 秒內回答每個客戶問題。哪個方案可用最少維運工作滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"啟用 Amazon Bedrock 代理追蹤。設定結構化提示，指示模型呈現證據。將 Bedrock 知識庫與資料來源整合以啟用 RAG，設定應用程式參照並引用權威內容。採用多可用區架構部署，使用 API Gateway 及 Lambda 函數擴展應用程式，並以 CloudFront 提供低延遲傳遞。","B":"啟用 Bedrock 代理追蹤，整合使用 OpenSearch Service 的自訂 RAG 管線以檢索並引用來源，設定結構化提示呈現檢索證據。將應用程式部署於 API Gateway REST API 後方，使用 Lambda 與 CloudFront 擴展及提供低延遲。將日誌存至 S3，並使用 CloudTrail 擷取稽核軌跡。","C":"使用 CloudWatch 監控延遲及錯誤率，在後端直接嵌入模型提示來引用來源，並將使用者互動存入 Amazon RDS 供稽核。","D":"將生成回應及支持證據存於 S3 儲存貯體，啟用版本控制供稽核。使用 Glue 編目檢索文件，並在 Athena 處理文件以產生定期合規報告。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A uses managed Knowledge Bases and agent traces to reduce custom RAG operations and expose retrieval/orchestration evidence. Traces and citation payloads must be captured and durably stored with request identity to form an audit trail; enabling tracing alone is insufficient. CloudFront and serverless scaling do not guarantee 10,000 concurrent model invocations or a two-second completion. Validate service quotas, model latency, token budgets, and end-to-end load under the required SLO.","explanation_zh":"A 使用託管知識庫及代理追蹤，降低自訂 RAG 維運工作並提供檢索及協作過程證據。追蹤與引用內容須連同請求身分擷取並持久保存，才能成為稽核軌跡；只啟用追蹤並不足夠。CloudFront 與無伺服器擴展不保證可同時進行一萬次模型呼叫，也不保證兩秒內完成。須依服務目標驗證配額、模型延遲、token 預算及端到端負載。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom retrieval pipeline increases maintenance compared with managed Knowledge Bases; CloudTrail alone is not a response-content audit.","why_zh":"自訂檢索管線比託管知識庫增加維護；CloudTrail 本身不是回應內容稽核。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Metrics and embedded prompts do not implement grounded retrieval, citations, or agent execution traces.","why_zh":"指標與嵌入提示未實作有依據的檢索、引用及代理執行追蹤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Archival analytics does not provide the live retrieval, serving, and orchestration system.","why_zh":"封存分析未提供即時檢索、服務及代理協作系統。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/trace-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_Citation.html"],"issues":["latency_and_concurrency_not_guaranteed","trace_persistence_unspecified"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.416391+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":63,"question_en":"A healthcare company is developing a document management system that stores medical research papers in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to build a comprehensive metadata framework that will improve search precision for a generative AI (GenAI) application that analyzes the research papers. The metadata framework must include document timestamps, author information, and research domain classifications. The solution must maintain a consistent metadata structure across all uploaded documents. The solution must give foundation models (FMs) the ability to understand document context without accessing the full content. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Store document timestamps in Amazon S3 system metadata. Use S3 object tags to implement domain classification. Implement custom user-defined metadata to store author information.","B":"Set up S3 Object Lock with legal holds to track document timestamps. Use S3 object tags to store author information. Implement S3 access points for domain classification.","C":"Use S3 Inventory reports to track document timestamps. Create S3 access points to implement domain classification. Store author information in S3 Storage Lens dashboards.","D":"Use custom user-defined metadata to store author information. Use S3 Object Lock retention periods to track document timestamps. Use S3 Event Notifications to implement domain classification."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":63,"pages":[123]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司開發文件管理系統，將醫學研究論文存於 Amazon S3。公司需要完整中繼資料架構，提高分析論文的生成式 AI 應用程式搜尋精確度。架構須包含文件時間戳記、作者資訊及研究領域分類，所有上傳文件須維持一致中繼資料結構，並讓基礎模型不必存取全文即可了解文件脈絡。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將文件時間戳記存於 S3 系統中繼資料，以 S3 物件標籤實作領域分類，使用自訂使用者中繼資料儲存作者資訊。","B":"設定具法律保留的 S3 Object Lock 追蹤文件時間戳記，以 S3 物件標籤儲存作者資訊，並使用 S3 存取點實作領域分類。","C":"使用 S3 Inventory 報告追蹤文件時間戳記，以 S3 存取點實作領域分類，並將作者資訊存於 S3 Storage Lens 儀表板。","D":"使用自訂使用者中繼資料儲存作者資訊，以 S3 Object Lock 保留期間追蹤文件時間戳記，並使用 S3 Event Notifications 實作領域分類。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A maps timestamps, classification tags, and authors to appropriate S3 metadata facilities. HeadObject retrieves metadata without the object body. System timestamps describe the S3 object, not necessarily the paper publication date; a domain timestamp may require a custom field. A schema-validation upload pipeline and explicit metadata delivery to retrieval/prompts are still required because S3 does not enforce a universal research schema or automatically inform an FM.","explanation_zh":"A 將時間戳記、分類標籤及作者對應至合適的 S3 中繼資料機制。HeadObject 可不取回物件本文而取得中繼資料。系統時間描述 S3 物件，不一定等於論文發表日期；領域特有日期可能需自訂欄位。仍須透過上傳流程驗證結構，並明確將中繼資料交給檢索或提示，因為 S3 不會強制統一研究結構或自動告知模型。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Legal holds prevent deletion and access points manage access; neither represents classification or document dates.","why_zh":"法律保留防止刪除，存取點管理存取，均不是分類或文件日期欄位。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storage Lens reports storage activity, not per-document author records; access points are not classifiers.","why_zh":"Storage Lens 報告儲存活動，不儲存逐文件作者紀錄；存取點不是分類器。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Retention periods and event notifications do not replace timestamps and classification metadata.","why_zh":"保留期間及事件通知不能取代時間戳記與分類中繼資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingMetadata.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_HeadObject.html"],"issues":["system_timestamp_not_publication_date","schema_and_model_integration_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.417881+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":64,"question_en":"Example Corp provides a personalized video generation service that millions of enterprise customers use. Customers generate marketing videos by submitting prompts to the company's proprietary generative AI (GenAI) model. To improve output relevance and personalization, Example Corp wants to enhance the prompts by using customer-specific context such as product preferences, customer attributes, and business history. The customers have strict data governance requirements. The customers must retain full ownership and control over their own data. The customers do not require real-time access. However, semantic accuracy must be high and retrieval latency must remain low to support customer experience use cases. Example Corp wants to minimize architectural complexity in its integration pattern. Example Corp does not want to deploy and manage services in each customer's environment unless necessary. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that each customer sets up an Amazon Q Business index that includes the customer's internal data. Ensure that each customer designates Example Corp as a data accessor to allow Example Corp to retrieve relevant content by using a secure API to enrich prompts at runtime.","B":"Use federated search with Model Context Protocol (MCP) by deploying real-time MCP servers for each customer. Retrieve data in real time during prompt generation.","C":"Ensure that each customer configures an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Allow cross-account querying so Example Corp can retrieve structured data for prompt augmentation.","D":"Configure Amazon Kendra to crawl customer data sources. Share the resulting indexes across accounts so Example Corp can query each customer's Amazon Kendra index to retrieve augmentation data."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":53,"C":41,"B":6},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":64,"pages":[124,125]},"question_zh":"Example Corp 提供數百萬企業客戶使用的個人化影片生成服務，客戶提交提示給公司專有生成式 AI 模型以製作行銷影片。公司希望以客戶專屬脈絡，例如商品偏好、客戶屬性及業務歷史，增強提示以改善相關性及個人化。客戶有嚴格資料治理要求，須完整保有資料所有權及控制權，不需要即時存取，但語意準確性須高、檢索延遲須低，以支援客戶體驗情境。公司希望整合架構盡量簡單，非必要時不想在各客戶環境部署及管理服務。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"讓每個客戶建立包含內部資料的 Amazon Q Business 索引，並將 Example Corp 指定為資料存取者，允許公司透過安全 API 檢索相關內容，在執行時增強提示。","B":"在各客戶環境部署即時 Model Context Protocol（MCP）伺服器，使用 MCP 聯合搜尋，在生成提示時即時擷取資料。","C":"讓每個客戶設定 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫，允許跨帳戶查詢，使 Example Corp 可取得結構化資料以增強提示。","D":"設定 Amazon Kendra 爬取客戶資料來源，跨帳戶分享索引，讓 Example Corp 可查詢各客戶 Kendra 索引以取得增強資料。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The customer-owned Q index data-accessor workflow directly supports registered ISVs, selected data sources/users, and cross-account retrieval. It fits managed semantic retrieval without deploying an MCP server per customer. Registration and IAM Identity Center requirements apply, and latency must still be measured. Current AWS documentation also states Q Business is closed to new customers; A describes the intended existing-customer architecture rather than a universally available new deployment.","explanation_zh":"客戶持有 Q 索引的資料存取者流程直接支援已註冊 ISV、指定資料來源與使用者及跨帳戶檢索，符合不必逐客戶部署 MCP 伺服器的託管語意檢索需求。須符合 ISV 註冊及 IAM Identity Center 條件，延遲仍需實測。目前 AWS 文件也表示 Q Business 已不開放新客戶；A 描述的是既有客戶適用的預期架構，不代表所有新部署都可使用。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Per-customer real-time servers add operations for a freshness requirement that does not exist.","why_zh":"每客戶即時伺服器增加維運，且題目沒有即時性要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cross-account Knowledge Base retrieval requires explicit identity and authorization design; this is not the named managed ISV accessor workflow.","why_zh":"跨帳戶知識庫檢索需要明確身分及授權設計，並非所述託管 ISV 存取者流程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Crawling and index-sharing require additional cross-account authorization and connector governance.","why_zh":"爬取及索引分享另需跨帳戶授權與連接器治理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/isv-getting-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qbusiness-ug/qbusiness-availability-change.html"],"issues":["Q_Business_new_customer_availability_changed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.418932+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":65,"question_en":"A company is building a legal research AI assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock with an Anthropic Claude foundation model (FM). The AI assistant must retrieve highly relevant case law documents to augment the FM's responses. The AI assistant must identify semantic relationships between legal concepts, specific legal terminology, and citations. The AI assistant must perform quickly and return precise results. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to use a default vector search configuration. Use Amazon Bedrock to expand queries to improve retrieval for legal documents based on specific terminology and citations.","B":"Use Amazon OpenSearch service to deploy a hybrid search architecture that combines vector search with keyword search. Apply an Amazon Bedrock reranker model to optimize result relevance.","C":"Enable the Amazon Kendra query suggestion feature for end users. Use Amazon Bedrock to perform post-processing of search results to identify semantic similarity in the documents and to produce precise results.","D":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Service with vector search and Amazon Bedrock Titan embeddings to index and search legal documents. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to merge results with keyword-based filters that are stored in an Amazon RDS database."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":65,"pages":[126,127]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 的 Anthropic Claude 基礎模型建立法律研究 AI 助理。助理須檢索高度相關判例文件以增強模型回應，辨識法律概念的語意關係、特定法律術語及引用，並快速回傳精確結果。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Bedrock 知識庫採用預設向量搜尋，使用 Bedrock 擴展查詢，以改善特定術語及引用相關法律文件的檢索。","B":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch Service 部署結合向量及關鍵字搜尋的混合搜尋架構，套用 Amazon Bedrock 重排序模型以最佳化結果相關性。","C":"對終端使用者啟用 Amazon Kendra 查詢建議功能，使用 Bedrock 後處理搜尋結果，辨識文件語意相似度並產生精確結果。","D":"使用 OpenSearch Service 向量搜尋及 Bedrock Titan 嵌入索引並搜尋法律文件，以自訂 Lambda 函數將結果與存於 RDS 資料庫的關鍵字篩選條件合併。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Hybrid retrieval combines semantic similarity with lexical matching, which is valuable for precise legal citations and specialized terms. A reranker can reorder candidates by query relevance. This directly addresses both matching modes with fewer bespoke components than D. Reranking adds work, so candidate count and latency still need benchmarking rather than assuming universally faster responses.","explanation_zh":"混合檢索結合語意相似度與文字匹配，適合精確法律引用及專門術語。重排序模型能依查詢相關性重新排列候選結果。B 直接涵蓋兩種匹配，且比 D 少自訂元件。重排序會增加運算，仍須測試候選數量及延遲，不能假設回應一定更快。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Vector-only retrieval can miss exact identifiers; query expansion does not replace explicit lexical retrieval and reranking.","why_zh":"只有向量檢索可能漏掉精確識別碼；查詢擴展不能取代明確文字檢索及重排序。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Query suggestions assist query entry rather than implement the required hybrid retrieval/ranking.","why_zh":"查詢建議協助輸入查詢，未實作要求的混合檢索及排序。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom RDS/Lambda merging adds coordination and ranking complexity.","why_zh":"自訂 RDS/Lambda 合併增加協調及排序複雜度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_KnowledgeBaseVectorSearchConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/rerank.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:20.419769+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":66,"question_en":"A company deploys multiple Amazon Bedrock based generative AI (GenAI) applications across multiple business units for customer service, content generation, and document analysis. Some applications show unpredictable token consumption patterns. The company requires a comprehensive observability solution that provides real-time visibility into token usage patterns across multiple models. The observability solution must support custom dashboards for multiple stakeholder groups and provide alerting capabilities for token consumption across all the foundational models that the company's applications use. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics as data sources to create custom Amazon QuickSight dashboards that show token usage trends and usage patterns across FMs.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze Amazon Bedrock invocation logs for token consumption patterns and usage attribution by application. Create custom queries to identify high-usage scenarios. Add log widgets to dashboards to enable continuous monitoring.","C":"Create custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards that combine native Amazon Bedrock token and invocation CloudWatch metrics. Set up CloudWatch alarms to monitor token usage thresholds.","D":"Create dashboards that show token usage trends and patterns across the company's FMs by using an Amazon Bedrock zero-ETL integration with Amazon Managed Grafana.","E":"Implement Amazon EventBridge rules to capture Amazon Bedrock model invocation events. Route token usage data to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream that targets Amazon OpenSearch Serverless. Use OpenSearch dashboards to analyze usage patterns."},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BC":82,"B":9,"CD":9},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":66,"pages":[128,129]},"question_zh":"一家公司在多個事業單位部署以 Amazon Bedrock 為基礎的生成式 AI 應用程式，用於客服、內容生成及文件分析。部分應用程式的 token 消耗難以預測。公司需要完整可觀測性方案，即時掌握多種模型的 token 使用模式，為不同利害關係人提供自訂儀表板，並針對應用程式所用全部基礎模型提供 token 消耗警示。哪兩個方案可用最少維運工作滿足需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"以 CloudWatch 指標為資料來源建立自訂 QuickSight 儀表板，呈現跨模型 token 使用趨勢及模式。","B":"使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 分析 Bedrock 呼叫日誌的 token 消耗模式與應用程式使用歸屬。建立自訂查詢找出高用量情境，並將日誌小工具加入儀表板，持續監控。","C":"建立自訂 CloudWatch 儀表板，整合 Bedrock 原生 token 及呼叫指標，設定 CloudWatch 警報監控 token 使用門檻。","D":"使用 Bedrock 與 Amazon Managed Grafana 的零 ETL 整合，建立呈現公司各模型 token 使用趨勢及模式的儀表板。","E":"實作 EventBridge 規則擷取 Bedrock 模型呼叫事件，將 token 使用資料路由至以 OpenSearch Serverless 為目的地的 Amazon Data Firehose 傳遞串流，使用 OpenSearch 儀表板分析使用模式。"},"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Native Bedrock CloudWatch metrics provide per-model input/output token counts and invocation metrics for dashboards and alarms. Invocation logs and Logs Insights add request/application attribution and deeper usage queries. Together B and C avoid a separate analytics ingestion stack. Enable invocation logging explicitly and supply application identifiers; token metrics are not monetary cost metrics and telemetry delivery is not instantaneous.","explanation_zh":"Bedrock 原生 CloudWatch 指標提供各模型輸入/輸出 token 計數及呼叫指標，可用於儀表板與警報。呼叫日誌及 Logs Insights 補上請求/應用程式歸屬及深入用量查詢。B、C 結合後不需另建分析擷取架構。仍須明確啟用呼叫日誌並提供應用程式識別；token 指標不等於費用指標，監控資料也非零延遲送達。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A direct CloudWatch-metrics QuickSight source is not established here and adds integration compared with native dashboards.","why_zh":"題目未建立 CloudWatch 指標直接作為 QuickSight 來源的方式，且比原生儀表板多整合。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The claimed Bedrock-to-Grafana zero-ETL integration is not the documented native metric path.","why_zh":"宣稱的 Bedrock 至 Grafana 零 ETL 整合並非文件所述原生指標路徑。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Custom event routing, Firehose, and OpenSearch add operations and do not automatically supply invocation token payloads.","why_zh":"自訂事件路由、Firehose 及 OpenSearch 增加維運，且不會自動取得呼叫 token 負載。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-runtime-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.963898+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・複選"},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company is designing a solution that uses foundation models (FMs) to support multiple AI workloads. Some FMs must be invoked on demand and in real time. Other FMs require consistent high-throughput access for batch processing. The solution must support hybrid deployment patterns and run workloads across cloud infrastructure and on- premises infrastructure to comply with data residency and compliance requirements. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Lambda to orchestrate low-latency FM inference by invoking FMs hosted on Amazon SageMaker AI asynchronous endpoints.","B":"Configure provisioned throughput in Amazon Bedrock to ensure consistent performance for high-volume workloads.","C":"Deploy FMs to Amazon SageMaker AI endpoints with support for edge deployment by using Amazon SageMaker Neo. Orchestrate the FMs by using AWS Lambda to support hybrid deployment.","D":"Use Amazon Bedrock with auto-scaling to handle unpredictable traffic surges.","E":"Use Amazon SageMaker JumpStart to host and invoke the FMs."},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BC":67,"BD":33},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":67,"pages":[130,131]},"question_zh":"一家公司設計使用基礎模型支援多種 AI 工作負載的方案。部分模型須隨需即時呼叫，其他模型則需穩定高輸送量進行批次處理。方案須支援混合部署，在雲端與內部部署基礎設施執行工作負載，以符合資料落地及合規要求。哪兩項步驟符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Lambda 協調低延遲模型推論，呼叫託管於 SageMaker AI 非同步端點的模型。","B":"設定 Bedrock 佈建輸送量，確保高用量工作負載效能穩定。","C":"將模型部署至 SageMaker AI 端點，使用 SageMaker Neo 支援邊緣部署，並以 Lambda 協調模型以支援混合部署。","D":"使用具自動擴展功能的 Bedrock 處理不可預測的流量突增。","E":"使用 SageMaker JumpStart 託管並呼叫基礎模型。"},"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B is appropriate for supported models with predictable high-volume capacity requirements. C is the intended hybrid/edge answer, but Neo supports specific frameworks, operators, models, and device targets; it does not make arbitrary foundation models or SageMaker hosted endpoints run on premises. Cloud Lambda orchestration also does not establish an on-premises data boundary. No two options fully specify the required hybrid deployment; validate model portability and implement a supported local serving stack.","explanation_zh":"B 適合支援佈建輸送量且具有可預測高用量容量需求的模型。C 是題目預期的混合/邊緣答案，但 Neo 僅支援特定框架、運算子、模型及裝置目標，不會讓任意基礎模型或 SageMaker 託管端點自動在地端執行。雲端 Lambda 協調也不等於建立地端資料邊界。沒有兩個選項完整交代所需混合部署；須驗證模型可移植性並實作受支援的本地服務架構。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Asynchronous endpoints queue work and do not meet the stated immediate low-latency path.","why_zh":"非同步端點會排隊處理，未符合要求的即時低延遲路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Unspecified auto-scaling does not address on-premises deployment or reserved predictable throughput.","why_zh":"未明確定義的自動擴展未處理地端部署或可預測的保留輸送量。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"JumpStart simplifies cloud model deployment but does not itself solve on-premises serving/residency.","why_zh":"JumpStart 簡化雲端模型部署，但本身未解決地端服務及資料落地要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/neo-supported-devices-edge-frameworks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prov-thru-purchase.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/neo-getting-started-edge-step1.html"],"issues":["no_fully_specified_hybrid_solution","Neo_not_general_FM_edge_hosting"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.965486+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":68,"question_en":"A company is planning to deploy multiple generative AI (GenAI) applications to five independent business units that operate in multiple countries in Europe and the Americas. Each application uses Amazon Bedrock Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) patterns with business unit-specific knowledge bases that store terabytes of unstructured data. The company must establish well-architected, standardized components for security controls, observability practices, and deployment patterns across all the GenAI applications. The components must be reusable, versioned, and governed consistently. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoints for the GenAI applications. Deploy common security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens in standardized AWS CloudFormation templates. Use CloudFormation Guard after the deployment to validate policy compliance in each business unit.","B":"Create standardized AWS CloudFormation templates to implement security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Establish a centralized repository that performs version control. Integrate a CI/CD pipeline with CloudFormation Guard to enforce consistent and repeatable deployments across business units.","C":"Use AWS Service Catalog to define standardized portfolios and versioned products for each business unit. Use the portfolios to enforce security, observability, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well- Architected Generative AI Lens. Require the business units to use the Service Catalog console to deploy resources.","D":"Document security controls, observability requirements, and RAG patterns based on the AWS Well- Architected Generative AI Lens in a shared design document. Use Amazon Macie to enforce deployment. Delegate implementation responsibility to each business unit."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":83,"C":17},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":68,"pages":[132,133]},"question_zh":"一家公司計畫為分布歐洲及美洲多國的五個獨立事業單位部署多個生成式 AI 應用程式。各應用程式使用 Bedrock RAG 模式，搭配存有數 TB 非結構化資料的事業單位專屬知識庫。公司須為所有應用程式建立符合良好架構實務的標準化安全控制、可觀測性及部署元件，且元件須可重用、具版本控制並一致治理。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為應用程式設定 API Gateway REST API 端點。依 AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens，在標準 CloudFormation 範本中部署共用安全、可觀測性及 RAG 模式。部署後使用 CloudFormation Guard 驗證各事業單位政策合規。","B":"依 AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens 建立標準 CloudFormation 範本，實作安全、可觀測性及 RAG 模式。建立中央版本控制儲存庫，將 CloudFormation Guard 整合至 CI/CD 管線，強制各事業單位一致且可重複部署。","C":"使用 Service Catalog 為各事業單位定義標準產品組合及具版本的產品，以產品組合強制遵循 AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens 的安全、可觀測性與 RAG 模式。要求事業單位透過 Service Catalog 主控台部署資源。","D":"在共用設計文件記錄依 AWS Well-Architected Generative AI Lens 制定的安全控制、可觀測性要求及 RAG 模式。使用 Macie 強制執行部署，將實作責任交給各事業單位。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Versioned infrastructure templates provide reusable implementations, and Guard checks JSON/YAML against policy-as-code rules before deployment. CI/CD can block builds on validation failures, making B a direct consistent governance workflow. Guard only enforces rules that are authored and does not certify every architectural or runtime property. Service Catalog is also useful governance infrastructure, but C does not explicitly provide the same automated policy-validation pipeline.","explanation_zh":"具版本的基礎設施範本提供可重用實作，Guard 在部署前依政策即程式碼規則檢查 JSON/YAML。CI/CD 可在驗證失敗時阻擋建置，使 B 直接形成一致治理流程。Guard 只執行已編寫的規則，並不認證所有架構或執行期特性。Service Catalog 也是有用治理工具，但 C 未明確提供同樣的自動政策驗證管線。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Post-deployment checks detect issues after resources already exist and omit explicit repository versioning.","why_zh":"部署後檢查在資源已建立後才發現問題，也未明確納入儲存庫版本控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Catalog products can govern provisioning, but console-only deployment is unnecessary and does not explicitly gate changes with Guard.","why_zh":"產品目錄能治理佈建，但限制只能使用主控台並非必要，也未明確使用 Guard 阻擋違規變更。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Macie discovers sensitive S3 data; it is not a deployment-policy enforcement engine.","why_zh":"Macie 偵測 S3 敏感資料，不是部署政策執行引擎。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cloudformation-guard.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.966823+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧"},{"id":69,"question_en":"A company upgraded its Amazon Bedrock powered foundation model (FM) that supports a multilingual customer service assistant. After the upgrade, the assistant exhibited inconsistent behavior across languages. The assistant began generating different responses in some languages when presented with identical questions. The company needs a solution to detect and address similar problems for future updates. The evaluation must be completed within 45 minutes for all supported languages. The evaluation must process at least 15,000 test conversations in parallel. The evaluation process must be fully automated and integrated into the CI/CD pipeline. The solution must block deployment if quality thresholds are not met. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a distributed traffic simulation framework that sends translation-heavy workloads to the assistant in multiple languages simultaneously. Use Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor latency, concurrency, and throughput. Run simulations before production releases to identify infrastructure bottlenecks.","B":"Deploy the assistant in multiple AWS Regions with Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing and AWS Global Accelerator to improve global performance. Store multilingual conversation logs in Amazon S3. Perform weekly post-deployment audits to review consistency.","C":"Create a pre-processing pipeline that normalizes all incoming messages into a consistent format before sending the messages to the assistant. Apply rule-based checks to flag potential hallucinations in the outputs. Focus the evaluation on the normalized text to simplify testing across languages.","D":"Set up standardized multilingual test conversations with identical meaning. Run the test conversations in parallel by using Amazon Bedrock model evaluation jobs. Apply similarity and hallucination thresholds. Integrate the process into the CI/CD pipeline to block releases that fail."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":69,"pages":[134,135]},"question_zh":"一家公司升級支援多語客服助理的 Bedrock 基礎模型後，發現不同語言表現不一致：對相同問題，某些語言開始產生不同回應。公司希望在未來更新時偵測並解決類似問題。評估須在 45 分鐘內涵蓋所有支援語言，平行處理至少 15,000 個測試對話，全自動整合至 CI/CD 管線，並在品質未達門檻時阻止部署。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立分散式流量模擬框架，同時向助理傳送多語且大量翻譯的工作負載。使用 CloudWatch 指標監控延遲、並行及輸送量，在正式發佈前執行模擬以找出基礎設施瓶頸。","B":"在多個 AWS 區域部署助理，使用 Route 53 延遲路由及 Global Accelerator 改善全球效能。將多語對話日誌存於 S3，每週在部署後稽核一致性。","C":"建立前處理管線，將所有輸入訊息正規化為一致格式後送給助理。使用規則式檢查標示潛在幻覺，集中評估正規化文字以簡化跨語言測試。","D":"建立語意相同的標準多語測試對話，使用 Bedrock 模型評估工作平行執行，套用相似度及幻覺門檻，整合至 CI/CD 以阻止未通過的發佈。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D is the only option that evaluates semantic quality across languages before release and makes quality thresholds a deployment gate. Bedrock supports automated evaluations, including model-judge workflows. However, no cited guarantee establishes 15,000 simultaneous conversations or completion within 45 minutes; job/dataset/model quotas, supported evaluation languages, and throughput must be checked. A dataset of 15,000 cases is not the same as 15,000 concurrent executions.","explanation_zh":"D 是唯一在發佈前評估跨語言語意品質，並以品質門檻控制部署的選項。Bedrock 支援自動評估，包括模型評審流程。但文件不保證可同時執行 15,000 個對話或在 45 分鐘內完成；須確認工作、資料集及模型配額、評估語言支援及輸送量。包含 15,000 筆案例的資料集不等於同時執行 15,000 個測試。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Infrastructure load metrics do not measure cross-language answer consistency or hallucination.","why_zh":"基礎設施負載指標不衡量跨語言答案一致性或幻覺。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Weekly audits occur after deployment and do not block bad releases.","why_zh":"每週稽核發生在部署後，無法阻止品質不良版本發佈。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Normalizing text can conceal language-specific regressions and does not implement representative parallel quality gates.","why_zh":"文字正規化可能掩蓋語言特有退化，也未實作具代表性的平行品質關卡。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-automatic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-support.html"],"issues":["15000_parallel_and_45_minutes_unproven"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.967713+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application has several custom tool integrations. The application has experienced unexpected token consumption surges despite consistent user traffic. The company needs a solution that uses Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging to monitor InputTokenCount metrics and OutputTokenCount metrics. The solution must detect unusual patterns in tool usage and identify which specific tool integrations cause abnormal token consumption. The solution must also automatically adjust thresholds as traffic patterns change. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch dashboards based on InputTokenCount metrics and OutputTokenCount metrics. Configure static CloudWatch alarms with fixed thresholds for each tool integration.","B":"Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use AWS Glue to catalog the logs. Analyze token consumption patterns by using scheduled Amazon Athena queries that generate reports on tool usage trends.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to capture model invocation logs. Create CloudWatch metric filters to extract tool-specific invocation patterns. Apply CloudWatch anomaly detection alarms that adjust baselines for each tool's metrics.","D":"Store model invocation logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function to process logs in real time. Manually update Amazon CloudWatch alarm thresholds based on token consumption trends that the Lambda function identifies."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":86,"D":14},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":70,"pages":[136,137]},"question_zh":"一家公司開發使用 Bedrock 基礎模型的生成式 AI 應用程式，整合數種自訂工具。使用者流量穩定，token 消耗卻意外突增。公司需要透過 Bedrock 模型呼叫日誌監控 InputTokenCount 與 OutputTokenCount 指標，偵測不尋常工具使用模式、找出造成異常 token 消耗的特定工具，並隨流量模式變化自動調整門檻。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudWatch Logs 擷取模型呼叫日誌，根據 InputTokenCount 及 OutputTokenCount 建立儀表板，為各工具設定固定門檻的靜態警報。","B":"將模型呼叫日誌存於 S3，以 Glue 編目，定期執行 Athena 查詢分析 token 消耗並產生工具用量趨勢報告。","C":"使用 CloudWatch Logs 擷取模型呼叫日誌，建立指標篩選器擷取工具專屬呼叫模式，並套用 CloudWatch 異常偵測警報，調整各工具指標的基準。","D":"將模型呼叫日誌存於 S3，建立 Lambda 函數即時處理日誌，根據函數找出的 token 趨勢手動更新 CloudWatch 警報門檻。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Metric filters can transform structured log fields into tool-dimension custom metrics, and CloudWatch anomaly detection learns changing baselines. C therefore supplies both attribution and adaptive alert bands. Native Bedrock token metrics are per model, not automatically per custom tool: log tool identifiers and correlate invocations, including multi-tool calls. Anomaly detection identifies deviations, not proof that a particular tool is the causal source.","explanation_zh":"指標篩選器能將結構化日誌欄位轉成帶工具維度的自訂指標，CloudWatch 異常偵測則學習變動基準，因此 C 同時提供歸屬與自適應警示區間。Bedrock 原生 token 指標以模型區分，不會自動依自訂工具區分；須記錄工具識別並關聯呼叫，包含多工具呼叫情況。異常偵測指出偏離模式，不等於證明某工具是因果來源。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Fixed thresholds do not adapt to changing traffic patterns.","why_zh":"固定門檻不會隨流量模式變化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Scheduled reports do not provide adaptive anomaly alarms.","why_zh":"排程報告未提供自適應異常警報。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Manual threshold updates contradict automatic adaptation.","why_zh":"手動更新門檻不符合自動調整要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Anomaly_Detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-runtime-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html"],"issues":["tool_attribution_requires_structured_context"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.969024+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群有分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":71,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop an AI-powered application that uses a foundation model (FM) that supports cross-Region inference and provisioned throughput. The application must serve users in Europe and North America with consistently low latency. The application must comply with data residency regulations that require European user data to remain within Europe-based AWS Regions. During testing, the application experiences service degradation when Regional traffic spikes reach service quotas. The company needs a solution that maintains application resilience and minimizes operational complexity. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy separate Amazon Bedrock instances in North American and European Regions. Use a custom routing layer that directs traffic based on user location. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor Regional service usage. Use Amazon SNS to send email alerts to the company when usage approaches specified thresholds.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference profiles by specifying geographical codes in profile IDs when the application calls the InvokeModel API. Configure separate Amazon API Gateway HTTP APIs to direct European and North American users to the appropriate Regional endpoints.","C":"Deploy a multi-Region Amazon API Gateway HTTP API and AWS Lambda functions that implement retry logic to handle throttling. Configure the Lambda functions to call the FM in the nearest secondary Region when the application reaches service quotas in the primary Region. Use intelligent routing to ensure compliance with data residency requirements.","D":"Configure provisioned throughput for Amazon Bedrock in multiple Regions. Implement failover logic in the application code to switch between Regions when throttling occurs. Use AWS Global Accelerator to route traffic to the appropriate endpoints based on user location."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":71,"pages":[138,139]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用支援跨區域推論與佈建輸送量的 Bedrock 基礎模型開發 AI 應用程式。應用程式須持續以低延遲服務歐洲及北美使用者，且歐洲使用者資料必須留在歐洲 AWS 區域內。測試時，區域流量突增達服務配額，造成服務下降。公司需要維持韌性並盡量降低維運複雜度的方案。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在北美及歐洲區域部署個別 Bedrock 執行個體，用自訂路由層依使用者位置分流。設定 CloudWatch 警報監控區域服務用量，接近門檻時以 SNS 寄信通知公司。","B":"呼叫 InvokeModel API 時，在設定檔 ID 指定地理代碼，使用 Bedrock 跨區域推論設定檔。設定個別 API Gateway HTTP API，將歐洲及北美使用者導向適當區域端點。","C":"部署多區域 API Gateway HTTP API 及實作重試邏輯的 Lambda 函數處理節流。主要區域達配額時，讓函數在最近的次要區域呼叫模型，以智慧路由確保資料落地合規。","D":"在多區域設定 Bedrock 佈建輸送量，在應用程式實作節流時切換區域的容錯移轉邏輯，並使用 Global Accelerator 依使用者位置路由至適當端點。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Geographic inference profiles route across supported Regions within a defined geography such as EU or US, reducing custom failover logic. Use the appropriate geographic profile rather than a global profile, and verify all destination Regions against the residency boundary. Configure IAM/SCP access and geography-specific routing. Cross-Region inference improves available capacity but still has quotas and does not guarantee a fixed latency.","explanation_zh":"地理推論設定檔在 EU、US 等明確地理範圍內的支援區域間路由，減少自訂容錯移轉邏輯。須使用相符的地理設定檔而非全球設定檔，並檢查所有目的地區域是否符合資料落地邊界。也須設定 IAM/SCP 權限及依地理位置分流。跨區域推論提高可用容量，但仍受配額限制，也不保證固定延遲。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Email alerts do not redistribute traffic or provide automated capacity resilience.","why_zh":"電子郵件警報不會重新分配流量或提供自動容量韌性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Custom retry and Region selection add operations compared with managed geographic profiles.","why_zh":"自訂重試及區域選擇比託管地理設定檔增加維運。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Provisioning in multiple Regions and custom failover add fixed capacity management and routing complexity.","why_zh":"多區域佈建及自訂容錯增加固定容量管理與路由複雜度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.970375+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":72,"question_en":"An international company is building an AI assistant that uses RAG. The company wants the AI assistant to have near real-time, low-latency performance. The AI assistant must provide service to several geographic areas. The company's customers will use proprietary data with the AI assistant. The proprietary data must not leave the company's immediate geographic area. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region model inference profile. Create Amazon S3 buckets in each AWS Region the company operates in. Store a knowledge base in each respective S3 bucket. In each Region, configure Amazon Kendra to interact with the respective knowledge base. In each Region, configure an AWS Lambda function that uses Kendra and Amazon Bedrock to process AI assistant prompts.","B":"Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model in each AWS Region the company operates in. Configure an Amazon Bedrock cross-Region model inference profile. Configure a vector database that uses Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Store the knowledge bases in Amazon S3 in each Region the company operates in.","C":"Use AWS Outposts to deploy an outpost in each AWS Region the company operates in. Create Amazon S3 buckets to store knowledge bases in each corresponding Region. Deploy Amazon RDS configured as a vector database to each outpost. Deploy an Amazon Bedrock model with a cross-Region inference profile in a central Region.","D":"Configure a knowledge base stored in the Amazon S3 Express One Zone storage class in each AWS Local Zone the company operates in. Use Amazon RDS to deploy a vector database in each Local Zone the company operates in. Deploy a large language model (LLM) to Amazon EC2 instances in each Local Zone. Configure the AI assistant to route prompts to the model in the respective Local Zone."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":63,"D":38},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":72,"pages":[140,141]},"question_zh":"一家跨國公司建立使用 RAG 的 AI 助理，希望近乎即時、低延遲服務多個地理區域。客戶會向助理提供專有資料，該資料不得離開公司當地的地理範圍。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"部署使用跨區域模型推論設定檔的 Bedrock 模型，在公司營運的各 AWS 區域建立 S3 儲存貯體並存放各自知識庫。各區域設定 Kendra 與對應知識庫互動，再設定 Lambda 使用 Kendra 及 Bedrock 處理助理提示。","B":"在公司營運的每個 AWS 區域部署 Bedrock 模型，設定 Bedrock 跨區域模型推論設定檔及使用 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 的向量資料庫，並在各區域 S3 存放知識庫。","C":"使用 Outposts 在公司營運的每個 AWS 區域部署 Outpost，在對應區域建立存放知識庫的 S3 儲存貯體。於各 Outpost 部署設定為向量資料庫的 RDS，並在中央區域部署使用跨區域推論設定檔的 Bedrock 模型。","D":"在公司營運的每個 AWS Local Zone，以 S3 Express One Zone 儲存類別存放知識庫，並於各 Local Zone 使用 RDS 部署向量資料庫。將大型語言模型部署至各 Local Zone 的 EC2 執行個體，讓助理將提示路由至對應 Local Zone 模型。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B is the intended managed RAG design only if each inference profile is geographic and all its destinations lie inside the permitted boundary. The wording does not specify this: a generic cross-Region profile can send prompts outside the source Region, and a global profile is unsuitable for the stated restriction. S3 stores source documents; the retrieval index resides in a supported vector store, not simply a knowledge base inside a bucket. If immediate geographic area means a single Region or locality, B does not satisfy it as written.","explanation_zh":"B 只有在各推論設定檔皆為地理設定檔，且全部目的地位於允許邊界內時，才是題目預期的託管 RAG 設計。原文未限定這點：一般跨區域設定檔可能將提示送出來源區域，全球設定檔更不適用。S3 儲存來源文件；檢索索引位於受支援向量儲存區，不能簡化為貯體內的知識庫。若當地地理範圍指單一區域或城市，B 依原文不符合要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Kendra adds a separate retrieval integration and the same unspecified cross-Region residency issue remains.","why_zh":"Kendra 增加獨立檢索整合，且仍有跨區域資料邊界未明的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Central inference exports prompts from local sites; Outposts placement and cloud-region terminology are also imprecise.","why_zh":"中央推論會將提示送出當地，且 Outposts 部署位置與雲端區域用語不精確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Express One Zone is an Availability Zone-scoped regional storage class, not automatically a storage service in every Local Zone; the option also adds self-managed models.","why_zh":"S3 Express One Zone 是以可用區為範圍的區域儲存類別，並非每個 Local Zone 都有的儲存服務，且選項增加自管模型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/directory-bucket-high-performance.html"],"issues":["geographic_boundary_underspecified","S3_source_not_vector_index"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.971356+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company is building a generative AI (GenAI) application that processes financial reports and provides summaries for analysts. The application must run two compute environments. In one environment, AWS Lambda function must use the Python SDK to analyze reports on demand. In the second environment, Amazon EKS containers must use the JavaScript SDK to batch process multiple reports on a schedule. The application must maintain conversational context throughout multi-tum interactions, use the same foundation model (FM) across environments, and ensure consistent authentication. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel API with a separate authentication method for each environment. Store conversation states in Amazon DynamoDB. Use custom I/O formatting logic for each programming language.","B":"Use the Amazon Bedrock Converse API directly in both environments with a common authentication mechanism that uses IAM roles. Store conversation states in Amazon ElastiCache. Creating programming language-specific wrappers for model parameters.","C":"Create a centralized Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoint that handles all model interactions by using the InvokeModel API. Store interaction history in application process memory in each Lambda function or EKS container. Use environment variables to configure model parameters.","D":"Use the Amazon Bedrock Converse API and IAM roles for authentication. Pass previous messages in the request messages array to maintain conversational context. Use programming language-specific SDKs to establish consistent API interfaces."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":73,"pages":[142,143]},"question_zh":"一家公司建立處理財務報告並向分析師提供摘要的生成式 AI 應用程式。應用程式需執行於兩種運算環境：其一由 Lambda 函數使用 Python SDK 隨需分析報告，其二由 EKS 容器使用 JavaScript SDK 排程批次處理多份報告。應用程式須在多輪互動維持對話脈絡，兩環境使用相同基礎模型，並確保一致驗證。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Bedrock InvokeModel API，為每個環境採用不同驗證方法，將對話狀態存於 DynamoDB，並為每種語言使用自訂輸入/輸出格式邏輯。","B":"兩環境直接使用 Bedrock Converse API，以 IAM 角色提供共通驗證機制，將對話狀態存於 ElastiCache，並為模型參數建立語言專屬包裝程式。","C":"建立集中式 API Gateway REST API 端點，以 InvokeModel API 處理全部模型互動。將互動歷史存於各 Lambda 或 EKS 容器的應用程式程序記憶體，並以環境變數設定模型參數。","D":"使用 Bedrock Converse API 及 IAM 角色驗證，在請求 messages 陣列傳入先前訊息以維持對話脈絡，使用各程式語言 SDK 建立一致 API 介面。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Converse exposes a consistent messages-based interface across supported models and SDK languages. Use the same modelId and IAM role-based credentials in Lambda and EKS, with least-privilege policies for each workload identity. Bedrock does not persist conversation content for this API: the application must retain history and send previous messages on subsequent turns. D states this essential context mechanism directly.","explanation_zh":"Converse 對支援模型及不同語言 SDK 提供一致的 messages 介面。Lambda 與 EKS 使用相同 modelId 和 IAM 角色憑證，並為各工作負載身分配置最小權限。Bedrock 不會為此 API 保存對話內容；應用程式須保留歷史，並在後續輪次傳入先前訊息。D 直接交代這個關鍵脈絡機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Separate authentication and custom formatting conflict with the requested consistency.","why_zh":"不同驗證方式與自訂格式不利於所要求的一致性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"External state storage is valid, but the option omits replaying history and adds unnecessary model-parameter wrappers.","why_zh":"外部狀態儲存可行，但此項未說明重送歷史，且增加不必要的模型參數包裝。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Process memory is not durable/shared across Lambda invocations and container replicas.","why_zh":"程序記憶體無法在不同 Lambda 呼叫與容器副本間提供持久共用狀態。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/conversation-inference.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.972300+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is building a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions to help students around the world summarize notes. The application uses Anthropic Claude through Amazon Bedrock. The company observed that most of the traffic occurs during evenings in each time zone. Users report experiencing throttling errors during peak usage times in their times zones. The company needs to resolve the throttling issues by ensuring continuous operation of the application. The solution must maintain application performance quality. The company needs a solution that does not require a fixed hourly cost during low traffic periods. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set provisioned throughput to a value that is safely higher than the peak traffic observed.","B":"Create custom Amazon CloudWatch metrics to monitor model errors. Set up a failover mechanism to redirect invocations to a backup AWS Region when the errors exceed a specified threshold.","C":"Enable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor key metrics such as Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, and Invocation Throttles. Distribute traffic across cross-Region inference endpoints.","D":"Enable invocation logging in Amazon Bedrock. Monitor InvocationLatency, InvocationClientErrors, and InvocationServerErrors metrics. Distribute traffic across multiple versions of the same model."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":74,"pages":[144]},"question_zh":"一家公司建立使用 Lambda 函數的無伺服器應用程式，協助全球學生摘要筆記，並透過 Bedrock 使用 Anthropic Claude。公司發現各時區晚間流量最高，使用者在所在地尖峰期間遇到節流錯誤。公司需要解決節流並確保持續運作、維持效能品質，且低流量時不需支付固定每小時費用。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立 CloudWatch 自訂指標監控模型錯誤，將佈建輸送量設為安全高於已觀察尖峰流量的值。","B":"建立 CloudWatch 自訂指標監控模型錯誤，當錯誤超過門檻時，透過容錯機制將呼叫導向備援 AWS 區域。","C":"啟用 Bedrock 呼叫日誌，監控 Invocations、InputTokenCount、OutputTokenCount 及 Invocation Throttles 等關鍵指標，將流量分散至跨區域推論端點。","D":"啟用 Bedrock 呼叫日誌，監控 InvocationLatency、InvocationClientErrors 及 InvocationServerErrors，將流量分散至同一模型的多個版本。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Cross-Region inference profiles provide managed routing across capacity pools without committing to fixed provisioned model units. Use the same supported model/version to avoid behavior changes, monitor token quotas and InvocationThrottles, and apply bounded retries. Native metrics do not require enabling invocation logging; logs provide additional diagnostics. No architecture eliminates every throttle, and profile quotas and residency constraints still apply.","explanation_zh":"跨區域推論設定檔提供跨容量池的託管路由，不必承諾固定佈建模型單位。使用相同的支援模型及版本以避免行為變動，監控 token 配額與 InvocationThrottles，並採用有上限的重試。原生指標不需要先啟用呼叫日誌；日誌提供額外診斷。任何架構都不能消除全部節流，仍須遵守設定檔配額及資料落地限制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Provisioned capacity introduces costs during low traffic and requires sizing.","why_zh":"佈建容量在低流量時仍有費用，且須預估容量。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Custom error-triggered failover is more operational work than managed profile routing.","why_zh":"自訂依錯誤觸發的容錯移轉，比託管設定檔路由增加維運。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Changing model versions can change summary quality and does not directly address the required capacity strategy.","why_zh":"改模型版本可能改變摘要品質，也未直接解決要求的容量策略。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-runtime-metrics.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:51:57.973298+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":75,"question_en":"A company is developing a new AI-powered application that needs to integrate with various specialized tools. These tools currently run as Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers on the local machines of developers and do not maintain states between invocations. The company plans to deploy each MCP server as an AWS Lambda function to support the company's production application. The solution must be accessible to both internal applications and authorized third-party partners. The solution must use strict authentication and authorization controls. Which additional steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom Lambda invocation transport by using the Lambda Invoke API. Implement IAM authentication and grant InvokeFunction permissions to authorized users and roles.","B":"Expose the Lambda functions through Amazon API Gateway REST API endpoints. Implement API keys for authentication. Configure the applications that need to access the MCP servers to use standard HTTP requests instead of the MCP protocol.","C":"Create Lambda function URLs and enable a custom Streamable HTTP transport and SigV4. Implement AWS IAM authentication. Grant InvokeFunctionUrl permissions to authorized users and roles.","D":"Expose the Lambda function through Amazon API Gateway HTTP API endpoints with the Streamable HTTP transport. Use Amazon Cognito to implement OAuth authentication. Configure API Gateway to validate OAuth tokens."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":63,"D":25,"A":13},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":75,"pages":[145,146]},"question_zh":"一家公司開發需整合各種專業工具的新 AI 應用程式。目前工具在開發者本機以 Model Context Protocol（MCP）伺服器執行，呼叫間不保留狀態。公司計畫將每個 MCP 伺服器部署成 Lambda 函數供正式應用程式使用，須讓內部應用程式及獲授權第三方夥伴存取，並採嚴格身分驗證與授權。哪些額外步驟可用最少維運工作滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Lambda Invoke API 建立自訂 Lambda 呼叫傳輸層，實作 IAM 驗證並授予獲授權使用者及角色 InvokeFunction 權限。","B":"透過 API Gateway REST API 端點公開 Lambda 函數，以 API 金鑰驗證，讓需要存取 MCP 伺服器的應用程式改用標準 HTTP 請求而非 MCP 協定。","C":"建立 Lambda 函數 URL，啟用自訂 Streamable HTTP 傳輸層及 SigV4，實作 AWS IAM 驗證，授予獲授權使用者及角色 InvokeFunctionUrl 權限。","D":"透過 API Gateway HTTP API 端點與 Streamable HTTP 傳輸層公開 Lambda 函數，使用 Cognito 實作 OAuth 驗證，設定 API Gateway 驗證 OAuth token。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"D is the more complete managed access design for internal clients and authorized third-party partners: Cognito issues OAuth tokens and an HTTP API JWT authorizer validates issuer, audience, expiry, and route scopes. Stateless Streamable HTTP can use ordinary JSON responses; a requirement for long-lived SSE would need separate transport/timeout validation. C is the marked answer but adds custom SigV4 client integration and omits the currently required InvokeFunction permission alongside InvokeFunctionUrl. The fewest components does not necessarily mean the least overall operational effort for partner authentication.","explanation_zh":"D 對內部用戶端及授權第三方夥伴提供較完整的託管存取設計：Cognito 簽發 OAuth token，HTTP API 的 JWT 授權器驗證簽發者、受眾、期限及路由範圍。無狀態 Streamable HTTP 可使用一般 JSON 回應；若需要長時間 SSE，則須另驗證傳輸與逾時限制。C 雖為原標答，卻增加自訂 SigV4 用戶端整合，且除 InvokeFunctionUrl 外，漏列目前必要的 InvokeFunction 權限。元件最少不一定代表夥伴驗證的整體維運最少。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A proprietary Invoke transport requires custom MCP client integration.","why_zh":"專用 Invoke 傳輸層需要自訂 MCP 用戶端整合。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"API keys are not sufficient authentication/authorization and replacing MCP breaks the requested protocol integration.","why_zh":"API 金鑰不足以提供驗證與授權，改掉 MCP 也破壞要求的協定整合。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Custom SigV4 integration increases partner-client work, and InvokeFunctionUrl alone is insufficient for current function URLs.","why_zh":"自訂 SigV4 增加夥伴用戶端整合，且目前函數 URL 僅有 InvokeFunctionUrl 權限並不足夠。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/urls-auth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-jwt-authorizer.html"],"issues":["verdict_differs_from_marked","C_missing_InvokeFunction_permission","MCP_streaming_mode_requires_validation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:55:28.757604+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌・查證與標答及社群不同"},{"id":76,"question_en":"A company has a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to provide real-time responses to customer queries. The company has noticed intermittent failures with API calls to foundation models (FMs) during peak traffic periods. The company needs a solution to handle transient errors and provide detailed observability into FM performance. The solution must prevent cascading failures during throttling events and provide distributed tracing across service boundaries to identify latency contributors. The solution must also enable correlation of performance issues with specific FM characteristics. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Implement a custom retry mechanism with a fixed delay of 1 second between retries. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the application's error rates and latency metrics.","B":"Configure the AWS SDK with standard retry mode and exponential backoff with jitter. Use AWS X-Ray tracing with annotations to identify and filter service components.","C":"Implement client-side caching of all FM responses. Add custom logging statements in the application code to record API call durations.","D":"Configure the AWS SDK with adaptive retry mode. Use AWS CloudTrail distributed tracing to monitor throttling events."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":71,"D":14,"A":14},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":76,"pages":[147,148]},"question_zh":"一家公司有使用 Bedrock 即時回答客戶問題的生成式 AI 應用程式，尖峰時呼叫基礎模型 API 偶發失敗。公司需要處理暫時性錯誤並詳細觀測模型效能，防止節流時連鎖失敗，跨服務邊界分散式追蹤以找出延遲來源，並能將效能問題與特定模型特性關聯。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"實作每次固定等待 1 秒的自訂重試機制，設定 CloudWatch 警報監控應用程式錯誤率及延遲。","B":"將 AWS SDK 設為標準重試模式，採帶抖動的指數退避，使用帶註記的 X-Ray 追蹤識別並篩選服務元件。","C":"在用戶端快取全部模型回應，在應用程式加入自訂日誌，記錄 API 呼叫時間。","D":"將 AWS SDK 設為自適應重試模式，使用 CloudTrail 分散式追蹤監控節流事件。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Standard SDK retries provide exponential backoff with jitter and retry quota protection to reduce retry storms. X-Ray traces show cross-service latency, and indexed annotations can carry modelId, model version, or relevant request characteristics. Instrument and propagate trace context across components; ordinary logs or alarms do not create distributed traces. Current AWS guidance recommends OpenTelemetry instrumentation as X-Ray SDKs enter maintenance, while the X-Ray tracing concept in B remains valid.","explanation_zh":"標準 SDK 重試提供帶抖動的指數退避與重試配額保護，減少重試風暴。X-Ray 追蹤可顯示跨服務延遲，可索引註記則可記錄 modelId、版本及相關請求特性。須在各元件實作追蹤並傳播脈絡；一般日誌或警報不會形成分散式追蹤。目前 AWS 建議在 X-Ray SDK 進入維護期後使用 OpenTelemetry 儀器化，但 B 的 X-Ray 追蹤概念仍有效。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Fixed delays synchronize retries and metrics alone cannot attribute cross-service latency.","why_zh":"固定延遲會使重試同步，只有指標無法定位跨服務延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Caching every response is unsuitable for unique/private requests and duration logs lack trace propagation.","why_zh":"快取全部回應不適用於獨特或私密請求，時間日誌也缺乏追蹤傳播。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail is API auditing, not a distributed tracing service.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 是 API 稽核服務，不是分散式追蹤服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdkref/latest/guide/feature-retry-behavior.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-sdk-python-segment.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.115940+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"社群分歧大"},{"id":77,"question_en":"A company is building a video analysis platform on AWS. The platform will analyze a large video archive by using Amazon Rekognition and Amazon Bedrock. The platform must comply with predefined privacy standards. The platform must also use secure model I/O, control foundation model (FM) access patterns, and provide an audit of who accessed what and when. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Implement Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter harmful or unauthorized content in prompts and responses. Use Amazon Bedrock trace events to track all agent and model invocations for auditing purposes. Export the traces to Amazon CloudWatch Logs as an audit record of model usage. Store all prompts and outputs in Amazon S3 with server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).","B":"Define access control by using IAM with attribute-based controls to map departments to specific permissions. Configure VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock model API calls. Use IAM condition keys to enforce specific GuardrailIdentifier and ModelId values. Configure AWS CloudTrail to capture management and data events for S3 objects and KMS key usage activities. Enable S3 server access logging to record detailed file-level interactions with the video archives. Send all CloudTrail logs to AWS CloudTrail Lake. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to detect and alert on unexpected activity from Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Rekognition, and AWS KMS.","C":"Restrict access to services by using VPC endpoint policies. Use AWS Config to track resource changes and compliance with security rules. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt data at rest. Store the model's I/O in separate Amazon S3 buckets. Enable S3 server access logging to track file-level interactions.","D":"Configure AWS CloudTrail Insights to analyze API call patterns across accounts and detect anomalous activity in Amazon Bedrock, Amazon Rekognition, Amazon S3, and AWS KMS. Deploy Amazon Macie to scan and classify the video archive. Use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt all stored data. Configure CloudTrail to capture KMS API usage events for audit purposes. Configure Amazon EventBridge rules to process CloudTrail Insights anomalies and Macie findings. Use CloudWatch alarms to trigger automated notifications and security responses when potential security issues are detected."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":77,"pages":[149,150]},"question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 建立影片分析平台，使用 Rekognition 及 Bedrock 分析大型影片封存。平台須遵守預定隱私標準，安全處理模型輸入/輸出、控制基礎模型存取模式，並稽核誰在何時存取什麼。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為 Bedrock 模型 API 呼叫設定 VPC 端點，以 Bedrock Guardrails 篩除提示及回應中的有害或未授權內容。使用 Bedrock 追蹤事件追蹤所有代理及模型呼叫並匯出至 CloudWatch Logs 作為模型用量稽核紀錄。將所有提示及輸出以 SSE-KMS 加密存至 S3。","B":"使用具屬性型控制的 IAM 將部門對應至特定權限，為 Bedrock API 設定 VPC 端點，使用 IAM 條件鍵強制特定 GuardrailIdentifier 及 ModelId 值。設定 CloudTrail 擷取 S3 物件及 KMS 金鑰使用活動的管理與資料事件，啟用 S3 伺服器存取日誌記錄影片封存檔案層級互動。將所有 CloudTrail 日誌送至 CloudTrail Lake，設定 CloudWatch 警報偵測並通知 Bedrock、Rekognition 與 KMS 的非預期活動。","C":"使用 VPC 端點政策限制服務存取，以 AWS Config 追蹤資源變更及安全規則合規。使用 SSE-KMS 加密靜態資料，將模型輸入/輸出分存於不同 S3 貯體，啟用 S3 伺服器存取日誌追蹤檔案互動。","D":"設定 CloudTrail Insights 分析跨帳戶 API 模式，偵測 Bedrock、Rekognition、S3 與 KMS 異常。部署 Macie 掃描並分類影片封存，對全部儲存資料採 SSE-KMS，讓 CloudTrail 擷取 KMS API 使用事件供稽核。以 EventBridge 處理 Insights 異常與 Macie 發現，再用 CloudWatch 警報觸發自動通知及安全回應。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B combines identity authorization, private API access, guardrail enforcement, and resource access auditing. GuardrailIdentifier is a documented condition key; restrict approved model resources through their ARNs rather than assuming a universal ModelId condition key. CloudTrail identifies API actors/times, but model-content/decision auditing additionally requires invocation/application logs; S3 data events must be explicitly enabled. Macie does not interpret raw video content for privacy classification, and guardrails are not an authorization substitute.","explanation_zh":"B 結合身分授權、私有 API 存取、防護措施強制及資源存取稽核。GuardrailIdentifier 是文件記載條件鍵；核准模型應透過資源 ARN 限制，不能假設有通用 ModelId 條件鍵。CloudTrail 記錄 API 操作者及時間，但模型內容/決策稽核另需呼叫或應用程式日誌，S3 資料事件也須明確啟用。Macie 不會理解原始影片內容來作隱私分類，防護措施也不能取代授權。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Agent traces do not automatically cover all direct model calls or establish department authorization.","why_zh":"代理追蹤不會自動涵蓋全部直接模型呼叫，也未建立部門授權。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Configuration and storage controls omit explicit model/guardrail enforcement and full identity-aware service auditing.","why_zh":"設定與儲存控制缺少明確模型/防護強制與完整身分服務稽核。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Anomaly detection is not preventive access control, and Macie is not a raw-video content classifier.","why_zh":"異常偵測不是預防存取控制，Macie 也不是原始影片內容分類器。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-permissions-id.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.html"],"issues":["ModelId_condition_key_imprecise","CloudTrail_not_model_content_log"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:05:07.223087+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":78,"question_en":"An insurance company uses existing Amazon SageMaker AI infrastructure to support a web-based application that allows customers to predict what their insurance premiums will be. The company stores customer data that is used to train the SageMaker AI model in an Amazon S3 bucket. The dataset is growing rapidly. The company wants a solution to continuously re-train the model. The solution must automatically re-train and re-deploy the model to the application when an employee uploads a new customer data file to the S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Glue to run an ETL job on each uploaded file. Configure the ETL job to use the AWS SDK to invoke the Sage Maker AI model endpoint. Use real-time inference with the endpoint to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function and webhook handlers to generate an event when an employee uploads a new file. Configure SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it is re-trained on the updated customer dataset. Use Amazon EventBridge to create an event bus. Set the Lambda function event as the source and SageMaker Pipelines as the target.","C":"Create an AWS Step Functions Express workflow with AWS SDK integrations to retrieve the customer data from the S3 bucket when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a SageMaker Data Wrangler flow to export the data from the S3 bucket to SageMaker Autopilot. Use SageMaker Autopilot to re- deploy the model after it has been re-trained on the updated customer dataset.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions Standard workflow. Configure the first state to call an AWS Lambda function to respond when an employee uploads a new file to the S3 bucket. Use a pipeline in SageMaker Pipelines to re-deploy the model after it has been re-trained on the updated customer dataset. Use the next state in the workflow to run the pipeline when the first state receives a response."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":78,"B":22},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":78,"pages":[151,152]},"question_zh":"一家保險公司以現有 SageMaker AI 基礎設施支援網頁應用程式，讓客戶預測保費。訓練模型的客戶資料存於 S3，資料集快速成長。公司希望持續重訓，員工每次上傳新客戶資料檔案至 S3 時，都自動重新訓練模型並重新部署至應用程式。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"對每個上傳檔案執行 Glue ETL 工作，設定工作使用 AWS SDK 呼叫 SageMaker AI 模型端點。模型依更新資料集重新訓練後，使用端點即時推論重新部署模型。","B":"建立 Lambda 函數及 webhook 處理器，在員工上傳新檔時產生事件。設定 SageMaker Pipelines 在依更新資料集重新訓練後重新部署模型。使用 EventBridge 建立事件匯流排，以 Lambda 函數事件為來源、SageMaker Pipelines 為目標。","C":"建立使用 AWS SDK 整合的 Step Functions Express 工作流程，在員工上傳新檔至 S3 時取得客戶資料。使用 SageMaker Data Wrangler 流程將資料由 S3 匯出至 Autopilot，並以 Autopilot 在依更新資料集重訓後重新部署模型。","D":"建立 Step Functions Standard 工作流程，第一狀態呼叫 Lambda 函數以回應員工向 S3 上傳新檔。使用 SageMaker Pipelines 管線，在依更新資料集重訓後重新部署模型；當第一狀態收到回應時，下一狀態執行該管線。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"AWS explicitly documents EventBridge events, including new S3 files, starting SageMaker Pipelines. B can publish the upload event from its handler and invoke a training/evaluation/deployment pipeline; direct S3 EventBridge notification can simplify it further. D uses a valid long-running orchestrator but places upload detection inside an already-running workflow and never specifies what starts that workflow. Therefore B is better supported than the marked D; all implementations still need idempotent event handling and an explicit deployment step in the pipeline.","explanation_zh":"AWS 明確記載 EventBridge 事件（包含 S3 新檔）可啟動 SageMaker Pipelines。B 可由上傳處理器發佈事件，啟動訓練、評估及部署管線；直接使用 S3 EventBridge 通知還能更簡化。D 採用適合長時間工作的協調器，但將上傳偵測放在已啟動的工作流程內，未說明什麼事件啟動流程。因此 B 比原標答 D 更有文件依據；各實作仍須處理事件冪等性並在管線明確加入部署步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Invoking an inference endpoint neither retrains nor redeploys the model.","why_zh":"呼叫推論端點不會重訓或重新部署模型。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Express is limited to short executions and Autopilot does not by itself define a complete upload-triggered deployment workflow.","why_zh":"Express 僅支援短時間執行，Autopilot 本身也未定義完整上傳觸發部署流程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Standard workflows can orchestrate training, but a first-state Lambda cannot itself be the missing trigger that starts the workflow.","why_zh":"Standard 流程可協調訓練，但第一狀態 Lambda 不能自行取代缺漏的流程啟動事件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipeline-eventbridge.html"],"issues":["verdict_differs_from_marked","D_missing_workflow_trigger"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.118566+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定需斟酌・查證與標答及社群不同"},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Bedrock to implement a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)-based system to serve medical information to users. The company needs to compare multiple chunking strategies, evaluate the generation quality of two foundation models (FMs), and enforce quality thresholds for deployment. Which Amazon Bedrock evaluation configuration will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a retrieve-only evaluation job that uses a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet as the evaluator model. Configure metrics for context relevance and context coverage. Define deployment thresholds in a separate CI/CD pipeline.","B":"Create a retrieve-and-generate evaluation job that uses custom precision at k metrics and an LLM-as-a- judge metric that uses a scale of 1-5. Include each chunking strategy in the evaluation dataset. Use a supported version of Anthropic Claude Sonnet to evaluate responses from both FMs.","C":"Create a separate evaluation job for each chunking strategy and FM combination. Use Amazon Bedrock built-in metrics for correctness and completeness. Manually review scores before deployment approval.","D":"Set up a pipeline that uses multiple retrieve-only evaluation jobs to assess retrieval quality. Create separate evaluation jobs for both FMs that use Amazon Nova Pro as the LLM-as-a-judge model. Evaluate based on faithfulness and citation precision metrics."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":79,"pages":[153]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Bedrock 實作 RAG 系統，向使用者提供醫學資訊。公司需要比較多種分塊策略、評估兩個基礎模型的生成品質，並強制部署品質門檻。哪個 Bedrock 評估設定符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立僅檢索評估工作，使用支援版本的 Anthropic Claude Sonnet 作為評估模型，設定脈絡相關性及脈絡涵蓋率指標，另在 CI/CD 管線定義部署門檻。","B":"建立檢索並生成評估工作，使用自訂 precision at k 指標及 1–5 分的 LLM 評審指標，將每種分塊策略納入評估資料集，並以支援版本的 Claude Sonnet 評估兩個模型的回應。","C":"為每種分塊策略及基礎模型組合建立個別評估工作，使用 Bedrock 內建正確性與完整性指標，在批准部署前人工審查分數。","D":"建立管線，以多個僅檢索工作評估檢索品質，再為兩個基礎模型建立個別評估工作，使用 Amazon Nova Pro 作為 LLM 評審，依忠實度與引用精確度評估。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"C is the most directly executable comparison: separate RAG configurations for each chunking/model combination, the same test set, and a scored approval gate. The evaluation API permits one ragConfigs item per job; merely listing chunking strategies in a dataset does not switch the underlying chunked indexes or generator models. B is the intended custom-metric answer but omits how to produce and separate those configurations and how to enforce deployment thresholds. A manual approval in C can enforce explicit thresholds because the question does not require an automated gate; automation can be added in CI/CD.","explanation_zh":"C 是最直接可執行的比較方式：每個分塊/模型組合使用個別 RAG 設定、相同測試集及依分數批准的關卡。評估 API 每工作僅允許一個 ragConfigs；只在資料集列出分塊策略，不會切換底層分塊索引或生成模型。B 是題目預期的自訂指標方案，但未說明如何產生並區分這些設定，也未說明如何強制部署門檻。題幹未要求自動關卡，因此 C 的人工批准可套用明確門檻；也可另在 CI/CD 自動化。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Retrieve-only evaluation cannot assess either generator model output.","why_zh":"僅檢索評估無法評估生成模型輸出。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Custom judge scales are supported, but dataset entries alone do not implement multiple chunking/model configurations or a deployment gate.","why_zh":"自訂評審量表受支援，但資料集項目本身不會實作多種分塊/模型設定或部署關卡。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Splitting retrieval and model evaluation can work, but this option omits the per-chunking generation comparison and explicit deployment threshold gate.","why_zh":"拆分檢索及模型評估可行，但此項未交代各分塊下的生成比較與明確部署門檻。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-evaluation-create-randg-custom.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_EvaluationInferenceConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-eval-llm-results.html"],"issues":["verdict_differs_from_marked","B_dataset_not_configuration_switch"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.119650+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・查證與標答及社群不同"},{"id":80,"question_en":"A wildlife conservation agency operates zoos globally. The agency uses various sensors, trackers, and audiovisual recorders to monitor animal behavior. The agency wants to launch a generative AI (GenAI) assistant that can ingest multimodal data to study animal behavior. The GenAI assistant must support natural language queries, avoid speculative behavioral interpretations, and maintain audit logs for ethical research audits. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Ingest raw videos into Amazon Rekognition to detect animal postures and expressions. Use Amazon Data Firehose to stream sensor and GPS data into an Amazon S3 data lake. Prompt an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM) by using basic templates that are stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Use IAM policies to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail for audit logging.","B":"Use Amazon SageMaker Processing and Amazon Transcribe to pre-process multimodal data. Ingest summaries into an Amazon Bedrock Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) knowledge base. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to restrict speculative outputs. Use AWS AppConfig to manage prompt templates. Use AWS CloudTrail to log research activity for audits.","C":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Serverless to index behavioral logs and telemetry events. Use Amazon Comprehend to extract entities. Use Amazon Bedrock to build a layer to answer questions. Embed study summaries into OpenSearch Serverless documents. Use IAM to control access. Use AWS CloudTrail to log user interactions with the AI assistant.","D":"Configure Amazon Q Business to federate data across Amazon S3, Amazon Kinesis, and Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. Configure Amazon EventBridge to invoke data ingestion jobs. Use custom AWS Lambda functions to filter large language model (LLM) outputs for ethical compliance before returning results to users."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":80,"pages":[154,155]},"question_zh":"一家野生動物保育機構在全球經營動物園，以各種感測器、追蹤器及影音記錄器監測動物行為。機構希望推出可擷取多模態資料以研究動物行為的生成式 AI 助理。助理須支援自然語言查詢、避免臆測式行為解釋，並保留日誌供研究倫理稽核。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將原始影片送至 Rekognition 偵測動物姿態及表情，以 Data Firehose 將感測器及 GPS 資料串流至 S3 資料湖。使用存於 Systems Manager Parameter Store 的基本範本提示 Bedrock 模型，以 IAM 政策控制存取，並使用 CloudTrail 稽核日誌。","B":"使用 SageMaker Processing 及 Transcribe 前處理多模態資料，將摘要擷取至 Bedrock RAG 知識庫，套用 Bedrock 防護措施限制臆測輸出，以 AppConfig 管理提示範本，並用 CloudTrail 記錄研究活動供稽核。","C":"以 OpenSearch Serverless 索引行為日誌及遙測事件，以 Comprehend 擷取實體，使用 Bedrock 建立問答層。將研究摘要嵌入 OpenSearch Serverless 文件，以 IAM 控制存取，並用 CloudTrail 記錄使用者與助理的互動。","D":"設定 Q Business 跨 S3、Kinesis 與 SageMaker Feature Store 聯合資料，以 EventBridge 觸發擷取工作。使用自訂 Lambda 函數，在傳回結果前依倫理合規要求篩選 LLM 輸出。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B supplies an explicit multimodal preprocessing path and RAG grounding, making it the closest architecture. Transcribe transcribes speech; it does not infer animal vocalization semantics, and specialized sensor/video interpretation still requires validated processing. Guardrails reduce specified harmful or ungrounded text but do not guarantee elimination of speculative science. CloudTrail logs API actions rather than full research conversations, so retain evidence, prompts, outputs, citations, and application identity separately for ethical audits.","explanation_zh":"B 提供明確多模態前處理與 RAG 依據，是最接近需求的架構。Transcribe 轉錄語音，不會推斷動物叫聲語意，感測器及影片專業解讀仍需經驗證的處理。防護措施可減少特定有害或無依據文字，但不保證消除臆測科學解釋。CloudTrail 記錄 API 動作而非完整研究對話，因此倫理稽核仍需另存證據、提示、輸出、引用及應用程式身分。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Generic video labels/basic prompts do not establish validated animal-behavior interpretation or output grounding controls.","why_zh":"通用影片標籤及基本提示未建立經驗證動物行為解讀或輸出依據控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Text entity extraction and indexing omit explicit multimodal processing and anti-speculation controls.","why_zh":"文字實體擷取及索引缺少明確多模態處理與避免臆測的控制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The claimed federation does not establish supported ingestion for all sources and adds custom ethical filtering.","why_zh":"所述聯合資料未建立所有來源的受支援擷取方式，且增加自訂倫理篩選。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-automated-reasoning-checks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/how-it-works.html"],"issues":["Transcribe_not_animal_vocalization_interpreter","CloudTrail_not_conversation_log","speculation_not_guaranteed_blocked"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.120896+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations with all features enabled to manage multiple AWS accounts. Employees use Amazon Bedrock across multiple accounts. The company must prevent specific topics and proprietary information from being included in prompts to Amazon Bedrock models. The company must ensure that employees can use only approved Amazon Bedrock models. The company centrally manages IAM roles for employees. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM permissions boundary for each employee's IAM role. Configure the permissions boundary to require an approved Amazon Bedrock guardrail identifier to invoke Amazon Bedrock models. Create an SCP that allows employees to use only approved models.","B":"Create an SCP that allows employees to use only approved models. Configure the SCP to require employees to specify a guardrail identifier in calls to invoke an approved model.","C":"Create an SCP that prevents an employee from invoking a model if a centrally deployed guardrail identifier is not specified in a call to the model. Create a permissions boundary on each employee's IAM role that allows each employee to invoke only approved models.","D":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create a custom Amazon Bedrock guardrail that has a block filtering policy. Use stack sets to deploy the guardrail to each account in the organization.","E":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create a custom Amazon Bedrock guardrail that has a mask filtering policy. Use stack sets to deploy the guardrail to each account in the organization."},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"BD":90,"D":10},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":81,"pages":[156,157]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用已啟用所有功能的 AWS Organizations 組織管理多帳戶。員工在多帳戶使用 Bedrock。公司須防止特定主題及專有資訊出現在傳給 Bedrock 模型的提示，並確保員工只能使用核准模型。公司集中管理員工 IAM 角色。哪兩個方案符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"為每位員工的 IAM 角色建立權限界限，要求呼叫 Bedrock 模型時使用核准的防護措施識別碼。建立 SCP，只允許員工使用核准模型。","B":"建立 SCP，只允許員工使用核准模型，並要求員工呼叫核准模型時指定防護措施識別碼。","C":"建立 SCP，在呼叫未指定中央部署的防護措施識別碼時阻止員工呼叫模型。為各員工 IAM 角色建立權限界限，只允許呼叫核准模型。","D":"使用 CloudFormation 建立採封鎖篩選政策的自訂 Bedrock 防護措施，再用 StackSets 部署至組織各帳戶。","E":"使用 CloudFormation 建立採遮蔽篩選政策的自訂 Bedrock 防護措施，再用 StackSets 部署至組織各帳戶。"},"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D deploys blocking controls and B can centrally constrain both approved model resources and the required approved guardrail/version. Merely requiring any guardrail identifier is insufficient; use an explicit approved identifier condition and prevent guardrail policy tampering. SCPs constrain permissions but do not grant them. A and C can also enforce equivalent restrictions for centrally managed roles when boundaries are protected, so BD is the most centralized intended pair rather than the only technically valid combination.","explanation_zh":"D 部署封鎖控制，B 可集中限制核准模型資源及必要的核准防護措施/版本。只要求任意防護措施識別碼並不足夠；須明確比對核准識別碼並防止政策遭修改。SCP 限制權限但不授予權限。若權限界限受保護，A、C 對中央管理角色也能提供等效限制，因此 BD 是最集中化的預期組合，並非唯一技術可行組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Protected boundaries plus SCPs can work, but spread guardrail enforcement across per-role boundaries instead of a single organization-level control.","why_zh":"受保護權限界限搭配 SCP 可行，但將防護強制分散至各角色，而非單一組織層控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is also feasible with protected boundaries, but distributes model restrictions across roles.","why_zh":"若界限受保護，此方案也可行，但將模型限制分散至各角色。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Masking sensitive entities is not a general block policy for forbidden topics and proprietary content.","why_zh":"遮蔽敏感實體不是禁止主題及專有內容的通用封鎖政策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-permissions-id.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.html"],"issues":["multiple_permission_control_pairs_viable","B_must_require_approved_guardrail"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:05:07.224243+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":82,"question_en":"A company is designing an API for a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses a foundation model (FM) that is hosted on a managed model service. The API must stream responses to reduce latency, enforce token limits to manage compute resource usage, and implement retry logic to handle model timeouts and partial responses. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Integrate an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API with an AWS Lambda function to invoke Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic for model timeouts by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations.","B":"Connect an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API directly to Amazon Bedrock. Simulate streaming by using client-side polling. Enforce token limits on the frontend. Configure retry behavior by using API Gateway integration settings.","C":"Connect an Amazon API Gateway WebSocket API to an Amazon ECS service that hosts a containerized inference server. Stream responses by using the WebSocket protocol. Enforce token limits within Amazon ECS. Handle model timeouts by using ECS task lifecycle hooks and restart policies.","D":"Integrate an Amazon API Gateway REST API with an AWS Lambda function that invokes Amazon Bedrock. Use Lambda response streaming to stream responses. Enforce token limits within the Lambda function. Implement retry logic by using Lambda and API Gateway timeout configurations."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":63,"A":37},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":82,"pages":[158,159]},"question_zh":"一家公司設計生成式 AI 應用程式 API，使用託管模型服務上的基礎模型。API 須串流回應以降低延遲，強制 token 限制管理運算用量，並實作重試處理模型逾時及部分回應。哪個方案可用最少維運工作滿足需求？","options_zh":{"A":"將 API Gateway HTTP API 與呼叫 Bedrock 的 Lambda 函數整合，使用 Lambda 回應串流傳回結果，在函數內強制 token 限制，並透過 Lambda 及 API Gateway 逾時設定實作模型逾時重試。","B":"讓 API Gateway HTTP API 直接連接 Bedrock，以用戶端輪詢模擬串流，在前端限制 token，並透過 API Gateway 整合設定配置重試。","C":"將 API Gateway WebSocket API 連至託管容器化推論伺服器的 ECS 服務，透過 WebSocket 串流回應，在 ECS 強制 token 限制，以 ECS 任務生命週期掛鉤及重新啟動政策處理模型逾時。","D":"將 API Gateway REST API 與呼叫 Bedrock 的 Lambda 函數整合，使用 Lambda 回應串流，在函數內強制 token 限制，並透過 Lambda 及 API Gateway 逾時設定實作重試。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"REST API Lambda proxy response streaming supports forwarding partial model output with managed infrastructure. Configure the response transfer mode and InvokeWithResponseStream integration, enforce input/output token budgets server-side, and implement bounded retry logic in code. Timeout settings alone do not implement retries, and once bytes are sent a failed generation cannot be transparently resumed from a chunk cursor. D is the closest managed design, with that required application-level error handling.","explanation_zh":"REST API 的 Lambda 代理回應串流能以託管架構轉送部分模型輸出。須配置串流傳輸模式及 InvokeWithResponseStream 整合，在伺服器端限制輸入/輸出 token 預算，並在程式內實作有上限的重試。逾時設定本身不會實作重試，傳出位元組後也無法用區塊游標透明續傳失敗生成。D 是最接近的託管設計，但仍需上述應用層錯誤處理。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The documented API Gateway Lambda response-streaming integration is for REST APIs, not the HTTP API integration stated here.","why_zh":"文件所述 API Gateway Lambda 回應串流整合適用 REST API，非此項的 HTTP API 整合。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Polling is not streaming, and frontend-only token limits are bypassable.","why_zh":"輪詢不是串流，且僅前端 token 限制可被繞過。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Self-managed container inference adds operations, and task restarts are not request-level partial-response retries.","why_zh":"自管容器推論增加維運，任務重啟也不是請求層部分回應重試。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/response-transfer-mode-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_ConverseStream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/response-transfer-mode.html"],"issues":["timeouts_not_retry_implementation","partial_stream_not_resumable"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.071487+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":83,"question_en":"A retail company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a customer service AI assistant. Analysis shows that 70% of customer inquiries are simple product questions that a smaller model can effectively handle. However, 30% of inquiries are complex return policy questions that require advanced reasoning. The company wants to implement a cost-effective model selection framework to automatically route customer inquiries to appropriate models based on inquiry complexity. The framework must maintain high customer satisfaction and minimize response latency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST implementation effort?","options_en":{"A":"Create a multi-stage architecture that uses a small foundation model (FM) to classify the complexity of each inquiry. Route simple inquiries to a smaller, more cost-effective model. Route complex inquiries to a larger, more capable model. Use AWS Lambda functions to handle the routing logic.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock intelligent prompt routing to automatically analyze inquiries. Route simple product inquiries to smaller models, and route complex return policy inquiries to more capable larger models.","C":"Implement a single-model solution that uses an Amazon Bedrock mid-sized foundation model (FM) with on-demand pricing. Include special instructions in model prompts to handle both simple and complex inquiries by using the same model.","D":"Create separate Amazon Bedrock endpoints for simple and complex inquiries. Implement a rule-based routing system based on keyword detection. Use on-demand pricing for the smaller model and provisioned throughput for the larger model."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":83,"pages":[160]},"question_zh":"一家零售公司使用 Bedrock 建立客服助理。分析顯示 70% 客戶問題為小模型可有效處理的簡單商品問題，30% 為需要進階推理的複雜退貨政策問題。公司希望建立具成本效益的模型選擇框架，依複雜度自動路由至適合模型，維持高滿意度並盡量降低回應延遲。哪個方案實作工作最少？","options_zh":{"A":"建立多階段架構，先以小型基礎模型分類各問題複雜度，將簡單問題導向較小低成本模型，複雜問題導向較大高能力模型，以 Lambda 處理路由邏輯。","B":"使用 Bedrock 智慧提示路由自動分析問題，將簡單商品問題導向較小模型，複雜退貨政策問題導向較大高能力模型。","C":"使用 Bedrock 中型模型的隨需定價建立單模型方案，在提示加入特殊指示，讓同一模型處理簡單與複雜問題。","D":"為簡單與複雜問題建立個別 Bedrock 端點，依關鍵字規則路由。小模型採隨需定價，大模型採佈建輸送量。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Intelligent prompt routing provides a managed endpoint that predicts response quality and chooses between supported models within a family. It removes the bespoke classifier and routing code required by A or D. Supported model pairs, Regions, and English-optimized behavior must be validated against the workload. Routing predicts quality rather than guaranteeing a fixed 70/30 split, perfect satisfaction, or minimum latency for every query.","explanation_zh":"智慧提示路由提供託管端點，預測回應品質並在同一模型系列的支援模型間選擇，省去 A 或 D 的自訂分類器與路由程式。須依工作負載驗證模型配對、區域及偏重英文的最佳化行為。路由預測品質，不保證固定 70/30 分流、完美滿意度或每次查詢最低延遲。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Custom classification and Lambda routing require more implementation.","why_zh":"自訂分類與 Lambda 路由需要較多實作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"One model does not implement complexity-based model selection.","why_zh":"單一模型未實作依複雜度選擇模型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keyword rules require maintenance and poorly capture semantic reasoning complexity.","why_zh":"關鍵字規則需要維護，也難充分判斷語意推理複雜度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-routing.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.124455+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":84,"question_en":"A specialty coffee company has a mobile app that generates personalized coffee roast profiles by using Amazon Bedrock with a three-stage prompt chain. The prompt chain converts user inputs into structured metadata, retrieves relevant logs for coffee roasts, and generates a personalized roast recommendation for each customer. Users in multiple AWS Regions report inconsistent roast recommendations for identical inputs, slow inference during the retrieval step, and unsafe recommendations such as brewing at excessively high temperatures. The company must improve the stability of outputs for repeated inputs. The company must also improve app performance and the safety of the app's outputs. The updated solution must ensure 99.5% output consistency for identical inputs and achieve inference latency of less than 1 second. The solution must also block unsafe or hallucinated recommendations by using validated safety controls. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy Amazon Bedrock with provisioned throughput to stabilize inference latency. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails that have semantic denial rules to block unsafe outputs. Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to manage prompts by using approval workflows.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Agents to manage chaining. Log model inputs and outputs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use logs from Amazon CloudWatch to perform A/B testing for prompt versions.","C":"Cache prompt results in Amazon ElastiCache. Use AWS Lambda functions to pre-process metadata and to trace end-to-end latency. Use AWS X-Ray to identify and remediate performance bottlenecks.","D":"Use Amazon Kendra to improve roast log retrieval accuracy. Store normalized prompt metadata within Amazon DynamoDB. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate multistep prompts."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":84,"pages":[162,163]},"question_zh":"一家精品咖啡公司有行動應用程式，使用 Bedrock 的三階段提示鏈產生個人化烘焙設定：將輸入轉為結構化中繼資料、檢索相關烘焙紀錄，再產生個人化建議。多個 AWS 區域使用者回報相同輸入卻得到不一致建議、檢索步驟推論緩慢，以及例如過高沖煮溫度的不安全建議。公司須改善重複輸入的輸出穩定性、效能及安全。更新後相同輸入的輸出一致率須達 99.5%，推論延遲低於 1 秒，並以經驗證安全控制封鎖不安全或幻覺建議。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"部署具佈建輸送量的 Bedrock 以穩定推論延遲，套用有語意拒絕規則的 Bedrock 防護措施封鎖不安全輸出，使用 Bedrock Prompt Management 透過批准流程管理提示。","B":"使用 Bedrock Agents 管理提示鏈，將模型輸入/輸出記錄至 CloudWatch Logs，再以日誌對提示版本進行 A/B 測試。","C":"在 ElastiCache 快取提示結果，以 Lambda 前處理中繼資料並追蹤端到端延遲，使用 X-Ray 找出並修正效能瓶頸。","D":"使用 Kendra 改善烘焙紀錄檢索準確性，將正規化提示中繼資料存於 DynamoDB，以 Step Functions 協調多步驟提示。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A is the intended answer because it includes capacity, prompt governance, and safety controls, but no option guarantees the stated 99.5% consistency and subsecond end-to-end latency. Provisioned throughput reserves capacity, not deterministic outputs or a latency SLA. Denied topics do not reliably enforce numeric brewing-temperature limits or eliminate hallucinations; validate explicit rules and use suitable grounding/reasoning checks with application rejection logic. Prompt Management versioning also does not by itself create an approval workflow, which must be implemented separately.","explanation_zh":"A 是預期答案，因為涵蓋容量、提示治理及安全控制，但沒有選項保證 99.5% 一致性及低於一秒的端到端延遲。佈建輸送量保留容量，不提供確定性輸出或延遲 SLA。拒絕主題無法可靠強制沖煮溫度數值界限或消除幻覺；須驗證明確規則，採適當依據/推理檢查並在應用層拒絕不合格結果。Prompt Management 版本管理本身也不會產生批准流程，須另外實作。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Tracing and A/B testing diagnose quality but do not enforce deterministic safety or latency targets.","why_zh":"追蹤及 A/B 測試用於診斷品質，不會強制確定性安全或延遲目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Caching can stabilize repeated outputs and latency, but without safety validation it can cache unsafe recommendations.","why_zh":"快取可穩定重複輸出及延遲，但未經安全驗證時也可能快取不安全建議。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Retrieval and orchestration improvements omit explicit output-safety enforcement and consistency guarantees.","why_zh":"檢索及協調改善缺少明確輸出安全控制與一致性保證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prov-thru-purchase.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-automated-reasoning-checks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html"],"issues":["no_fully_correct_option","numeric_SLOs_not_guaranteed","Prompt_Management_approval_workflow_unspecified"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:05:07.224892+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":85,"question_en":"A company is developing a generative AI (GenAI) application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application will analyze patterns and relationships in the company's data. The application will process millions of new data points daily across AWS Regions in Europe, North America, and Asia before storing the data in Amazon S3. The application must comply with local data protection and storage regulations. Data residency and processing must occur within the same continent. The application must also maintain audit trails of the application's decision-making processes and provide data classification capabilities. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application in each Region with local IAM policies. Use Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference to distribute the workload. Use Amazon CloudWatch to log AI decision-making processes and data processing activities. Manually track compliance certifications across Regions.","B":"Use SCPs with AWS Organizations to manage location-specific permissions. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes. Import a custom model into Amazon Bedrock and deploy the model to each Region.","C":"Use Amazon S3 Object Lock with Region-specific S3 bucket policies. Pre-process the data points within the Region based on geographic origin before sending the data points to Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Macie to classify the data. Use AWS CloudTrail immutable logs to audit the decision-making processes.","D":"Create separate AWS accounts for each Region with individual compliance frameworks. Use Amazon SageMaker AI with custom monitoring to track model performance and compliance with data residency requirements. Create manual reports for each regulatory jurisdiction."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":85,"pages":[164,165]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Bedrock 開發分析資料模式與關係的生成式 AI 應用程式。應用程式每日在歐洲、北美及亞洲 AWS 區域處理數百萬筆新資料，再存至 S3。應用程式須符合當地資料保護與儲存規定，資料儲存及處理皆須在同一洲內，也須保留決策過程稽核軌跡並提供資料分類。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在各區域部署應用程式及當地 IAM 政策，以 Bedrock 跨區域推論分配工作負載。使用 CloudWatch 記錄 AI 決策過程與處理活動，手動追蹤各區域合規認證。","B":"使用 Organizations SCP 管理依位置區分的權限，以 CloudTrail 不可變日誌稽核決策過程。將自訂模型匯入 Bedrock 並部署至每個區域。","C":"使用 S3 Object Lock 及區域專屬貯體政策，依地理來源在區域內前處理資料，再送往 Bedrock。使用 Macie 分類資料，以 CloudTrail 不可變日誌稽核決策過程。","D":"為每個區域建立個別 AWS 帳戶及合規架構，以 SageMaker AI 自訂監控追蹤模型效能與資料落地合規，為每個監管轄區手動製作報告。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C best combines regional data handling, S3 retention protection, and Macie classification, but it does not fully establish the required controls. Object Lock prevents deletion/overwrite of protected versions; it does not enforce inference geography. Route Bedrock processing only to approved same-continent Regions and protect logs with explicit retention policies. CloudTrail audits API actions, not model decision reasoning, so application traces, evidence, prompts, and outputs must be logged separately; Macie classifies supported S3 objects after storage rather than all arbitrary streams.","explanation_zh":"C 最完整結合區域資料處理、S3 保留保護及 Macie 分類，但尚未完整建立要求的控制。Object Lock 防止受保護版本被刪除/覆寫，不會強制推論地理位置。須將 Bedrock 處理限制在同洲核准區域，並明確設定日誌保留。CloudTrail 稽核 API 動作而非模型決策推理，因此應用追蹤、證據、提示及輸出須另存；Macie 分類的是儲存後受支援的 S3 物件，而非任意串流。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Unqualified cross-Region inference may cross the permitted boundary, and no data-classification mechanism is provided.","why_zh":"未限定的跨區域推論可能跨越允許邊界，且未提供資料分類機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs can restrict Regions, but CloudTrail is not decision reasoning and custom model import does not add classification.","why_zh":"SCP 可限制區域，但 CloudTrail 不是決策推理，自訂模型匯入也未提供分類。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Separate accounts and manual reports do not supply the specified managed classification and decision audit path.","why_zh":"個別帳戶及人工報告未提供所需託管分類與決策稽核流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html"],"issues":["CloudTrail_not_reasoning_audit","residency_not_enforced_by_ObjectLock"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:58:38.126462+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":86,"question_en":"A financial services company is deploying a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock to assist customer service representatives to provide personalized investment advice to customers. The company must implement a comprehensive governance solution that follows responsible AI practices and meets regulatory requirements. The solution must detect and prevent hallucinations in recommendations. The solution must have safety controls for customer interactions. The solution must also monitor model behavior drift in real time and maintain audit trails of all prompt-response pairs for regulatory review. The company must deploy the solution within 60 days. The solution must integrate with the company's existing compliance dashboard and respond to customers within 200 ms. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to apply custom content filters and toxicity detection. Use Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation to detect hallucinations. Store prompt-response pairs in Amazon DynamoDB to capture audit trails and set a TTL. Integrate Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with the existing compliance dashboard.","B":"Deploy Amazon Bedrock and use AWS PrivateLink to access the application securely. Use AWS Lambda functions to implement custom prompt validation. Store prompt-response pairs in an Amazon S3 bucket and configure S3 Lifecycle policies. Create custom Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to monitor model performance metrics.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Agents and Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to ground responses. Use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to enforce content safety. Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to store and index prompt- responses pairs. Integrate OpenSearch Service with Amazon QuickSight to create compliance reports and to detect model behavior drift.","D":"Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect model behavior drift. Use AWS WAF to filter content. Store customer interactions in an encrypted Amazon RDS database. Use Amazon API Gateway to create custom HTTP APIs to integrate with the compliance dashboard."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":63,"C":38},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":86,"pages":[166,167]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司部署使用 Bedrock 的生成式 AI 應用程式，協助客服人員向客戶提供個人化投資建議。公司須實作遵循負責任 AI 且符合監管要求的完整治理方案，偵測並防止建議中的幻覺、提供客戶互動安全控制、即時監控模型行為漂移，並保留所有提示與回應配對供監管稽核。公司須在 60 天內部署，整合現有合規儀表板，並在 200 毫秒內回應客戶。哪個方案維運工作最少？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Bedrock 防護措施，套用自訂內容篩選及毒性偵測。使用 Bedrock Model Evaluation 偵測幻覺，將提示/回應配對存至 DynamoDB 並設定 TTL 以保留稽核軌跡，將 CloudWatch 自訂指標整合至現有合規儀表板。","B":"部署 Bedrock 並透過 PrivateLink 安全存取應用程式。使用 Lambda 自訂驗證提示，將提示/回應配對存至 S3 並設定 Lifecycle 政策，建立自訂 CloudWatch 儀表板監控模型效能。","C":"使用 Bedrock Agents 及 Knowledge Bases 為回應提供依據，以 Guardrails 強制內容安全，使用 OpenSearch Service 儲存並索引提示/回應配對，整合 QuickSight 建立合規報告並偵測模型行為漂移。","D":"使用 SageMaker Model Monitor 偵測模型行為漂移，使用 WAF 篩選內容，將客戶互動存於加密 RDS 資料庫，以 API Gateway 建立自訂 HTTP API 整合合規儀表板。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A is the intended managed-governance combination, but no answer meets every stated requirement. Bedrock evaluation jobs are offline assessments, not per-request hallucination prevention or automatic real-time drift monitors. Guardrails provide configured safety checks, while 200 ms end-to-end generation and a 60-day delivery deadline are not service guarantees. Audit retention must be defined before enabling TTL deletion, and drift/grounding checks and existing-dashboard integration require explicit design.","explanation_zh":"A 是預期的託管治理組合，但沒有答案符合全部要求。Bedrock 評估工作屬離線評估，不是逐請求幻覺防護或自動即時漂移監控。防護措施提供已設定的安全檢查，而端到端 200 毫秒生成及 60 天交付並非服務保證。啟用 TTL 刪除前須定義稽核保留期間，漂移/依據檢查及現有儀表板整合也須明確設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Private networking and custom prompt validation do not supply semantic hallucination or behavior-drift controls.","why_zh":"私有網路及自訂提示驗證未提供語意幻覺或行為漂移控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"RAG and logging help, but QuickSight reports do not inherently detect real-time drift and this adds a separate analytics stack.","why_zh":"RAG 與日誌有幫助，但 QuickSight 報告本身不會偵測即時漂移，且另增分析架構。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"WAF is not a semantic model-content guardrail and Model Monitor is not automatically attached to Bedrock invocations.","why_zh":"WAF 不是模型語意內容防護，Model Monitor 也不會自動套用於 Bedrock 呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/TTL.html"],"issues":["no_fully_correct_option","200ms_unsubstantiated","offline_evaluation_not_runtime_prevention"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.059838+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":87,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Lake Formation to set up a data lake that contains databases and tables for multiple business units across multiple AWS Regions. The company wants to use a foundation model (FM) through Amazon Bedrock to perform fraud detection. The FM must ingest sensitive financial data from the data lake. The data includes some customer personally identifiable information (PM). The company must design an access control solution that prevents PI I from appearing in a production environment. The FM must access only authorized data subsets that have PH redacted from specific data columns. The company must capture audit trails for all data access. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a separate dataset in a separate Amazon S3 bucket for each business unit and Region combination. Configure S3 bucket policies to control access based on IAM roles that are assigned to FM training instances. Use S3 access logs to track data access.","B":"Configure the FM to authenticate by using IAM roles and Lake Formation permissions based on LF-Tag expressions. Define business units and Regions as LF-Tags that are assigned to databases and tables. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access.","C":"Use direct IAM principal grants on specific databases and tables in Lake Formation. Create a custom application layer that logs access requests and further filters sensitive columns before sending data to the FM.","D":"Configure the FM to request temporary credentials from AWS STS. Access the data by using presigned S3 URLs that are generated by an API that applies business unit and Regional filters. Use AWS CloudTrail to collect comprehensive audit trails of data access."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":87,"pages":[168,169]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Lake Formation 建立資料湖，內含跨多個 AWS 區域及事業單位的資料庫與資料表，想透過 Bedrock 基礎模型偵測詐欺。模型須擷取資料湖中的敏感財務資料，其中包含客戶個人識別資訊（原文混用 PM、PI I、PH，皆指 PII）。公司須設計存取控制，防止 PII 出現在正式環境；模型只能存取已從特定欄位遮蔽 PII 的授權資料子集，且須保留所有資料存取稽核軌跡。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"為每個事業單位與區域組合，在個別 S3 貯體建立獨立資料集。設定貯體政策，依指派給模型訓練執行個體的 IAM 角色控制存取，使用 S3 存取日誌追蹤資料存取。","B":"讓模型透過 IAM 角色及以 LF-Tag 運算式為基礎的 Lake Formation 權限驗證。將事業單位及區域定義為 LF-Tag 並指派至資料庫與資料表，以 CloudTrail 收集完整資料存取稽核軌跡。","C":"在 Lake Formation 對特定資料庫與資料表直接授予 IAM 主體權限，建立自訂應用層記錄存取請求，並在資料送至模型前進一步篩除敏感欄位。","D":"讓模型向 STS 請求暫時憑證，透過會套用事業單位及區域篩選的 API 產生 S3 預先簽署 URL 以存取資料，使用 CloudTrail 收集完整資料存取稽核軌跡。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"C is the only option explicitly filtering sensitive columns before model input while recording access requests. Lake Formation data filters support column/row/cell restrictions through integrated query engines; table/database LF-Tags alone in B do not redact PII values. The application role, not the FM itself, retrieves authorized data and sends a sanitized subset to Bedrock. Secure the application path against bypass and persist its access logs alongside service audit records; filtering columns is distinct from transforming PII substrings within a column.","explanation_zh":"C 是唯一明確在送入模型前篩除敏感欄位並記錄存取請求的選項。Lake Formation 資料篩選可透過整合查詢引擎限制欄、列及儲存格；B 只有資料表/資料庫 LF-Tag，不會遮蔽 PII 值。應由應用程式角色取得授權資料並將淨化子集送至 Bedrock，而非模型本身取得資料。須防止繞過應用層，並將其存取日誌與服務稽核紀錄持久保存；篩除整欄與轉換欄內 PII 字串仍是不同操作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Bucket segregation is coarse-grained and does not remove sensitive columns.","why_zh":"貯體隔離粒度較粗，不會移除敏感欄位。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"LF-Tags on databases/tables govern access but do not perform the specified column redaction.","why_zh":"資料庫/資料表 LF-Tag 管理存取，不會執行指定欄位遮蔽。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Presigned URLs expose authorized S3 objects, not a column-redacted query result.","why_zh":"預先簽署 URL 提供授權 S3 物件，不是已遮蔽欄位的查詢結果。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/data-filtering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/tag-based-access-control.html"],"issues":["verdict_differs_from_marked","LF_tags_not_PII_redaction","source_PII_typographical_errors"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.061670+00:00"},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・查證與標答及社群不同"},{"id":88,"question_en":"A company runs a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) application that uses Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to perform regulatory compliance queries. The application uses the RetrieveAndGenerateStream API. The application retrieves relevant documents from a knowledge base that contains more than 50,000 regulatory documents, legal precedents, and policy updates. The RAG application is producing suboptimal responses because the initial retrieval often returns semantically similar but contextually irrelevant documents. The poor responses are causing model hallucinations and incorrect regulatory guidance. The company needs to improve the performance of the RAG application so it returns more relevant documents. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon SageMaker endpoint to run a fine-tuned ranking model. Use an Amazon API Gateway REST API to route requests. Configure the application to make requests through the REST API to rerank the results.","B":"Use Amazon Comprehend to classify documents and apply relevance scores. Integrate the RAG application’s reranking process with Amazon Textract to run document analysis. Use Amazon Neptune to perform graph-based relevance calculations.","C":"Implement a retrieval pipeline that uses the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases Retrieve API to perform initial document retrieval. Call the Amazon Bedrock Rerank API to rerank the results. Invoke the InvokeModelWithResponseStream operation to generate responses.","D":"Use the latest Amazon reranker model through the reranking configuration within Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases. Use the model to improve document relevance scoring and to reorder results based on contextual assessments."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":88,"pages":[170,171]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 的 RAG 應用程式查詢監管合規，呼叫 RetrieveAndGenerateStream API。知識庫有超過 50,000 份監管文件、法律判例及政策更新，但初次檢索常回傳語意相似卻與脈絡無關的文件，造成低品質回應、模型幻覺及錯誤監管指引。公司需要讓檢索文件更相關。哪個方案維運工作最少？","options_zh":{"A":"部署 SageMaker 端點執行微調排序模型，以 API Gateway REST API 路由請求，讓應用程式透過 REST API 重排序結果。","B":"使用 Comprehend 分類文件並給予相關性分數，在 RAG 重排序流程整合 Textract 文件分析，並用 Neptune 進行圖形相關性計算。","C":"實作檢索管線，先呼叫 Knowledge Bases Retrieve API，再呼叫 Bedrock Rerank API，最後使用 InvokeModelWithResponseStream 生成回應。","D":"透過 Knowledge Bases 的重排序設定使用最新 Amazon 重排序模型，以脈絡評估改善文件相關性評分並重新排列結果。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Knowledge Bases supports rerankingConfiguration directly in vector retrieval configuration, including retrieval-generation flows. The reranker assesses query-to-chunk relevance and reorders the candidates without a separately hosted ranking endpoint. D preserves the managed workflow and requires less orchestration than C. Select a supported model ARN/Region and benchmark retrieval quality; reranking cannot recover relevant documents absent from the candidate set or guarantee elimination of hallucinations.","explanation_zh":"Knowledge Bases 在向量檢索設定直接支援 rerankingConfiguration，包含檢索生成流程。重排序模型評估查詢與區塊相關性並重排候選，不必另託管排序端點。D 保留託管流程，比 C 少協調工作。須選受支援模型 ARN/區域並實測檢索品質；重排序無法找回根本沒進候選集的文件，也不保證消除幻覺。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Hosting a fine-tuned ranker and API increases operations compared with managed reranking.","why_zh":"自管微調排序器及 API 比託管重排序增加維運。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Classification, OCR, and graph services add components without implementing a simple query-aware reranking path.","why_zh":"分類、OCR 及圖形服務增加元件，未形成簡單依查詢重排的流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The APIs are valid but manually splitting retrieval, reranking, and generation adds unnecessary orchestration.","why_zh":"這些 API 有效，但手動拆開檢索、重排與生成增加不必要協調。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_KnowledgeBaseVectorSearchConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/rerank.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_RetrieveAndGenerateStream.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.062612+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":89,"question_en":"A company is developing a customer communication platform that uses an AI assistant powered by an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM). The AI assistant summarizes customer messages and generates initial response drafts. The company wants to use Amazon Comprehend to implement layered content filtering. The layered content filtering must prevent sharing of offensive content, protect customer privacy, and detect potential inappropriate advice solicitation. Inappropriate advice solicitation includes requests for unethical practices, harmful activities, or manipulative behaviors. The solution must maintain acceptable overall response times, so all pre-processing filters must finish before the content reaches the FM. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use parallel processing with asynchronous API calls. Use toxicity detection for offensive content. Use prompt safety classification for inappropriate advice solicitation. Use personally identifiable information (PII) detection without redaction.","B":"Use custom classification to build an FM that detects offensive content and inappropriate advice solicitation. Apply personally identifiable information (PII) detection as a secondary filter only when messages pass the custom classifier.","C":"Deploy a multi-stage process. Configure the process to use prompt safety classification first, then toxicity detection on safe prompts only, and finally personally identifiable information (PII) detection in streaming mode. Route flagged messages through Amazon EventBridge for human review.","D":"Use toxicity detection with thresholds configured to 0.5 for all categories. Use parallel processing for both prompt safety classification and personally identifiable information (PII) detection with entity redaction. Apply Amazon CloudWatch alarms to filter metrics."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":50,"A":38,"C":13},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":89,"pages":[172,173]},"question_zh":"一家公司建立客戶溝通平台，由 Bedrock 基礎模型驅動助理，摘要客戶訊息並產生初步回覆。公司希望以 Comprehend 實作多層內容篩選，防止分享冒犯內容、保護隱私，並偵測不適當建議徵詢，包括要求不道德作法、有害活動或操控行為。為維持可接受回應時間，所有前處理篩選必須在內容送達模型前完成。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"以非同步 API 呼叫平行處理，使用毒性偵測找冒犯內容，以提示安全分類偵測不當建議徵詢，僅偵測 PII 而不遮蔽。","B":"使用自訂分類建立可偵測冒犯內容及不當建議徵詢的基礎模型，只有通過分類的訊息才套用第二層 PII 偵測。","C":"部署多階段流程：先做提示安全分類，只有安全提示再進行毒性偵測，最後以串流模式偵測 PII。將被標示的訊息經 EventBridge 送人工審查。","D":"使用毒性偵測，所有類別門檻設為 0.5。平行執行提示安全分類及含實體遮蔽的 PII 偵測，對篩選指標套用 CloudWatch 警報。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D covers toxicity, malicious-intent classification, and actual PII removal. Await all filters before invoking the FM and apply the decision in the request path; CloudWatch alarms are observability, not inline blocking. Comprehend real-time PII detection returns entities, so low-latency redaction must be applied by the application; native redaction jobs are asynchronous. A 0.5 threshold needs evaluation, and current documentation restricts prompt safety classification to existing eligible customers and English input.","explanation_zh":"D 涵蓋毒性、惡意意圖分類及實際 PII 移除。須等待全部篩選完成才呼叫模型，並在請求路徑執行決策；CloudWatch 警報屬可觀測性，不是即時封鎖。Comprehend 即時 PII 偵測回傳實體，低延遲遮蔽須由應用程式套用；原生遮蔽工作採非同步。0.5 門檻仍須驗證，目前文件也限制提示安全分類僅供符合條件的既有客戶使用，且輸入須為英文。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Detecting PII without removing or blocking it does not protect privacy.","why_zh":"只偵測而不移除或封鎖 PII 無法保護隱私。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Comprehend custom classification is not building an FM and omits explicit redaction.","why_zh":"Comprehend 自訂分類不是建立基礎模型，且缺少明確遮蔽。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no Comprehend PII streaming API matching this claim; serial checks also increase latency.","why_zh":"沒有符合此描述的 Comprehend PII 串流 API，序列檢查也增加延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/trust-safety.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/trust-safety.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/comprehend-availability-change.html"],"issues":["synchronous_redaction_requires_application","prompt_safety_new_customer_availability_changed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.063987+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群幾乎無共識・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":90,"question_en":"A software as a service (SaaS) company is building a recommendation model that uses Amazon SageMaker AI to support an application that recommends airline cabin upgrades to customers. The company will host SageMaker AI models on Amazon Bedrock by using Amazon Bedrock Custom Model Import. Airline companies will use the application to send customized offers to customers. The model must examine the travel history of customers to help make more relevant recommendations. The company stores customer travel history data in an Amazon RDS database. The company must ensure that the application delivers consistent, relevant, and accurate results across multiple airlines and customer populations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to implement a RAG architecture to analyze customer travel history data to give the application semantic search capabilities. Use the semantic search capabilities to retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.","B":"Implement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter content. Use AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate validation workflows to reduce hallucinations.","C":"Use Amazon OpenSearch Service to implement vector searches of customer travel history embeddings. Use the vector searches to give the application the ability to perform similarity-based retrieval of booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations.","D":"Implement text-to-SQL transformations with SQL validations to accurately retrieve relevant booking patterns, preferences, and loyalty information from the RDS database. Use the results to generate personalized cabin upgrade recommendations. Apply Amazon Bedrock guardrails to filter responses. Use confidence scoring and semantic similarity searches to reduce hallucinations."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":60,"D":40},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":90,"pages":[174,175]},"question_zh":"一家 SaaS 公司使用 SageMaker AI 建立推薦模型，為應用程式推薦航空艙等升級。公司計畫透過 Bedrock Custom Model Import 託管 SageMaker AI 模型，航空公司會用應用程式向客戶傳送個人化優惠。模型須檢視客戶旅行歷史以提高推薦相關性，旅行歷史存於 RDS。公司須確保跨航空公司及客戶族群的結果一致、相關且準確。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"以 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 建立分析旅行歷史的 RAG 架構，提供語意搜尋，檢索相關訂位模式、偏好及會員忠誠資訊，產生個人化艙等升級推薦。套用 Guardrails 篩選內容，以 Step Functions 與 Lambda 協調驗證流程以減少幻覺。","B":"實作文字轉 SQL 並驗證 SQL，準確從 RDS 取得相關訂位模式、偏好及會員忠誠資訊，據此產生個人化艙等升級推薦。套用 Guardrails 篩選內容，以 Step Functions 與 Lambda 協調驗證流程以減少幻覺。","C":"使用 OpenSearch Service 對旅行歷史嵌入進行向量搜尋，透過相似性檢索訂位模式、偏好及會員忠誠資訊，產生個人化艙等升級推薦。套用 Guardrails 篩選回應，並使用信心評分與語意相似搜尋減少幻覺。","D":"實作文字轉 SQL 並驗證 SQL，準確從 RDS 取得相關訂位模式、偏好及會員忠誠資訊，據此產生個人化艙等升級推薦。套用 Guardrails 篩選回應，以信心評分與語意相似搜尋減少幻覺。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Validated SQL preserves exact structured booking, loyalty, and customer relationships better than approximate similarity retrieval. B adds explicit validation orchestration rather than treating model confidence or semantic similarity as factual proof. Enforce read-only queries, tenant/customer authorization, schema constraints, and outcome evaluation across populations. Custom Model Import accepts supported model architectures and formats, not arbitrary SageMaker recommendation models; the source assumption must be checked before deployment.","explanation_zh":"經驗證 SQL 比近似相似性檢索更能保留精確訂位、會員及客戶關係。B 加入明確驗證協調，不將模型信心或語意相似當作事實證明。仍須強制唯讀查詢、租戶/客戶授權、結構限制，並跨族群評估結果。Custom Model Import 只接受支援架構及格式，並非任意 SageMaker 推薦模型；部署前須核對原題此項假設。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Semantic retrieval is not a substitute for exact authorized relational lookups of individual travel history.","why_zh":"語意檢索不能取代個人旅行歷史的精確授權關聯查詢。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Similarity of embeddings does not guarantee the correct customer records or recommendation factuality.","why_zh":"嵌入相似度不能保證取得正確客戶紀錄或推薦事實正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Confidence and similarity scores are weaker than explicit factual/business validation workflows.","why_zh":"信心與相似度分數不如明確事實/業務驗證流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base-build-structured.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-customization-import-model.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_GenerateQuery.html"],"issues":["Custom_Model_Import_architecture_restrictions"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.065187+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop a customer support AI assistant. The AI assistant must respond to customer questions about their accounts. The AI assistant must not expose personal information in responses. The company must comply with data residency policies by ensuring that all processing occurs within the same AWS Region where each customer is located. The company wants to evaluate how effective the AI assistant is at preventing the exposure of personal information before the company makes the AI assistant available to customers. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment.","B":"Configure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply sensitive information filters. Set the guardrail to mask mode during development and testing. Switch to block mode for production deployment. Deploy a copy of the guardrail to each Region where the company operates.","C":"Configure an Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply content and topic filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development, testing, and production. Disable invocation logging for the Amazon Bedrock model.","D":"Configure a cross-Region Amazon Bedrock guardrail to apply a set of content and word filters. Set the guardrail to detect mode during development and testing. Switch to mask mode for production deployment."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":91,"pages":[176,177]},"question_zh":"一家公司使用 Bedrock 開發客服 AI 助理，回答客戶帳戶問題，且不得在回應洩漏個資。公司須遵守資料落地政策，確保所有處理都在客戶所在的同一 AWS 區域執行。公司希望在開放服務前評估助理防止個資外洩的效果。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定跨區域 Bedrock 防護措施套用敏感資訊篩選，在開發與測試時採偵測模式，正式部署改封鎖模式。","B":"設定 Bedrock 防護措施套用敏感資訊篩選，在開發與測試時採遮蔽模式，正式部署改封鎖模式，並在公司營運的每個區域部署一份防護措施。","C":"設定 Bedrock 防護措施套用內容及主題篩選，在開發、測試及正式環境皆採偵測模式，停用模型呼叫日誌。","D":"設定跨區域 Bedrock 防護措施套用內容及詞語篩選，在開發與測試時採偵測模式，正式部署改遮蔽模式。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Regional guardrail copies with sensitive-information policies and mask/block actions best match B. Test representative PII cases and false negatives; masking is a policy action, not a complete evaluation methodology. Keep both model inference and guardrail processing in the permitted Region and avoid cross-Region profiles; guardrail placement alone cannot constrain the whole application. PII detection is probabilistic, so additional authorization and data minimization remain necessary.","explanation_zh":"各區域部署具有敏感資訊政策及遮蔽/封鎖動作的防護措施，最符合 B。須測試具代表性的 PII 案例及漏判率；遮蔽是政策動作，不是完整評估方法。模型推論與防護處理都須留在核准區域，避免跨區域設定檔；只有防護措施位置不能限制整個應用程式。PII 偵測具機率性，仍需授權與資料最小化。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cross-Region guardrail processing conflicts with the strict same-Region requirement.","why_zh":"跨區域防護處理違反嚴格同區域要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Content/topic filters do not replace PII filters; detect-only does not prevent disclosure.","why_zh":"內容/主題篩選不能取代 PII 篩選，僅偵測也不防止洩漏。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Cross-Region processing violates residency, and word/content filters do not supply entity-aware PII masking.","why_zh":"跨區域處理違反落地要求，詞語/內容篩選也未提供辨識實體的 PII 遮蔽。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-use-independent-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-cross-region.html"],"issues":["whole_application_regionality_must_be_enforced"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.066228+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":92,"question_en":"A university recently digitized a collection of archival documents, academic journals, and manuscripts. The university stores the digital files in an AWS Lake Formation data lake. The university hires a GenAI developer to build a solution to allow users to search the digital files by using text queries. The solution must return journal abstracts that are semantically similar to a user's query. Users must be able to search the digitized collection based on text and metadata that is associated with the journal abstracts. The metadata of the digitized files does not contain keywords. The solution must match similar abstracts to one another based on the similarity of their text. The data lake contains fewer than 1 million files. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in the OpenSearch Neural Plugin for Amazon OpenSearch Service.","B":"Use Amazon Comprehend to extract topics from the digitized files. Store the topics and file metadata in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database. Query the abstract metadata against the data in the Aurora database.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker AI to deploy a sentence-transformer model. Use the model to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database that has the pgvector extension.","D":"Use Amazon Titan Embeddings in Amazon Bedrock to create vector representations of the digitized files. Store embeddings in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless database that has the pgvector extension."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":92,"pages":[178,179]},"question_zh":"一所大學將典藏文件、學術期刊及手稿數位化，存於 Lake Formation 資料湖，聘請生成式 AI 開發者建立文字查詢搜尋方案。方案須回傳與查詢語意相似的期刊摘要，並允許依摘要文字及相關中繼資料搜尋。中繼資料未包含關鍵字，方案須依文字相似性匹配類似摘要。資料湖少於一百萬個檔案。哪個方案維運工作最少？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Bedrock Amazon Titan Embeddings 為數位檔案建立向量表示，將嵌入存於 OpenSearch Service 的 OpenSearch Neural Plugin。","B":"使用 Comprehend 從數位檔案擷取主題，將主題與檔案中繼資料存於 Aurora PostgreSQL，對 Aurora 資料查詢摘要中繼資料。","C":"使用 SageMaker AI 部署 sentence-transformer 模型來產生數位檔案向量，將嵌入存於具 pgvector 擴充的 Aurora PostgreSQL。","D":"使用 Bedrock Titan Embeddings 為數位檔案建立向量表示，將嵌入存於具 pgvector 擴充的 Aurora PostgreSQL Serverless。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Managed Titan embeddings avoid hosting an embedding model, and Aurora Serverless with pgvector combines semantic vector search with relational metadata predicates. This fits the modest corpus without an additional self-managed embedding endpoint. Size vectors, indexes, and capacity according to measured workload; fewer than one million files is not itself a performance guarantee. Lake Formation permissions must also be propagated/enforced in the search application because copying embeddings does not automatically preserve source authorization.","explanation_zh":"託管 Titan 嵌入省去模型託管，Aurora Serverless 的 pgvector 則將語意向量搜尋與關聯中繼資料條件結合，適合此規模語料且不需另管嵌入端點。須依實測工作負載配置向量、索引及容量；少於一百萬檔案本身不是效能保證。搜尋應用程式也須傳遞/執行 Lake Formation 權限，複製嵌入不會自動保留來源授權。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Neural search is a plugin capability, not the embedding storage itself; an OpenSearch domain adds a separate search-service operation model.","why_zh":"神經搜尋是外掛功能，不是嵌入儲存本身；OpenSearch 網域增加獨立搜尋服務維運模式。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Topic labels and metadata queries do not provide direct semantic similarity between abstract text.","why_zh":"主題標籤及中繼資料查詢未提供摘要文字的直接語意相似搜尋。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hosting and scaling a sentence-transformer endpoint adds model operations compared with managed embeddings.","why_zh":"託管及擴展 sentence-transformer 端點，比託管嵌入服務增加模型維運。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rds/latest/auroraextendedcontent/aurora-faq-agentic-ai.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraPostgreSQL.VectorDB.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.067166+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":93,"question_en":"A financial services company wants to use Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to analyze call center recordings. When calls end, the call center stores recordings as MP3 files in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to generate summaries and sentiment analysis for the recordings in a structured format as soon as new files are created. The recordings average 20 MB in size. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to process the text by using Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate structured analysis output.","B":"Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to directly invoke Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate summaries and sentiment analysis in JSON format.","C":"Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow to process the recordings. Configure steps to invoke Amazon Transcribe to convert audio to text, validate job completion, and to invoke an AWS Lambda function to create a prompt to invoke Amazon Bedrock FMs to generate structured analysis output.","D":"Configure the source S3 bucket to send events to Amazon EventBridge. Create an EventBridge rule to invoke the Step Functions workflow when an object is created in the bucket.","E":"Configure the source S3 bucket to send notifications to the Step Functions workflow when an object is created in the bucket."},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{"CD":67,"AD":33},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":93,"pages":[180,181]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司希望以 Bedrock 基礎模型分析客服中心錄音。通話結束後，錄音以 MP3 存入 S3，平均大小 20 MB。公司需要新檔建立後盡快以結構化格式產生摘要及情緒分析。哪兩個方案符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Step Functions 協調錄音處理：呼叫 Transcribe 將音訊轉文字、確認工作完成，再呼叫 Lambda 使用 Bedrock 模型處理文字並產生結構化分析。","B":"使用 Step Functions 協調錄音處理：呼叫 Transcribe 將音訊轉文字、確認工作完成，再直接呼叫 Bedrock 模型以 JSON 產生摘要及情緒分析。","C":"使用 Step Functions 協調錄音處理：呼叫 Transcribe 將音訊轉文字、確認工作完成，再呼叫 Lambda 建立提示並呼叫 Bedrock 模型產生結構化分析。","D":"設定來源 S3 貯體將事件送至 EventBridge，建立規則在物件建立時啟動 Step Functions 工作流程。","E":"設定來源 S3 貯體在物件建立時直接將通知送至 Step Functions 工作流程。"},"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D supplies the documented S3 Object Created to EventBridge trigger, and C supplies a valid transcription-then-generation workflow. Keep the 20 MB audio in S3 and pass object references, not raw audio through Step Functions state payloads. A is effectively equivalent to C, and B is also supported because Step Functions has a native Bedrock InvokeModel integration, including S3 input/output references. Thus CD is a valid marked pair but the question has multiple valid pairs; validate JSON output and handle duplicate events and failed transcription jobs.","explanation_zh":"D 提供文件記載的 S3 Object Created 至 EventBridge 觸發路徑，C 提供有效的先轉錄再生成流程。20 MB 音訊應留在 S3 並傳遞物件參照，不要將原始音訊放進 Step Functions 狀態負載。A 與 C 實質等效，B 也受支援，因為 Step Functions 原生整合 Bedrock InvokeModel，且可使用 S3 輸入/輸出參照。因此 CD 是有效標答組合，但此題有多個有效組合；還須驗證 JSON 輸出、處理重複事件及轉錄失敗。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is also technically valid and nearly equivalent to C; it is not excluded by the requirements.","why_zh":"此項技術上也有效，與 C 幾乎等效，需求未排除此項。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Direct Bedrock invocation is supported by Step Functions; this is another valid workflow when transcript/prompt data is supplied correctly.","why_zh":"Step Functions 支援直接呼叫 Bedrock，正確提供逐字稿/提示時此項也是有效流程。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Step Functions is not a direct S3 notification destination; EventBridge or another supported trigger is needed.","why_zh":"Step Functions 不是直接 S3 通知目的地，須透過 EventBridge 或其他受支援觸發器。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventBridge.html"],"issues":["multiple_valid_pairs_AD_BD_CD"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.068223+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":94,"question_en":"A medical device company wants to feed reports of medical procedures that used the company's devices into an AI assistant. To protect patient privacy, the AI assistant must expose patient personally identifiable information (PII) only to surgeons. The AI assistant must redact PII for engineers. The AI assistant must reference only medical reports that are less than 3 years old. The company stores reports in an Amazon S3 bucket as soon as each report is published. The company has already set up an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. The AI assistant uses Amazon Cognito to authenticate users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon Macie PII detection on the S3 bucket. Use an S3 trigger to invoke an AWS Lambda function that redacts PII from the reports. Configure the Lambda function to delete outdated documents from the bucket and to invoke knowledge base syncing.","B":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function to sync the S3 bucket and the knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use a second Lambda function to invoke Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII if a user is part of the engineer Cognito user group. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration to remove reports that are older than 3 years from the bucket.","C":"Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Schedule an AWS Lambda function to run daily syncs between the bucket and the knowledge base. When users interact with the AI assistant, call the ApplyGuardrail configuration that matches the user's Cognito user group to redact PII from the agent’s responses if appropriate.","D":"Create a second knowledge base. Set up an S3 Lifecycle configuration on the bucket to remove reports that are older than 3 years. Invoke an AWS Lambda function that syncs the bucket with the original knowledge base when a new report is uploaded to the bucket. Use Amazon Comprehend to detect and redact PII before syncing the bucket with the second knowledge base. When a user interacts with the AI assistant, redirect the model to the appropriate knowledge base depending on the user’s Cognito user group."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":57,"D":43},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":94,"pages":[182,183]},"question_zh":"一家醫療器材公司希望將使用其器材的醫療程序報告提供給 AI 助理。為保護病患隱私，助理只能向外科醫師顯示病患 PII，對工程師須遮蔽 PII，且只能引用未滿三年的報告。報告出版後立即存至 S3。公司已建立 Bedrock 知識庫，助理以 Cognito 驗證使用者。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"對 S3 貯體啟用 Macie PII 偵測，以 S3 觸發器呼叫 Lambda 遮蔽報告中的 PII。讓 Lambda 刪除過期文件並呼叫知識庫同步。","B":"新報告上傳時，以 Lambda 同步 S3 與知識庫。若使用者屬 Cognito 工程師群組，由第二個 Lambda 呼叫 Comprehend 偵測及遮蔽 PII。設定 S3 Lifecycle 移除超過三年的報告。","C":"設定 S3 Lifecycle 移除超過三年的報告，排程 Lambda 每日同步 S3 與知識庫。使用者與助理互動時，呼叫符合其 Cognito 群組的 ApplyGuardrail 設定，視需要遮蔽代理回應中的 PII。","D":"建立第二個知識庫，設定 S3 Lifecycle 移除超過三年的報告。新報告上傳時，以 Lambda 將貯體同步至原知識庫；同步第二個知識庫前，先用 Comprehend 偵測及遮蔽 PII。使用者互動時，依 Cognito 群組導向適當知識庫。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C combines role-dependent output guardrails with regular synchronization, making it the intended managed solution. S3 expiration is asynchronous and daily sync adds delay, so this does not strictly guarantee that every retrieved report is less than three years old. Enforce a publication-date metadata filter at retrieval time and ensure deleted documents are removed from the vector index. Validate Cognito groups server-side and apply PII controls to all response and citation paths; output-only probabilistic masking is not a complete data-isolation boundary.","explanation_zh":"C 結合依角色套用輸出防護及定期同步，是題目預期的託管方案。但 S3 到期刪除非同步，每日同步又增加延遲，因此不能嚴格保證每份檢索報告均未滿三年。須在檢索當下依出版日期中繼資料篩選，並確保已刪文件從向量索引移除。應在伺服器端驗證 Cognito 群組，對所有回應及引用路徑套用 PII 控制；僅輸出機率式遮蔽不是完整資料隔離邊界。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Redacting the sole source removes PII for surgeons as well and lacks group-dependent behavior.","why_zh":"將唯一來源全部遮蔽也會讓醫師失去 PII，未提供依群組區分行為。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Upload-only sync does not reliably propagate later lifecycle deletions to the existing vector index.","why_zh":"只有上傳時同步，無法可靠把之後 Lifecycle 刪除反映至向量索引。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two indexes support isolation but add maintenance, and upload-triggered sync still misses age-out deletions.","why_zh":"兩索引支援隔離但增加維護，上傳觸發同步仍會漏掉因年限到期的刪除。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-use-independent-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_KnowledgeBaseVectorSearchConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-data-source-sync-ingest.html"],"issues":["no_strict_three_year_cutoff","PII_citations_and_auth_enforcement_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.069133+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群嚴重分歧・官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":95,"question_en":"A large ecommerce company has deployed a foundation model (FM) to generate product descriptions. The company's engineering team monitors technical metrics such as token usage, latency, and error rates by using Amazon CloudWatch. The company's marketing team tracks business metrics such as conversion rates and revenue impact in its own systems. The company needs a unified observability solution that correlates technical performance with business outcomes. The solution must provide automatic alerts to stakeholders when operational metrics indicate degradation. The solution must provide comprehensive visibility across both technical and business metrics. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create CloudWatch dashboards that include technical metrics and imported business metrics. Configure CloudWatch composite alarms that combine technical data and business data. Use Amazon SNS to set up notifications to stakeholders.","B":"Use Amazon Managed Grafana to visualize technical metrics from CloudWatch with business metrics from external sources. Configure Amazon Managed Grafana alerts to invoke AWS Lambda functions. Configure the Lambda functions to remediate issues automatically when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.","C":"Stream CloudWatch metrics to Amazon S3 by using CloudWatch metric streams. Create Amazon QuickSight dashboards to visualize the combined technical metrics and business metrics. Set up Amazon EventBridge rules to send notifications to stakeholders when metrics exceed predefined thresholds.","D":"Configure CloudWatch custom dashboards that integrate operational metrics with imported business metrics. Set up CloudWatch composite alarms with anomaly detection. Use Amazon SNS to create alarm actions to notify stakeholders when correlated metrics indicate performance issues."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{"D":75,"A":25},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":95,"pages":[184,185]},"question_zh":"一家大型電商公司部署基礎模型產生商品描述。工程團隊用 CloudWatch 監控 token 用量、延遲及錯誤率，行銷團隊在自己的系統追蹤轉換率及營收影響。公司需要統一可觀測性方案，關聯技術效能與業務成果，在營運指標顯示退化時自動通知利害關係人，並全面呈現技術與業務指標。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立 CloudWatch 儀表板，納入技術指標及匯入的業務指標，設定結合技術與業務資料的複合警報，以 SNS 通知利害關係人。","B":"使用 Managed Grafana 將 CloudWatch 技術指標與外部業務資料視覺化，設定 Grafana 警示呼叫 Lambda，讓函數在指標超過門檻時自動修復問題。","C":"透過 CloudWatch metric streams 將指標串流至 S3，用 QuickSight 儀表板呈現技術與業務指標，設定 EventBridge 規則在超過門檻時通知利害關係人。","D":"建立 CloudWatch 自訂儀表板，整合營運指標與匯入業務指標，設定具異常偵測的複合警報，以 SNS 警報動作在關聯指標顯示效能問題時通知利害關係人。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D adds adaptive anomaly detection to unified dashboards and SNS notifications, making it the intended richer solution. Implement anomaly detection on underlying metric alarms, then combine their alarm states in a composite rule; a composite alarm does not itself run an anomaly model over raw metrics. A also meets the written requirements, which do not explicitly demand adaptive baselines. Ensure the composite logic still alerts on operational degradation when a business metric has not yet changed.","explanation_zh":"D 在統一儀表板及 SNS 通知外加入自適應異常偵測，是題目預期較完整的方案。應先在底層指標警報套用異常偵測，再以複合規則結合警報狀態；複合警報本身不直接對原始指標執行異常模型。A 也符合原文需求，因為題幹未明確要求自適應基準。複合邏輯須確保業務指標尚未變化時，營運退化仍會告警。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is a valid simpler solution; D only adds adaptive detection not explicitly required by the stem.","why_zh":"此項是有效較簡單方案；D 只是多了題幹未明確要求的自適應偵測。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Automatic remediation does not explicitly provide the required stakeholder notifications.","why_zh":"自動修復未明確提供所需利害關係人通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Metric streams require a delivery pipeline and EventBridge rules do not directly evaluate arbitrary metric thresholds.","why_zh":"指標串流需要傳遞管線，EventBridge 規則不會直接評估任意指標門檻。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Create_Composite_Alarm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Anomaly_Detection.html"],"issues":["A_also_meets_requirements","anomaly_detection_belongs_to_underlying_metric_alarms"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:04:36.070065+00:00"},"difficulty":5,"diff_why":"社群分歧大・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":96,"question_en":"A GenAI developer is evaluating Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to enhance a Europe-based company's internal business application. The company has a multi-account landing zone in AWS Control Tower. The company uses SCPs to allow its accounts to use only the eu-north-1 Region and the eu-west-1 Region. All customer data must remain in private networks within the approved AWS Regions. The GenAI developer selects an FM based on analysis and testing and hosts the model in the eu-central-1 Region and the eu-west-3 Region. The GenAI developer must enable access to the FM for the company’s employees. The GenAI developer must ensure that requests to the FM are private and remain with the same Regions as the FM. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that is exposed by a private Amazon API Gateway REST API to a VPC in eu-north-1. Create a VPC endpoint for the selected FM in eu-central-1 and eu-west-3. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM. Integrate the REST API with the business application.","B":"Deploy the FM on Amazon EC2 instances in eu-north-1. Deploy a private Amazon API Gateway REST API in front of the EC2 instances. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Integrate the REST API with the business application.","C":"Configure the FM to use cross-Region inference through an eu.amazon.* endpoint to ensure that all calls remain within Europe. Configure an Amazon Bedrock VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the FM through inference profiles in Europe-based Regions where the FM is available. Use an inference profile to integrate Amazon Bedrock with the business application.","D":"Deploy the FM in Amazon SageMaker AI in eu-north-1. Configure a SageMaker AI VPC endpoint. Extend existing SCPs to allow employees to use the SageMaker AI endpoint. Integrate the FM in SageMaker AI with the business application."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{"C":100},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":96,"pages":[186,187]},"question_zh":"一位 GenAI 開發人員正在評估 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM），以改善一家歐洲公司的內部業務應用程式。公司在 AWS Control Tower 中有多帳戶登陸區，並用 SCP 限制帳戶只能使用 eu-north-1 與 eu-west-1。所有客戶資料都必須留在核准 AWS 區域的私人網路內。開發人員經分析與測試選定一個 FM，並將模型託管於 eu-central-1 與 eu-west-3。開發人員必須讓員工可以存取 FM，且請求必須透過私人連線，並留在與 FM 相同的區域。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 eu-north-1 的 VPC 中部署 AWS Lambda 函數，透過私有 Amazon API Gateway REST API 對外提供服務。在 eu-central-1 與 eu-west-3 為所選 FM 建立 VPC 端點。擴充現有 SCP 以允許員工使用 FM，並將 REST API 整合至業務應用程式。","B":"在 eu-north-1 的 Amazon EC2 執行個體上部署 FM，在 EC2 前部署私有 Amazon API Gateway REST API。設定 Amazon Bedrock VPC 端點，並將 REST API 整合至業務應用程式。","C":"設定 FM 透過 eu.amazon.* 端點使用跨區域推論，確保所有呼叫留在歐洲。設定 Amazon Bedrock VPC 端點。擴充現有 SCP，允許員工透過歐洲可用區域的推論設定檔使用 FM，並以推論設定檔將 Amazon Bedrock 整合至業務應用程式。","D":"在 eu-north-1 的 Amazon SageMaker AI 中部署 FM，設定 SageMaker AI VPC 端點。擴充現有 SCP 以允許員工使用 SageMaker AI 端點，並將託管於 SageMaker AI 的 FM 整合至業務應用程式。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C is the intended and closest architecture: a geographic EU inference profile keeps processing within its listed European destinations, and PrivateLink provides private access to Bedrock. Cross-Region traffic remains on the AWS network, but SCPs must permit every destination in the chosen profile. The source is inconsistent: its initially approved Regions exclude both stated model Regions, and an EU profile does not restrict processing to just those two model Regions. Also eu.amazon.* describes a possible profile ID prefix, not a network endpoint; the application calls a regional Bedrock Runtime endpoint with a valid profile ID. Compliance therefore requires explicitly approving the profile destination set; no option satisfies the unchanged original allowlist.","explanation_zh":"C 是命題意圖中最接近的架構：EU 地理推論設定檔會將處理限制在其列出的歐洲目的區域，PrivateLink 提供 Bedrock 私人存取。跨區域流量留在 AWS 網路，但 SCP 必須允許所選設定檔的所有目的區域。題目本身矛盾：最初核准的區域不包含兩個模型區域，EU 設定檔也不保證只送到這兩區。另外 eu.amazon.* 是可能的設定檔 ID 前綴概念，不是網路端點；應用程式應呼叫區域 Bedrock Runtime 端點並傳入有效設定檔 ID。因此必須明確核准目的區域集合；若原本允許清單不能變更，沒有選項完整符合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cross-Region endpoint reachability and routing are not supplied merely by creating remote VPC endpoints; the Region conflict remains.","why_zh":"只建立遠端 VPC 端點不會自動提供跨區域可達性與路由，區域限制矛盾仍在。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The selected Bedrock model is not assumed to be exportable to EC2, and a Bedrock endpoint does not front an EC2 model.","why_zh":"不能假定所選 Bedrock 模型可匯出至 EC2，Bedrock 端點也不會代理 EC2 模型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The question does not establish that this model can be deployed on SageMaker; it changes the stipulated hosting Regions.","why_zh":"題目未證明此模型可部署於 SageMaker，且此方案改變既定託管區域。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-prereq.html"],"issues":["contradictory_region_allowlist","profile_id_not_endpoint","geography_not_specific_two_regions"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.911862+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":97,"question_en":"A healthcare company is developing an application to process medical queries. The application must answer complex queries with high accuracy by reducing semantic dilution. The application must refer to domain-specific terminology in medical documents to reduce ambiguity in medical terminology. The application must be able to respond to 1,000 queries each minute with response times less than 2 seconds. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon API Gateway to route incoming queries to an Amazon Bedrock agent. Configure the agent to use an Anthropic Claude model to decompose queries and an Amazon Titan model to expand queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents.","B":"Configure an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Enable query decomposition in the knowledge base. Configure an Amazon Bedrock flow that uses a foundation model (FM) and the knowledge base to support the application.","C":"Use Amazon SageMaker Al to host custom ML models for both query decomposition and query expansion. Configure Amazon Bedrock knowledge bases to store the reference medical documents. Encrypt the documents in the knowledge base.","D":"Create an Amazon Bedrock agent to orchestrate multiple AWS Lambda functions to decompose queries. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base to store the reference medical documents. Use the agent's built-in knowledge base capabilities. Add deep research and reasoning capabilities to the agent to reduce ambiguity in the medical terminology."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{"B":100},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":97,"pages":[188,189]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司正在開發處理醫療查詢的應用程式。應用程式必須降低語意稀釋，以高準確度回答複雜查詢，並參照醫療文件中的領域專用術語，降低醫學名詞歧義。系統必須每分鐘處理 1,000 個查詢，回應時間少於 2 秒。哪個方案以最少維運負擔符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon API Gateway 將查詢路由至 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式。設定代理程式用 Anthropic Claude 模型拆解查詢，並用 Amazon Titan 模型擴充查詢。建立 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫儲存參考醫療文件。","B":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫儲存參考醫療文件，啟用知識庫的查詢拆解。設定使用基礎模型（FM）與知識庫的 Amazon Bedrock 流程來支援應用程式。","C":"使用 Amazon SageMaker AI 託管自訂 ML 模型，分別執行查詢拆解與查詢擴充。設定 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫儲存參考醫療文件，並加密知識庫中的文件。","D":"建立 Amazon Bedrock 代理程式，協調多個 AWS Lambda 函數拆解查詢。建立 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫儲存參考醫療文件，使用代理程式內建的知識庫功能，並增加深度研究與推理能力以降低醫學術語歧義。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B uses the managed query-decomposition capability to split complex questions into simpler subqueries and retrieve relevant medical context. This avoids hosting custom decomposition models or maintaining multiple orchestration functions. Query decomposition can add latency, and neither a flow nor a knowledge base guarantees 1,000 queries per minute with a two-second response. Capacity, model choice, quotas and end-to-end load tests are required, and domain accuracy still needs representative medical evaluation.","explanation_zh":"B 使用託管的查詢拆解功能，把複雜問題拆成較簡單的子查詢，取得相關醫療脈絡。這能免去自建拆解模型及維護多個協調函數的負擔。查詢拆解可能增加延遲；流程或知識庫本身都不保證每分鐘 1,000 次查詢及兩秒內回覆。仍須驗證容量、模型選擇、配額及端到端負載，並用具代表性的醫療資料評估領域準確性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Two-model orchestration adds work and latency compared with managed decomposition.","why_zh":"雙模型協調比託管拆解增加工作量與延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hosting and maintaining custom models increases operational overhead.","why_zh":"託管與維護自訂模型增加維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom Lambda orchestration and unspecified deep research add complexity without proving the latency target.","why_zh":"自訂 Lambda 協調及未具體定義的深度研究增加複雜度，也未證明延遲目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_QueryTransformationConfiguration.html"],"issues":["throughput_and_latency_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.913169+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":98,"question_en":"A company has a customer service application that uses Amazon Bedrock to generate personalized responses to customer inquiries. The company needs to establish a quality assurance process to evaluate prompt effectiveness and model configurations across updates. The process must automatically compare outputs from multiple prompt templates, detect response quality issues, provide quantitative metrics, and allow human reviewers to give feedback on responses. The process must prevent configurations that do not meet a predefined quality threshold from being deployed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that sends sample customer inquiries to multiple Amazon Bedrock model configurations and stores responses in Amazon S3. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize response patterns. Manually review outputs daily. Use AWS CodePipeline to deploy the configurations that have quality scores above the specified quality threshold.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock evaluation jobs to compare model outputs by using custom prompt datasets. Configure AWS CodePipeline to run the evaluation jobs when prompt templates change. Configure CodePipeline to deploy the configurations that have quality scores above the specified quality threshold.","C":"Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor response latency and error rates from Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon EventBridge rules to notify the company when latency and error rate metrics exceed thresholds. Configure an approval workflow in AWS Systems Manager to perform manual quality checks.","D":"Use AWS Lambda functions to create an automated testing framework that samples production traffic and routes duplicate requests to the updated model version. Use Amazon Comprehend sentiment analysis to compare results. Block deployment if sentiment scores decrease."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":98,"pages":[189]},"question_zh":"一家公司的客服應用程式使用 Amazon Bedrock，為客戶詢問產生個人化回覆。公司需要建立品質保證流程，在更新時評估提示效果與模型組態。流程必須自動比較多個提示範本的輸出、偵測回覆品質問題、提供量化指標，並讓人工審查者提供回饋。流程必須阻止未達預設品質門檻的組態部署。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立 AWS Lambda 函數，把範例客戶詢問送到多個 Amazon Bedrock 模型組態，並將回覆存入 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon QuickSight 顯示回覆模式，每天人工審查輸出，使用 AWS CodePipeline 部署品質分數超過指定門檻的組態。","B":"使用 Amazon Bedrock 評估工作，透過自訂提示資料集比較模型輸出。設定 AWS CodePipeline 在提示範本變更時執行評估工作，並只部署品質分數超過指定門檻的組態。","C":"設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警示監控 Amazon Bedrock 的回覆延遲與錯誤率。使用 Amazon EventBridge 規則在指標超標時通知公司，並在 AWS Systems Manager 設定核准流程執行人工品質檢查。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 建立自動測試框架，抽樣正式流量並將重複請求送至更新的模型版本。使用 Amazon Comprehend 情緒分析比較結果，若情緒分數下降就阻止部署。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B provides the appropriate managed evaluation mechanism and an explicit deployment gate. Bedrock supports custom prompt datasets and separate human-worker evaluation jobs, so both quantitative scoring and reviewer feedback can be included. CodePipeline must orchestrate job creation, wait for completion, inspect metrics and fail the stage below threshold; those gates are not created automatically by starting a job. The selected evaluation mode and dataset must measure the actual response-quality requirements.","explanation_zh":"B 提供合適的託管評估機制及明確的部署門檻。Bedrock 支援自訂提示資料集，也有獨立的人工評估工作，因此可以納入量化評分與審查回饋。CodePipeline 必須協調建立工作、等待完成、檢查指標，並在未達門檻時讓階段失敗；單純啟動評估不會自動建立這些控制。評估模式與資料集必須對應實際回覆品質需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Daily manual inspection does not implement the required automatic quality comparison.","why_zh":"每日人工檢查未實作所需的自動品質比較。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Latency and errors measure service health rather than semantic response quality.","why_zh":"延遲與錯誤率衡量服務健康，不能替代語意回覆品質。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sentiment alone cannot measure correctness or comprehensive prompt quality and does not supply human review.","why_zh":"單靠情緒分數無法衡量正確性或完整提示品質，也未提供人工審查。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-human.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.914336+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":99,"question_en":"A retail company runs an application that makes product recommendations to customers on the company’s website. The application uses Amazon Bedrock to generate recommendations by dynamically constructing prompts and sending them to foundation models (FMs). A GenAI developer has deployed an update to the application that instructs the FM to include a specific promotional message when the FM generates a response to prompts. When the developer tests the application, the promotional message does not always appear in the responses. When the promotional message does appear in the responses, it does not always flow with the rest of the text. The GenAI developer must ensure that the promotional message always appears in the FM responses. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon Bedrock Guardrails filter on the prompt. Set the input filter strength to HIGH.","B":"Generate multiple response variants that include the promotional message in different ways. Use a reranker model to select the most coherent version based on relevance to the original prompt.","C":"Run the prompt through Amazon Bedrock. Process the response through Amazon Bedrock Agents to add the promotional message. Rerank the results by using the original prompt and the desired message as context.","D":"Reinforce the requirement to include the new promotional message within product recommendations by using an output indicator in prompts to the FM."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":99,"pages":[190]},"question_zh":"一家零售公司的網站應用程式會向客戶推薦商品。應用程式動態建構提示並送至 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）產生推薦。GenAI 開發人員部署更新，要求 FM 在回覆提示時加入特定促銷訊息。測試發現促銷訊息不一定出現，即使出現，也不一定與其餘文字銜接自然。開發人員必須確保 FM 回覆一定包含促銷訊息。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在提示套用 Amazon Bedrock Guardrails 篩選器，將輸入篩選強度設為 HIGH。","B":"產生多個以不同方式加入促銷訊息的回覆版本，使用重新排名模型依與原提示的相關性選出最連貫的版本。","C":"將提示送入 Amazon Bedrock，再用 Amazon Bedrock Agents 處理回覆以加入促銷訊息，並以原提示及所需訊息為脈絡重新排名。","D":"在送至 FM 的提示中使用輸出指示，強化商品推薦中必須包含新促銷訊息的要求。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"D most directly improves prompt adherence by explicitly specifying required output content and format. AWS prompt guidance recommends output indicators to constrain the desired response. However prompting remains probabilistic: no output indicator guarantees that a phrase always appears. A strict business requirement needs deterministic composition or output validation with a safe fallback; none of the listed options fully guarantees it.","explanation_zh":"D 透過明確指定必要輸出內容與格式，最直接改善提示遵循。AWS 提示設計文件建議使用輸出指示限制預期回覆。但提示仍是機率性機制，不能保證某句文字每次出現。若業務要求絕對成立，需要確定性的文字組合，或輸出驗證與安全備援；題目列出的方案都未完整保證。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Input safety filters block unsafe content; they do not insert promotional text.","why_zh":"輸入安全篩選器阻擋不安全內容，不負責插入促銷文字。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reranking chooses among candidates and cannot guarantee that every candidate contains the mandatory phrase.","why_zh":"重新排名只會在候選回覆間選擇，不能保證候選都包含必要文字。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Additional generative agent calls remain probabilistic and add complexity.","why_zh":"額外的生成式代理呼叫仍具有機率性，且增加複雜度。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/design-a-prompt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html"],"issues":["prompting_cannot_guarantee_always"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.915236+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":100,"question_en":"A company is creating a generative AI (GenAI) application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The application must use Microsoft Entra ID to authenticate. All FM API calls must stay on private network paths. Access to the application must be limited by department to specific model families. The company also needs a comprehensive audit trail of model interactions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure SAML federation between Microsoft Entra ID and IAM. Create department-specific IAM roles that allow only the required ModelId values. Create AWS PrivateLink interface VPC endpoints for Amazon Bedrock runtime services. Enable AWS CloudTrail to capture Amazon Bedrock API calls. Configure Amazon Bedrock model invocation logging to record detailed model interactions.","B":"Create an identity provider (IdP) connection in IAM to authenticate by using Microsoft Entra ID. Assign department permission sets to control access to specific model families. Deploy AWS Lambda functions in private subnets with a NAT gateway for egress to Amazon Bedrock public endpoints. Enable CloudWatch Logs to capture model interactions for auditing purposes.","C":"Create a SAML identity provider (IdP) in IAM to authenticate by using Microsoft Entra ID. Use IAM permissions boundaries to limit department roles’ access to specific model families. Configure public Amazon Bedrock API endpoints with VPC routing to maintain private network connectivity. Set up AWS CloudTrail with Amazon S3 Lifecycle rules to manage audit logs of model interactions.","D":"Configure OpenID Connect (OIDC) federation between Microsoft Entra ID and IAM. Use attribute-based access control to map department attributes to specific model access permissions. Apply SCP policies to restrict access to Amazon Bedrock FM families based on department. Use Microsoft Entra ID’s built-in logging capabilities to maintain an audit trail of model interactions."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":100,"pages":[191]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在建立使用 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）的生成式 AI 應用程式。應用程式必須透過 Microsoft Entra ID 驗證身分，所有 FM API 呼叫都必須留在私人網路路徑。應用程式必須依部門限制可使用的特定模型家族，並建立完整的模型互動稽核軌跡。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 Microsoft Entra ID 與 IAM 之間設定 SAML 聯合身分，建立僅允許所需 ModelId 值的部門專屬 IAM 角色。為 Amazon Bedrock Runtime 服務建立 AWS PrivateLink 介面 VPC 端點。啟用 AWS CloudTrail 記錄 Amazon Bedrock API 呼叫，並設定模型呼叫日誌記錄詳細互動。","B":"在 IAM 建立身分提供者（IdP）連線以使用 Microsoft Entra ID 驗證。指派部門權限集控制特定模型家族存取。在私有子網部署 AWS Lambda，透過 NAT 閘道連往 Bedrock 公開端點，並啟用 CloudWatch Logs 記錄模型互動以供稽核。","C":"在 IAM 建立 SAML IdP 以使用 Microsoft Entra ID 驗證。使用 IAM 權限界限限制部門角色可存取的模型家族。設定 Bedrock 公開 API 端點與 VPC 路由以維持私人網路連線，並設定 AWS CloudTrail 與 Amazon S3 生命週期規則管理模型互動稽核日誌。","D":"在 Microsoft Entra ID 與 IAM 之間設定 OIDC 聯合身分。使用屬性式存取控制將部門屬性映射至模型存取權限，套用 SCP 依部門限制 Bedrock FM 家族，並以 Microsoft Entra ID 內建日誌維持模型互動稽核軌跡。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A combines identity federation, least-privilege model access, private runtime connectivity and the two complementary audit layers. Model restrictions should be expressed through supported Bedrock actions and model-resource ARNs, including inference-profile permissions where applicable; ModelId is not a universal IAM condition key. CloudTrail records API activity, while model invocation logging records supported request and response content to S3 or CloudWatch Logs. Invocation logging must be explicitly enabled and protected because it can contain sensitive prompts.","explanation_zh":"A 結合聯合身分、模型最小權限、Runtime 私人連線及兩種互補稽核紀錄。模型限制應以受支援的 Bedrock 動作與模型資源 ARN 表達，使用推論設定檔時還需對應權限；ModelId 並不是通用的 IAM 條件鍵。CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動，模型呼叫日誌則把受支援的請求與回覆內容寫入 S3 或 CloudWatch Logs。呼叫日誌必須明確啟用並保護，因為可能包含敏感提示。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"NAT access to public endpoints does not satisfy the specified PrivateLink-style private path.","why_zh":"透過 NAT 存取公開端點不符合題目要求的私人連線路徑。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC routing alone does not turn a public API endpoint into a private endpoint, and CloudTrail does not replace payload logging.","why_zh":"只有 VPC 路由不會把公開 API 變成私人端點，CloudTrail 也不能替代內容日誌。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Identity-provider logs do not capture Bedrock prompts/completions, and this option omits private runtime networking.","why_zh":"身分提供者日誌不會記錄 Bedrock 提示與完成內容，且此方案缺少 Runtime 私人連線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-prereq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.916259+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":101,"question_en":"A healthcare company is developing an AI application to retrieve medical literature to help doctors conduct research. The company wants to deploy the application to multiple countries. The application needs to index 50,000 text-heavy medical documents that contain specialized terminology in English, French, and German. The application must provide high search accuracy for medical terminology. The company wants a solution that requires minimal custom code development and ongoing maintenance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Titan Text Embeddings to process all documents in their original language without translation. Apply semantic chunking at the medical section level to preserve medical terminology context and to maintain moderate vector dimensions.","B":"Use Amazon Titan Text Embeddings to translate all non-English documents to English before processing. Implement document chunking strategies based on logical sections to improve retrieval accuracy.","C":"Use Amazon Titan Multimodal Embeddings to convert document pages to images. Generate text captions for the images to create a multimodal knowledge base that handles medical content.","D":"Use an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base as the vector store. Use Amazon Kendra to perform multilingual document processing. Configure the vector store to automatically handle language detection and translation for each query."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":101,"pages":[192]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司正在開發協助醫師研究的醫學文獻檢索 AI 應用程式，並希望部署至多個國家。應用程式需要索引 50,000 份以文字為主的醫學文件，內容包含英文、法文與德文專業術語。系統必須提供高準確度的醫學術語搜尋，並盡量減少自訂程式開發及持續維護。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Titan Text Embeddings，直接處理所有文件的原始語言而不翻譯。在醫學章節層級進行語意分塊，以保留專業術語脈絡，並使用適中的向量維度。","B":"使用 Amazon Titan Text Embeddings，先將所有非英文文件翻譯為英文再處理。依邏輯章節實作分塊策略，提高檢索準確度。","C":"使用 Amazon Titan Multimodal Embeddings 將文件頁面轉成影像，為影像產生文字說明，建立處理醫學內容的多模態知識庫。","D":"將 Amazon Bedrock 知識庫當作向量儲存庫，使用 Amazon Kendra 處理多語文件，並設定向量儲存庫自動偵測語言與翻譯每個查詢。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is the closest low-maintenance approach: Titan Text Embeddings V2 supports French and German, and logical section-sized chunks preserve useful context. Embedding models create vectors rather than translate text or render pages. AWS states that this model is optimized for English and that cross-language retrieval can be suboptimal. High medical-term accuracy and the chosen vector dimension therefore require multilingual domain evaluation rather than assuming support equals validated accuracy.","explanation_zh":"A 是最接近低維護需求的作法：Titan Text Embeddings V2 支援法文與德文，依邏輯章節分塊可保留有效脈絡。嵌入模型負責產生向量，不是翻譯文字或把頁面轉成影像。AWS 說明此模型主要針對英文最佳化，跨語言檢索可能效果不佳。因此仍須以多語醫療資料驗證術語準確性及向量維度，不能把語言支援視為已證明的高準確性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Titan Text Embeddings does not translate documents.","why_zh":"Titan Text Embeddings 不提供文件翻譯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Converting text-heavy documents to images and captions adds unnecessary loss and processing.","why_zh":"把文字文件轉成影像與圖說增加不必要的資訊損失及處理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A knowledge base orchestrates retrieval over supported stores; it is not itself a vector database with automatic translation.","why_zh":"知識庫協調對受支援儲存庫的檢索，本身不是具有自動翻譯的向量資料庫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/titan-embedding-models.html"],"issues":["multilingual_medical_accuracy_requires_evaluation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.917091+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":102,"question_en":"A publishing company is developing a chat assistant that uses a containerized large language model (LLM) that runs on Amazon SageMaker AI. The architecture consists of an Amazon API Gateway REST API that routes user requests to an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function invokes a SageMaker AI real-time endpoint that hosts the LLM. Users report uneven response times. Analytics show that a high number of chats are abandoned after 2 seconds of waiting for the first token. The company wants a solution to ensure that p95 latency is under 800 ms for interactive requests to the chat assistant. Which combination of solutions will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Enable model preload upon container startup. Implement dynamic batching to process multiple user requests together in a single inference pass.","B":"Select a larger GPU instance type for the SageMaker AI endpoint. Set the minimum number of instances to 0. Continue to perform per-request processing. Lazily load model weights on the first request.","C":"Switch to a multi-model endpoint. Use lazy loading without request batching.","D":"Set the minimum number of instances to greater than 0. Enable response streaming.","E":"Switch to Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference for all requests. Store requests in an Amazon S3 bucket. Set the minimum number of instances to 0."},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":102,"pages":[193]},"question_zh":"一家出版公司正在開發聊天助理，使用在 Amazon SageMaker AI 上執行的容器化大型語言模型（LLM）。架構由 Amazon API Gateway REST API 將使用者請求送至 AWS Lambda，Lambda 再呼叫託管 LLM 的 SageMaker AI 即時端點。使用者反映回應時間不穩；分析顯示許多使用者等待第一個 token 超過 2 秒就放棄聊天。公司希望互動請求的 p95 延遲低於 800 毫秒。哪兩個方案的組合符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"在容器啟動時預載模型，實作動態批次處理，在一次推論中處理多個使用者請求。","B":"為 SageMaker AI 端點選擇較大的 GPU 執行個體，將最小執行個體數設為 0，維持逐請求處理，並在第一個請求到達時才延遲載入模型權重。","C":"改用多模型端點，採用延遲載入且不進行請求批次處理。","D":"將最小執行個體數設為大於 0，並啟用回應串流。","E":"將所有請求改用 Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference，將請求存入 Amazon S3，並將最小執行個體數設為 0。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A and D address cold loading, capacity utilization and time to the first visible token. A warm endpoint with preloaded weights avoids scale-from-zero and lazy-load penalties, while streaming returns incremental output from a streaming-capable container. Dynamic batching needs a tightly controlled wait budget because excessive batching delay can worsen p95 latency. The Lambda/API Gateway path must also deliver the stream end to end, and an 800-ms p95 must be demonstrated by load tests rather than inferred from these settings.","explanation_zh":"A 與 D 分別處理冷載入、容量利用率及第一個可見 token 的等待時間。保留預載權重的溫熱端點可避免從零擴展及延遲載入成本，串流則讓支援串流的容器逐段回傳輸出。動態批次必須嚴格控制等待預算，否則排隊時間可能惡化 p95 延遲。Lambda/API Gateway 路徑也必須端到端傳遞串流；800 毫秒 p95 需負載測試證明，不能由設定推定。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Scale-to-zero plus lazy loading introduces cold-start delay even on a larger GPU.","why_zh":"即使使用較大 GPU，縮至零與延遲載入仍會產生冷啟動等待。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Lazy loading on a multi-model endpoint can add model-loading latency.","why_zh":"多模型端點的延遲載入可能增加模型載入延遲。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Asynchronous queuing and scale-to-zero are unsuitable for this immediate interactive response target.","why_zh":"非同步排隊及縮至零不適合此立即互動回覆目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-optimize.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_InvokeEndpointWithResponseStream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/response-transfer-mode-lambda.html"],"issues":["p95_target_requires_measurement","end_to_end_streaming_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.918405+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":103,"question_en":"A company runs a GenAI application that uses multiple foundation models (FMs) from Amazon Bedrock to generate text. The application serves users across three AWS Regions. The application runs on AWS Lambda functions. The company needs to implement dynamic model selection based on response quality and latency metrics. The company must be able to switch between models without modifying or redeploying the application code. The company wants to gradually roll out new models, starting with 20% of traffic. The company needs a solution that will automatically roll back if error rates exceed 1%. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS AppConfig to create feature flags for model selection criteria. Set up validation rules for error rates. Implement the AWS AppConfig Agent Lambda extension to retrieve model configurations when the functions run. Define linear deployment strategies to gradually release new models, starting with 20% of traffic.","B":"Store model selection configurations in Amazon DynamoDUse global tables to enable multi-Region replication. Configure Amazon EventBridge rules to monitor Amazon CloudWatch metrics for errors and invoke AWS Lambda functions that update the DynamoDB table with model preferences. Add custom code to the Lambda functions to query DynamoDB before each model invocation.","C":"Create Lambda function versions for each model configuration. Use Lambda aliases and set up routing configurations to gradually shift traffic between versions, starting with 20% of traffic. Implement AWS CodeDeploy deployments that monitor Amazon CloudWatch metrics for the Lambda function versions to automatically roll back deployments when error rales exceed thresholds.","D":"Create Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to monitor response quality and latency metrics. Implement custom logic in the Lambda functions to select models based on metric thresholds. Use environment variables that are stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to define model selection parameters that can be updated across Regions."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":103,"pages":[194]},"question_zh":"一家 GenAI 應用程式使用多個 Amazon Bedrock 基礎模型（FM）產生文字，在三個 AWS 區域透過 AWS Lambda 服務使用者。公司需要依回覆品質與延遲指標動態選擇模型，且切換模型時不必修改或重新部署應用程式碼。新模型必須從 20% 流量開始逐步推出，若錯誤率超過 1% 就自動回復。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS AppConfig 建立模型選擇條件的功能旗標，設定錯誤率驗證規則。使用 AWS AppConfig Agent Lambda 擴充功能在函數執行時取得模型組態，定義線性部署策略，從 20% 流量開始逐步推出新模型。","B":"將模型選擇組態存入 Amazon DynamoDB，使用全域資料表進行多區域複寫。設定 Amazon EventBridge 規則監控 CloudWatch 錯誤指標，並呼叫 Lambda 更新資料表中的模型偏好；在 Lambda 加入自訂程式碼，每次呼叫模型前查詢 DynamoDB。","C":"為各模型組態建立 Lambda 函數版本，使用 Lambda 別名與路由組態，從 20% 流量開始逐步轉移版本。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 監控 Lambda 版本的 CloudWatch 指標，在錯誤率超標時自動回復。","D":"建立 CloudWatch 儀表板監控回覆品質與延遲，在 Lambda 實作依指標門檻選模型的自訂邏輯，並使用存於 Systems Manager Parameter Store 的環境變數定義可跨區域更新的選擇參數。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is the intended configuration-driven rollout pattern and avoids redeploying model-specific code once configuration consumption is implemented. AppConfig can distribute gradual deployments through its Lambda extension. However configuration validators do not monitor live error rates: automatic rollback requires an associated CloudWatch alarm configured for the 1% threshold. A 20% linear deployment increment concerns configuration rollout targets, not automatically an exact global request-traffic split; request-level cohort logic or feature-flag variants must implement that requirement.","explanation_zh":"A 是命題意圖中的組態式推出方式；應用程式實作讀取組態後，切換模型不需重新部署專屬程式碼。AppConfig 可透過 Lambda 擴充功能逐步派送組態。但組態驗證器不會監控即時錯誤率，自動回復需要關聯設定為 1% 門檻的 CloudWatch 警示。另外 20% 線性部署增量代表組態推出目標比例，不會自動形成精確的全球請求分流；請求層級的群組邏輯或功能旗標變體仍須實作。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This builds custom polling, monitoring and rollback logic instead of using managed configuration deployment.","why_zh":"此方案需自行實作查詢、監控與回復邏輯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It rolls out Lambda versions, contrary to switching model configuration without application deployment.","why_zh":"此方案推出的是 Lambda 版本，與無需部署應用程式即可切換模型組態的要求不符。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Dashboards and Parameter Store alone do not provide controlled rollout and automatic rollback.","why_zh":"只有儀表板與 Parameter Store 不提供受控推出及自動回復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/monitoring-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-creating-deployment-strategy.html"],"issues":["validators_not_error_alarms","rollout_percentage_not_exact_request_split"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.919949+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":104,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing an AI-powered search assistant application to help investment advisors quickly retrieve investment data. The application runs as an AWS Lambda function. The company is using Amazon Bedrock to develop the application by using an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that uses Amazon OpenSearch Serverless as its data source. The application agent must manage collections at scale by automatically assigning access permissions to collections and indexes that match a specific pattern. The company uses Amazon Bedrock tools to test the knowledge base. The knowledge base sync process finishes successfully. However, the test reveals a 400 Bad Authorization error from the BedrockAgentRuntime API and a 403 Forbidden error when the test attempts to access OpenSearch Serverless. The company must resolve the permissions issues. Which combination of solutions will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Update the Lambda function execution role to include the bedrock:InvokeAgent permission. Add the aoss:APIAccessAll permission to the Lambda execution role.","B":"Create an OpenSearch Serverless data access policy that includes pattern-based resource rules.","C":"Configure a VPC endpoint policy for OpenSearch Serverless. Add the endpoint to the Lambda function’s VPC configuration.","D":"Configure AWS Secrets Manager to store OpenSearch Serverless credentials. Grant the Lambda function access to retrieve the credentials.","E":"Enable IAM authentication for the OpenSearch Serverless domain. Add the es:ESHttp* permission to the Lambda function execution role."},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":104,"pages":[195]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發 AI 搜尋助理，協助投資顧問快速檢索投資資料。應用程式以 AWS Lambda 執行，使用 Amazon Bedrock 及以 Amazon OpenSearch Serverless 為資料來源的知識庫。應用程式代理必須以符合特定模式的規則，自動指派集合與索引存取權限，以便大規模管理集合。公司使用 Bedrock 工具測試知識庫；同步成功，但測試時 BedrockAgentRuntime API 回傳 400 Bad Authorization，存取 OpenSearch Serverless 時回傳 403 Forbidden。哪兩個方案可解決權限問題？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"更新 Lambda 執行角色，加入 bedrock:InvokeAgent 與 aoss:APIAccessAll 權限。","B":"建立含有模式式資源規則的 OpenSearch Serverless 資料存取政策。","C":"設定 OpenSearch Serverless 的 VPC 端點政策，並將端點加入 Lambda 的 VPC 組態。","D":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 儲存 OpenSearch Serverless 憑證，授權 Lambda 取得憑證。","E":"為 OpenSearch Serverless 網域啟用 IAM 驗證，並在 Lambda 執行角色加入 es:ESHttp* 權限。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A and B are the intended IAM-plus-data-policy combination. OpenSearch Serverless data access policies support collection/index patterns, and data-plane access additionally requires the appropriate aoss IAM permissions. The principal actually calling OpenSearch must be authorized: for knowledge-base retrieval this is generally the Bedrock knowledge-base service role, not automatically the Lambda role. InvokeAgent applies when invoking an agent; direct knowledge-base calls need Retrieve or RetrieveAndGenerate permissions instead. OpenSearch is the vector store rather than the source documents, so the question conflates roles and APIs and requires tracing the denied principal before applying the fix.","explanation_zh":"A 與 B 是命題意圖中的 IAM 加資料政策組合。OpenSearch Serverless 資料存取政策支援集合／索引模式，資料平面還需要對應的 aoss IAM 權限。但必須授權實際呼叫 OpenSearch 的身分：知識庫檢索通常使用 Bedrock 知識庫服務角色，不會自動使用 Lambda 角色。InvokeAgent 適用於呼叫代理；直接呼叫知識庫則需要 Retrieve 或 RetrieveAndGenerate 權限。此外 OpenSearch 是向量儲存庫而非原始文件來源。題目混用了角色及 API，修復前應追查被拒絕的實際身分。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Network/endpoint policy cannot replace missing identity and data-access grants.","why_zh":"網路／端點政策不能替代缺少的身分與資料存取授權。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Serverless access uses IAM/SAML policy authorization, not stored domain passwords.","why_zh":"Serverless 使用 IAM／SAML 政策授權，並非儲存網域密碼。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"es:ESHttp* belongs to provisioned OpenSearch domains, not the aoss serverless permission model.","why_zh":"es:ESHttp* 屬於佈建式 OpenSearch 網域，不是 aoss Serverless 權限模型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/serverless-data-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-permissions.html"],"issues":["denied_principal_and_bedrock_api_ambiguous"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.921257+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":105,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a GenAI application that allows business analysts to query sensitive customer data by using natural language. A GenAI developer must implement a content safety framework that performs text-to-SQL transformations while preventing harmful outputs. The solution must detect and block SQL injection attempts in natural language prompts, validate generated SQL queries against predefined schemas, and create an audit trail of query transformations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock with an integrated content filtering system. Deploy Amazon GuardDuty with custom SQL threat detection rules. Use AWS Lambda functions to check generated queries against schema definitions in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Use Amazon EventBridge to store records of all transformations in Amazon S3.","B":"Implement a multi-stage validation pipeline that uses Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter inputs. Configure AWS Lambda functions to use with SQL parsing libraries to validate query syntax. Use the Amazon RDS Data API to verify queries against defined schemas and collect audit logs before the pipeline runs each query.","C":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to log all database API calls. Implement IAM roles that have least privilege access to the application. Use AWS WAF to filter malicious inputs to the application.","D":"Train a custom Amazon SageMaker AI model to securely transform text to SQL. Attach VPC endpoints to isolate the customer data database. Store query history in Amazon DynamoDB."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":105,"pages":[196]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發 GenAI 應用程式，讓業務分析師以自然語言查詢敏感客戶資料。開發人員必須建立安全框架，執行文字轉 SQL 並防止有害輸出。方案必須偵測及阻擋自然語言提示中的 SQL 注入攻擊、依預定結構描述驗證產生的 SQL，並建立查詢轉換的稽核軌跡。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用整合內容篩選系統的 Amazon Bedrock，部署帶有自訂 SQL 威脅偵測規則的 Amazon GuardDuty。用 Lambda 依 Systems Manager Parameter Store 中的結構描述檢查查詢，並用 EventBridge 將所有轉換紀錄存入 S3。","B":"建立多階段驗證管線，使用 Bedrock Guardrails 篩選輸入，設定 Lambda 搭配 SQL 解析程式庫驗證語法。使用 Amazon RDS Data API 對照已定義結構描述驗證查詢，並在每次執行前收集稽核日誌。","C":"設定 CloudTrail 記錄所有資料庫 API 呼叫，實作最小權限 IAM 角色，並用 AWS WAF 篩選應用程式惡意輸入。","D":"訓練自訂 SageMaker AI 模型安全地把文字轉為 SQL，附加 VPC 端點隔離客戶資料庫，並將查詢歷史存入 DynamoDB。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B is closest because it explicitly separates input filtering, SQL parsing and pre-execution validation. Guardrails prompt-attack detection is not a complete SQL injection defense; the application must enforce an allowed SQL AST, tables/columns, read-only operations, parameter binding and database privileges. RDS Data API executes statements and is not a standalone validate-only schema checker, so metadata inspection or a safe database-specific validation step must be implemented. Audit records must correlate original input, generated SQL and validation outcome before any permitted execution.","explanation_zh":"B 最接近需求，因為它明確區分輸入篩選、SQL 解析及執行前驗證。Guardrails 提示攻擊偵測不是完整的 SQL 注入防禦；應用程式仍須限制 SQL 語法樹、資料表／欄位、唯讀操作、參數綁定及資料庫權限。RDS Data API 負責執行陳述式，不是只驗證結構描述的獨立檢查器，因此須實作中繼資料檢查或資料庫適用的安全驗證步驟。稽核紀錄應在允許執行前串連原始輸入、產生的 SQL 與驗證結果。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty does not provide the proposed user-defined SQL threat-rule engine.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 不提供此處所稱的自訂 SQL 威脅規則引擎。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Logging and perimeter filtering omit validation of generated SQL semantics and schema.","why_zh":"日誌與周界篩選未驗證產生的 SQL 語意及結構描述。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Training and network isolation do not deterministically validate generated queries.","why_zh":"模型訓練及網路隔離不能確定性驗證產生的查詢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-prompt-attack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rdsdataservice/latest/APIReference/API_ExecuteStatement.html"],"issues":["data_api_not_validate_only","prompt_filters_not_sql_security_boundary"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.922083+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":106,"question_en":"A company needs a system to automatically generate study materials from multiple content sources. The content sources include document files (PDF files, PowerPoint presentations, and Word documents) and multimedia files (recorded videos). The system must process more than 10,000 content sources daily with peak loads of 500 concurrent uploads. The system must also extract key concepts from document files and multimedia files and create and store contextually accurate summaries. The generated study materials must support real-time collaboration with version control. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation (BDA) with AWS Lambda functions to orchestrate document file processing. Use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to process all multimedia. Store the content in Amazon DocumentDB with replication. Collaborate by using Amazon SNS topic subscriptions. Track changes by using Amazon Bedrock Agents.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation (BDA) with foundation models (FMs) to process document files. Integrate BDA with Amazon Textract for PDF extraction and with Amazon Transcribe for multimedia files. Store the processed content in Amazon S3 with versioning enabled. Store the metadata in Amazon DynamoDCollaborate in real time by using AWS AppSync GraphQL subscriptions with DynamoDB.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation (BDA) with Amazon SageMaker AI endpoints to host content extraction and summarization models. Use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to extract content from all file types. Store document files in Amazon Neptune for time series analysis. Collaborate by using Amazon Bedrock Chat for real-time messaging.","D":"Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation (BDA) with AWS Lambda functions to process batches of content files. Fine-tune foundation models (FMs) in Amazon Bedrock to classify documents across all content types. Store the processed data in Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) by using Cluster Mode with sharding. Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management for version control."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":106,"pages":[197]},"question_zh":"一家公司需要從多種內容來源自動產生教材。來源包含 PDF、PowerPoint、Word 文件及錄影等多媒體，每天須處理超過 10,000 個來源，尖峰同時上傳 500 份。系統必須從文件與多媒體擷取關鍵概念，產生及儲存符合脈絡的準確摘要，且教材必須支援即時協作與版本控制。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Bedrock Data Automation（BDA）與 Lambda 協調文件處理，以 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 處理全部多媒體。將內容存入具有複寫的 DocumentDB，以 SNS 主題訂閱進行協作，並用 Bedrock Agents 追蹤變更。","B":"使用 BDA 與基礎模型處理文件，整合 Textract 擷取 PDF，整合 Transcribe 處理多媒體。將處理後內容存入啟用版本控制的 S3，中繼資料存入 DynamoDB，透過搭配 DynamoDB 的 AppSync GraphQL 訂閱即時協作。","C":"使用 BDA 與 SageMaker AI 端點託管擷取及摘要模型，使用 Bedrock Guardrails 擷取所有檔案類型。將文件存入 Neptune 做時間序列分析，並透過 Bedrock Chat 即時傳訊協作。","D":"使用 BDA 與 Lambda 批次處理內容，微調 Bedrock FM 對各內容類型的文件分類。將資料存入啟用 Cluster Mode 分片的 ElastiCache（Redis OSS），以 Bedrock Prompt Management 進行版本控制。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B combines managed multimodal processing, durable versioned content storage and AppSync subscriptions for live updates. BDA already supports document, video and audio insights, so Textract/Transcribe are optional pipeline components rather than mandatory BDA internals. The BDA limits page lists DOCX for asynchronous document processing but not PowerPoint, so presentations require conversion to a supported format; synchronous document processing has a narrower format list. Queues, concurrency quotas and conflict/version handling still need design and testing; the listed services alone do not certify 500 simultaneous processing jobs or summary accuracy.","explanation_zh":"B 結合託管多模態處理、耐久且具版本的內容儲存，以及 AppSync 訂閱即時更新。BDA 本身已有文件、影片與音訊分析能力，所以 Textract／Transcribe 是可選管線元件，不是 BDA 必須依賴的內部元件。BDA 限制頁列出非同步文件處理支援 DOCX，但未列 PowerPoint，因此簡報須先轉為受支援格式；同步文件處理的格式清單更窄。佇列、並行配額、衝突與版本處理仍須設計驗證；僅列出這些服務不能證明支援 500 個同時處理工作或保證摘要準確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Knowledge Bases and SNS do not by themselves implement multimedia extraction and collaborative versioning.","why_zh":"Knowledge Bases 與 SNS 本身不會實作完整多媒體擷取及協作版本管理。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Guardrails is not a universal extraction engine and Neptune is not the proposed time-series document store.","why_zh":"Guardrails 不是通用擷取引擎，Neptune 也不是所述的時間序列文件儲存庫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ElastiCache is not the durable versioned content repository, and Prompt Management versions prompts rather than study documents.","why_zh":"ElastiCache 不是耐久的版本化內容儲存庫，Prompt Management 管的是提示版本而非教材文件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/bda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appsync/latest/devguide/aws-appsync-real-time-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/bda-limits.html"],"issues":["file_formats_and_concurrency_require_validation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.923018+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":107,"question_en":"A healthcare company wants to develop a proof-of-concept application that uses Amazon Bedrock to automatically summarize medical documents. The company has 3 weeks to validate the application’s accuracy. The application must comply with the company’s data privacy policies. The application must include metrics to evaluate summarization accuracy and processing time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create a dataset that includes 50-100 anonymized patient records. Implement Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with a secure knowledge base. Use a judge model to evaluate accuracy metrics across three foundation models (FMs).","B":"Fine-tune a single foundation model (FM) on patient records. Deploy the FM on Amazon Bedrock. Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to configure the FM as an agent. Conduct user testing on 500 company staff members.","C":"Select the most powerful available AWS foundation model (FM). Create a chat interface by using Converse APIs. Test the application on 50-100 actual patient records by using only qualitative feedback from stakeholders. Use a custom web interface to gather real-world performance metrics.","D":"Use the Strands SDK to deploy multiple agents that connect to multiple knowledge bases that contain specialized medical documents. Compare the responses of the agents. Evaluate the integration of the agents with the company’s existing systems."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":107,"pages":[198]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司希望在三週內開發並驗證概念驗證應用程式，使用 Amazon Bedrock 自動摘要醫療文件。應用程式必須符合公司資料隱私政策，並提供摘要準確度及處理時間的評估指標。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立含 50–100 份匿名化病歷的資料集，搭配安全知識庫實作 RAG，並用裁判模型評估三個 FM 的準確度指標。","B":"用病歷微調單一 FM，部署至 Bedrock，再用 AgentCore 將 FM 設為代理程式，並對 500 名員工進行使用者測試。","C":"選擇最強的 AWS FM，用 Converse API 建立聊天介面，以 50–100 份真實病歷測試，只收集利害關係人的質性回饋，並用自訂網頁介面收集實際效能指標。","D":"用 Strands SDK 部署多個連接專業醫療文件知識庫的代理程式，比較回覆，並評估代理程式與既有系統的整合。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is a bounded, privacy-conscious model-comparison experiment appropriate for the three-week proof of concept. A judge can score generated summaries against reference information while secure RAG supplies source context. The proposed option still omits explicit processing-time measurement, which must be collected for each model and pipeline. A 50–100-record sample supports initial evaluation, not clinical validation, and anonymization plus approved access controls must be verified.","explanation_zh":"A 是範圍明確、考慮隱私的模型比較實驗，適合三週概念驗證。裁判模型可依參考資訊評分摘要，安全 RAG 則提供原文脈絡。但此選項仍未明列處理時間測量，必須逐模型及管線收集。50–100 份資料只適合初步評估，不等於臨床驗證；匿名化與核准的存取控制也須確認。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Fine-tuning and a large staff study add effort before establishing a baseline across models.","why_zh":"尚未比較模型基準就微調及進行大型員工研究，增加工作量。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Actual records without a defined privacy control and qualitative-only accuracy feedback do not meet the stated evaluation design.","why_zh":"未定義隱私控制的真實病歷及僅質性準確度回饋不符合評估設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Multi-agent integration expands scope and lacks explicit privacy and accuracy/time metrics.","why_zh":"多代理整合擴大範圍，且未明列隱私與準確度／時間指標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html"],"issues":["processing_time_metric_omitted","poc_not_clinical_validation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.923640+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":108,"question_en":"A company wants to select a new FM for its AI assistant. A GenAI developer needs to generate evaluation reports to help a data scientist assess the quality and safety of various foundation models (FMs). The data scientist provides the GenAI developer with sample prompts for evaluation. The GenAI developer wants to use Amazon Bedrock to automate report generation and evaluation. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Combine the sample prompts into a single JSON document. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base with the document. Write a prompt that asks the FM to generate a response to each sample prompt. Use the RetrieveAndGenerate API to generate a report for each model.","B":"Combine the sample prompts into a single JSONL document. Store the document in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify the S3 location as input and a different S3 location as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the generator.","C":"Combine the sample prompts into a single JSONL document. Store the document in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Bedrock evaluation job that uses a judge model. Specify the S3 location as input and Amazon Quick Sight as output. Run an evaluation job for each FM and select the FM as the evaluator.","D":"Combine the sample prompts into a single JSON document. Create an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base from the document. Create an Amazon Bedrock evaluation job that uses the retrieval and response generation evaluation type. Specify an Amazon S3 bucket as the output. Run an evaluation job for each FM."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":108,"pages":[199]},"question_zh":"一家公司希望為 AI 助理選擇新 FM。GenAI 開發人員需要產生評估報告，協助資料科學家評估各基礎模型的品質與安全性。資料科學家已提供範例提示，開發人員希望透過 Amazon Bedrock 自動執行評估與產生報告。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"把範例提示合併成單一 JSON 文件，使用該文件建立 Bedrock 知識庫。撰寫提示要求 FM 回答每個範例提示，並用 RetrieveAndGenerate API 為各模型產生報告。","B":"把範例提示合併成單一 JSONL 文件並存入 S3。建立使用裁判模型的 Bedrock 評估工作，指定該 S3 位置為輸入、另一 S3 位置為輸出。為每個 FM 執行評估，並將該 FM 選為生成模型。","C":"把範例提示合併成單一 JSONL 文件並存入 S3。建立使用裁判模型的 Bedrock 評估工作，指定該 S3 位置為輸入、QuickSight 為輸出。為每個 FM 執行評估，並將該 FM 選為評估模型。","D":"把範例提示合併成單一 JSON 文件，據此建立 Bedrock 知識庫。建立檢索與回覆生成類型的 Bedrock 評估工作，指定 S3 儲存貯體作為輸出，並為每個 FM 執行評估。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B matches the model-as-judge evaluation data flow. The custom dataset is JSONL in S3, the candidate FM generates the responses, and a separately selected judge evaluates those responses using chosen metrics. Evaluation output is stored in S3 for reporting. A knowledge base is unnecessary for this model-comparison task, and the candidate generator must not be confused with the evaluator.","explanation_zh":"B 符合模型裁判評估的資料流程。自訂資料集以 JSONL 儲存在 S3，由候選 FM 生成回覆，再由另選的裁判模型按指定指標評估。評估輸出存入 S3 供報告使用。這種模型比較不需建立知識庫，也不能把候選生成模型與裁判混為一談。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RetrieveAndGenerate performs RAG; it is not the managed evaluation-report pipeline.","why_zh":"RetrieveAndGenerate 執行 RAG，不是託管評估報告管線。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"QuickSight is not the evaluation output location, and selecting candidates as evaluators reverses their role.","why_zh":"QuickSight 不是評估工作的輸出位置，將候選模型設為裁判也顛倒了角色。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This configures a knowledge-base evaluation rather than the requested direct model evaluation, with the wrong dataset format.","why_zh":"此方案設定的是知識庫評估而非直接模型評估，且資料集格式錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.924478+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":109,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a natural language processing (NLP) application that uses an AWS Lambda function to process customer trade inquiries by using Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs). The Lambda function must generate comprehensive trade analysis responses that typically exceed 4 MB and require 15-20 seconds to complete. The application must respond to customer inquiries in less than 10 seconds and comply with financial regulatory requirements to retain records for 10 years. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Implement response streaming to display partial responses as the application generates them. Set a 15- second timeout for Lambda function execution time. Enable AWS X-Ray tracing to monitor performance.","B":"Use Amazon SQS queues to implement asynchronous invocations. Set a 30-second timeout for Lambda function execution time. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor response times.","C":"Use Amazon API Gateway to poll the application. Integrate the application with Amazon ElastiCache to cache responses. Set a 30-second timeout for Lambda function execution time. Collect detailed Amazon CloudWatch logs for application performance.","D":"Implement response streaming to display partial responses as the application generates them. Set a 30- second timeout for Lambda function execution time. Store complete response records in Amazon S3."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":109,"pages":[200]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發 NLP 應用程式，以 AWS Lambda 呼叫 Amazon Bedrock FM 處理客戶交易詢問。完整交易分析回覆通常超過 4 MB，產生需要 15–20 秒。應用程式必須在 10 秒內回應，並依金融監管要求保留紀錄 10 年。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"實作回應串流，在產生過程顯示部分回覆；將 Lambda 執行逾時設為 15 秒，啟用 X-Ray 追蹤效能。","B":"使用 SQS 佇列進行非同步呼叫，將 Lambda 逾時設為 30 秒，以 CloudWatch 監控回應時間。","C":"使用 API Gateway 輪詢應用程式，整合 ElastiCache 快取回覆，將 Lambda 逾時設為 30 秒，並收集詳細 CloudWatch 效能日誌。","D":"實作回應串流，在產生過程顯示部分回覆；將 Lambda 執行逾時設為 30 秒，並將完整回覆紀錄存入 S3。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"D is the closest option: streaming improves time to first byte while a 30-second timeout accommodates the stated 15–20-second generation. It does not make the complete answer finish within ten seconds; the requirement must mean an initial visible response. S3 provides durable storage, but ten-year regulatory retention requires an explicit retention policy and, where required, versioning and Object Lock compliance retention. Merely writing to S3 neither enforces ten years nor prevents deletion.","explanation_zh":"D 最接近需求：串流改善第一個位元組的等待時間，30 秒逾時可容納題述 15–20 秒生成。它不會讓完整答案在十秒內完成，因此需求必須指初始可見回覆。S3 提供耐久儲存，但十年法規保存還需明確保存政策，必要時使用版本控制及 Object Lock 合規保留。只寫入 S3 不會強制保留十年，也不會防止刪除。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A 15-second timeout can terminate a 20-second response and tracing is not ten-year record retention.","why_zh":"15 秒逾時可能截斷 20 秒回覆，追蹤也不是十年紀錄保存。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Asynchronous acceptance does not provide the requested incremental response or retained complete records.","why_zh":"非同步受理未提供所需的逐段回覆或完整紀錄保存。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Polling and caching do not guarantee new analyses return sooner and omit durable regulatory records.","why_zh":"輪詢與快取不能保證新的分析提早回覆，也缺少耐久法規紀錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-response-streaming.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/response-transfer-mode-lambda.html"],"issues":["initial_response_not_completion","ten_year_retention_configuration_missing"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.925355+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":110,"question_en":"A university is building an AI-powered application that includes several sub-applications. The sub-applications include AI assistants, assignment graders, and internal analytics applications. The university is defining and testing multiple prompts by using various foundation models (FMs). The university wants to compare variants of each prompt and choose the variant that yield outputs that are best-suited for specified use cases. The university requires a version control solution for the prompts. The university must be able to test prompt variations and collect audit trails for prompt changes and usage. The solution must also maintain consistency while allowing the prompts to integrate into the main application. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to create versioned prompts. Include parameterized variables for each use case.","B":"Store prompts in Amazon S3. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate the model interactions and service integrations.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Flows to create workflows that combine FMs and AWS services.","D":"Configure AWS Config to record prompt changes. Use AWS CloudTrail to track prompt usage.","E":"Configure Amazon Bedrock intelligent prompt routing."},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":110,"pages":[201]},"question_zh":"一所大學正在建立包含 AI 助理、作業評分及內部分析等子應用程式的 AI 系統。大學使用各種 FM 定義並測試多個提示，希望比較每個提示的變體，選出最適合用途的輸出。大學需要提示版本控制，能測試變化並收集提示修改與使用的稽核軌跡，同時維持一致性並整合至主應用程式。哪兩個方案以最少維運負擔符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Bedrock Prompt Management 建立版本化提示，為各用途加入參數化變數。","B":"將提示存入 S3，使用 Step Functions 協調模型互動與服務整合。","C":"使用 Bedrock Flows 建立結合 FM 與 AWS 服務的工作流程。","D":"設定 AWS Config 記錄提示修改，以 CloudTrail 追蹤提示使用。","E":"設定 Bedrock 智慧提示路由。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A and C provide native prompt variants, variables, version snapshots and managed workflow integration. Prompt Management supports comparing variants and reusing the chosen version in a flow. Flows connects prompts, models and services without assembling a separate orchestration layer. Version history is not a complete usage audit: CloudTrail and appropriate invocation/application logs must still be configured to capture the required changes and uses.","explanation_zh":"A 與 C 提供原生提示變體、變數、版本快照及託管流程整合。Prompt Management 支援比較變體並在流程重用選定版本；Flows 串接提示、模型與服務，減少另建協調層的工作。版本歷史不等於完整使用稽核，仍需設定 CloudTrail 及適當的呼叫／應用程式日誌，記錄要求的修改與使用。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 plus custom Step Functions workflows adds orchestration and prompt-management work.","why_zh":"S3 加自訂 Step Functions 增加協調及提示管理工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config is not the native prompt variant/version manager and this combination omits the required workflow capability.","why_zh":"AWS Config 不是原生提示變體／版本管理器，且此組合缺少所需流程能力。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Intelligent prompt routing selects models; it does not version or compare prompt variants.","why_zh":"智慧提示路由選擇模型，不負責提示變體版本管理或比較。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/flows.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html"],"issues":["audit_logging_requires_configuration"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.926122+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":111,"question_en":"A company is building a multicloud generative AI (GenAI)-powered secret resolution application that uses Amazon Bedrock and Agent Squad. The application resolves secrets from multiple sources, including key stores and hardware security modules (HSMs). The application uses AWS Lambda functions to retrieve secrets from the sources. The application uses AWS AppConfig to implement dynamic feature gating. The application supports secret chaining and detects secret drift. The application handles short-lived and expiring secrets. The application also supports prompt flows for templated instructions. The application uses AWS Step Functions to orchestrate agents to resolve the secrets and to manage secret validation and drift detection. The company finds multiple issues during application testing. The application does not refresh expired secrets in time for agents to use. The application sends alerts for secret drift, but agents still use stale data. Prompt flows within the application reuse outdated templates, which cause cascading failures. The company must resolve the performance issues. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Use Step Functions Map states to run agent workflows in parallel. Pass updated secret metadata through Lambda function outputs. Use AWS AppConfig to version all prompt flows to gate and roll back faulty templates.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore only. Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails to restrict prompt variation. Use an inline JSON schema for a single agent’s workflow definition to chain tool calls.","C":"Use a centralized Amazon EventBridge pipeline to invoke each event agent. Store intermediate prompts in Amazon DynamoDB. Resolve agent ordering by using TTL-based backoff and retries.","D":"Use Amazon EventBridge Pipes to invoke resolvers based on Amazon CloudWatch log patterns. Store response metadata in Amazon DynamoDB. Configure a TTL and versioned writes. Use Amazon Q Developer to dynamically generate fallback prompts that are routed through a Lambda coordinator."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":111,"pages":[202]},"question_zh":"一家公司以 Amazon Bedrock 與 Agent Squad 建立多雲 GenAI 密鑰解析應用程式，透過 Lambda 從金鑰儲存庫、HSM 等多種來源取得密鑰，並用 AppConfig 動態控制功能。系統支援密鑰鏈結、密鑰漂移偵測、短效及即將到期密鑰，以及範本指令的提示流程。Step Functions 協調代理解析密鑰、驗證及漂移偵測。測試發現過期密鑰未及時更新；即使發出漂移警示，代理仍使用舊資料；提示流程也重用過期範本，導致連鎖失敗。哪個方案可解決問題？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Step Functions Map 狀態並行執行代理流程，透過 Lambda 輸出傳遞更新後的密鑰中繼資料。使用 AppConfig 為所有提示流程建立版本，以控制啟用並回復有問題的範本。","B":"只使用 Bedrock AgentCore，設定 Guardrails 限制提示變化，以單一代理流程定義中的內嵌 JSON 結構描述串接工具呼叫。","C":"用集中式 EventBridge 管線呼叫每個事件代理，將中間提示存入 DynamoDB，並用基於 TTL 的退避與重試處理代理順序。","D":"使用 EventBridge Pipes 依 CloudWatch 日誌模式呼叫解析器，將回應中繼資料存入 DynamoDB，設定 TTL 與版本化寫入。使用 Amazon Q Developer 動態產生備援提示，再送至 Lambda 協調器。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A most directly improves state propagation and controlled template rollout. Map states can parallelize independent work, Lambda outputs can carry current version/expiry metadata, and AppConfig supports staged configuration deployment and rollback. Parallelism itself does not refresh secrets: dependent chains still require correct ordering, explicit refresh and cache invalidation. Pass identifiers and metadata rather than exposing secret values in workflow history, and implement expiry checks before each dependent use.","explanation_zh":"A 最直接改善狀態傳遞及受控範本推出。Map 可並行處理獨立工作，Lambda 輸出可攜帶最新版本／到期中繼資料，AppConfig 則支援分階段組態部署與回復。但並行本身不會更新密鑰；有相依性的鏈仍須正確排序、明確更新及使快取失效。應傳遞識別碼與中繼資料，避免密鑰值暴露於流程歷史，並在每次相依使用前檢查到期狀態。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Guardrails and a single schema do not implement expiry refresh or template version propagation.","why_zh":"Guardrails 與單一結構描述不會實作到期更新及範本版本傳遞。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"TTL-based retries do not establish correct dependency ordering or invalidate stale values immediately.","why_zh":"TTL 重試不會建立正確相依順序，也不會立即使舊值失效。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reactive log-driven resolution and generated fallback prompts add nondeterminism without fixing the source-of-truth state flow.","why_zh":"被動日誌觸發及臨時生成備援提示增加不確定性，未修復權威狀態傳遞。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-map.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/monitoring-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/appconfig/latest/userguide/appconfig-creating-deployment-strategy.html"],"issues":["parallelism_not_secret_refresh","dependent_chains_need_ordering"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.927084+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":112,"question_en":"A financial services company processes more than 10,000 customer inquiries every day through a multi-agent GenAI application that uses Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. The application agents invoke several custom tools. During peak usage periods, users report that the custom tools experience up to 40% failure rates. The tools perform inconsistently for different teams at the company. A GenAI developer must implement an observability solution that provides end-to-end visibility into agent interactions and tool behavior. The solution must use built-in Amazon Bedrock capabilities and must not require custom instrumentation. The GenAI developer needs a solution that requires minimal performance overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Enable AgentCore Observability and trace collection. Use AWS X-Ray to capture distributed traces for the custom tools. Build Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to visualize metrics for errors, throttling, and latency during peak usage periods.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights to monitor the agents. Configure an AWS Lambda function to poll the Amazon Bedrock API for tool usage metrics. Configure the function to store results in CloudWatch to generate alerts.","C":"Build a custom ETL pipeline that uses AWS Lambda functions to process Amazon CloudWatch logs from Amazon Bedrock. Store the processed data in Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon Quick Sight to visualize cross-team performance patterns.","D":"Enable AgentCore Observability and send trace data to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use a custom AWS Lambda function to extract tool performance metrics from the logs. Use Amazon Managed Grafana to visualize trends."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":112,"pages":[203]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司每天透過使用 Bedrock AgentCore 的多代理 GenAI 應用程式處理超過 10,000 筆客戶詢問。代理會呼叫數個自訂工具。尖峰期間工具失敗率高達 40%，不同團隊使用時表現也不一致。GenAI 開發人員必須以內建 Bedrock 能力建立可觀測方案，端到端查看代理互動與工具行為，不需自訂插樁，且效能負擔最小。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"啟用 AgentCore Observability 及追蹤收集，使用 X-Ray 擷取自訂工具的分散式追蹤，建立 CloudWatch 儀表板顯示尖峰錯誤、節流與延遲指標。","B":"用 CloudWatch Container Insights 監控代理，設定 Lambda 輪詢 Bedrock API 的工具使用指標並存入 CloudWatch 產生警示。","C":"建立自訂 ETL 管線，以 Lambda 處理 Bedrock 的 CloudWatch 日誌，將結果存入 DynamoDB，以 QuickSight 顯示跨團隊效能。","D":"啟用 AgentCore Observability 並將追蹤送至 CloudWatch Logs，使用自訂 Lambda 擷取工具效能指標，再用 Managed Grafana 顯示趨勢。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A best uses AgentCore Observability with CloudWatch metrics and distributed traces. Built-in telemetry covers AgentCore resources and supported instrumentation can expose agent/tool spans with little application work. However arbitrary custom tools do not automatically emit full internal X-Ray traces merely because Observability is enabled; supported framework instrumentation, OTEL configuration and context propagation must be verified. Minimal overhead requires appropriate sampling, so the no-custom-instrumentation claim is conditional on the actual tool stack.","explanation_zh":"A 最符合使用 AgentCore Observability、CloudWatch 指標及分散式追蹤的方向。內建遙測涵蓋 AgentCore 資源，受支援的插樁可用少量應用程式工作呈現代理／工具 span。但任意自訂工具不會因啟用 Observability 就自動輸出完整內部 X-Ray 追蹤，仍須確認框架插樁、OTEL 設定及追蹤脈絡傳遞。降低負擔也需適當抽樣，因此「不需自訂插樁」取決於實際工具技術。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Container metrics and polling do not provide causal end-to-end agent/tool traces.","why_zh":"容器指標與輪詢不提供具因果關係的端到端代理／工具追蹤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A custom ETL pipeline violates the low-custom-work requirement and adds processing overhead.","why_zh":"自訂 ETL 不符合減少自訂工作的要求，也增加處理負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The custom log extraction function is unnecessary for available built-in metrics and increases maintenance.","why_zh":"對已有內建指標另寫日誌擷取函數增加不必要維護。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/observability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/observability-configure.html"],"issues":["custom_tool_trace_coverage_requires_instrumentation"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.927840+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":113,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is using an Anthropic Claude Sonnet model in Amazon Bedrock to generate product recommendations. An AWS Lambda function retrieves customer purchase data from Amazon DynamoDB, product reviews from Amazon S3, and customer profile information from Amazon RDS. Then the function sends the data directly to the Amazon Bedrock model through API calls. Recently, customers who have extensive purchase histories have begun to receive incomplete recommendations. Amazon CloudWatch logs for the Lambda function show execution timeouts. CloudWatch logs for Amazon Bedrock API calls show intermittent errors. The company reviews the logs and finds that some requests are failing with context length exceeded errors. Other requests finish but appear to ignore portions of the input data. The company wants the recommendation system to consider all customer data when the system generates recommendations. The company wants to use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to improve data organization and retrieval. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","options_en":{"A":"Implement a chunking strategy that divides the customer data into smaller segments. Configure the model to process each segment separately. Invoke the model a final time to synthesize the individual responses into comprehensive recommendations.","B":"Modify the prompt structure to place the most critical information at the beginning and end of the context window. Implement token-counting logic to truncate less important data when the interaction approaches the model’s maximum context length.","C":"Replace Claude Sonnet with a model that has a larger context window capacity. Increase the Lambda function timeout to accommodate longer processing times for larger inputs.","D":"Configure the recommendation system to use the Converse API. Modify the additionalModelRequestFields parameter to increase the maximum token limit beyond the model’s default context window size.","E":"Implement RAG by using a knowledge base to index the customer data with vector embeddings. Retrieve only the most semantically relevant information for each recommendation request based on the current customer context."},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":113,"pages":[204]},"question_zh":"一家電商公司使用 Amazon Bedrock 的 Anthropic Claude Sonnet 模型產生商品推薦。Lambda 先從 DynamoDB 取得購買紀錄、從 S3 取得商品評論、從 RDS 取得客戶資料，再直接透過 API 將資料送至模型。近期購買紀錄豐富的客戶收到不完整推薦；Lambda 的 CloudWatch 日誌出現執行逾時，Bedrock API 日誌有間歇錯誤，其中部分請求超過脈絡長度，另一些雖完成卻忽略部分輸入。公司希望產生推薦時考慮所有客戶資料，並用 Bedrock Knowledge Bases 改善資料組織與檢索。哪兩個方案符合需求？（選兩項。）","options_zh":{"A":"實作分塊策略，把客戶資料分成較小區段，設定模型分別處理，再最後呼叫一次模型，將各回覆整合為完整推薦。","B":"修改提示結構，把最重要資訊放在脈絡開頭及結尾；實作 token 計數，在接近模型最大脈絡長度時截掉較不重要資料。","C":"將 Claude Sonnet 換成脈絡視窗更大的模型，增加 Lambda 逾時以容納較大輸入的處理時間。","D":"改用 Converse API，透過 additionalModelRequestFields 把最大 token 限制增加至模型預設脈絡視窗之外。","E":"使用知識庫向量嵌入索引客戶資料實作 RAG，依目前客戶脈絡，每次推薦只檢索語意最相關的資訊。"},"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A and E combine bounded processing with retrieval instead of sending an unbounded history in one prompt. A map-and-synthesize process can cover all input segments, while RAG selects relevant evidence within the model context budget. The final synthesis also needs a token budget or hierarchical reduction. RAG alone does not guarantee every record is considered, so exhaustive coverage requires explicit per-segment processing and coverage tracking; retrieval must also enforce customer-level authorization.","explanation_zh":"A 與 E 結合有界處理及檢索，避免把無限增長的歷史一次送入提示。分段處理再綜合可涵蓋所有輸入，RAG 則在模型脈絡預算內挑選相關證據。最終綜合仍需 token 預算或階層式歸納。單靠 RAG 不保證考慮每筆紀錄；若要求完整涵蓋，需明確逐段處理及追蹤涵蓋率，檢索也必須執行客戶層級授權。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Truncation intentionally drops records, conflicting with considering all customer data.","why_zh":"截斷會刻意捨棄紀錄，與考慮所有客戶資料矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A larger finite window only postpones the limit and does not implement the requested knowledge-base organization.","why_zh":"較大的有限視窗只是延後遇到上限，也未實作所需知識庫組織。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Request fields cannot override the model architecture context limit.","why_zh":"請求欄位不能突破模型架構的脈絡限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-map.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/titan-embedding-models.html"],"issues":["rag_not_exhaustive_coverage"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.928617+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":114,"question_en":"A company developed a multimodal content analysis application by using Amazon Bedrock. The application routes different content types (text, images, and code) to specialized foundation models (FMs). The application needs to handle multiple types of routing decisions. Simple routing based on file extension must have minimal latency. Complex routing based on content semantics requires analysis before FM selection. The application must provide detailed history and support fallback options when primary FMs fail. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Lambda functions that call Amazon Bedrock FMs for all routing logic. Use conditional statements to determine the appropriate FM based on content type and semantics.","B":"Create a hybrid solution. Handle simple routing based on file extensions in application code. Handle complex content-based routing by using an AWS Step Functions state machine with JSONata for content analysis and the InvokeModel API for specialized FMs.","C":"Deploy separate AWS Step Functions workflows for each content type with routing logic in AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon EventBridge to coordinate between workflows when fallback to alternate FMs is required.","D":"Use Amazon SQS with different SQS queues for each content type. Configure AWS Lambda consumers that analyze content and invoke appropriate FMs based on message attributes by using Amazon Bedrock with an AWS SDK."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":114,"pages":[205]},"question_zh":"一家公司以 Amazon Bedrock 建立多模態內容分析應用程式，將文字、影像及程式碼路由至專門的 FM。簡單的副檔名路由必須延遲極低；複雜的語意路由則需要先分析內容再選模型。應用程式還必須提供詳細歷史，並在主要 FM 失敗時支援備援。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"所有路由邏輯都使用呼叫 Bedrock FM 的 Lambda，透過條件陳述式依內容類型及語意決定模型。","B":"採混合方案：簡單的副檔名路由在應用程式碼中處理，複雜內容路由使用 Step Functions 狀態機，以 JSONata 分析內容並用 InvokeModel 呼叫專門 FM。","C":"為每種內容建立獨立 Step Functions 流程，路由邏輯放在 Lambda，並在需要替代 FM 時用 EventBridge 協調流程。","D":"為不同內容類型建立不同 SQS 佇列，設定 Lambda 消費者分析內容，依訊息屬性用 AWS SDK 呼叫合適的 Bedrock FM。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B keeps deterministic file-extension decisions on the fast path and uses a state machine for auditable multi-step routing and fallback. Step Functions can invoke Bedrock and use Choice, Retry and Catch logic around model results. JSONata selects and transforms JSON; it is not a semantic classifier for raw images or natural language. Complex semantic analysis must be performed by an invoked model or explicit classifier, with JSONata operating on that result.","explanation_zh":"B 讓確定性的副檔名判斷保留在快速路徑，複雜路由與備援則由可稽核的狀態機處理。Step Functions 可呼叫 Bedrock，並以 Choice、Retry、Catch 處理模型結果。JSONata 是 JSON 選取與轉換語言，不是原始影像或自然語言的語意分類器。複雜語意分析仍須由被呼叫的模型或明確分類器執行，再由 JSONata 處理結果。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Calling a model for deterministic extension routing adds latency and lacks an explicit durable workflow history.","why_zh":"為確定性的副檔名路由呼叫模型增加延遲，也缺少明確耐久流程歷史。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Separate workflows and cross-workflow events add unnecessary coordination for the simple fast path.","why_zh":"拆成多流程再用事件協調，對簡單快速路徑增加不必要成本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Queues support decoupling but do not alone implement the requested detailed routing history and fallback state machine.","why_zh":"佇列支援解耦，但本身未實作所需詳細路由歷史及備援狀態機。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/transforming-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/concepts-error-handling.html"],"issues":["jsonata_not_semantic_analysis"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.929329+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":115,"question_en":"A company is developing a customer support chat assistant that uses an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM). The company wants to update to a newer FM version but needs to implement a validation system to detect semantic drift in responses. The company wants to ensure that performance and functionality for end users remains consistent. The company needs a solution to compare responses between current and new FM versions for 500 test cases. The solution must detect changes in response meaning, generate quantitative similarity scores, complete validations, and log detailed results for historical comparison. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational complexity?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics canaries that use custom JavaScript code to send identical prompts to both new and existing FM versions. Store responses in Amazon S3. Perform manual reviews to identify semantic differences between FM versions.","B":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow that sends test prompts to both new and existing FM versions. Use Amazon Bedrock embedding models to calculate cosine similarity scores. Store the results in Amazon DynamoDB with a composite key schema.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock model evaluation jobs to compare the new FM version against the current version using the 500 test cases. Configure the evaluation to calculate semantic similarity metrics. Store results in Amazon S3 for historical comparison.","D":"Build a custom solution by using Amazon SageMaker AI to train a classifier model on historical responses to detect anomalies when the solution compares responses from the new FM version to previous patterns."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":115,"pages":[206]},"question_zh":"一家公司正在開發使用 Bedrock FM 的客服聊天助理。公司想升級模型版本，必須建立驗證系統偵測回覆的語意漂移，確保使用者的效能及功能一致。系統需用 500 個測試案例比較目前與新模型版本的回覆，辨識意思改變、產生量化相似度分數、完成驗證，並記錄詳細結果供歷史比較。哪個方案維運複雜度最低？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 CloudWatch Synthetics canary，以自訂 JavaScript 向兩個模型版本送相同提示，將回覆存入 S3，再人工審查語意差異。","B":"設定 Step Functions 將提示送至新舊模型，使用 Bedrock 嵌入模型計算餘弦相似度，並將結果存入具有複合鍵的 DynamoDB。","C":"使用 Bedrock 模型評估工作，以 500 個測試案例比較新舊 FM 版本，設定計算語意相似度指標，將結果存入 S3 供歷史比較。","D":"使用 SageMaker AI 自訂訓練分類模型，以歷史回覆訓練，在比較新版本回覆與舊模式時偵測異常。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C offers managed evaluation and persisted reports with less custom orchestration. Bedrock supports custom datasets, reference responses and judge-defined custom metrics, which can explicitly score semantic equivalence against baseline responses. The evaluator and scoring rubric must be configured; there is not a universal automatic semantic-drift switch. Five hundred cases fit the documented 1,000-prompt per-job dataset limit, and consistent datasets and evaluator versions support historical comparisons.","explanation_zh":"C 提供託管評估及報告保存，減少自訂協調。Bedrock 支援自訂資料集、參考回覆及裁判自訂指標，可以明確評量與基準回覆的語意等價程度。必須設定評估模型與評分準則，並不存在通用的「自動語意漂移」開關。500 個案例在文件所述每工作 1,000 筆提示限制內，固定資料集與裁判版本有助歷史比較。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Manual semantic review does not deliver the required automated quantitative validation.","why_zh":"人工語意審查不提供所需自動量化驗證。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Embeddings plus separately implemented cosine scoring can work, but require custom orchestration and reporting.","why_zh":"嵌入加另行實作的餘弦計分可行，但需自訂協調與報告。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Training and maintaining a classifier is substantially more complex than managed evaluation.","why_zh":"訓練與維護分類器比託管評估複雜得多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.930065+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":116,"question_en":"A media company is building an AI-powered content moderation system by using Amazon Bedrock. The system first classifies text by using a small, low-latency model. Then the system escalates requests that have a confidence score below 0.65 to a larger, more expensive model. The system must respond in near real time for high-confidence results. The system must process low- confidence requests asynchronously. The system must scale to meet sudden spikes in demand. The company wants to optimize costs for the system by invoking the larger model only when required. The company wants to use decoupled components to achieve high resiliency for the system. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon API Gateway to invoke the small model synchronously. If the small model’s confidence score is below 0.65, synchronously call the larger model. Use provisioned concurrency to handle traffic spikes.","B":"Use an AWS Step Functions workflow that has parallel branches to run both the small model and the large model for every request. Choose the large model result when confidence score values differ.","C":"Send requests to an Amazon SQS queue. Use AWS Fargate to process messages. Invoke the small model first. If the confidence score is below 0.65, place the request in a second SQS queue to process asynchronously by using the large model.","D":"Deploy both models on Amazon EC2 instances and enable auto scaling. Use a custom application heuristic to route requests to the appropriate instance based on phrase length and keyword rules."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":116,"pages":[207]},"question_zh":"一家媒體公司以 Bedrock 建立內容審核系統。系統先用小型低延遲模型分類文字，當信心分數低於 0.65 時才升級至較大且較昂貴模型。高信心結果必須近即時回覆；低信心請求須非同步處理。系統必須承受突發流量，只在必要時呼叫大模型以省成本，並透過元件解耦提高韌性。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 API Gateway 同步呼叫小模型，若信心低於 0.65，再同步呼叫大模型，並用預佈並行處理尖峰。","B":"用 Step Functions 平行分支對每個請求同時呼叫大小模型，信心分數不同時選大模型結果。","C":"將請求送入 SQS，以 Fargate 消費訊息，先呼叫小模型；若信心低於 0.65，將請求放入第二個 SQS 佇列，由大模型非同步處理。","D":"在 EC2 部署兩個模型並啟用自動擴展，用自訂啟發式規則按片語長度及關鍵字路由至適當執行個體。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C supplies a decoupled two-stage queue architecture and invokes the expensive model only for low-confidence cases. SQS buffers spikes and Fargate workers can scale with backlog. Because even the first stage is queued, near-real-time results require warm capacity, bounded queue delay and a response-delivery mechanism; the option does not itself specify those. Confidence must also be calibrated rather than assumed reliable from a self-reported model score.","explanation_zh":"C 提供解耦的雙階段佇列架構，只在低信心時呼叫昂貴模型。SQS 緩衝尖峰，Fargate worker 可依積壓量擴展。但第一階段本身也先排隊，因此近即時結果需要保留溫熱容量、限制排隊延遲及回覆傳遞機制，選項未完整說明。信心分數也須校準，不能直接假定模型自報分數可靠。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The low-confidence path remains synchronous and tightly couples both models.","why_zh":"低信心路徑仍同步執行，且緊密耦合兩個模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Always invoking both models defeats conditional escalation and cost savings.","why_zh":"每次都呼叫兩個模型違反條件升級及成本目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Length/keyword heuristics do not implement the specified confidence-based asynchronous escalation.","why_zh":"長度／關鍵字規則未實作指定的信心式非同步升級。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/reference-architecture-diagrams/latest/autoscaling-async-job-queues/autoscaling-async-job-queues.html"],"issues":["queued_first_stage_latency_requires_capacity"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.930751+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":117,"question_en":"A social messaging company is building an AI chat assistant by using Amazon Bedrock. The company must ensure that every inference complies with an approved safety policy. The company wants to block harmful prompts before model invocations, filter streamed model outputs in real time, and route flagged cases for human review. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow. Configure a step to use an AWS Lambda function to pre- check inputs by using the ApplyGuardrail API. Use an InvokeModelWithResponseStream API step that has the guardrail attached. Configure a second Lambda function step to post-check outputs by using the ApplyGuardrail API. Route flagged items to an Amazon SQS queue. Enforce guardrail use by using a bedrock:GuardrailIdentifier IAM condition.","B":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow. Configure a step to call the ApplyGuardrail API before inference. Then call the InvokeModel API without streaming and use the guardrail. Store the results in Amazon S3. Use the client UI to hide problematic tokens.","C":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow. Configure a step to use the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API that has the guardrail attached for in-stream filtering. Run an AWS Lambda post-check step by using the ApplyGuardrail API to check flagged cases. Do not perform pre- inference.","D":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow that includes steps to perform pre-checks and post-checks by using the ApplyGuardrail API and the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API. Attach the guardrail to the check steps. Use process controls such as code reviews instead of IAM enforcement to ensure that guardrails are always applied."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":117,"pages":[208]},"question_zh":"一家社交訊息公司以 Bedrock 建立 AI 聊天助理，必須確保每次推論都遵循核准安全政策。公司希望在模型呼叫前阻擋有害提示，即時篩選串流模型輸出，並將被標記案例送交人工審查。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Step Functions 流程，先用 Lambda 透過 ApplyGuardrail API 檢查輸入；使用附加護欄的 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API 步驟；再用另一 Lambda 透過 ApplyGuardrail 檢查輸出。把被標記項目送至 SQS，並用 bedrock:GuardrailIdentifier IAM 條件強制套用護欄。","B":"設定 Step Functions 先呼叫 ApplyGuardrail，再使用護欄呼叫非串流 InvokeModel；結果存入 S3，並由客戶端 UI 隱藏問題 token。","C":"設定 Step Functions 使用附加護欄的 InvokeModelWithResponseStream 進行串流篩選，執行 Lambda 後置步驟用 ApplyGuardrail 檢查被標記案例，不進行推論前檢查。","D":"設定 Step Functions，包含 ApplyGuardrail 前後檢查及 InvokeModelWithResponseStream 步驟，在檢查步驟附加護欄，以程式碼審查等流程控制取代 IAM 強制，確保每次套用護欄。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A includes the needed pre-check, guarded inference, review queue and enforceable IAM condition. Streaming must use synchronous guardrail processing when unsafe chunks must be checked before display; asynchronous mode can expose content before blocking. However Step Functions does not provide a native streaming Bedrock task that relays token events to clients: use a streaming-capable worker and delivery channel while the workflow coordinates control and review. The option is therefore a closest design rather than a directly executable state-machine definition, and safety detection is not a mathematical guarantee.","explanation_zh":"A 包含必要的前置檢查、附護欄推論、審查佇列及可強制的 IAM 條件。如果顯示前必須檢查不安全區塊，串流護欄須使用同步處理；非同步模式可能先洩出內容才阻擋。但 Step Functions 沒有可把 token 事件轉送客戶端的原生 Bedrock 串流工作，需用支援串流的 worker 與傳輸通道，讓流程協調控制及審查。因此此選項是最接近的設計，不是可直接執行的狀態機定義，安全偵測也不是數學上的保證。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"It removes streaming and UI hiding occurs too late to enforce server-side filtering.","why_zh":"此方案取消串流，且 UI 隱藏無法取代伺服器端過濾。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It omits the explicit pre-inference block and enforceable requirement that every call carry the approved guardrail.","why_zh":"缺少明確推論前阻擋，以及強制每次附核准護欄的控制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Code reviews cannot prevent an authorized caller from omitting a guardrail at runtime.","why_zh":"程式碼審查無法阻止有權呼叫者在執行時省略護欄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-streaming.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-permissions-id.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/connect-bedrock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/supported-services-awssdk.html"],"issues":["step_functions_not_client_token_stream","synchronous_guardrail_mode_required"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.931755+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":118,"question_en":"A financial services company uses Amazon Bedrock to analyze customer data that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The data includes personally identifiable information (PII). The company must mask PII from foundation model (FM) responses. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational effort?","options_en":{"A":"Create a guardrail in Amazon Bedrock to filter PII content. Define the PII type and set the guardrail action to MASK. Configure Amazon Bedrock to apply the filter to each FM response.","B":"Use Amazon Comprehend to detect PII entities in the S3 data before invoking Amazon Bed-rock. Configure an AWS Lambda function to call the Amazon Comprehend DetectPiiEntities API to mask detected PII. Store the processed data back to the original S3 bucket.","C":"Use Amazon Macie to scan the S3 bucket for PII data. Configure an AWS Lambda function to store PII in a second S3 bucket. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda func-tion.","D":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to search for PII data. Implement a step in the Lambda function code to store the PII in a second S3 bucket and non-PII data into a third S3 bucket."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":118,"pages":[209]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司使用 Bedrock 分析 S3 中的客戶資料，其中包含個人識別資訊（PII）。公司必須遮罩基礎模型回覆中的 PII。哪個方案維運負擔最低？","options_zh":{"A":"在 Bedrock 建立篩選 PII 的護欄，指定 PII 類型並將動作設為 MASK，設定每個 FM 回覆都套用篩選。","B":"呼叫 Bedrock 前先用 Comprehend 偵測 S3 資料中的 PII，以 Lambda 呼叫 DetectPiiEntities 並遮罩偵測結果，再寫回原 S3 儲存貯體。","C":"用 Macie 掃描 S3 中的 PII，設定 Lambda 將 PII 存入第二個 S3 儲存貯體，並用 EventBridge 規則呼叫 Lambda。","D":"設定 Lambda 搜尋 PII，自訂程式將 PII 存入第二個 S3 儲存貯體，非 PII 存入第三個儲存貯體。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A directly applies the managed sensitive-information filter to model responses with minimal custom processing. Select the relevant built-in PII entities and custom patterns as needed, then configure masking on every inference path. The API action name is ANONYMIZE, while the console/documentation describes the behavior as Mask; MASK in the option is conceptual terminology. Detection is probabilistic, and masking during streaming requires synchronous guardrail processing.","explanation_zh":"A 直接把託管敏感資訊篩選套用至模型回覆，自訂處理最少。應選擇適用的內建 PII 類型，必要時加入自訂樣式，並在每條推論路徑設定遮罩。API 動作名稱是 ANONYMIZE，主控台／說明文件稱為 Mask；選項中的 MASK 是概念用詞。偵測具有機率性，串流遮罩也必須使用同步護欄處理。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Input redaction does not catch newly generated PII in output and requires custom code.","why_zh":"輸入去識別化抓不到輸出新生成的 PII，且需自訂程式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Macie discovers sensitive data at rest; moving source PII does not mask generated responses.","why_zh":"Macie 發現靜態敏感資料；搬移來源 PII 不會遮罩生成回覆。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom source-data partitioning does not directly filter FM output.","why_zh":"自訂來源資料分流不會直接篩選 FM 輸出。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-streaming.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_GuardrailPiiEntityConfig.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.932848+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":119,"question_en":"A healthcare company is implementing a clinical knowledge base application on Amazon Bed-rock that provides medical information to doctors. During testing, a quality team discovers that the generative AI (GenAI) model occasionally fabricates medical treatment recommendations that do not originate from the approved clinical guidelines. The quality team needs to implement a solution to detect the hallucinations before releasing the application. The solution must analyze model responses against verified medical information. The solution must identify semantic inconsistencies when users ask similar questions in different ways. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a real-time monitoring system that uses Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze response patterns and to flag factual inaccuracies based on predefined keywords. Implement AWS Lambda functions to compare responses with known answers from an Amazon Dyna-moDB table.","B":"Create a reference dataset with validated question-answer pairs from clinical guidelines. Im-plement output diffing by using Amazon Bedrock Guardrails for response consistency analysis. Use Amazon Bedrock evaluation to detect factual inaccuracies.","C":"Configure Amazon Bedrock Guardrails with custom rules to detect and block potentially hal-lucinated content by identifying specific patterns in the GenAI responses. Use Amazon Sage-Maker Feature Store to maintain a repository of verified clinical guidelines.","D":"Create an Amazon Bedrock automatic model evaluation job with a custom prompt dataset. Set up anomaly detection alarms to identify factual inaccuracies. Implement Amazon SNS notifi-cations when inaccuracies are detected."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":119,"pages":[210]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司在 Bedrock 建立提供醫師醫療資訊的臨床知識庫應用程式。測試時品質團隊發現模型偶爾捏造不在核准臨床指引中的治療建議。團隊需要在上線前偵測幻覺，將模型回覆與已驗證的醫療資訊比對，並辨識使用者用不同說法問相似問題時的語意不一致。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 即時分析回覆模式，依預定關鍵字標記事實錯誤，再用 Lambda 與 DynamoDB 已知答案比對。","B":"依臨床指引建立經驗證的問答參考資料集，使用 Bedrock Guardrails 實作輸出差異比對及回覆一致性分析，並用 Bedrock 評估偵測事實錯誤。","C":"設定 Guardrails 自訂規則，依回覆特定模式偵測並阻擋可能幻覺，並用 SageMaker Feature Store 儲存已驗證臨床指引。","D":"使用自訂提示資料集建立 Bedrock 自動模型評估工作，設定異常偵測警示辨識事實錯誤，並以 SNS 通知。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B is the closest intended evaluation approach because it anchors testing in validated clinical references. Grounding checks compare a response against a supplied source and query, while model evaluation can score correctness with reference responses. Guardrails does not expose a general output-diffing or cross-prompt consistency engine, so paraphrase groups and a semantic-equivalence metric must be implemented in the evaluation harness. Consequently no option fully implements every stated requirement as written; keyword or metric anomaly detection cannot certify medical factuality.","explanation_zh":"B 是命題意圖中最接近的評估方向，因為它以已驗證臨床參考資料作為測試基礎。脈絡依據檢查會將回覆與所提供來源及查詢比對，模型評估可用參考答案計算正確性。但 Guardrails 不提供通用輸出差異比對或跨提示一致性引擎，因此需在評估框架建立改寫問題群組與語意等價指標。沒有選項按字面完整實作全部需求；關鍵字或指標異常偵測都不能證明醫療事實正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Keyword patterns are inadequate for semantic contradiction and factual hallucinations.","why_zh":"關鍵字模式不足以辨識語意矛盾及事實幻覺。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Pattern rules do not compare clinical meaning, and Feature Store is not a document grounding/evaluation engine.","why_zh":"模式規則未比較臨床語意，Feature Store 也不是文件依據／評估引擎。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Metric anomaly alarms do not establish verified reference answers or paraphrase consistency evaluation.","why_zh":"指標異常警示未建立經驗證參考答案或改寫一致性評估。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-prompt-datasets-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html"],"issues":["guardrails_has_no_output_diff_engine","no_option_fully_satisfies"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.933849+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":120,"question_en":"A company deploys a GenAI application that uses an Amazon Bedrock foundation model (FM) and custom prompts. The company must implement an automated quality assurance system to verify FM outputs against expected responses and detect regressions over time. The solution must compare outputs against more than 500 golden examples by using semantic similarity scoring. The solution must support regularly scheduled test rules. The solution must be able to scale to more than 2,000 test cases within 6 months without the need to make architecture changes. The company wants to generate visualizations for quality metrics. The company must receive alerts if the solution detects quality degradation. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to track data drift in the FM. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms for drift metrics. Use SageMaker AI processing jobs to run scheduled evalu-ations of FM outputs.","B":"Create AWS Lambda functions that invoke the FM on test cases. Compare results against ex-pected outputs. Configure Amazon EventBridge scheduled rules to run the test executions. Pub-lish custom metrics to Amazon CloudWatch to generate metric visualizations and alarms.","C":"Use AWS Step Functions workflows to run test cases and validate responses. Store the test results in Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon CloudWatch dashboards to visualize the results.","D":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics canaries to invoke the FM APIs. Compare re-sponses with baseline scripts. Create CloudWatch alarms based on canary success rates."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":120,"pages":[211]},"question_zh":"一家公司部署使用 Bedrock FM 與自訂提示的 GenAI 應用程式，需建立自動品質保證，將輸出與預期答案比較並偵測長期退化。方案必須以語意相似度計分比對超過 500 個黃金範例，支援定期測試規則，並在六個月內擴展至超過 2,000 個案例而不需改架構。公司也要品質指標視覺化，以及偵測退化時的警示。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"用 SageMaker Model Monitor 追蹤 FM 資料漂移，為漂移指標設定 CloudWatch 警示，並以 SageMaker AI Processing 工作定期評估輸出。","B":"建立 Lambda 對測試案例呼叫 FM 並比較預期輸出，以 EventBridge 排程規則啟動測試，將自訂指標發布至 CloudWatch 以產生視覺化與警示。","C":"用 Step Functions 執行測試及驗證回覆，將結果存入 DynamoDB，以 CloudWatch 儀表板顯示結果。","D":"設定 CloudWatch Synthetics canary 呼叫 FM API，透過基準腳本比對回覆，依 canary 成功率建立警示。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B includes all required scheduling, custom semantic scoring, metrics and alarm components. Implement similarity scoring explicitly, such as embeddings with cosine similarity or an evaluated semantic judge, rather than literal string comparison. Fan out bounded batches across Lambda invocations with concurrency and retry controls so thousands of cases do not depend on one function duration limit. Persist per-case outputs and version identifiers as well as aggregate CloudWatch metrics to make regressions diagnosable.","explanation_zh":"B 包含排程、自訂語意評分、指標及警示等必要元件。必須明確實作相似度計分，例如嵌入加餘弦相似度或經驗證的語意裁判，不能只比對字串。應跨多個 Lambda 分散有界批次並控制並行與重試，讓數千案例不受單次函數時間上限限制。除 CloudWatch 彙總指標外，也應保存逐案輸出及版本識別碼，才能診斷退化。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Data drift monitoring is not a golden-answer semantic regression suite.","why_zh":"資料漂移監控不是黃金答案語意回歸測試。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This could be extended, but as written omits scheduled triggers and degradation alarms.","why_zh":"此方案可以擴充，但原文缺少排程觸發及品質退化警示。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Canary success rates do not by themselves supply scalable semantic scoring across thousands of examples.","why_zh":"Canary 成功率本身未提供數千範例可擴展的語意評分。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-run-lambda-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/titan-embedding-models.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.934803+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":121,"question_en":"A financial services company needs to build a zero-touch promotion workflow for a multilingual AI assistant that automatically moves prompt updates from a development environment to a pro-duction environment. The workflow must promote prompt updates only if the updates meet sev-eral criteria. The updates must improve accuracy in all five languages that the AI assistant supports. The up-dates must show lower variance across similar queries than older prompt versions. The updates must pass all regulatory compliance checks for content related to investment risks and fee disclo-sures. The workflow must run inside the company’s existing CI/CD pipeline, support prompt version comparisons, generate auditable evaluation reports, and remain cost-effective over time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon SageMaker Canvas to visually compare prompt outputs. Create a dashboard to display metrics. Export findings to a document collaboration system to review for regulatory compliance. Schedule weekly meetings between prompt engineers and compliance officers to discuss improvements.","B":"Implement prompt version control by using Amazon S3 object versions. Configure AWS Lambda functions to manually score responses. Store evaluation metrics in an Amazon Dyna-moDB table. Build a custom Amazon Quick Sight dashboard to visualize accuracy across lan-guages and product types.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management to implement prompt version control and to per-form A/B testing for prompts. Use Amazon Bedrock Evaluations and LLM-based judges to per-form automated evaluations for accuracy and consistency metrics. Create a flow in Amazon Bed-rock to streamline testing across languages. Integrate the flow with the existing CI/CD pipeline.","D":"Build a custom evaluation framework that uses AWS Amplify as the frontend and AWS Lambda functions as the backend. Implement crowd-sourcing features in which team members vote on response quality. Use Amazon Comprehend to analyze sentiments in responses and to evaluate for consistency across languages."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":121,"pages":[212]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司需要為多語 AI 助理建立無人介入的提示升版流程，自動將開發環境的提示更新推至正式環境。只有在下列條件皆滿足時才能升版：五種支援語言的準確度皆提升、相似查詢間的差異比舊版小，以及投資風險與費用揭露內容通過所有法遵檢查。流程需整合既有 CI/CD，支援提示版本比較、可稽核評估報告，並長期維持成本效益。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"用 SageMaker Canvas 視覺比較提示輸出，建立指標儀表板，匯出結果至文件協作系統進行法遵審查，每週安排提示工程師與法遵人員會議。","B":"用 S3 物件版本管理提示，以 Lambda 手動評分回覆，將指標存入 DynamoDB，建立 QuickSight 儀表板比較各語言與產品準確度。","C":"用 Bedrock Prompt Management 管理提示版本及 A/B 測試，使用 Bedrock Evaluations 與 LLM 裁判自動評估準確度與一致性。建立 Bedrock 流程簡化跨語言測試，並整合既有 CI/CD。","D":"以 Amplify 前端與 Lambda 後端自建評估框架，讓團隊透過群眾投票評回覆品質，再用 Comprehend 情緒分析評估跨語言一致性。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C is the appropriate managed foundation for versioned prompts, automated evaluation and reusable test orchestration. Each language needs a fixed reference dataset, repeated paraphrase tests and explicit acceptance thresholds; the CI/CD gate must require every criterion to pass. Prompt variants support comparison but do not automatically implement production traffic A/B splitting. Regulatory checks require approved deterministic tests and validated scoring rubrics, because an LLM judge cannot itself guarantee complete regulatory compliance.","explanation_zh":"C 是建立提示版本、自動評估及可重用測試流程的合適託管基礎。每種語言都需固定參考資料集、重複改寫測試及明確門檻，CI/CD 必須要求所有條件通過才升版。提示變體支援比較，但不會自動實作正式流量 A/B 分流。法遵檢查需要核准的確定性測試及經驗證評分準則，LLM 裁判本身不能保證完整法遵。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Weekly manual review is not zero-touch CI/CD promotion.","why_zh":"每週人工審查不屬於無人介入 CI/CD 升版。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manual scores and custom dashboards do not implement automatic multidimensional release gates.","why_zh":"人工評分與自訂儀表板未實作自動多條件發版門檻。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Crowd votes and sentiment do not validate accuracy, consistency and mandatory disclosures in every language.","why_zh":"群眾投票及情緒分數無法驗證各語言的準確性、一致性及必要揭露。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation-judge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/flows.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-custom-metrics-prompt-formats.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html"],"issues":["explicit_multilingual_compliance_gate_required","prompt_variants_not_production_ab_router"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.935655+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":122,"question_en":"A financial company is building an AI-powered recommendation system. The system uses real-time market data and verified internal documents. The system must include evaluation capabili-ties that collect explicit user ratings and detect problematic responses in real time. The system must include evaluation capabilities that track model performance over time and support A/B testing of different prompt or model variants. The system must orchestrate multi-step workflows. The workflows must retrieve trusted knowledge, validate inputs, and generate recommendations. The system must securely store all user feedback, flagged events, and audit logs in a compliance-ready immutable repository. The repository must be write- once, tamper-evident storage that is suitable for regulated audit reten-tion. Which architecture will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a fine-tuned FM on Amazon SageMaker JumpStart. Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to orchestrate input validation and retrieval workflows. Store user feedback and flagged queries in Amazon DynamoDB. Run scheduled Amazon Athena queries on AWS CloudTrail logs for anomaly detection. Store generated outputs in encrypted Amazon S3 buckets. Enable S3 Object Lock.","B":"Configure Amazon API Gateway to invoke an Amazon Bedrock FM that retrieves from Am-azon Kendra. Store all responses in encrypted Amazon S3 buckets. Enable S3 Object Lock. Use Amazon Macie to scan stored logs for problematic content.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to orchestrate retrieval from curated Amazon Kendra in-dexes. Configure an AWS Lambda function to sanitize input. Configure a function to check post-generation fact consistency. Configure a function to split traffic for A/B testing. Store user feedback in Amazon DynamoDB. Write audit logs through AWS CloudTrail. Store the logs in Amazon S3. Enable S3 Object Lock. Use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to track data drift and output anomalies continuously.","D":"Build an Amazon Lex chat-based AI assistant with aliases that route a percentage of queries to two Amazon SageMaker AI endpoints for recommendations. Log interactions to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Conduct quarterly manual audits for hallucination and prompt-injection de-tection. Store feedback in Amazon RDS with encryption."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":122,"pages":[213]},"question_zh":"一家金融公司正在建立 AI 推薦系統，使用即時市場資料及已驗證內部文件。系統必須收集使用者明確評分、即時偵測問題回覆、追蹤長期模型表現，並支援提示或模型變體 A/B 測試。系統需協調檢索可信知識、驗證輸入及產生推薦等多步驟流程，且所有使用者回饋、標記事件及稽核日誌都須安全存入符合規範的不可變更儲存庫，具備一次寫入、防竄改跡證及監管稽核保留能力。哪個架構符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"在 SageMaker JumpStart 部署微調 FM，以 AgentCore 協調輸入驗證及檢索。使用者回饋與標記查詢存入 DynamoDB，定期用 Athena 查詢 CloudTrail 日誌找異常。將生成輸出存入加密 S3，並啟用 Object Lock。","B":"設定 API Gateway 呼叫從 Kendra 檢索的 Bedrock FM，將所有回覆存入加密 S3 並啟用 Object Lock，使用 Macie 掃描日誌中的問題內容。","C":"用 AgentCore 協調對整理後 Kendra 索引的檢索，設定 Lambda 清理輸入、檢查生成後事實一致性，並進行 A/B 流量分配。使用者回饋存入 DynamoDB，透過 CloudTrail 寫稽核日誌，日誌存入啟用 Object Lock 的 S3，並用 SageMaker Model Monitor 持續追蹤資料漂移及輸出異常。","D":"建立 Lex 聊天助理，用別名按比例把查詢路由至兩個 SageMaker AI 推薦端點。將互動記錄至 CloudWatch Logs，每季人工稽核幻覺與提示注入，回饋存入加密 RDS。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C is the closest intended architecture because it includes input/output checks, A/B routing and S3 Object Lock. It is incomplete: feedback stored only in DynamoDB is mutable, so feedback and flagged-event payloads must also be archived to locked S3 with the required retention. CloudTrail records supported API activity, not arbitrary application feedback or complete model outputs. Model Monitor targets SageMaker model data and quality, not automatically AgentCore response factuality; current documentation also states it is unavailable to new customers. No listed option fully satisfies the immutable-all-records and real-time quality requirements without these changes.","explanation_zh":"C 是命題意圖中最接近的架構，包含輸入／輸出檢查、A/B 分流及 S3 Object Lock，但仍不完整。只存於 DynamoDB 的回饋可被修改，因此回饋及標記事件內容也必須封存至設定所需保留期的鎖定 S3。CloudTrail 記錄受支援 API 活動，不會自動記錄任意應用程式回饋或完整模型輸出。Model Monitor 針對 SageMaker 模型資料與品質，不會自動監控 AgentCore 回覆事實性；目前文件還說明已不開放新客戶。若不補上這些設計，沒有列出的選項完整滿足所有紀錄不可變更及即時品質需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Scheduled log queries are not real-time output checks, and mutable feedback is not covered by locked output storage.","why_zh":"定期日誌查詢不是即時輸出檢查，鎖定生成輸出也未涵蓋可變更的回饋。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Macie detects sensitive data at rest rather than general factual errors, and A/B testing and feedback tracking are absent.","why_zh":"Macie 偵測靜態敏感資料而非一般事實錯誤，且缺少 A/B 測試及回饋追蹤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Quarterly audits are not real-time detection; encrypted RDS is not WORM retention.","why_zh":"每季稽核不是即時偵測；加密 RDS 也不是 WORM 保留。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/observability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-availability-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html"],"issues":["feedback_not_in_immutable_repository","model_monitor_not_general_genai_checker","model_monitor_closed_to_new_customers","no_option_fully_satisfies"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.937090+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":123,"question_en":"A retail company has a product recommendation system that uses a foundation model (FM) in Amazon Bedrock. The system processes and searches millions of product embeddings that are updated hourly. The company regularly adds new products. During peak shopping events, the current solution experiences high latency and occasional fail-ures when the system performs similarity searches across the product catalog. The company must resolve the performance issues. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Implement Amazon OpenSearch Service with a multi-node architecture. Configure vector-specific index settings and memory circuit breakers. Establish dedicated vector operation queues to handle surge capacity during peak usage events.","B":"Deploy an Amazon DynamoDB table that uses sparse vector compression. Implement parallel query executors to handle search operations. Configure DynamoDB Streams and AWS Lambda functions to maintain the vector index in real time.","C":"Set up an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that uses custom vector partitioning. Implement hierarchical metadata structures. Integrate the knowledge base with Amazon EventBridge to provide synchronized catalog updates and to generate vectors.","D":"Deploy an Amazon Neptune cluster with specialized vector endpoints. Configure custom similarity computation functions. Use the Neptune bulk loader API to manage vector updates across the product catalog."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":123,"pages":[214]},"question_zh":"一家零售公司的推薦系統使用 Bedrock FM，處理並搜尋數百萬筆每小時更新的商品嵌入，公司也持續新增商品。購物尖峰時，商品目錄的相似度搜尋延遲很高且偶爾失敗。哪個方案可解決效能問題？","options_zh":{"A":"部署多節點 OpenSearch Service，設定向量專用索引及記憶體斷路器，建立專屬向量作業佇列處理尖峰容量。","B":"部署使用稀疏向量壓縮的 DynamoDB 資料表，實作平行查詢執行器，並以 DynamoDB Streams 與 Lambda 即時維護向量索引。","C":"建立使用自訂向量分割的 Bedrock 知識庫，實作階層中繼資料，整合 EventBridge 同步目錄更新及產生向量。","D":"部署具有專用向量端點的 Neptune 叢集，設定自訂相似度函數，用 Neptune bulk loader API 管理整個目錄的向量更新。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A selects the appropriate scalable vector-search engine with index and memory tuning. OpenSearch k-NN supports vector indexes, and the KNNGraphMemoryUsage metric and circuit-breaker limits help identify memory pressure. Circuit breakers prevent exhaustion by rejecting work; they do not add capacity or guarantee lower latency. Dedicated vector-operation queues are not a general managed-service feature to assume: verify supported thread-pool controls and use application buffering/backpressure with shard, replica and node sizing.","explanation_zh":"A 選擇適合擴展的向量搜尋引擎，並納入索引及記憶體調校。OpenSearch k-NN 支援向量索引，可透過 KNNGraphMemoryUsage 及斷路器限制辨識記憶體壓力。斷路器藉拒絕工作避免耗盡資源，不會增加容量或保證降低延遲。「專屬向量作業佇列」不能直接當成通用託管功能；應核對受支援的執行緒池控制，搭配應用程式緩衝／背壓，以及分片、副本與節點容量規劃。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"DynamoDB does not natively provide the asserted sparse-vector similarity index and executor.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 未原生提供選項宣稱的稀疏向量相似度索引與執行器。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Knowledge-base orchestration does not expose the asserted custom partitioning or make EventBridge an embedding generator.","why_zh":"知識庫協調不提供所述自訂分割，也不會讓 EventBridge 變成嵌入產生器。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The proposed Neptune bulk-loader/custom-function architecture is not the direct scalable vector-search remedy described here.","why_zh":"所述 Neptune bulk loader／自訂函數架構不是此情境直接的可擴展向量搜尋解方。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/knn.html"],"issues":["dedicated_vector_queue_not_established","circuit_breaker_not_capacity"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.937809+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":124,"question_en":"A healthcare company is developing an application that processes sensitive patient data and gen-erates treatment summaries by using a foundation model (FM). The application must maintain an audit trail of all prompts and completions. The application must securely handle protected health information (PHI) data throughout the processing lifecycle. The company must track all prompt-completion pairs with original patient data, but the company must redact any PHI from stored records. The company must enforce healthcare-specific data retention policies. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Store prompt-completion pairs in Amazon S3 and enable default server-side encryption. De-ploy an AWS Lambda function that scans records by using Amazon Comprehend Medical. Con-figure the Lambda function to delete PHI data after a required retention period.","B":"Use Amazon Bedrock Prompt Management and Amazon Bedrock Flows to detect PHI. Con-figure Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to use sensitive information filters to mask PHI automatical-ly. Store logs in Amazon S3 and configure appropriate retention settings.","C":"Store prompt-completion pairs in Amazon S3. Configure S3 Object Lock in compliance mode. Apply tag- based S3 Lifecycle policies to PHI data. Configure an AWS Lambda function to re-dact patient information after the application processes the data.","D":"Store patient data in an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Use Amazon Comprehend Medi-cal to identify PHI. Configure an AWS Lambda function to manage data retention according to healthcare policies."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":124,"pages":[215]},"question_zh":"一家醫療公司正在開發以 FM 處理敏感病患資料及產生治療摘要的應用程式。系統必須稽核所有提示與完成內容，在整個處理生命週期安全處理 PHI。公司必須追蹤全部提示－完成配對及其原始病患資料，但儲存紀錄必須去除任何 PHI，並強制執行醫療資料保留政策。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"把提示－完成配對存入 S3 並啟用預設伺服器端加密，部署 Lambda 用 Comprehend Medical 掃描紀錄，並設定在所需保留期後刪除 PHI。","B":"用 Bedrock Prompt Management 與 Flows 偵測 PHI，設定 Guardrails 敏感資訊篩選自動遮罩 PHI，將日誌存入 S3 並設定適當保存規則。","C":"把提示－完成配對存入 S3，設定 Object Lock 合規模式及依標籤的 S3 生命週期政策，再用 Lambda 在應用程式處理後去除病患資訊。","D":"把病患資料存入 Bedrock 知識庫，以 Comprehend Medical 辨識 PHI，設定 Lambda 依醫療政策管理保留。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B is only the closest intended pre-storage masking pattern; no option is complete as written. Prompt Management and Flows do not themselves detect PHI, although a flow can orchestrate an actual detection/redaction service. Guardrails detects selected PII categories and custom regex probabilistically, not every healthcare PHI identifier, and raw invocation logs must not be assumed automatically redacted. A sound design redacts both prompt and completion before audit persistence, correlates them to originals through an access-controlled non-PHI identifier, validates clinical PHI detection and enforces explicit retention. Storing an unchanged original and removing all its PHI from that same stored record are contradictory requirements without such separation.","explanation_zh":"B 只是命題意圖中最接近儲存前遮罩的方向，沒有選項按字面完整正確。Prompt Management 與 Flows 本身不偵測 PHI，但流程可協調真正的偵測／去識別化服務。Guardrails 以機率方式偵測選定 PII 類別及自訂正規表示式，不代表涵蓋所有醫療 PHI，也不能假定原始模型呼叫日誌已自動去識別化。合理設計須在寫稽核紀錄前處理提示與回覆，以受控非 PHI 識別碼關聯原始資料，驗證臨床 PHI 偵測並明確設定保留。若不作這種區隔，同一儲存紀錄既保留完整原文又去除所有 PHI 本身矛盾。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It persists raw PHI first and only deletes later; encryption is not redaction.","why_zh":"它先存原始 PHI，之後才刪除；加密不是去識別化。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Locking a raw version in compliance mode prevents replacing or deleting that PHI-bearing version during retention.","why_zh":"把原始版本鎖成合規模式後，在保留期間不能覆寫或刪掉含 PHI 的原版本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"PHI detection is relevant, but the option omits redacted prompt-completion audit capture.","why_zh":"PHI 偵測相關，但選項未提供已去識別化的提示－完成稽核紀錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/textanalysis-phi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_GuardrailPiiEntityConfig.html"],"issues":["prompt_management_flows_not_phi_detector","pii_not_all_phi","redact_before_storage","no_option_fully_satisfies"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.938787+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":125,"question_en":"A financial services company runs an AI application that uses Amazon Bedrock foundation models (FMs) to generate personalized investment recommendations based on customer docu-ments. The AI application processes customer portfolios, financial statements, and regulatory documentation to create personalized recommendations. The company is experiencing inconsistent model performance because of poor data quality. Some documents contain personally identifiable information (PII) that the company must redact. Other documents contain formatting inconsistencies that confuse the FMs. The company needs a solu-tion that ensures consistent, high- quality inputs to optimize FM. The solution must comply with financial regulations and PII handling policies. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Macie to automatically detect and redact PII. Use AWS Lambda functions and Amazon Textract to enforce standard document formatting. Create dynamic prompts that adapt to individual document schemas to improve model consistency.","B":"Use Amazon Comprehend to detect PII by using custom entity recognition. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate document preprocessing workflows. Use prompt templates with condi-tional logic to handle schema variations effectively.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter out PII during inference. Use pre-processing AWS Lambda functions to standardized document formatting. Use few-shot prompting techniques and standardized examples to improve model performance across document types.","D":"Use Amazon Textract to analyze document structures and extract text. Use Amazon Compre-hend to detect PII and analyze sentiment. Design prompt engineering strategies that use struc-tured metadata to improve FM reasoning and reduce hallucinations."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":125,"pages":[216]},"question_zh":"一家金融公司使用 Bedrock FM，依客戶投資組合、財務報表及監管文件產生個人化投資建議。資料品質不佳導致模型表現不一致：部分文件有必須去除的 PII，其他文件格式不一致令 FM 混淆。公司需要一致且高品質的輸入改善模型表現，同時符合金融規範及 PII 政策。哪個方案維運負擔最低？","options_zh":{"A":"用 Macie 自動偵測及去除 PII，以 Lambda 與 Textract 強制文件格式標準化，並建立依個別文件結構調整的動態提示。","B":"用 Comprehend 自訂實體辨識偵測 PII，以 Step Functions 協調文件前處理，使用具條件邏輯的提示範本處理結構差異。","C":"用 Bedrock Guardrails 在推論時篩除 PII，以前處理 Lambda 統一文件格式，再使用少樣本提示與標準範例改善跨文件類型表現。","D":"用 Textract 分析文件結構並擷取文字，以 Comprehend 偵測 PII 及分析情緒，設計利用結構化中繼資料的提示策略改善推理、降低幻覺。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C combines managed inference-time sensitive-information controls, deterministic formatting and examples that demonstrate the desired structure. Configure the sensitive filter to mask the required entities in the input before generation, with output filtering as appropriate. A generic filter setting is not equivalent to a validated financial compliance policy, and source documents and logs need separate PII handling. Few-shot examples can improve consistency but must be evaluated on representative document types.","explanation_zh":"C 結合託管推論時敏感資訊控制、確定性的格式整理，以及示範所需結構的範例。應將敏感資訊篩選設定為在生成前遮罩輸入必要實體，並按需求篩選輸出。一般篩選設定不等於已驗證的金融法遵政策，來源文件與日誌也需另外處理 PII。少樣本範例可改善一致性，但仍須以具代表性的文件類型評估。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Macie discovers sensitive data but does not automatically redact document contents.","why_zh":"Macie 發現敏感資料，但不會自動改寫文件去除 PII。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Built-in PII detection does not require custom entity training; this option adds orchestration and does not explicitly redact detected entities.","why_zh":"內建 PII 偵測不需自訂實體訓練；此方案增加協調，且未明列去除偵測到的實體。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Detection and sentiment do not themselves redact PII or standardize input structure.","why_zh":"偵測與情緒分析本身不會去除 PII 或統一輸入結構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/design-a-prompt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_GuardrailPiiEntityConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-parameters.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.939659+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"},{"id":126,"question_en":"A global company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage 25 AWS accounts. The company’s products have 50,000 daily user interactions. The company is using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to build an AI assistant. The AI assistant must access customer data that is stored in multiple AWS accounts across sever-al business units. The AI assistant needs to perform actions on behalf of specific users by query-ing Amazon DynamoDB tables that contain customer information in each business unit's AWS account. Each business unit maintains its own AWS account that hosts its own DynamoDB ta-bles. The company must enforce strict data access security boundaries and must collect full audit trails that show which user’s credentials are used to perform each action. The solution must allow the AgentCore application to access resources across multiple accounts while preserving user identity context. The solution must support the company’s plan to expand to more than 40 AWS accounts in the next year. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Configure the AI assistant to use an outbound credential provider that runs AssumeRole op-erations to dynamically obtain temporary credentials so the AI assistant can access resources across accounts. Create an IAM role in each business unit account that has a trust relationship to the AI assistant’s execution role and permissions to access the DynamoDB tables. Ensure that AssumeRole calls include session tags to identify the end user.","B":"Create a separate AI assistant in each business unit account. Deploy an Amazon API Gateway REST API that runs request routing logic. Create AWS Lambda authorizers to direct user queries to the appropriate AI assistant based on the customer’s business unit identifier from the request context.","C":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the DynamoDB tables from each business unit account to a central account where the AI assistant runs. Configure AWS RAM permissions to allow cross-account access to the DynamoDB tables. Grant the AgentCore execu-tion role permissions to access the shared resources directly.","D":"Configure SCPs for the organization to explicitly allow the AI assistant’s execution role prin-cipal to perform dynamodb:Getltem and dynamodb:Query actions across all member accounts. Configure the AI assistant to reference cross-account DynamoDB table ARNs directly in their resource definitions."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":126,"pages":[217]},"question_zh":"一家全球公司以 AWS Organizations 管理 25 個 AWS 帳戶，每天有 50,000 次使用者互動，正在用 Bedrock AgentCore 建立 AI 助理。助理需代表特定使用者，跨多個事業單位帳戶查詢各自 DynamoDB 中的客戶資料。公司必須嚴格隔離資料權限，完整稽核每個動作使用哪位使用者的憑證，並在跨帳戶存取時保留使用者身分脈絡。方案還需支援明年擴展至超過 40 個帳戶。哪個方案維運負擔最低？","options_zh":{"A":"設定助理使用會執行 AssumeRole 的輸出憑證提供者，動態取得跨帳戶暫時憑證。在各事業帳戶建立信任助理執行角色且可存取 DynamoDB 的 IAM 角色，確保 AssumeRole 帶有辨識最終使用者的工作階段標籤。","B":"在各事業帳戶建立獨立 AI 助理，以 API Gateway REST API 實作路由，並用 Lambda authorizer 依請求脈絡的事業單位識別碼把查詢送至對應助理。","C":"使用 AWS RAM 將各帳戶的 DynamoDB 資料表分享至助理所在中央帳戶，設定 RAM 跨帳戶權限，並直接授權 AgentCore 執行角色存取分享資源。","D":"設定組織 SCP 明確允許助理執行角色跨成員帳戶執行 dynamodb:GetItem 及 dynamodb:Query，並讓助理直接參照跨帳戶資料表 ARN。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A uses the correct core cross-account pattern: STS temporary role sessions, target-account trust and least-privilege DynamoDB permissions. Session tags can carry verified user attributes for ABAC and audit correlation; trust policies must permit TagSession and constrain which tags may be asserted. Do not treat an execution-role AssumeRole session as the end user’s own credentials, and use source identity plus correlated CloudTrail records where needed. AgentCore credential-provider terminology does not by itself establish a native STS provider, so the application or supported gateway credential path must implement the AssumeRole operation explicitly.","explanation_zh":"A 採用正確的跨帳戶核心模式：STS 暫時角色工作階段、目的帳戶信任及 DynamoDB 最小權限。工作階段標籤可承載已驗證使用者屬性以供 ABAC 及稽核關聯；信任政策須允許 TagSession 並限制可宣告標籤。不能把執行角色 AssumeRole 工作階段當成使用者本人的憑證，必要時應搭配 source identity 及關聯 CloudTrail 紀錄。AgentCore 憑證提供者這個名稱本身不代表存在原生 STS 提供者，須由應用程式或受支援閘道憑證路徑明確實作 AssumeRole。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Per-account assistants duplicate deployment and do not inherently preserve delegated identity at the database.","why_zh":"每帳戶各建助理增加部署維護，也不自然保留資料庫層的委派身分。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The proposed RAM table-sharing mechanism is not the standard DynamoDB cross-account access model; use IAM/resource policies or roles.","why_zh":"所述 RAM 資料表分享不是標準 DynamoDB 跨帳戶存取模式，應使用 IAM／資源政策或角色。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs limit maximum permissions and never grant cross-account access on their own.","why_zh":"SCP 限制最大權限，本身不會授予跨帳戶存取權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_session-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/identity-outbound-credential-provider.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/resource-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html"],"issues":["native_sts_provider_not_established","session_tags_not_user_credentials"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.941098+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":127,"question_en":"A hospital is building an AI application to help medical clinicians to make treatment decisions. The application uses Amazon Bedrock to analyze patient case histories and suggest diagnoses. The application must maintain sub-500 ms response times to integrate with the hospital’s existing real-time clinical workflow. To comply with privacy regulations, the application must log all per-sonally identifiable information (PII) handling decisions for audits. The application must detect and remove PII from responses with at least 99% accuracy. After initial deployment, clinicians report that diagnostic summaries from the application occa-sionally include patient names and medical record numbers that were not present in the original case history inputs. An investigation reveals that Amazon Comprehend Medical successfully de-tects and removes PII from inputs with 95% accuracy, and the application replaces all detected entities with tokens before it sends inputs to Amazon Bedrock. However, the application contin-ues to generate patient-identifying information in approximately 3-5% of outputs. The company needs a solution to prevent the application from displaying PII in outputs while meeting all other operational requirements. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails with sensitive information filters to detect and block PII in model outputs.","B":"Implement a secondary PII detection layer by using regular expressions and custom entity recognition to detect identifiers that Amazon Comprehend Medical misses before sending inputs to Amazon Bedrock.","C":"Remove detailed medical context from case histories during pre-processing to prevent the model from generating patient-specific information based on clinical pattern associations.","D":"Enable session isolation in Amazon Bedrock API calls. Clear conversation history between requests to prevent patient information from persisting across multiple case analyses."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{"A":100},"tags":["GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":127,"pages":[218,219]},"question_zh":"一家醫院以 Bedrock 建立 AI 應用程式，分析病歷並提出診斷，協助臨床人員決策。系統需在 500 毫秒內回覆以融入即時臨床流程，記錄所有 PII 處理決策供稽核，並以至少 99% 準確度偵測及移除回覆中的 PII。上線後，摘要偶爾出現原始輸入未包含的姓名及病歷號。調查顯示 Comprehend Medical 以 95% 準確度偵測並移除輸入 PII，送至 Bedrock 前所有偵測實體也都已換成 token，但約 3–5% 輸出仍生成病患識別資訊。公司需阻止顯示輸出 PII，並滿足其他營運需求。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 Bedrock Guardrails 敏感資訊篩選器，偵測並阻擋模型輸出的 PII。","B":"增加正規表示式及自訂實體辨識的第二層 PII 偵測，在送至 Bedrock 前補抓 Comprehend Medical 漏掉的識別資訊。","C":"前處理時移除詳細醫療脈絡，避免模型依臨床樣式關聯生成病患專屬資訊。","D":"啟用 Bedrock API 工作階段隔離，每次請求清除對話歷史，避免病患資訊在不同病例分析間保留。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A addresses the actual failure point by checking generated output, including identifiers that were absent from the input. Configure relevant PII types and custom patterns for medical-record identifiers and block or mask before display. AWS describes this filter as probabilistic and provides no blanket 99% detection or sub-500-ms end-to-end guarantee. Therefore A is the best mitigation, while validated clinical test data, measured latency and explicit decision audit logging are still required to establish the numerical and audit requirements.","explanation_zh":"A 在實際失敗點檢查生成輸出，可處理輸入原本不存在的識別資訊。應設定適用 PII 類型及病歷號自訂樣式，在顯示前阻擋或遮罩。AWS 將此篩選描述為機率性機制，沒有通用 99% 偵測或端到端低於 500 毫秒的保證。因此 A 是最佳改善措施，但要證明數值及稽核需求，仍需經驗證的臨床測試資料、實測延遲與明確決策日誌。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Additional input checks cannot catch identifiers newly generated in output.","why_zh":"再加輸入檢查仍抓不到輸出新生成的識別資訊。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Removing clinical detail damages diagnostic utility and does not reliably prevent invented identifiers.","why_zh":"移除臨床細節損害診斷用途，也不能可靠阻止捏造識別資訊。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Session isolation is not an output PII detector and the evidence does not establish cross-session leakage.","why_zh":"工作階段隔離不是輸出 PII 偵測器，題目也未證明跨工作階段洩漏。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend-medical/latest/dev/textanalysis-phi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_GuardrailPiiEntityConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html"],"issues":["99_percent_accuracy_not_guaranteed","latency_and_audit_not_automatic"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.941725+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":128,"question_en":"A company is designing a GenAI solution to help children between the ages of 8 and 14 understand world history. The system must support concurrent use for up to 30 children in a classroom and provide responses in less than 1 second. The company is using Amazon Bedrock and Amazon Nova Pro with a knowledge base that contains history textbooks that are written for students between the ages of 6 and 21. The company uses an Amazon Bedrock flow to ensure that the solution uses the knowledge base to generate every response. The company sets the prompt response temperature to 0.7. Early testing of the solution results in some responses that are historically inaccurate, violent, and not appropriate for children. A GenAI developer must prevent the solution from responding to prompts inaccurately and inappropriately. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Increase the inference temperature in the flow. Add a node to the flow after the initial response that calls the Amazon Nova model to remove any violence from the response. Return the result of the model call.","B":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails for the model responses by using content filters. Set the content filter strength high and set the guardrail action to block. Add the guardrail to the flow. Reduce the inference temperature in the flow.","C":"Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation with a custom output that removes all violent content from the knowledge base. Increase the inference temperature in the flow.","D":"Configure Amazon Bedrock guardrails for the prompts by using content filters. Set the content filter strength to high and set the guardrail action to block. Add the guardrail to the flow. Reduce the inference temperature in the flow."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":128,"pages":[219]},"question_zh":"一家公司設計 GenAI 系統，協助 8–14 歲兒童理解世界歷史。每間教室須支援最多 30 名兒童同時使用，並在一秒內回覆。公司使用 Bedrock 與 Nova Pro，知識庫包含為 6–21 歲學生撰寫的歷史教科書，透過 Bedrock 流程確保每次回覆都使用知識庫，temperature 設為 0.7。早期測試發現部分回覆歷史事實不正確、含暴力且不適合兒童。開發人員必須防止不準確及不適當回覆。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"提高流程的推論 temperature，在初始回覆後加一個節點，呼叫 Nova 移除回覆中的暴力，再回傳模型結果。","B":"對模型回覆設定 Guardrails 內容篩選，強度設為高、動作設為阻擋，把護欄加至流程，並降低 temperature。","C":"使用 BDA 自訂輸出移除知識庫全部暴力內容，並提高推論 temperature。","D":"對提示設定 Guardrails 內容篩選，強度設為高、動作設為阻擋，把護欄加至流程，並降低 temperature。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B filters the generated content where harmful text is observed, and reducing temperature can reduce sampling variability. Input-only filtering cannot prevent a safe question from producing an unsafe response. Content filters detect harmful categories, not historical truth; lower temperature likewise does not guarantee factual accuracy. Age-appropriate source filtering, grounding checks and evaluation are needed, and the added guardrail latency must be measured against the one-second target at classroom concurrency.","explanation_zh":"B 在已觀察到有害文字的生成輸出端篩選，降低 temperature 也可減少抽樣變異。只篩輸入無法防止安全問題產生不安全回覆。內容篩選偵測有害類別，不查核歷史真相；低 temperature 同樣不保證事實正確。仍需適齡來源篩選、依據檢查及評估，並在教室並行情境實測加入護欄後能否達到一秒目標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Higher temperature increases variability and a second unconstrained generation call adds latency without guaranteed safety.","why_zh":"提高 temperature 增加變異，第二次未受控制的生成增加延遲，也不保證安全。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Data extraction is not a complete age-safety or historical-factuality filter, and higher temperature is counterproductive.","why_zh":"資料擷取不是完整適齡或歷史正確性篩選，提高 temperature 也不利一致性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Input-only filtering leaves harmful generated responses unchecked.","why_zh":"只檢查提示會漏掉模型生成的不當回覆。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-content-filters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-contextual-grounding-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-metrics.html"],"issues":["content_safety_not_factuality","latency_not_guaranteed"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.942353+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":129,"question_en":"A legal research company is developing an AI-powered chat assistant that uses Amazon Bedrock with a knowledge base that contains millions of legal documents. When attorneys search for legal case precedents, the initial retrieval returns many documents. The company wants the chat assistant to generate all responses within 3 seconds. The foundation model (FM) that the chat assistant uses has a context window limitation that allows effective processing for only 10 documents for each query. Currently, the retrieval configuration fetches 50 documents by using semantic search. Attorneys report that highly relevant precedents frequently appear in positions 15-40 of the results. The company needs a solution to improve the relevance of query results. The solution must meet the company's latency and context window constraints. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Maintain the 50-document retrieval but increase the FM's temperature parameter. Implement prompt engineering techniques that instruct the model to identify the most relevant documents from the full result set before the model generates responses.","B":"Enable reranking on the knowledge base by using a reranker model with language-specific configurations. Configure the chat assistant to initially retrieve 50 documents. Use the reranker model's cross-encoder architecture to evaluate query-document pairs. Return only the top 10 highest-scored documents.","C":"Configure three separate knowledge bases. Configure one knowledge base to use 500 token chunks, another to use 1,000 token chunks, and the third to use 2,000 token chunks. Implement a pre-processing action group by using an AWS Lambda function that retrieves 50 documents from each knowledge base, merges the 150 total results, and uses term frequency - inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) scoring to select the top 10 documents.","D":"Implement a post-processing action group by using an AWS Lambda function that retrieves 50 documents and calculates cosine similarity scores between the query embedding and each document embedding by using Amazon Titan Embeddings. Configure the action group to sort by similarity score and return the top 10 documents."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Prompting","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":129,"pages":[220]},"question_zh":"一家法律研究公司使用 Bedrock 與含數百萬份法律文件的知識庫，開發 AI 聊天助理。律師查判例時初步檢索會回傳許多文件；公司希望所有回覆在三秒內產生，但 FM 的脈絡視窗每次只能有效處理 10 份文件。目前語意搜尋取回 50 份，高度相關判例卻常落在第 15–40 名。公司需提高結果相關性，同時符合延遲與脈絡限制。哪個方案符合需求？","options_zh":{"A":"維持取回 50 份文件，提高 FM temperature，透過提示要求模型先從完整結果找最相關文件再回覆。","B":"在知識庫啟用具有語言特定設定的重新排名模型，先取回 50 份，再用交叉編碼器評估查詢－文件配對，只回傳前 10 個最高分文件。","C":"建立三個知識庫，分別使用 500、1,000、2,000 token 分塊；透過 Lambda 前處理動作群組各取回 50 份，共 150 份合併後以 TF-IDF 選前 10 份。","D":"實作 Lambda 後處理動作群組，取回 50 份後用 Titan Embeddings 計算查詢與各文件的餘弦相似度，再排序回傳前 10 份。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B retains a broad recall set and applies a relevance reranker before the generation context is constructed. Query-document reranking can promote relevant candidates that the initial embedding search ranked lower, while limiting the final context to ten results. Configure a supported reranker and its actual API parameters; language support is model-specific rather than a universal language configuration switch. Reranking adds computation, so the three-second end-to-end target requires measurement and capacity planning.","explanation_zh":"B 先保留較廣候選集合，再於建立生成脈絡前用相關性模型重新排名。查詢－文件配對評分可提升初步嵌入搜尋排名較低的相關結果，同時把最終脈絡限制為十份。應選受支援模型及真實 API 參數；語言支援依模型而異，並非通用語言設定開關。重新排名會增加運算，因此三秒端到端目標仍需實測及容量規劃。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"All 50 documents exceed the stated effective context, and temperature does not improve retrieval ranking.","why_zh":"50 份文件超出有效脈絡限制，temperature 也不改善檢索排名。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Three retrieval paths and custom TF-IDF add complexity and latency without the semantic reranker advantage.","why_zh":"三條檢索路徑及自訂 TF-IDF 增加複雜度與延遲，卻沒有語意重新排名優勢。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Repeating embedding cosine ranking largely repeats the initial retrieval signal instead of adding query-document interaction scoring.","why_zh":"再次用嵌入餘弦排名大致重複初步搜尋訊號，未加入查詢－文件交互評分。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent-runtime_VectorSearchBedrockRerankingConfiguration.html"],"issues":["rerank_latency_requires_measurement","model_specific_language_support"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.943093+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":130,"question_en":"A multinational healthcare company is building a GenAI solution to analyze patient medical records and clinical trial data to identify treatment patterns and generate research insights. Some of the countries where the company operates require the company to store patient data on premises within each country. The solution must provide low-latency, AI-assisted diagnostics for remote clinics around the world. The solution must use cloud-based foundation models (FMs) to perform advanced, large-scale analytics. The company needs a solution that ensures data residency, delivers sub-100 ms inference at clinics, and supports consistent development workflows across hybrid environments. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Global Accelerator to reduce latency for remote clinics. Replicate on-premises patient data to Amazon S3 by using AWS DataSync. Process all model requests through a centralized inference endpoint that is hosted in one AWS Region.","B":"Deploy open source FMs on Amazon EC2 instances in each country to comply with data residency requirements. Store patient data locally on Amazon EBS volumes. Use AWS Systems Manager to manage model updates across countries. Manually export aggregated research insights as CSV files to Amazon S3 buckets in each AWS Region to perform cross-country analysis.","C":"Deploy FMs in multiple AWS Regions on Amazon EC2 GPU instances. Replicate patient data from on- premises systems to the cloud. Centralize model training and inference.","D":"Use AWS Outposts to process and store sensitive on-premises patient data in countries that have data residency requirements. Deploy AWS Wavelength at remote clinics to perform real-time inference."},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":130,"pages":[221]},"question_zh":"一家跨國醫療公司正在建立 GenAI 系統，分析病歷及臨床試驗資料以找出治療模式與研究洞見。部分營運國家要求病患資料儲存在國內自有場域。系統必須為世界各地偏遠診所提供低延遲 AI 輔助診斷，也需用雲端 FM 進行進階大規模分析。公司希望確保資料駐留、診所推論低於 100 毫秒，並維持混合環境一致的開發流程。哪個方案維運負擔最低？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 Global Accelerator 降低偏遠診所延遲，以 DataSync 將內部病患資料複寫至 S3，所有模型請求都送至單一區域的集中推論端點。","B":"在各國 EC2 部署開源 FM 以符合資料駐留，資料存於當地 EBS，以 Systems Manager 管理各國模型更新，再人工匯出彙總研究洞見 CSV 至各區域 S3 進行跨國分析。","C":"在多個 AWS 區域的 EC2 GPU 部署 FM，將病患資料從內部系統複寫至雲端，並集中訓練與推論。","D":"在有駐留要求的國家使用 Outposts 處理及儲存敏感內部病患資料，並在偏遠診所部署 Wavelength 進行即時推論。"},"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"D is only the closest intended hybrid direction because Outposts can keep selected processing and storage on premises. Wavelength is deployed in supported telecommunications-provider locations, not as equipment that a customer installs at arbitrary remote clinics. It does not guarantee sub-100-ms FM inference, and sending patient data to a carrier zone may violate an on-premises-only rule even if it remains in the country. The option also omits the governed cloud-analytics data path; a compliant design must define what anonymized or approved data can leave premises. No listed option fully satisfies the literal requirements.","explanation_zh":"D 只是命題意圖中最接近的混合架構方向，因為 Outposts 可讓選定運算及儲存留在自有場域。Wavelength 部署於支援的電信商據點，不是客戶可安裝在任意偏遠診所的設備。它不保證 FM 推論低於 100 毫秒；即使資料仍在國內，送至電信商區域也可能違反「只能留在自有場域」的限制。此選項也未定義受治理的雲端分析資料路徑，合規設計須明確規範哪些匿名化或核准資料可離開場域。沒有選項完整符合字面需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Replicating raw patient data to a centralized Region violates the on-premises requirement.","why_zh":"將原始病患資料複寫至集中區域違反自有場域要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Regional EC2/EBS is not on premises, and availability of a Region in every country is not established.","why_zh":"區域 EC2／EBS 不在自有場域，也不能假定每國都有 AWS 區域。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cloud replication and centralized inference conflict with local storage and do not establish clinic latency.","why_zh":"雲端複寫及集中推論違反本地儲存要求，也未證明診所延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/data-residency-hybrid-cloud-services-lens/drhcrel03-bp01.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wavelength/latest/developerguide/how-wavelengths-work.html"],"issues":["wavelength_not_deployed_at_arbitrary_clinics","sub100ms_not_guaranteed","cloud_analytics_path_missing","no_option_fully_satisfies"],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T10:03:04.944211+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":131,"question_en":"A global company runs an AI-powered document-processing pipeline that uses Amazon Bedrock to summarize text documents. The pipeline occasionally times out during peak traffic periods. The timeouts cause service degradation. The company needs a solution to detect when error rates exceed 10% within any 60-second window. The solution must switch to an alternate process path when the error rate threshold is exceeded. The solution must automatically resume normal Amazon Bedrock processing when the pipeline recovers. The company must ensure that the pipeline processes all documents within 15 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow that implements a circuit breaker pattern by tracking Amazon Bedrock invocation failures in Amazon DynamoDB. Configure the workflow to route processing jobs between normal and alternate processing paths based on the current failure state.","B":"Configure an AWS Step Functions workflow that uses an AWS Lambda function to poll Amazon CloudWatch metrics for Amazon Bedrock. Store error rate metrics in Amazon DynamoDWhen the error rate exceeds 10%, instruct company staff to manually update the workflow to divert traffic to the alternate processing path.","C":"Configure an AWS Step Functions state machine that includes a Task state to implement Retry/Catch logic for Amazon Bedrock calls. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that triggers an Amazon EventBridge rule to direct traffic from the state machine to the alternate processing path when the error rate exceeds 10%.","D":"Deploy multiple identical AWS Step Functions state machines that use multiple Amazon Bedrock models behind an Amazon API Gateway API. Use a custom health check AWS Lambda function to route requests to whichever state machine responds fastest."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":131,"pages":[222]},"question_zh":"一家全球性公司執行以 AI 驅動的文件處理管線，使用 Amazon Bedrock 摘要文字文件。管線在流量尖峰時偶爾會逾時，造成服務品質下降。公司需要偵測任意 60 秒視窗內錯誤率超過 10% 的情況，並在超過門檻時切換至替代處理路徑。管線恢復後，方案必須自動恢復正常的 Amazon Bedrock 處理。公司必須確保所有文件都在 15 分鐘內處理完畢。哪個方案符合這些需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 AWS Step Functions 工作流程，以 Amazon DynamoDB 追蹤 Amazon Bedrock 呼叫失敗，實作斷路器模式。設定工作流程根據目前的失敗狀態，在正常與替代處理路徑之間路由處理工作。","B":"設定 AWS Step Functions 工作流程，使用 AWS Lambda 函數輪詢 Amazon Bedrock 的 Amazon CloudWatch 指標。將錯誤率指標儲存於 Amazon DynamoDB。錯誤率超過 10% 時，指示公司人員手動更新工作流程，將流量導向替代處理路徑。","C":"設定 AWS Step Functions 狀態機，以 Task 狀態為 Amazon Bedrock 呼叫實作 Retry/Catch 邏輯。設定 Amazon CloudWatch 警報，在錯誤率超過 10% 時觸發 Amazon EventBridge 規則，將狀態機的流量導向替代處理路徑。","D":"部署多個相同的 AWS Step Functions 狀態機，在 Amazon API Gateway API 後方使用多個 Amazon Bedrock 模型。使用自訂健康檢查 AWS Lambda 函數，將請求導向回應最快的狀態機。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is the best architectural fit: a shared circuit state supports automatic diversion and controlled recovery, and AWS documents Step Functions with DynamoDB for this pattern. The implementation must count both requests and failures over a rolling 60-second window, then probe recovery before closing the circuit. DynamoDB TTL deletion is asynchronous, so code must compare expiry timestamps rather than wait for the item to disappear. The pattern alone does not guarantee a 15-minute document deadline; bounded retries, durable work tracking, and adequate alternate-path capacity are also required.","explanation_zh":"A 最符合所需架構：共用斷路器狀態可支援自動切換與受控恢復，AWS 也提供 Step Functions 搭配 DynamoDB 的實作模式。實作仍須統計滾動 60 秒視窗內的請求總數及失敗數，並在恢復探測成功後關閉斷路器。DynamoDB TTL 的刪除是非同步作業，因此程式必須比較到期時間，不能等待資料列消失才恢復。這種模式本身不保證文件在 15 分鐘內完成；仍需限制重試、持久追蹤工作，並確保替代路徑容量足夠。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manual workflow changes violate automatic failover and recovery.","why_zh":"人工修改工作流程不符合自動切換及恢復要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Retry/Catch handles individual executions; an alarm and EventBridge rule do not by themselves implement shared rolling-window circuit state or recovery routing.","why_zh":"Retry/Catch 處理個別執行；警報及 EventBridge 規則本身未實作共用滾動視窗斷路器狀態或恢復路由。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fastest-response routing does not implement the specified error-rate threshold or controlled recovery.","why_zh":"依最快回應路由並未實作指定錯誤率門檻及受控恢復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/cloud-design-patterns/circuit-breaker.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/TTL.html"],"issues":["The rolling window, recovery probe, and 15-minute deadline need implementation details not supplied by any option.","The source has a typographic join: DynamoDWhen."],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.868789+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":132,"question_en":"A media company needs to automatically generate searchable metadata for a video library that contains 10,000 hours of content. Each video includes visual scenes, spoken dialogue, background music, and on-screen text. The company needs a solution to extract scene descriptions, speaker transcripts with timestamps, text overlay content, and emotional context from each video. The output must synchronize all metadata types with one another and create a searchable index. Users must be able to search based on any metadata type and jump directly to a specific moment in each video. What solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon SageMaker AI processing job that extracts video frames at regular intervals. Use Amazon Transcribe to process audio and perform speech-to-text conversions. Use an Anthropic Claude model in Amazon Bedrock to process frames individually to produce multimodal scene analyses. Store outputs in separate Amazon S3 buckets that are organized by content type.","B":"Create an Amazon SageMaker AI processing job that extracts video frames at fixed intervals and attaches timestamps. Use Amazon Transcribe with time markers enabled to process audio. Use an Anthropic Claude model in Amazon Bedrock to analyze frame-transcript pairs. Store outputs in a unified JSON structure that preserves temporal relationships.","C":"Create an Amazon SageMaker AI parallel processing job that is orchestrated by a SageMaker AI pipeline. Configure multiple steps in the pipeline to extract video segments, process audio streams by using Amazon Transcribe, analyze video frames by using Amazon Rekognition to detect text in scenes, use Amazon Comprehend to perform sentiment analysis, and store unified metadata in Amazon DynamoDB with time- based partitioning.","D":"Create an Amazon SageMaker AI processing job that configures Anthropic Claude Opus in Amazon Bedrock to produce a comprehensive multimodal analysis for each video. Configure the processing job to extract metadata by using a single inference request and to index results in Amazon OpenSearch Service to provide temporal search capabilities."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":132,"pages":[223]},"question_zh":"一家媒體公司需要為含有 10,000 小時內容的影片庫，自動產生可搜尋的中繼資料。每部影片包含視覺場景、口語對話、背景音樂及螢幕上的文字。公司需要從每部影片擷取場景描述、附有時間戳記的說話者逐字稿、文字疊加內容及情緒脈絡。輸出必須讓各類中繼資料彼此在時間上同步，並建立可搜尋的索引。使用者必須能依任一類中繼資料搜尋，並直接跳至每部影片的特定時刻。哪個方案符合這些需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立 Amazon SageMaker AI 處理工作，以固定間隔擷取影片影格。使用 Amazon Transcribe 處理音訊並轉換為文字。使用 Amazon Bedrock 中的 Anthropic Claude 模型逐張處理影格，產生多模態場景分析。依內容類型整理輸出，分別儲存於不同的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體。","B":"建立 Amazon SageMaker AI 處理工作，以固定間隔擷取影片影格並附上時間戳記。使用啟用時間標記的 Amazon Transcribe 處理音訊。使用 Amazon Bedrock 中的 Anthropic Claude 模型分析影格與逐字稿配對。將輸出儲存為保留時間關係的統一 JSON 結構。","C":"建立由 SageMaker AI 管線協調的 Amazon SageMaker AI 平行處理工作。設定管線的多個步驟來擷取影片片段、使用 Amazon Transcribe 處理音訊串流、使用 Amazon Rekognition 分析影片影格以偵測場景文字、使用 Amazon Comprehend 執行情緒分析，並將統一的中繼資料以依時間分割的方式儲存於 Amazon DynamoDB。","D":"建立 Amazon SageMaker AI 處理工作，設定 Amazon Bedrock 中的 Anthropic Claude Opus，為每部影片產生完整多模態分析。設定處理工作以單一推論請求擷取中繼資料，並將結果索引至 Amazon OpenSearch Service，以提供時間搜尋能力。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B best preserves the common timeline by pairing timestamped frames with the corresponding transcript before multimodal analysis. Transcribe provides word timing and optional speaker labels, while supported Claude models can analyze image-and-text inputs. However, unified JSON is not itself a searchable index: a retrieval/indexing layer and video offset links must still be implemented. Fixed-interval sampling can miss brief on-screen text, and transcripts do not capture every musical or emotional cue. Thus B is the intended foundation, not a fully specified guarantee of every stated requirement.","explanation_zh":"B 在多模態分析前，先將附有時間戳記的影格與對應逐字稿配對，最能保留共用時間軸。Transcribe 提供字詞時間資訊及可選用的說話者標籤，支援影像輸入的 Claude 模型則可分析影像與文字。但是統一 JSON 本身不是可搜尋索引；仍須建置檢索／索引層及指向影片時間位置的連結。固定間隔取樣可能漏掉短暫出現的螢幕文字，而逐字稿也無法涵蓋所有音樂或情緒線索。因此 B 是題目預期的基礎方案，尚不足以保證所有要求都已完整實作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Separate outputs without shared temporal alignment do not support synchronized multimodal retrieval.","why_zh":"分開儲存且未建立共用時間對齊，無法支援同步的多模態檢索。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The service combination can extract useful features, but time-based DynamoDB storage is not arbitrary metadata search and the option lacks joint scene-transcript reasoning.","why_zh":"這些服務可擷取部分特徵，但依時間儲存於 DynamoDB 不等於可依任意中繼資料搜尋，且此選項未整合場景與逐字稿進行推理。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It assumes an unspecified Claude Opus version can analyze an entire video in one request; image/text support and context limits do not establish that capability.","why_zh":"它假設未指定版本的 Claude Opus 可用單一請求分析整部影片；支援影像／文字及其上下文限制並不能證明這項能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/diarization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-parameters-anthropic-claude-messages.html"],"issues":["B omits the actual search index and complete coverage of short-lived visual/audio signals."],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.870465+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":133,"question_en":"A financial services company is developing a GenAI application that needs to analyze data across multiple AWS accounts by using a foundation model (FM). The data and application are in Amazon S3 buckets in three separate accounts. Account A contains transaction data. Account B contains customer profiles, including personally identifiable information (PII). Account C hosts the GenAI application. The company plans to add data sources from seven more business units within the next few months. The company must have strict control over PII data. The company must ensure that the FM accesses only necessary data fields. The company needs a solution to establish secure cross-account access for the GenAI application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Identity Center to create a permission set for the FM service account. Configure resource- based policies on each S3 bucket to allow specific access to Account C. Deploy a custom AWS Lambda authorizer to filter PII data before passing it to the FM.","B":"Configure Amazon Bedrock cross-account IAM roles. Create role-based access policies in each source account that allow access only for specific S3 bucket paths. Apply tagbased access controls on S3 objects to classify and control access to PII data.","C":"Set up AWS Lake Formation in each source account. Register the S3 buckets with Lake Formation. Create IAM roles in each source account that have permissions to access specific S3 bucket paths. Configure Lake Formation permissions to allow access only to specific data columns by using Lake Formation tag-based access controls. Use Amazon SageMaker AI to deploy the FM with an execution role in Account C that can assume the cross-account IAM roles to access the data through Lake Formation.","D":"Configure resource-based policies on S3 buckets in each source account to allow access from the GenAI application in Account C. Configure identity-based policies for the FM's service role that allow access only to specific data columns by using AWS Lake Formation tag-based access controls. Set up a VPC endpoint in each account to provide secure cross-account access."},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Safety","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":133,"pages":[224]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在開發 GenAI 應用程式，必須使用基礎模型（FM）分析多個 AWS 帳戶的資料。資料及應用程式位於三個不同帳戶的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體。帳戶 A 包含交易資料；帳戶 B 包含客戶資料，其中有個人識別資訊（PII）；帳戶 C 託管 GenAI 應用程式。公司計畫在未來幾個月加入另外七個事業單位的資料來源。公司必須嚴格控管 PII，並確保 FM 只能存取必要的資料欄位。公司需要為 GenAI 應用程式建立安全的跨帳戶存取。哪個方案符合這些需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Identity Center 為 FM 服務帳戶建立許可集。在每個 S3 儲存貯體設定以資源為基礎的政策，允許帳戶 C 進行特定存取。部署自訂 AWS Lambda 授權器，在將資料傳送給 FM 前過濾 PII。","B":"設定 Amazon Bedrock 跨帳戶 IAM 角色。在各來源帳戶建立以角色為基礎的存取政策，只允許存取特定 S3 儲存貯體路徑。對 S3 物件套用以標籤為基礎的存取控制，以分類及控管 PII 資料。","C":"在每個來源帳戶設定 AWS Lake Formation，並向 Lake Formation 註冊 S3 儲存貯體。在來源帳戶建立 IAM 角色，使其具有存取特定 S3 儲存貯體路徑的權限。設定 Lake Formation 權限，使用 Lake Formation 標籤式存取控制，只允許存取特定資料欄位。使用 Amazon SageMaker AI 部署 FM，其執行角色位於帳戶 C，可擔任跨帳戶 IAM 角色，透過 Lake Formation 存取資料。","D":"在每個來源帳戶的 S3 儲存貯體設定以資源為基礎的政策，允許帳戶 C 的 GenAI 應用程式存取。為 FM 服務角色設定以身分為基礎的政策，使用 AWS Lake Formation 標籤式存取控制，只允許存取特定資料欄位。在每個帳戶設定 VPC 端點，以提供安全的跨帳戶存取。"},"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C is the intended choice because Lake Formation can share catalog resources across accounts and apply LF-Tags to tables and columns. The application must retrieve filtered data through a Lake Formation-integrated query engine before passing it to the FM; merely assuming a role or hosting a model in SageMaker does not enforce column filtering. Direct S3 object access must not provide a bypass around those permissions. S3 path/object policies alone cannot select columns inside an object, and IAM identity policies cannot substitute for Lake Formation data permissions.","explanation_zh":"C 是題目預期答案，因為 Lake Formation 可跨帳戶分享目錄資源，並將 LF-Tags 套用至資料表及欄位。應用程式必須透過整合 Lake Formation 的查詢引擎取得已過濾資料，再提供給 FM；僅擔任角色或在 SageMaker 託管模型，不會自動實施欄位過濾。直接讀取 S3 物件的權限也不能成為繞過這些控制的途徑。S3 路徑／物件政策本身無法選取物件內的特定欄位，IAM 身分政策也不能取代 Lake Formation 資料權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Identity Center permission sets and a Lambda authorizer are not a managed column-level cross-account data governance mechanism; an authorizer does not automatically transform the payload.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 許可集及 Lambda 授權器不等於受管的跨帳戶欄位治理機制；授權器也不會自動轉換資料內容。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Object tags and path permissions govern whole objects or prefixes, not PII columns within an object.","why_zh":"物件標籤及路徑權限控制整個物件或前綴，無法控管物件內的 PII 欄位。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It misplaces Lake Formation column grants in IAM identity policies; VPC endpoints provide a network path, not column filtering.","why_zh":"它錯把 Lake Formation 欄位授權當成 IAM 身分政策設定；VPC 端點提供網路路徑，不負責欄位過濾。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/cross-account-TBAC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/how-it-works.html"],"issues":["C needs an integrated query/data access path and prevention of direct S3 bypass."],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.871289+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":134,"question_en":"A logistics company is building an agentic GenAI-powered solution to automate freight optimization. The solution must retrieve data in real time from multiple internal and external systems. The solution must include a human- in-the-loop approval step before the optimization process is finished. The solution must support modular growth as the number of integrations and amount of logic increases. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","options_en":{"A":"Use an Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint that hosts a large language model (LLM) that directly calls all internal databases and external APIs. Use a custom web application that provides a UI to implement the human-in-the-loop review step.","B":"Build a hierarchical system by using the Strands Agents SDK and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. Configure a coordinating agent to delegate tasks to multiple specialized agents. Use MCP to facilitate inter-agent messaging. Use AWS Step Functions to implement a human-in-the-loop approval step.","C":"Use AWS Glue to aggregate operational data into Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query the data. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to generate route assignments. Use Amazon SNS to send notifications to supervisor agents.","D":"Use a single Amazon Bedrock AgentCore agent with AWS Lambda based tools to integrate with all internal and external systems. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate the approval workflow."},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/RAG","GenAI/Agents","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":134,"pages":[225]},"question_zh":"一家物流公司正在建置代理式 GenAI 方案，以自動化貨運最佳化。方案必須即時從多個內部及外部系統擷取資料，且必須在最佳化流程完成前加入人工參與的核准步驟。隨著整合數量及邏輯增加，方案必須支援模組化成長。哪個方案能以最少的維運負擔符合這些需求？","options_zh":{"A":"使用託管大型語言模型（LLM）的 Amazon SageMaker AI 端點，由 LLM 直接呼叫所有內部資料庫及外部 API。使用提供 UI 的自訂 Web 應用程式，實作人工參與的審核步驟。","B":"使用 Strands Agents SDK 及 Amazon Bedrock AgentCore 建立階層式系統。設定協調代理，將任務委派給多個專門代理。使用 MCP 促進代理間的訊息傳遞。使用 AWS Step Functions 實作人工參與的核准步驟。","C":"使用 AWS Glue 將作業資料彙整至 Amazon S3，並使用 Amazon Athena 查詢。呼叫 AWS Lambda 函數產生路線指派，再以 Amazon SNS 將通知傳送給監督代理。","D":"使用單一 Amazon Bedrock AgentCore 代理，以 AWS Lambda 工具整合所有內部及外部系統。使用 AWS Step Functions 協調核准工作流程。"},"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"B most directly addresses growth through specialized agents and delegated responsibilities, with AgentCore providing managed runtime infrastructure. Step Functions can pause for human approval using a task token before the workflow continues. The phrase about MCP inter-agent messaging is imprecise: MCP exposes tools/resources, while A2A is designed for agent-to-agent communication; an agent may still be exposed as an MCP tool through an explicit integration. D can be simpler for a small system, so B is preferable here because the stem emphasizes expanding integrations and modular logic, not because multi-agent systems always have less overhead.","explanation_zh":"B 透過專門代理及責任委派，最直接回應系統成長需求，並由 AgentCore 提供受管執行環境。Step Functions 可用任務權杖暫停工作流程，等待人工核准後才繼續。選項所稱 MCP 代理間訊息傳遞並不精確：MCP 用於公開工具／資源，A2A 才是針對代理間通訊設計；若明確實作整合，也可把代理公開成 MCP 工具。小型系統採 D 可能更簡單，因此此題偏向 B 的理由是題幹強調持續增加的整合及模組化邏輯，而不是多代理一定比較省維運。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A monolithic model endpoint plus custom integrations and approval UI increases maintenance and lacks delegated modular responsibilities.","why_zh":"單一模型端點加上自訂整合及核准 UI，會增加維護負擔，也缺乏分工的模組責任。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Batch-style aggregation and supervisor notifications do not provide the stated real-time agent orchestration or a blocking human approval gate.","why_zh":"資料彙整及監督代理通知，未提供所需即時代理協調及會暫停流程的人工核准關卡。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A single agent with tools is viable and initially simpler, but B more explicitly separates growing domains and reasoning responsibilities.","why_zh":"單一代理搭配工具是可行且初期較簡單的作法，但 B 更明確分離持續成長的領域與推理責任。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/runtime-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-step-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/runtime-service-contract.html"],"issues":["MCP is described as inter-agent messaging without explaining agent-as-tool integration.","Least overhead depends on scale; D remains a plausible smaller-system design."],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.872658+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":135,"question_en":"A financial services company is building a fraud detection system by using Amazon Bedrock. The system will monitor activity in multiple stock trading applications that run in the United States and Europe. The system must process 1,000 transactions every second with sub-500 ms response times. The system must also maintain high availability during connectivity disruptions. The company must ensure that data for European customers is processed only in AWS Regions that are based in Europe. Which solution will meet these requirements?","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Lambda functions and Amazon EKS applications to use the InvokeModel API with a global inference profile. Deploy an automated failover system that uses Amazon Route 53 health checks. Create a dedicated European inference profile and enable Geographic cross-Region inference for European applications. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor utilization metrics.","B":"Configure all applications to use the InvokeModel API with provisioned throughput for an Anthropic Claude model in each Region separately. Set up a custom Application Load Balancer to distribute traffic based on Regional capacity and response times. Implement a Regional failover mechanism that uses Amazon EventBridge rules to handle connectivity disruptions.","C":"Configure all applications to use the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API with on-demand throughput. Deploy an Amazon API Gateway REST API with Regional endpoints in each location where the company operates to route requests to the closest Amazon Bedrock endpoint. Create separate IAM roles for applications that run in the United States and Europe. Grant the IAM roles Region-specific permissions.","D":"Configure applications that run in the United States to use provisioned throughput with the InvokeModel API. Configure European applications to use a Europe-specific geographic inference profile to ensure data sovereignty. Configure automatic scaling for provisioned capacity based on utilization metrics. Use Amazon EventBridge and AWS Lambda functions to implement cross-Region failover mechanisms."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":135,"pages":[226]},"question_zh":"一家金融服務公司正在使用 Amazon Bedrock 建置詐欺偵測系統。系統將監控多個在美國及歐洲執行的股票交易應用程式活動。系統每秒必須處理 1,000 筆交易，回應時間低於 500 毫秒，且在連線中斷期間仍須維持高可用性。公司必須確保歐洲客戶的資料只在位於歐洲的 AWS 區域處理。哪個方案符合這些需求？","options_zh":{"A":"設定 AWS Lambda 函數及 Amazon EKS 應用程式，使用全域推論設定檔呼叫 InvokeModel API。部署使用 Amazon Route 53 健康檢查的自動容錯移轉系統。建立專用的歐洲推論設定檔，為歐洲應用程式啟用地理範圍跨區域推論。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警報監控使用率指標。","B":"設定所有應用程式，分別在每個區域使用 Anthropic Claude 模型的佈建輸送量呼叫 InvokeModel API。設定自訂 Application Load Balancer，根據區域容量及回應時間分散流量。實作以 Amazon EventBridge 規則處理連線中斷的區域容錯移轉機制。","C":"設定所有應用程式，使用隨需輸送量呼叫 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API。在公司營運的各地部署具有區域端點的 Amazon API Gateway REST API，將請求導向最近的 Amazon Bedrock 端點。為美國及歐洲應用程式建立不同 IAM 角色，授予各角色特定區域的權限。","D":"設定美國應用程式，使用佈建輸送量呼叫 InvokeModel API。設定歐洲應用程式使用歐洲專屬的地理範圍推論設定檔，以確保資料主權。設定依使用率指標自動擴展佈建容量。使用 Amazon EventBridge 及 AWS Lambda 函數實作跨區域容錯移轉機制。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"low","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is the closest intended answer only if every European request, including failover traffic, uses a Europe geographic profile instead of the global profile. Geographic profiles keep processing within their geography; global profiles do not provide that restriction. Cross-Region inference can improve access to capacity, but neither it nor Route 53 guarantees 1,000 requests per second with end-to-end latency below 500 ms. Model choice, token volume, quotas, and failover behavior require measurement and explicit design. D has a reasonable geographic split, but its automatic provisioned-capacity scaling is unspecified, and inference profiles do not support Provisioned Throughput. No option establishes all numeric requirements as written.","explanation_zh":"只有在所有歐洲請求（包含容錯移轉流量）都使用歐洲地理範圍設定檔、而非全域設定檔的前提下，A 才是最接近題意的答案。地理範圍設定檔會將處理限制在該地理範圍內，全域設定檔則沒有這項限制。跨區域推論有助取得更多容量，但它與 Route 53 都不保證每秒 1,000 筆請求及低於 500 毫秒的端到端延遲。模型選擇、token 數量、配額及容錯移轉行為仍須實測與明確設計。D 的地理分流方向合理，但未交代如何自動擴展佈建容量，而且推論設定檔不支援 Provisioned Throughput。依題目原文，沒有任何選項已證明全部數值要求可達成。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"It does not constrain European failover destinations and a regional ALB is not by itself a cross-Region Bedrock capacity router.","why_zh":"它未限制歐洲流量的容錯移轉目的地，區域性 ALB 本身也不是 Bedrock 跨區域容量路由器。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Streaming improves perceived first output, not guaranteed complete fraud-decision latency; nearest endpoints and regional roles do not supply an automatic recovery architecture.","why_zh":"串流改善首段輸出的感受時間，不保證完整詐欺判定延遲；最近端點及區域角色也未提供自動恢復架構。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The geographic split is sensible, but unspecified automatic provisioned-capacity scaling and custom failover do not prove the throughput/latency target.","why_zh":"地理分流合理，但未具體說明的佈建容量自動擴展及自訂容錯移轉，無法證明輸送量／延遲目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html"],"issues":["No option guarantees the stated 1,000 TPS and sub-500 ms deadline.","A must exclude all European traffic from global inference, including failover."],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.873609+00:00"},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定有疑義"},{"id":136,"question_en":"A company is implementing a 2-week initiative to incorporate GenAI into several hundred existing applications to provide context-driven natural language help for users. To simplify the process to choose an appropriate model for each application, a GenAI Developer is building a system to automatically compare foundation models (FMs) based on general text generation accuracy. The system runs a job that performs a series of steps. First, the system creates a service role and attaches an IAM permissions policy that allows Amazon Bedrock to invoke the FMs and grants access to Amazon S3. Then the system requests and receives access to all the FMs that need to be tested. Then the system creates S3 buckets to store the evaluation results. Then the system creates evaluation configurations by using the TREX built-in dataset. Finally, the system specifies the Accuracy metric and Generation evaluation type in each evaluation configuration. When the GenAI developer attempts to run the system, it fails with an AccessDenied exception. The GenAI developer must resolve the issue. Which solution will meet this requirement?","options_en":{"A":"Create a trust policy that defines Amazon Bedrock as the service principal. Attach the trust policy to the service role.","B":"Configure cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) permissions that allow GET and DELETE actions on the S3 buckets.","C":"Change the test dataset from TREX to Gigaword in the evaluation configurations.","D":"Change the evaluation type to Summarization and the metric type to Correctness in the evaluation configurations."},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["GenAI/Evaluation","GenAI/Models"],"source":{"file":"136题_AIP-C01_202609_en.pdf","sha256":"59f9cdc300117bb8de8119ce36b87be5c845e01b78d34b8a94c1dae41e7011a6","batch":"2026-09","question":136,"pages":[227]},"question_zh":"一家公司正執行為期兩週的計畫，要將 GenAI 整合到現有數百個應用程式，為使用者提供依上下文產生的自然語言協助。為簡化各應用程式的模型選擇，GenAI 開發人員正在建置一套系統，依一般文字生成的準確度自動比較基礎模型（FM）。系統執行的工作包含多個步驟：首先建立服務角色，附加 IAM 權限政策，允許 Amazon Bedrock 呼叫 FM 並存取 Amazon S3；接著請求並取得所有待測 FM 的存取權；然後建立 S3 儲存貯體以存放評估結果；再使用 TREX 內建資料集建立評估設定；最後在各評估設定指定 Accuracy 指標及 Generation 評估類型。GenAI 開發人員嘗試執行系統時，發生 AccessDenied 例外而失敗。開發人員必須解決這個問題。哪個方案符合此需求？","options_zh":{"A":"建立信任政策，將 Amazon Bedrock 定義為服務主體，並將信任政策附加至服務角色。","B":"設定跨來源資源共用（CORS）權限，允許對 S3 儲存貯體執行 GET 及 DELETE 動作。","C":"在評估設定中，將測試資料集由 TREX 改為 Gigaword。","D":"在評估設定中，將評估類型改為 Summarization，並將指標類型改為 Correctness。"},"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A supplies the missing trust relationship that lets bedrock.amazonaws.com assume the evaluation service role with sts:AssumeRole. An identity permissions policy grants actions after assumption but does not itself allow the service to assume the role. AWS documents TREX with Accuracy for general text generation, so the dataset and task combination is appropriate. Browser CORS settings and unrelated evaluation changes do not repair this missing service-role trust. In a real failure, other IAM and KMS denials should also be investigated if correcting the trust policy is insufficient.","explanation_zh":"A 補上必要的信任關係，允許 bedrock.amazonaws.com 使用 sts:AssumeRole 擔任評估服務角色。身分權限政策規範擔任角色後可執行的動作，本身不會允許服務擔任該角色。AWS 文件列出一般文字生成可使用 TREX 搭配 Accuracy，因此資料集與任務的組合正確。瀏覽器 CORS 設定及改動其他評估設定，都無法修復缺少的服務角色信任。在實際排錯中，若修正信任政策後仍失敗，還應檢查其他 IAM 及 KMS 拒絕原因。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CORS controls browser cross-origin requests and does not grant the Bedrock service permission to assume an IAM role.","why_zh":"CORS 控制瀏覽器跨來源請求，不會授予 Bedrock 服務擔任 IAM 角色的權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"TREX is a documented dataset for general-generation Accuracy; changing datasets does not fix authorization.","why_zh":"TREX 是文件列出的通用生成 Accuracy 資料集；更換資料集無法修正授權。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Changing the evaluation task would change the objective and still leave the service-role trust missing.","why_zh":"更換評估任務會改變評估目標，且仍然缺少服務角色信任。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/automatic-service-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-evaluation-tasks-general-text.html"],"issues":[],"verified":true,"checked_at":"2026-09-30T09:46:00.874304+00:00"},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"無社群票、單選"}];
